/div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Veryyyyyy interesting. Does Hard-A-Lee localize on one part of Massachusetts or on the entire state?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ipswich, specifically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T12:59:51-08:00","id":1158602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1158543#post1158543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The whole book will be in the backer previews. Those will be in the third week. We'll also do one or more settings as public previews. (Caveat on that, though -- I'm gonna want to lead with Tumbledown Market, which people who follow the blog have already seen. I'm just really in love with that one and want to share it with the larger KS update audience.)<br /> <br /> I think I mentioned this before, but the settings are:<ul><li><b>Eighty-Nine Dreams of Home</b>, Hong Kong (the Societies of Morning, Day, and Night)</li> <li><b>The Council of Elves</b>, Reykjavik (the four seasons, but not as you know them)</li> <li><b>Hard-a-Lee</b>, Massachusetts (the Courts of High Tide, Ebb Tide, Low Tide, and Flood Tide)</li> <li><b>Tumbledown Market</b>, New Orleans and other linked locations (the Courts of Coin, Barter, Favors, and Shady Deals)</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div> What happened to Miami and Toronto Freeholds, I mean Toronto is still in the Anthology, so I thought it was still in as a setting for the core???","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T13:02:08-08:00","id":1158603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1158602#post1158602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What happened to Miami and Toronto Freeholds, I mean Toronto is still in the Anthology, so I thought it was still in as a setting for the core???</div> </div> </div> </div>Miami and Toronto are not in the core book, but may appear later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T13:03:10-08:00","id":1158604,"title":"","content":"I'm afraid to say I'm pretty disappointed with the smattering of Kiths, and the return to four seasonal courts. I'm sincerely hoping Contracts haven't followed suit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T13:06:54-08:00","id":1158606,"title":"","content":"Contracts had <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/contracts-of-steed-changeling-the-lost/\" target=\"_blank\">a pretty extensive preview</a> on the blog, if you want to look that over.<br /> <br /> There's support for custom courts with custom mantles, and each of the sample settings has its own courts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T13:08:46-08:00","id":1158607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1158568#post1158568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@<b><a href=\"http://&quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Charlaquin</a></b> There's a couple mechanics that references Clarity. There's a couple that say &quot;you risk Clarity damage,&quot; which I originally presumed to mean &quot;roll for a breaking point&quot; in different language. Then, I saw a bit that talked about taking mild Clarity damage and severe Clarity damage. Don't know if that perks your interest or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I have heard here and there that Clarity works like a health track, and I <i>really</i> dont like the sound of that. I would like to see the full context before coming to any conclusions, but everything I\u2019ve heard about it so far has only reminded me of everything I dislike about Sanity systems in other games, particularly those influenced by Call of Cthulhu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T13:17:43-08:00","id":1158610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1158603#post1158603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Miami and Toronto are not in the core book, but may appear later.</div> </div> </div> </div> I hope so, I'm really upset they aren't there, perhaps those courts would be perfect for the companion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T13:21:22-08:00","id":1158612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1158607#post1158607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I have heard here and there that Clarity works like a health track, and I <i>really</i> dont like the sound of that. I would like to see the full context before coming to any conclusions, but everything I\u2019ve heard about it so far has only reminded me of everything I dislike about Sanity systems in other games, particularly those influenced by Call of Cthulhu.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's definitely not Sanity, or, for that matter, sanity. It's also not Integrity or Morality. But there's not much more detail I can give before the preview gets put up -- I posted above about what it <i>means</i>, and you'll see the roll-by-roll stuff in a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T13:22:37-08:00","id":1158613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1158606#post1158606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Contracts had <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/contracts-of-steed-changeling-the-lost/\" target=\"_blank\">a pretty extensive preview</a> on the blog, if you want to look that over.<br /> <br /> There's support for custom courts with custom mantles, and each of the sample settings has its own courts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent news! Here's hoping for 5x the number of Kiths. (Though I totally get the limit, word count being what it is)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T13:26:45-08:00","id":1158614,"title":"","content":"I've only skimmed here and there but overall I like what I'm seeing. While I liked the concept of your Seeming being how you escaped rather than what your Keeper did to you, I have to admit the new write ups feel more flexible. The previous set felt like a specific charachter rather than a foundation. I think the physical decscriptions of Wizened fit much better than the old cyborg ones. I'm still hopeful that one day there will be a damsel in distress kith who's blessing helps convince others that they are innocnent, harmless, and should be rescued (truthfully or to trick them). The Notary Kith was a pretty awesome addition, I'm hoping at some point there'll be some mechanics for a Notary using the specific pledge they represent against their keeper.<br /> <br /> The give and take for the Courts were also a step up from the old Approaches. Approaches gave points to Huntsmen, but nothing stopped a Huntsman taking it's full starting pool and going straight for the capture. Autumn and Winter were particularly good, since they forced the Gentry to play to the Changling Court's strength. Autumn gets plenty of time to hit the books, and since Winter inflicts a horrible disadvantage in open combat the Gentry are all but forced to try and catch changelings alone in dark alleyways - and Winter plays that game well. Spring and Summer didn't capture me the same way. Spring controls when the Gentry/Huntsmen/Loyalists are aloud to attack, but doesn't change the methods they can use after they make their move. Summer feels like it would discourage open conflicts in favour of striking isolated weak targets, but on the other hand we haven't seen the mechanics for Gentry and Huntsman yet. If there's plenty of ways for them to escape then this becomes a useful bonus, even if not specifically a bonus about not being abducted again.<br /> <br /> The Hedge seemed solid, but I'd like to see mechanics on that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1158604#post1158604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm afraid to say I'm pretty disappointed with the smattering of Kiths.</div> </div> </div> </div>What would you have liked to see differently? Or was it just not enough Kiths for your taste?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T13:46:27-08:00","id":1158621,"title":"","content":"Might someone at least confirm if Seeming and Kith are still separate <i>ala </i>Underhill? Because if we're back to the 1e mold, that's a solid pass from me even at full-release.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11533-bluegrass-beast","name":"Bluegrass Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T13:47:43-08:00","id":1158622,"title":"","content":"backer numer 537. right now I'm only to chapter one in the preview. I'm getting the feelings I got from when I read up the 1st edition that first time so far, hopefully it continues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12235-emmens","name":"emmens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12235_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T13:47:57-08:00","id":1158623,"title":"","content":"It looks like they're separate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T13:53:43-08:00","id":1158625,"title":"","content":"I like the Fairest Curse.<br /> <br /> A Lot.<br /> <br /> Actually I like all of them, but the Fairest Curse is. Well it's good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T13:58:32-08:00","id":1158626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1158625#post1158625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the Fairest Curse.<br /> <br /> A Lot.<br /> <br /> Actually I like all of them, but the Fairest Curse is. Well it's good.</div> </div> </div> </div>What was the curse again? I can't find the preview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T14:15:07-08:00","id":1158633,"title":"","content":"I've kicked in. My comments will wait until I actually see something. All I can say is that C:TL was my favourite NWoD game and I don't expect that I will be disappointed in the 2nd ed. \u263a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5435-mhicwombat","name":"MhicWombat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T14:18:17-08:00","id":1158634,"title":"","content":"A while when the old court creation preview was posted we all started posting courts. I thought I'd adapt the one I wrote, the Flower Courts, to the new Give and Take mechanics. They're a Freehold deeply focused on being a part of mundane society.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Flower Courts.</b><br /> <br /> The Freehold claim that their fonders were born in the iron age, and they lived well and prospered for every generation the village would come togeather and choose the greatest of their number to be a king. They would obey their monarch in all things, and so each became as great as the village's best. But one king decreed upon his deathbed that they would choose his eldest son; for the king loved his son as all fathers do and could not see that his son was not the greatest in the village.<br /> <br /> Under the king's son's rule the village fell into poverty. The walls crumbled, the warriors became lazy and arrogant. The Gentry saw this weakness and took the entire population as slaves.<br /> <br /> By the time the survivors escaped the world they remembered no longer existed. &quot;Do not fear.&quot; they told one another,. &quot;We will find a king who understands this new world&quot;.<br /> <br /> Following power itself the arrived at Washington where they saw congressmen and senators going about their business. &quot;Surely one of these powerful men will be our king&quot; they said. But the senators and congressmen spoke about elections, and checks, and balances, and the villagers could not understand them.<br /> <br /> Next they travelled to Boston, where they saw factories and industry on a scale they couldn't imagine. &quot;Surely a man who can create such marvels could be a king&quot; they said. But the industrialists spoke of shareholders, and investments, and capitol, and the villages could not understand them.<br /> <br /> Then they arrived at Pennsylvania, where they saw the university. &quot;These men have studied all things, surely one of them must know how to be a king&quot; they said. But the scientists spoke of methodology, and peer review, and the villagers could not understand them.<br /> <br /> Distraught the villagers wondered the streets, they feared that without a king to protect them their old masters would return. By change they came across a lover presenting flowers and this was a language they could understand, and so they asked the flowers to choose them a king.<br /> <br /> <b>Give and take:</b> Each Flower Court forces the Gentry or their servants to sabotage a Courtier's mundane life before they may attempt to attack them, enchant them, or drag them back to arcadia and every flower as two weaknesses: The gentry can either slip through it's <i>open petals</i> by convincing a mortal to break a pledge with the Changeling, which mortals qualify depends on the Court. Having no pledges goes against the fundamental nature of the Flower Courts and provides no protection, the Huntsman are free to target any Changeling who does not have at least Wyrd / 2 appropriate pledges at will. The exception is the Court of Honeysuckle who only ever require one pledge, but require greater intimacy at higher Wyrd. If the open petals do not attract, a Huntsman can instead <i>wilt the vine </i>by attacking the Changeling's place in society.<br /> <br /> As the Flower Courts are all and always subordinate to the Lilly Crown each Changeling always benefits from their own Court's protection.<br /> <br /> <b>The Court of Balsam, The Unyielding Flora, The Red Blossom, The Court of Stubbornness</b><br /> <br /> <i>I was subjected to tortures you mere mortals couldn\u2019t imagine so I\u2019d like some fucking sympathy please.</i><br /> <br /> The Court of Balsam do not return to mortal society so much as they expect mortal society to come to them on their terms. Almost every Changeling returns from Arcadia with phobias, supersitions and sometimes even frailties. The Court of Stubbornness doesn't even try to overcome these, they're offended by the notion that they should. Instead they mortal society to accommodate them. While the Freehold considers the Red Blossom to be stubborn gits who refuse to understand every relationship requires some give and take, they are invaluable to the Freehold because they remind the other changelings that yes, they do have issues, and yes they need to ask for accommodation before they snap.<br /> <br /> <b>Give and Take</b><b>:</b> The Gentry and their servants wilt the vine by convincing a member of the Red Blossom to compromise on some accommodation related to their traumas from Arcadia.<br /> <br /> <b>The Court of Hollyhock, The Proud Bloom, The Gold Blossom, The Court of Ambition</b><br /> <br /> <i>I\u2019m sure you\u2019ve read all sorts of faerie tales about our trickery, well that\u2019s the old way. Modern faeries understand the benefits of customer satisfaction. So here\u2019s my offer, seven years younger for seven million in cash, and I\u2019ll make the same offer in seven years time. </i><br /> <br /> The Court of Hollyhock want a life among mortals, but not just any life. Wealth, power or fame, their new life is going to be extraordinary if it takes every Contract they know to make it happen. This Court provides the Freehold with much of it's wealth and influence which makes up for the fact that the Gold Blossom is the least involved in day to day Freehold Life.<br /> <br /> <b>Give and Take</b><b>:</b> The Gentry and their servants wilt the vine by inflicting a serious career setback to a member of the Gold Blossom; such as a demotion.<br /> <br /> <b>The Court of Honeysuckle, The Choking Vine, The Pink Blossom, The Court of Dependency</b><br /> <br /> <i>Please, we can make it work. I can change.</i><br /> <br /> The True Fae break their slaves. Their souls are full of gaps, and the Court of Honeysuckle return to the mortal world looking for someone who can fill those gaps. Some seek out their old family or their old loves, others tumble through relationship after relationship always looking for &quot;the one&quot;. The Pink Blossom is infamous for the fragility of their members, especially when they're supressing their true personality for their lover's benefit, however the Choking Vine is invaluable to the Freehold because they're the only Court who, however clumsily, relate to average mortals on their own level.<br /> <br /> <b>Give and Take</b><b>:</b> The Gentry and their servants wilt the vine by tempting the Pink Blossom into betraying their relationship, such as seducing the changeling into cheating on their partner.<br /> <br /> <b>The Court of Violet, The Humble Herb, The Blue Blossom, The Court of Satisfaction </b><br /> <br /> <i>Hi Ho, Hi Ho, It\u2019s Off To Work We Go!</i><br /> <br /> If the Flower Courts are about fitting in with mortal society then the Court of Violet have figured it out. They find some quiet corner, usually one where their faerie talents are useful, and then they keep their heads down and do their job. Typically invisible, and happy that way, the Humble Herb take satisfaction in their work and being valuable to the mortals around them. In the Freehold the Blue Blossom are the ones who keep everything running. Few ever aim for status or influence, and those who have status or influence know better than to take the Court of Satisfaction for granted.<br /> <br /> <b>Give and Take</b><b>:</b> The Gentry and their servants wilt the vine by successfully tempting the Blue Blossom with wealth or status.<br /> <br /> <b>The Lily Crown The Royal Flower, The White Blossom, The Crown</b><br /> <br /> A pure white lily symbolises many things. It symbolises virginity and purity, a Changeling\u2019s lost state of grace before the Gentry plucked them from earth. To give someone a white lily says that it is heavenly to be with you, as it is heavenly for Changelings to be back home with humanity. Most importantly of all a white Lily symbolises majesty.<br /> <br /> <br /> Once a year the courts oneiromancers create a dreamscape. In this dreamscape there is a road beset by trials. The road leads to a hall with an empty throne with a crown of white lillies upon it. The oneiromancers take the dream and divide it up between as many vessels as they can, but by tradition every changeling must have at least one vessel.<br /> <br /> On the appointed day each Changeling secrets their vessels into people's beds. Some trust chance and Wyrd, others spend months before the day choosing their champions. That night each mortal with a vessel dreams themselves onto the path, they face the trials, and the first to reach the throne and claim the crown becomes king or queen of the freehold. Everyone else awakes with no memory and a good night's rest.<br /> <br /> The trials themselves can be as easy or as challenging as the freehold wishes. Only two rules remain in force, the first is that no king or queen may ever know of or influence the selection process, they're told the flowers, that is to say the Wyrd, chooses. The second is that one trial must rule out any mortal with a connection to the Gentry or to a changing freehold.<br /> <br /> In some desperate years those have been the only trials, but most have many more. A trial so that the new monarch cannot be cruel. A trial to exclude fae-tocuhed (for who wants a king to send his knights to Arcadia?) The Freehold often comes up with lengthy and elaborate criteria, but they must be careful. If no mortal makes it past all the trials the Bulwark shatters for the next year. Even setting too many trials will cause mortals to wake up before completing the quest or failing at a task.<br /> <br /> And thus every year one ignorant mortal suddenly discovers that they're king or queen of the faeries.<br /> <br /> None of the other Flower Courts have a Court Crown, their power is concentrated in the Lily Crown to grant a mortal everything they need to rule the faeries. The Crown provides:<ul><li>The Sight, Lily Kings can see through the Mask. (Former Kings retain this ability)</li> <li>Comfort with the Hedge: Lily Queens have a five die pool to open Hedge Gates and may open or create new ones by spending a point of Willpower. Once inside The Hedge they can navigate, are immune to any mental effect that does not affect Changelings and they are protected from both the thorns and transforming into a hobgoblin.</li> <li>The ability to make up to 5 Pledges, as well as Pledges of fealty and vassalage.</li> <li>Protection from magic: Any dice pool to activate a contract or which has been increased through magic takes a 5 Success penalty when targeting a Lily King, unless his majesty consciously allows it.</li> <li>Status in the courts, just as a Mantle provides social bonuses so does the Lily Crown. Lily Queens get a +3 bonus to all Flower Courts, which can stack with Court Goodwill to a maximum of +5. (Former Queens retain a +2 bonus and any Goodwill their previous subjects feel).</li> <li>Most potently of all, every month when the first sliver of the new moon shines the Lily King must declare one Court exemplary. They may choose based on any criteria they wish, and that Court's protection is enhanced. For the reminder of the month no Courter need fear the Gentry attacking them through the wilting vine.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Give and Take:</b> The Lilly Crown rests on a mortal head, but even they benefit from protection against the Gentry. No True Fae or servant thereof can attack the wearer of the Lilly Crown unless they are in the presence of at least four Changelings from the Flower Courts who genuinely wish them harm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-26-2019, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T14:21:28-08:00","id":1158636,"title":"","content":"Also.. I'm hearing a &quot;smattering of Kiths&quot; - is this small number a sample, or the entirety of what's to be provided in the book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11533-bluegrass-beast","name":"Bluegrass Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T14:25:52-08:00","id":1158639,"title":"","content":"Instead of the roughly 100 kiths we had, we now have 12, that's it, but I guess that is why the book of Kiths is being made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T14:26:36-08:00","id":1158640,"title":"","content":"Kiths are not dependent on seemings; you can pair any kith with any seeming. Each kith comes with two examples.<br /> <br /> We only had room to include so many kiths in the core book. But as you can see, we're hoping to reach some stretch goals with the Kickstarter that will allow us to create a Book of Kiths!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T14:28:48-08:00","id":1158641,"title":"","content":"The very first supplement revealed for the line is about Kiths. They only have so much space for the corebook, and while it would be nice to have hundreds of examples in the core I think you should temper your expectations with reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T14:32:22-08:00","id":1158642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1158626#post1158626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was the curse again? I can't find the preview.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CtL Preview</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Curse: In addition to your character\u2019s other breaking points, she risks Clarity damage with a dice pool equal to half her Wyrd (rounded up) whenever her action \u2014 or inaction \u2014 leads directly to misfortune for her allies.</div> </div> </div> </div>(I hope it's ok I quote it...If not I can take it down.)<br /> <br /> I like what it says about their mentality. I like what I would do if I were a Fairest in order to avoid this. I like the story potential of being a Fairest who loves her motley and tries very hard to help and lead them to better things but also tends to shut herself out hoping that she doesn't witness something where an action she took went badly. <br /> <br /> I like how weird and otherworldly that kind of behavior would seem. On the outside a Font of compassion but intermittently a scared-to-be-hurt shut-in. I've never thought about playing a Fairest before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T14:33:14-08:00","id":1158643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1158641#post1158641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The very first supplement revealed for the line is about Kiths. They only have so much space for the corebook, and while it would be nice to have hundreds of examples in the core I think you should temper your expectations with reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus all of the previews from Underhill are still avaliable, so you can use them as a stopgap until we get the Book of Kiths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T14:37:11-08:00","id":1158646,"title":"","content":"Hopefully I can say this without stirring up too much commotion.<br /> <br /> Underhill Seemings? Good.<br /> Rose-Meghan Seemings? Better.<br /> <br /> Still reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-14-2017, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T14:41:24-08:00","id":1158647,"title":"","content":"The seemings are Meghan's handiwork. I'm quite happy with them, and glad Ogres are &quot;metal.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T14:42:06-08:00","id":1158648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1158640#post1158640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kiths are not dependent on seemings; you can pair any kith with any seeming. Each kith comes with two examples.<br /> <br /> We only had room to include so many kiths in the core book. But as you can see, we're hoping to reach some stretch goals with the Kickstarter that will allow us to create a Book of Kiths!</div> </div> </div> </div>So, this is probably getting ahead of myself, but the use of additional Signature Settings in The Pack was a really awesome part of that book. Could something similar be possible in the Book of Kiths? Settings where Kiths were really important would be very cool to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T14:53:56-08:00","id":1158652,"title":"","content":"Also worth noting about Kiths is the mention of Kith creation rules in chapter 7. So updating the Underhill Kiths should be fairly simple, as should creating brand-new ones. So really, you're not limited to just the twelve in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T15:00:36-08:00","id":1158654,"title":"","content":"My expectations, frankly, were based on the preview material given us.<br /> <br /> I'm not meaning to be surly here, I'm really not. I know I probably sound that way. But after the extended re-shuffles,t he delays, and now what smacks, to me, of obfuscation of the changes made while asking for a financial commitment and support sight-unseen... but twelve or so Kiths? 1e had what, five or six on average per Seeming. What was the word-count needed for if not one of the core aspects of the game?<br /> <br /> <b><i>Now let me preface this next bit with 'I'm not saying this <span style=\"font-size:14px\">is <span style=\"font-size:12px\">the case, but rather <span style=\"font-size:14px\">circumstances make it look troubling in a vacuum</span></span></span></i></b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: when I hear &quot;a huge part of the character mechanics/customization has not only been cut down from what was shown previously, but (apparently) <i><b>from 1e </b></i>'s standards, and then am told &quot;but another book will make up the slack&quot;.. well, the only comparison that comes to mind is the old argument against DLC in the video game industry. It could be taken to look really bad, frankly.<br /> <br /> Now, just for reference, I'm an old warhorse here. I've played Lost 1e since its release back in '07 - and <i>Dreaming </i>was my game before that. Been with the WoD/CofD for twenty years and change. Every new sourcebook that released for Lost 1E was a bit like a birthday, Samhain, and Christmas at once for me - and when the word came down about <i>Dancers in the Dusk </i>and <i>Swords at Dawn? </i>Hoo boy!<br /> <br /> <i>Then </i>we get the Underhill preview and I fell for it, hard and fast, looked forward to a full release, did some homebrew, played in a couple beta venues. Then the game gets pulled back in and reworked under, charitably, messy-feeling circumstances.<br /> <br /> And then I hear about the Kickstarter, finally getting a date, waiting eagerly to finally put my mind at ease.. and.. get this whole affair. Which, to be blunt, has soured me entirely. I've not seen or heard a single thing to allay my concerns, and I <i>keep </i>seeing and hearing things that only increase them.<br /> <br /> I mean,ultimately, know OP is a business. I know my patronage is, in the grand scheme, completely irrelevant and won't be felt whether present or absent.<br /> <br /> But right now, as it stands, '<i>absent</i>' is where we're at, and given how much I love the game? That <i>hurts</i>.<br /> <br /> But that's just my two cents. Best of luck with it folks.</span></span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11533-bluegrass-beast","name":"Bluegrass Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T15:17:38-08:00","id":1158658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluegrass Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1158654#post1158654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.. well, the only comparison that comes to mind is the old argument against DLC in the video game industry. It could be taken to look really bad, frankly.</div> </div> </div> </div>...you mean the practice that has been a thing in the TRPG industry since the beginning?<br /> <br /> All the way back with D&amp;D was fresh and to get things started it required a Player's Guide, a Dungeon Master's Guide, and Monster Manual, or whatever variations of there for the bare minimum?<br /> <br /> Seems like the same as it's always been.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T15:18:13-08:00","id":1158659,"title":"","content":"Second edition kiths are a lot weightier in terms of wordcount than first edition kiths. In 1e, kiths were 50-60 words, essentially each just a name and one power, but there were hints they could mean a lot more. So in 2e, they're around 500-600 words, with a lot more setting info packed into them, plus powers. We're not doing anything tricksy with the wordcount -- we specifically presented fewer kiths in much better depth. We also provide what you need to make your own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T15:19:56-08:00","id":1158660,"title":"","content":"The small number of Kiths is troublesome, but we'll see what the guidelines for making your own are. Might be easy enough to convert most of the old playtest ones.<br /> <br /> Thing I'm wondering/worried about most right now is if the dream systems will remain compatible with the dream form type rules or not like in the old playtest (yes, I know, in the grand scheme it means little but I tend towards a lot of crossover type games, and enjoy system unity).<br /> <br /> Clarity, meanwhile, sounds interesting to me, the 'health track' type approach, but I do want to see more. Also interested in the larger array of merits and contracts; I'm still iffy about the revision to Contracts so far, but not on the 'dealbreaker' level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 11-14-2017, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value"