 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T17:42:39-08:00","id":1160061,"title":"","content":"I think it would be safer to average out how much we're doing per day after the first few days. Changeling could've just had a really strong start, which I can see, because there was plenty of buildup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T17:45:31-08:00","id":1160062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>E11even-E11even</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160061#post1160061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would be safer to average out how much we're doing per day after the first few days. Changeling could've just had a really strong start, which I can see, because there was plenty of buildup.</div> </div> </div> </div>So did Demon. Their arcs look very similar. Its impossible to tell, of course, until we reach the final days. But I am taking a strong start as a positive sign.<br /> <br /> EDIT: and if you look at the numbers, its actually days 2 and 4 that are stronger. Day 1 was only up about $3000.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 11-17-2017, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T17:52:52-08:00","id":1160064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160062#post1160062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So did Demon. Their arcs look very similar. Its impossible to tell, of course, until we reach the final days. But I am taking a strong start as a positive sign.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope so. And I want to make it known that I do want this to do well. I love Changeling- it's my favorite game ever. And, actually, I like the kiths I see. I just really, truly feel like there aren't enough at all (and also like they aren't explained very well). If the goals aren't hit and we get what amounts to an incomplete kiths book, I'll definitely be upset though. Because I believe more should've been included in the core, and that locking these behind stretch goals is a bit shady.<br /> A part of me really wants to pull out on the last day if we don't get the full kith book, because the thought of it being incomplete and hidden behind these monetary milestones is upsetting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T18:19:42-08:00","id":1160071,"title":"","content":"If you're backers then why don't you ask about the Book of Kiths? The update was not addressing what is already in the book. The guy was saying until the final size of the book is set they won't be able to set a price. Any suggestion that there is currently only one section planned is more than likely a mistake or misunderstanding. Assume nothing until that specific question is addressed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T18:23:21-08:00","id":1160072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160013#post1160013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive me if this already has been asked, but what exactly is the difference between the &quot;traditionally printed, hardcover copy of the CHANGELING: THE LOST 2nd Edition Core Rules&quot; received for pledging $50 (or more), and the &quot;CHANGELING: THE LOST 2ND EDITION CORE BOOK Print on Demand (PoD) version&quot; that you get a coupon for when pledging at that level?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unless I'm mistaken, the traditionally printed hardcover will be a prestige edition with a raised holo cover and nicer paper stock for the pages, whereas the PoD will be the regular style book. So the quality won't be as nice, but you can get your hands on it sooner if having a physical book ASAP is a priority. And then gift it to a friend once the prestige edition arrives? That's probably what I'll do.<br /> <br /> (Can somebody confirm if I got that right?)<br /> <br /> Anyway, I absolutely love the write ups for the seemings and the seasonal courts. The text really captures and conveys what they are and why you would want to be one (also why you really wouldn't want to be one).<br /> <br /> That said, count me among the skeptical on the small sampling of kiths. I'm backing at a level where I'll get the kithbook as a free pdf, so in practice I personally will likely have access to updated versions of most of the kiths I liked from 1e/underhill, but it does seem like wordcount could be trimmed <i>somewhere</i> to fit a few more into the core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T18:24:21-08:00","id":1160073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>E11even-E11even</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160064#post1160064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I believe more should've been included in the core, and that locking these behind stretch goals is a bit shady.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, here's the deal. If you don't like the number of Kiths in the core book, you are totally entitled to that opinion. However insinuating multiple times that they were deliberately left out of the book in order to get you to buy more is quite frankly insulting to the writers and developers, especially when they have come into this thread and talked about how important this game was to them personally, and what an honour it was to work on it. Keep in mind that there is a hard word limit on this book. I love the Underhill version of Changeling, but I still have no idea how David planned to fit hundreds of Kiths in. Also worth bearing in mind is that of the 1400 backers of this project, only 300 people have backed at PDF only levels. Those other 1000 people get the Book of Kiths included, <u><b>for free</b></u>, as part of their pledge because the value of the pledge is actually a little bit cheaper than what the final retail value of the book is likely to be on DTRPG. So the whole conspiracy of intentionally decreasing the number of Kiths in the main book to get people to buy another book does not hold up when the vast majority of people are getting that book included in their pledge. The reasons that the goals are spread out so much is so that the Kickstarter will still be able to pay for all of the extra content being created.<br /> <br /> If you don't like the design decision, that is fair. But it is not fair to suggest some nefarious purpose when in fact the Kickstarter is allowing people to get more content for less money. It's not the other way around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T18:28:03-08:00","id":1160075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160054#post1160054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, let's talk numbers people. As far as I can tell, the most successful CofD Kickstarter to date has been Demon. It made about $150k. By day four (on Kicktraq), it had raised about $82.2k. We are just about to finish day 4, as Kicktraq counts them (so really day 3 and a half) and Changeling is just shy of $91.4k.<br /> <br /> I think it is safe to say we are going to hit a metric shit ton of stretch goals still, and a lot of people are going to get a lot of extra content on top of what reward tier they pledge for. Depending of the order of the stretch goals, hitting all six regalia for the Book of Kiths is plausible.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, they tend to flatten about now. I personally will be rather surprised (positively surprised, mind) if we reach the level of Demon.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T18:31:30-08:00","id":1160077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160075#post1160075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the other hand, they tend to flatten about now. I personally will be rather surprised (positively surprised, mind) if we reach the level of Demon.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.kicktraq.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition/#chart-daily\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the dailies for Demon</a>. It looks pretty damn (ha! Pun!) to me. I'd be surprised if we didn't at least reach Demon levels.<br /> <br /> But, as we have said before, it is early days so it'll be tough to estimate unless the kickstarter doesn't flatten out as much as expected<br /> <br /> <u><b>EDIT</b></u>: <a href=\"http://www.kicktraq.com/projects/200664283/changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition/#chart-daily\" target=\"_blank\">Here is Changeling's dailies for comparison's sake. </a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T18:38:55-08:00","id":1160078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160073#post1160073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, here's the deal. If you don't like the number of Kiths in the core book, you are totally entitled to that opinion. However insinuating multiple times that they were deliberately left out of the book in order to get you to buy more is quite frankly insulting to the writers and developers, especially when they have come into this thread and talked about how important this game was to them personally, and what an honour it was to work on it. Keep in mind that there is a hard word limit on this book. I love the Underhill version of Changeling, but I still have no idea how David planned to fit hundreds of Kiths in. Also worth bearing in mind is that of the 1400 backers of this project, only 300 people have backed at PDF only levels. Those other 1000 people get the Book of Kiths included, <u><b>for free</b></u>, as part of their pledge because the value of the pledge is actually a little bit cheaper than what the final retail value of the book is likely to be on DTRPG. So the whole conspiracy of intentionally decreasing the number of Kiths in the main book to get people to buy another book does not hold up when the vast majority of people are getting that book included in their pledge. The reasons that the goals are spread out so much is so that the Kickstarter will still be able to pay for all of the extra content being created.<br /> <br /> If you don't like the design decision, that is fair. But it is not fair to suggest some nefarious purpose when in fact the Kickstarter is allowing people to get more content for less money. It's not the other way around.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can take what I said however you like, but at the end of the day I call em like I see em, and I'm not here to argue over the internet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T18:46:37-08:00","id":1160080,"title":"","content":"Here is what I expect from stretch goals after this one. <br /> <br /> Kith Regalia Mirror ($8,000)<br /> &quot; &quot; Steed ($8,000)<br /> &quot; &quot; Shield ($8,000)<br /> &quot; &quot; Sword ($8,000)<br /> Ready Made Characters ($5,000)<br /> Jump Start ($5,000-$10,000)<br /> Winter Novella ($5,000)<br /> Summer Novella ($5,000)<br /> Spring Novella ($5,000)<br /> Swords at Dawn ($2,000)<br /> Dancers at Dusk ($2,000)<br /> Goblin Market ($2,000)<br /> Setting book (?)<br /> <br /> $64,000, and that leaves plenty of room for odds and ends before reaching say what I expect Changeling to finish at, $200,000 to 300,000.<br /> <br /> I Suspect that when they finally offer the Book of Kiths as an add on it will cause a spike in add on pledges. <br /> <br /> Personally I hope they come up with more reward tiers and add ons for those with with deeper pockets.<br /> <br /> Some other possibilities are Art Budget increase, a full novel, and an interactive audio novel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 11-17-2017, 10:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T19:40:02-08:00","id":1160091,"title":"","content":"Look at MtC kickstarter, my Necropolis: DC book was $8,000 stretch goal and was promised to be 80 pages, but turned out to be 119 pages some how. <br /> <br /> So I suspect each section of the Book of Kiths to be about 80-119 pages, I could be wrong. If I'm right and we get all 6 regalia, I suspect the Book of Kiths to be 480-714 pages long, that's hundreds of Kiths.<br /> <br /> That is with the expanded space for each Kith they appear to get in 2e, a full page roughly each.<br /> <br /> That's means like at least 400 Kiths, assuming some space goes to discussion and advise on kiths and an introduction on Kiths. Holy crap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 11-17-2017, 10:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T19:55:01-08:00","id":1160095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160091#post1160091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look at MtC kickstarter, my Necropolis: DC book was $8,000 stretch goal and was promised to be 80 pages, but turned out to be 119 pages some how. <br /> <br /> So I suspect each section of the Book of Kiths to be about 80-119 pages, I could be wrong. If I'm right and we get all 6 regalia, I suspect the Book of Kiths to be 480-714 pages long, that's hundreds of Kiths.<br /> <br /> That is with the expanded space for each Kith they appear to get in 2e, a full page roughly each.<br /> <br /> That's means like at least 400 Kiths, assuming some space goes to discussion and advise on kiths and an introduction on Kiths. Holy crap.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be lit, but I would be surprised if it ended up larger than the core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T21:02:28-08:00","id":1160109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160072#post1160072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless I'm mistaken, the traditionally printed hardcover will be a prestige edition with a raised holo cover and nicer paper stock for the pages, whereas the PoD will be the regular style book. So the quality won't be as nice, but you can get your hands on it sooner if having a physical book ASAP is a priority. And then gift it to a friend once the prestige edition arrives? That's probably what I'll do.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly what I was looking for, thank you! It's funny; all my books so far have been the PoD versions, so it actually bugs me that my copy of CtL will be different! Haha. I may actually get the second copy, just with the idea of having the players use it (while I use my &quot;good&quot; version) during a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T01:24:25-08:00","id":1160149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160109#post1160109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is exactly what I was looking for, thank you! It's funny; all my books so far have been the PoD versions, so it actually bugs me that my copy of CtL will be different! Haha. I may actually get the second copy, just with the idea of having the players use it (while I use my &quot;good&quot; version) during a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely nothing wrong with that...<br /> <br /> Though I will admit I gave mine to my younger sibling as she enjoyed playing a beast so much that it just worked out. Her copy is the one passed around though. Being the older sibling has it's privileges, along with it's nobles oblige.<br /> <br /> Huh...I wonder if I could base a Fairest around that concept?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T02:10:49-08:00","id":1160151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160109#post1160109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is exactly what I was looking for, thank you! It's funny; all my books so far have been the PoD versions, so it actually bugs me that my copy of CtL will be different! Haha. I may actually get the second copy, just with the idea of having the players use it (while I use my &amp;quot;good&amp;quot; version) during a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition to getting a book of greater quality and shininess to the heavyweight premium print-on-demand, pledging at the level for the physical book will also save money in the long run over getting the pdf + book off drivethrurpg later. This is particularly true if you'd also be inclined to get the stretch goal book pdfs, as basically they'd be included for roughly the same price as getting the standard print version + pdf alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T05:24:52-08:00","id":1160175,"title":"","content":"Question are court (contract wise) gonna function like the Hill preview? They get 1 contract of Emotion, generic and talespinning? With the first being generic effects and i can fill them with whatever emotion my court is about. The second with any Contract that fit. And the third the fatebinding mechanic of 1st?Or its gonna be like 1st with each court having special unique contracts.<br /> <br /> And do Huntsman have the kind of focus than in Hills previews? Tied to how the changeling society works? Or are they like Strix/Idigams in that i can pretend they never exist and little would change from the setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T06:16:29-08:00","id":1160187,"title":"","content":"All I know is that there is Royal Court Contracts and Common Court Contracts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T06:28:42-08:00","id":1160189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160175#post1160175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question are court (contract wise) gonna function like the Hill preview? They get 1 contract of Emotion, generic and talespinning? With the first being generic effects and i can fill them with whatever emotion my court is about. The second with any Contract that fit. And the third the fatebinding mechanic of 1st?Or its gonna be like 1st with each court having special unique contracts.<br /> <br /> And do Huntsman have the kind of focus than in Hills previews? Tied to how the changeling society works? Or are they like Strix/Idigams in that i can pretend they never exist and little would change from the setting?</div> </div> </div> </div> Here's the preview that Rose dropped about the Autumn Court Contracts. They work on the same principle as Contracts of Steed we saw earlier, just without the added Regalia bonuses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1136055-court-contracts-on-2e?p=1141443#post1141443\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1136055-court-contracts-on-2e?p=1141443#post1141443\"> Court contracts on 2e? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1136055-court-contracts-on-2e?p=1141443#post1141443\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1136055-court-contracts-on-2e?p=1141443#post1141443 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I'm trying to run a changeling in my cross-gameline game by the available 2e info, but cannot understand how court contracts work or if they even still exist. Can anyone explain these to me in 'crunch' terms? I have trouble pulling the rules out of the multiple pages of narrative. :/ </div> </div> </div><br /> Here's the Contracts of Steed preview with some more info on how Contracts work - <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/contracts-of-steed-changeling-the-lost/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/contracts-of-...ling-the-lost/</a><br /> <br /> And for the fun of it, how to do your own contracts - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1128918#post1128918\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...18#post1128918</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T06:47:46-08:00","id":1160194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160175#post1160175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And do Huntsman have the kind of focus than in Hills previews? Tied to how the changeling society works? Or are they like Strix/Idigams in that i can pretend they never exist and little would change from the setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll say this...from what I have seen...you probably aren't going to totally ignore them. They are a big part of the agents of the Gentry. As well as loyalists, and other fey allies, huntsmen though are likely to come but be less likely to be encountered early. Seems to be other agents would be sent in first to probe the defenses and do the basic leg work. Everything else would come later. Chances are huntsmen will be something that is there like Abyssals in Mage. A looming threat that the players may accidentally summon. That's my current read on the situation at hand. We shall see more when we get more previews.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T08:53:43-08:00","id":1160224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160091#post1160091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look at MtC kickstarter, my Necropolis: DC book was $8,000 stretch goal and was promised to be 80 pages, but turned out to be 119 pages some how. <br /> <br /> So I suspect each section of the Book of Kiths to be about 80-119 pages, I could be wrong. If I'm right and we get all 6 regalia, I suspect the Book of Kiths to be 480-714 pages long, that's hundreds of Kiths.<br /> <br /> That is with the expanded space for each Kith they appear to get in 2e, a full page roughly each.<br /> <br /> That's means like at least 400 Kiths, assuming some space goes to discussion and advise on kiths and an introduction on Kiths. Holy crap.</div> </div> </div> </div>If this is the case, I would be extremely happy. Iv e yet to pledge myself (because I'm still figuring out which card to use) but some members of my game group pledged. I plan to soon, and if the kithbook could be that big and glorious, I might pledge more just to help hit the stretch goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T09:20:44-08:00","id":1160230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160080#post1160080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is what I expect from stretch goals after this one.<br /> <br /> Kith Regalia Mirror ($8,000)<br /> &quot; &quot; Steed ($8,000)<br /> &quot; &quot; Shield ($8,000)<br /> &quot; &quot; Sword ($8,000)<br /> Ready Made Characters ($5,000)<br /> Jump Start ($5,000-$10,000)<br /> Winter Novella ($5,000)<br /> Summer Novella ($5,000)<br /> Spring Novella ($5,000)<br /> Swords at Dawn ($2,000)<br /> Dancers at Dusk ($2,000)<br /> Goblin Market ($2,000)<br /> Setting book (?)<br /> ....<br /> <br /> Some other possibilities are Art Budget increase, a full novel, and an interactive audio novel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Add in a couple of more sections for a CtL Companion... and you should be a detective!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22659-kickstarter-james","name":"Kickstarter James","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar22659_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T09:22:37-08:00","id":1160231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160091#post1160091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look at MtC kickstarter, my Necropolis: DC book was $8,000 stretch goal and was promised to be 80 pages, but turned out to be 119 pages some how. <br /> <br /> So I suspect each section of the Book of Kiths to be about 80-119 pages, I could be wrong. If I'm right and we get all 6 regalia, I suspect the Book of Kiths to be 480-714 pages long, that's hundreds of Kiths.<br /> <br /> That is with the expanded space for each Kith they appear to get in 2e, a full page roughly each.<br /> <br /> That's means like at least 400 Kiths, assuming some space goes to discussion and advise on kiths and an introduction on Kiths. Holy crap.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Sorry to burst your bubble, but no, this is neither likely nor practical, nor feasible. The money simply isn't allotted that way, and while a handful of CofD books have broken 400 pages, the publishing costs don't bear out for a niche supplement like a book of Kiths, for too many reasons to enumerate here. Let alone for a <i>700</i> page supplement. Even Exalted clocks out at about 650, and that's a core rulebook.<br /> <br /> I won't make any guesses as to what the book will actually end up looking like, because that's not my wheelhouse, but if you're expecting a door stopper tome of nothing but pure, unleaded, high-triple-digit Kiths, you should temper your expectations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 11-18-2017, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T10:03:44-08:00","id":1160242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160194#post1160194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll say this...from what I have seen...you probably aren't going to totally ignore them. They are a big part of the agents of the Gentry. As well as loyalists, and other fey allies, huntsmen though are likely to come but be less likely to be encountered early. Seems to be other agents would be sent in first to probe the defenses and do the basic leg work. Everything else would come later. Chances are huntsmen will be something that is there like Abyssals in Mage. A looming threat that the players may accidentally summon. That's my current read on the situation at hand. We shall see more when we get more previews.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the way hill version made changeling society revolve around huntsmen more than the true fae. Why the Court system exist? For the bullwark that was a kind of pledge to keep the huntsmen away. There was a whole system about some kind of coins (i think) that were a get out of jail card with huntmen that could only be obtained by selling changelings to huntsmen. Etc. So unlike Strix and Idigam a big part of changeling society revolved around the huntsmen in Hill\u00b4s version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T10:28:16-08:00","id":1160246,"title":"","content":"I found out what's really going on. There is going to be a main kith Section, and then there are the Regalia Kith Sections built onto that. <br /> <br /> Also they front loaded the costs for the Book of Kith stretch goals, so not all of then will be $8,000.<br /> <br /> It's kind of like what they did for Demon Seed Collection. <br /> <br /> Demon Seed 1 was $10,000, Demon Seed 2 was $10,000, Demon Seed 3 was $2,500, Demon Seed 4 was $2,500, Demon Seed 5 was $2,500.<br /> <br /> So my guess will be the rest of the Kith Regalia stretch goal sections will be $2,000 to $4,000 each.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T12:41:55-08:00","id":1160283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160242#post1160242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean the way hill version made changeling society revolve around huntsmen more than the true fae. Why the Court system exist? For the bullwark that was a kind of pledge to keep the huntsmen away. There was a whole system about some kind of coins (i think) that were a get out of jail card with huntmen that could only be obtained by selling changelings to huntsmen. Etc. So unlike Strix and Idigam a big part of changeling society revolved around the huntsmen in Hill\u00b4s version.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again from what we have seen so far, it looks like huntsmen are going to be a present threat, but not an omnipresent threat. Something you have in the back of your mind, something you may deal with but most likely onely if someone &quot;dun goofed&quot; and did something to attract their attention. Otherwise the ST doesn't have to touch that plot point if they don't want to. Much like Gulmoths in Mage the Awakening. They might not show up if the ST doesn't want them to, but if a player somehow makes themselves into a paradox nuke, then one is going to show up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T13:12:30-08:00","id":1160292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160283#post1160283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again from what we have seen so far, it looks like huntsmen are going to be a present threat, but not an omnipresent threat. Something you have in the back of your mind, something you may deal with but most likely onely if someone &quot;dun goofed&quot; and did something to attract their attention. Otherwise the ST doesn't have to touch that plot point if they don't want to. Much like Gulmoths in Mage the Awakening. They might not show up if the ST doesn't want them to, but if a player somehow makes themselves into a paradox nuke, then one is going to show up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay thats what i needed to hear. One of my biggest grips of Hills Changeling is how it shove the huntsman as THE antagonist for all chronicles and tied it into the setting in a way that i cannot be removed without complications.<br /> <br /> So i guess i pledging next week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T15:10:20-08:00","id":1160323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160292#post1160292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay thats what i needed to hear. One of my biggest grips of Hills Changeling is how it shove the huntsman as THE antagonist for all chronicles and tied it into the setting in a way that i cannot be removed without complications.</div> </div> </div> </div>@_@ <br /> People's skim-readings of the Hill Changeling will always leave me so confused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T15:58:01-08:00","id":1160343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160323#post1160323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> @_@ <br /> People's skim-readings of the Hill Changeling will always leave me so confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like i said the fact that the court system was part of a pledge to keep specifically them away and the whole economy of &quot;get out of jail&quot; token put me off from Hills version<br /> <br /> Also his reliance of fatebinding tough that one was never clear to me if it was to be an actual mechanic or just obtuse flowery fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 11-18-2017, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T17:03:26-08:00","id":1160366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160343#post1160343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like i said the fact that the court system was part of a pledge to keep specifically them away and the whole economy of &quot;get out of jail&quot; token put me off from Hills version<br /> <br /> Also his reliance of fatebinding tough that one was never clear to me if it was to be an actual mechanic or just obtuse flowery fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>... the court system kept the Gentry from attacking, Huntsmen weren't prevented by this. The fact they can ignore the court system is the whole point given for why Huntsmen are ever relevant in the first place.<br /> <br /> The huntsmen were specifically something from outside that the GM could use or not use because they required a significant part of the gentry to even create and weren't actually loyal to the gentry at all. They were eldritch spirits which don't actually have any narrative tie to your changeling, so they get to ignore the narrative-based protection court's provide. They specifically are one of those things that you're game doesn't need to include and are meant to be used to go &quot;okay, you've gotten used to this world and everythings abit too stable. Lets throw this thing in to send the courts into chaos&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 11-18-2017, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T17:07:05-08:00","id":1160368,"title":"","content":"In other news, Changeling just passed Demon's 24 hour fundraising total for day 5 according to kicktraq. The amount of funds raised for the current kickstarter are about equivalent to the amount Demon had raised by day 10.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T19:09:54-08:00","id":1160385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160242#post1160242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">some kind of coins (i think)</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe bother to know what a thing actually is before proclaiming how much you dislike it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T19:24:15-08:00","id":1160389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160385#post1160385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe bother to know what a thing actually is before proclaiming how much you dislike it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it funny you think i would keep any specific names of a version of Changeling that i hate with a burning passion. I cant remember the name and if it wasnt taken for something else the name most appropiate would be token. <br /> <br /> This &quot;token&quot; that you could only get from helping a huntsmen, basically selling a changeling out. And it was a get out of jail card for the huntsmen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T19:40:08-08:00","id":1160394,"title":"","content":"... Yes, which was done by design in order to amp up the paranoia that's kiiinda one of the main pillars of Changeling's brand of horror. And was a side element that could have been excised at your table with basically <i>zero</i> impact on the rest of the game.<br /> <br /> Where exactly is the issue? Honest question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 11-18-2017, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T19:57:12-08:00","id":1160395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160389#post1160389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find it funny you think i would keep any specific names of a version of Changeling that i hate with a burning passion. I cant remember the name and if it wasnt taken for something else the name most appropiate would be token. <br /> <br /> This &amp;quot;token&amp;quot; that you could only get from helping a huntsmen, basically selling a changeling out. And it was a get out of jail card for the huntsmen.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is, what ever you \u201chate with a burning passion\u201d, it doesn\u2019t seem from the way you describe it to be David Hill\u2019s version of Changeling the Lost 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T20:01:29-08:00","id":1160396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sconce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160394#post1160394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Yes, which was done by design in order to amp up the paranoia that's kiiinda one of the main pillars of Changeling's brand of horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which to me felt (or feels, dont know if still there) heavy handed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sconce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160394#post1160394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where exactly is the issue? Honest question.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont like the Huntsmen, i read them as unnecesary same as the Strix but unlike the Strix at the time too many contracts and power interacted with them. From mantle, merits, pleges and even some contract interacted with them. Removing (at the time) included banning a bunch of elements of mechanics.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 11-18-2017, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T20:08:39-08:00","id":1160397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160395#post1160395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is, what ever you \u201chate with a burning passion\u201d, it doesn\u2019t seem from the way you describe it to be David Hill\u2019s version of Changeling the Lost 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hated seemings, Pledges, Fae touched, Huntsmen relevance and court contracts. <br /> <br /> So far Seeming changed for a version i like more. Pledges i still dont like but i can just use 1st. Fae touched i dont know but they werent terrible important. And Court contract we got court specific ones instead of a generic &quot;Emotion contract (fill with you emotion), Pick one of the list, and talespinning&quot;. Now just wanted to make sure before i put money (because i dont have a credit card i gotta call favors to do so) that the huntsmen arent as tied with the mechanics and setting as Hills version were. <br /> <br /> I would be happy if they are as Dreams were in 1st. Something that existed only for its own sake but didnt touched anything else and i can remove them completely from the setting with minimal fuss.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T20:16:45-08:00","id":1160398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160396#post1160396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which to me felt (or feels, dont know if still there) heavy handed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I dont like the Huntsmen, i read them as unnecesary same as the Strix but unlike the Strix at the time too many contracts and power interacted with them. From mantle, merits, pleges and even some contract interacted with them. Removing (at the time) included banning a bunch of mechanics.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Curious on how you mean unnecessary, both for Huntsmen and the Strix.<br /> <br /> But in the meantime, my problem with your objections stems from the fact that the elements that you take issue with are features that may have existed within Changeling's antagonists, but cheapened them for it(Particularly the True Fae), where as when those elements are excised and then compilated into the form of the Huntsmen, they not only are allowed to shine, but radiate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T20:20:31-08:00","id":1160399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160396#post1160396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont like the Huntsmen, i read them as unnecesary same as the Strix but unlike the Strix at the time too many contracts and power interacted with them. From mantle, merits, pleges and even some contract interacted with them. Removing (at the time) included banning a bunch of elements of mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so... I just skimmed through the compiled playtest documents from the Underhill drafts. Roughly half the mentions of the Huntsmen <i>also</i> mentioned the True Fae in the same breath, and where they weren't one could easily sub them or Hobgoblins in if you really wanted to (basically converting &quot;Call the Huntsmen&quot; back into &quot;Call the Wild Hunt&quot; from 1e). Aside from the Tokens of Reprieve and the Huntsmen section itself, which again, can be dropped without issue.<br /> <br /> I mean, this is really neither here nor there since this kickstarter isn't for the Underhill Changeling, but... yeah, I still don't see the problem, and I'm <i>trying</i> to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 11-18-2017, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T20:32:45-08:00","id":1160401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sconce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160399#post1160399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, this is really neither here nor there since this kickstarter isn't for the Underhill Changeling, but... yeah, I still don't see the problem, and I'm <i>trying</i> to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure Loki's problem with them is that they are an integrated part of the setting that has implications on the story whether you use them or not. You can very easily run an Underhill Lost game without a Huntsman ever showing up. But the existence of the huntsmen still informs the game, even if one never actually enters play. Personally, that's exactly what I love about them, I think it's a sign of a well-written setting. But, I suppose if what you want out of your RPGs is sterile systems with setting kept as generic as possible to avoid stepping on the GM's toes creatively, the richness and cohesion of Hill's setting might get in the way. I would question why, if that's what you want, you're fighting CofD's stoy-first approach instead of something that's actually <i>designed</i> to be generic and customizable like GURPS, FATE, BRP, D20, etc. But that seems to me to be where Loki is coming from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-18-2017, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T20:34:25-08:00","id":1160402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160401#post1160401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure Loki's problem with them is that they are an integrated part of the setting that has implications on the story whether you use them or not. You can very easily run an Underhill Lost game without a Huntsman ever showing up. But the existence of the huntsmen still informs the game, even if one never actually enters play. Personally, that's exactly what I love about them,</div> </div> </div> </div>And thats what i dislike about them in a very well explained way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160401#post1160401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, I suppose if what you want out of your RPGs is sterile systems with setting kept as generic as possible to avoid stepping on the GM's toes creatively, the richness and cohesion of Hill's setting might get in the way. I would question why, if that's what you want, you're fighting CofD's stoy-first approach instead of something that's actually <i>designed</i> to be generic and customizable like GURPS, FATE, or BRP. But that seems to me to be where Loki is coming from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats kind of a exageration. I just want 1st edition setting with better mechanics. I never had a huge problem with 1st edition setting (for changeling). Also, you assume i hate all settings which are well written etc. When i truth, i like many &quot;as written settings&quot; and i love changeling 1st but i dislike Hills changes (personal prefferences) from his take on the hedge, fae touched and his general narrative that i found it not to my liking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160398#post1160398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But in the meantime, my problem with your objections stems from the fact that the elements that you take issue with are features that may have existed within Changeling's antagonists,<u><b> but cheapened them for it(Particularly the True Fae)</b></u>, where as when those elements are excised and then compilated into the form of the Huntsmen, they not only are allowed to shine, but radiate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont really understand the sentence. The part i bolded in particular. But not here to discuss the merits or lack off of the Hill version but to ask &quot;Or are they like Strix/Idigams in that i can pretend they never existed in the setting and little to nothing would change from the setting? Beyond there arent huntsmen?&quot; Thats my main issue. I dont like them and like the Strix i gave them a fair chance and just dont work for me and how i run/like to play games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 11-18-2017, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T20:44:07-08:00","id":1160404,"title":"","content":"Currently we are $3,079 from the stretch goal. It is plausible, albeit a bit of a stretch, to hit it tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 11-19-2017, 12:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T21:13:28-08:00","id":1160414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160402#post1160402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thats kind of a exageration. I just want 1st edition setting with better mechanics. I never had a huge problem with 1st edition setting (for changeling). Also, you assume i hate all settings which are well written etc. When i truth, i like many &quot;as written settings&quot; and i love changeling 1st but i dislike Hills changes (personal prefferences) from his take on the hedge, fae touched and his general narrative that i found it not to my liking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't assume that you hate all settings which are well written. I have observed that your problems with the huntsmen seem to come down to &quot;they're different than 1st edition&quot; and &quot;they're deeply integrated within the setting (of David's 2e).&quot; For me, the integration justifies the change. For you, it seems to make the change worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T21:59:42-08:00","id":1160422,"title":"","content":"While we're discussing the Huntsmen, I personally found them a bit...I dunno. Overtly grim? I get that they're meant to inspire fear and paranoia in Changelings, and it's justified here. However, my interpretation from the text from David Hill's version was that a Huntsman was an inevitability, rather than a mere <i>possibility</i>. That, coupled with the fact the that a human dies every time a Huntsman comes through, and that by giving the token for a Huntsman over the Changeling makes the Huntsman return, it meant that any player character could have any number of deaths on her head by association, whether or not they slay every Huntsman that comes after them. That's also not helped by this text for the Token of Reprieve, which in my opinion kind of makes it too bleak: &quot;Possessing one by definition means that a changeling has sold out one of her comrades. That\u2019s an ugly thing, but even uglier is that scant few changelings would do any differently in the bargainer\u2019s position.&quot;<br /> <br /> I appreciate that Changeling is a horror game at the end of the day, fantastical as it may be, but the Huntsmen felt...I don't know. It almost made me feel guilty to be a Changeling in this game because, no matter how good a fae I end up being, someone completely innocent is going to die because I had the audacity to return to normal life. It would just be an NPC, and I wouldn't know the person who died...but that's still someone's blood on my hands. It's not a good feeling.<br /> <br /> Of course, this feeling is probably not what the writers had in mind for the game, and really in Chronicles of Darkness, expecting nobody to die from our actions is rather silly. It would be rather easy to not have any Huntsmen appear in the Chronicle. I just feel that the text went a bit too far in making them the dreaded, and I'm interested in how the current version is going to alter that, if at all. That said, I am &quot;horror-lite&quot; in a lot of ways, and if you enjoy them as they were, all the more power to you.<br /> <br /> ...sorry, that's rather rambly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 11-19-2017, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T22:16:21-08:00","id":1160425,"title":"","content":"Quick question on how the Court Give&amp;Takes work. Do the Fae and their minions instinctively know the rule of engagement for each court?<br /> <br /> Like does a hobgoblin in the employ of a Fae know that if they make a gesture or action that they won't be able to retreat?<br /> <br /> What happens if they disobey that? What if they do retreat? Can they or do their bodies force them to continue forward?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T22:22:08-08:00","id":1160426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160425#post1160425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question on how the Court Give&amp;Takes work. Do the Fae and their minions instinctively know the rule of engagement for each court?<br /> <br /> Like does a hobgoblin in the employ of a Fae know that if they make a gesture or action that they won't be able to retreat?<br /> <br /> What happens if they disobey that? What if they do retreat? Can they or do their bodies force them to continue forward?</div> </div> </div> </div>My interpretation is that hobgoblins cannot retreat from the Summer Court's blessing - just as Spring becoming Summer is an intrinsic fact, so too do the blessings of the various Courts establish rules that the Fae must obey. That is the power of the Courts, where the laws of the blessings are...well, law.<br /> <br /> As for if a hobgoblin or another Fae know that a blessing is in effect, I'm not sure, but I'm certain that hobs that have lived around a freehold long enough will catch on to the seasons and what they mean for any hobs abound, enough to be wary about particular things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T00:11:36-08:00","id":1160444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160426#post1160426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My interpretation is that hobgoblins cannot retreat from the Summer Court's blessing - just as Spring becoming Summer is an intrinsic fact, so too do the blessings of the various Courts establish rules that the Fae must obey. That is the power of the Courts, where the laws of the blessings are...well, law.</div> </div> </div> </div>The real question is WHEN Seasons Law in Freeho\u0142d really change - When Monarch of next Season is crowned High King / Queen? What if real weather is that sky Season is like previous one? Like very warm weather in Autumn or very cold Spring?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T01:00:54-08:00","id":1160448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160013#post1160013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive me if this already has been asked, but what exactly is the difference between the &quot;traditionally printed, hardcover copy of the CHANGELING: THE LOST 2nd Edition Core Rules&quot; received for pledging $50 (or more), and the &quot;CHANGELING: THE LOST 2ND EDITION CORE BOOK Print on Demand (PoD) version&quot; that you get a coupon for when pledging at that level?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's an example I took featuring the traditionally printed prestige edition Dark Eras (with embossing and metallic/iridescent layer and spot matte/glossy finish) vs. the print on demand version.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/11/2016-11-22-13.33.41b.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/11/2016-11-22-13.33.41b-300x225.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> Print-on-demand is on the right.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/11/2016-11-22-13.35.25.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/11/2016-11-22-13.35.25-300x225.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/11/2016-11-22-13.36.12.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/11/2016-11-22-13.36.12-300x225.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/11/2016-11-22-13.36.19.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/11/2016-11-22-13.36.19-300x225.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T03:33:45-08:00","id":1160466,"title":"","content":"still haven't decided if I'm going to back the Kickstarter or not. Most chances I would- even though my budget is only the 5$ for the preview- but if I do, it would be only next week. I must say that the game changing factor would probably be the reactions to the Antagonists section, especially how Fetches and Huntsmen would end up, as well as any new antagonist which we are yet to know more about (Hedge Ghosts and Eidolons)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T05:13:22-08:00","id":1160488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160422#post1160422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While we're discussing the Huntsmen, I personally found them a bit...I dunno. Overtly grim? I get that they're meant to inspire fear and paranoia in Changelings, and it's justified here. However, my interpretation from the text from David Hill's version was that a Huntsman was an inevitability, rather than a mere <i>possibility</i>. That, coupled with the fact the that a human dies every time a Huntsman comes through, and that by giving the token for a Huntsman over the Changeling makes the Huntsman return, it meant that any player character could have any number of deaths on her head by association, whether or not they slay every Huntsman that comes after them. That's also not helped by this text for the Token of Reprieve, which in my opinion kind of makes it too bleak: &quot;Possessing one by definition means that a changeling has sold out one of her comrades. That\u2019s an ugly thing, but even uglier is that scant few changelings would do any differently in the bargainer\u2019s position.&quot;<br /> <br /> I appreciate that Changeling is a horror game at the end of the day, fantastical as it may be, but the Huntsmen felt...I don't know. It almost made me feel guilty to be a Changeling in this game because, no matter how good a fae I end up being, someone completely innocent is going to die because I had the audacity to return to normal life. It would just be an NPC, and I wouldn't know the person who died...but that's still someone's blood on my hands. It's not a good feeling.<br /> <br /> Of course, this feeling is probably not what the writers had in mind for the game, and really in Chronicles of Darkness, expecting nobody to die from our actions is rather silly. It would be rather easy to not have any Huntsmen appear in the Chronicle. I just feel that the text went a bit too far in making them the dreaded, and I'm interested in how the current version is going to alter that, if at all. That said, I am &quot;horror-lite&quot; in a lot of ways, and if you enjoy them as they were, all the more power to you.<br /> <br /> ...sorry, that's rather rambly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds more like a tragedy than horror to me. Made me feel as though the world would be better off if Changelings didn't escape or should go back to their Keeper, a bit of backdoor pro-slavery thing going on. In reality, it was depressing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T06:50:42-08:00","id":1160499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160466#post1160466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">still haven't decided if I'm going to back the Kickstarter or not. Most chances I would- even though my budget is only the 5$ for the preview- but if I do, it would be only next week. I must say that the game changing factor would probably be the reactions to the Antagonists section, especially how Fetches and Huntsmen would end up, as well as any new antagonist which we are yet to know more about (Hedge Ghosts and Eidolons)</div> </div> </div> </div> There are also Mirror People now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T07:59:01-08:00","id":1160510,"title":"","content":"So for us that just recently got into Changeling the Lost and aren't very well versed in the setting etc etc. I look forward to the 2ed coming out and david hills version really sold me into changeling.<br /> But it seems to be more or less a flamewar going on about the 1st ed, &quot;Underhill ed&quot; and the new Rose and Meghan &quot;2nd ed&quot;.<br /> Im pretty aware that we can't really say that much about the kickstarted 2ed yet, but more to come. But could someone explain the differences between 1ed and Mr. Underhills version, eg. vision, of the game as it was. <br /> <br /> <br /> Also on the second thing, why are so many people 'upset' about the Kiths only being 12 in the core book when there will be rules to make your own. It seems like a minor thing that's easily customizable and a long writeup of dozens of them just seems like a waste of space that could be used for setting stuff or other more important things that's not as easy to just make yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T08:05:38-08:00","id":1160517,"title":"","content":"also not the biggest fan of the Huntsmen. they seem a little redundant to me. however, they look easily excised if they turn out to not be my taste. definitely not a deal breaker.<br /> <br /> while i was not a fan of the 100+ kiths in the previous developer's version of the game, i am a bit disappointed that the core went to the extreme in the opposite direction and only included 12 kiths. maybe this decision was made because of intentional severing of seeming and kith ... but yeah, I pledged high so I'll be getting the Book of Kiths ... so it reallly is a bit of a moot point.<br /> <br /> love give &amp; take and the fact that we still have the Seasonal Courts as the default organizational structure for the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T08:58:30-08:00","id":1160523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160510#post1160510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im pretty aware that we can't really say that much about the kickstarted 2ed yet, but more to come. But could someone explain the differences between 1ed and Mr. Underhills version, eg. vision, of the game as it was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Broadly speaking, the sorting of primary non-changeling antagonists in the Underhill version of the game was that your fetch was your main issue at low Wyrd, the Huntsman your Keeper sent after you at middling Wyrd, and your Keeper or other related Fae at high Wyrd.<br /> <br /> Huntsmen were generally not dispatched to retrieve a changeling until they had made a name for themselves, which made them a strong motivator for changelings trying to build greater sources of security to pursue higher ranks among the Courts and specialized jobs within the freehold, since the additional Approaches of a freehold's structural apparatus made them lower-priority targets when the Huntsmen came calling; the appeal of a Token of Reprieve was that, generally speaking, you were more likely to be offered one if you were on the lower rungs of the ladder or outright Courtless, since the Huntsmen could come after you to build up points of Yearning more easily without specialized Approaches and if you managed to hold onto one long enough you had some insurance.<br /> <br /> The above sorting structure also meant you were more likely to see powerful characters retreat to potent Hollows, act through proxies, and be drawn out of hermitage through the abduction or theft of characters and resources personally significant to them through history and/or pledgecraft, as well as the occasional disappearance of their Icons to elsewhere in the Hedge and the need to harvest Glamour through dreams or bounty or mortal emotion.<br /> <br /> The trajectory then went that at low Wyrd you could more readily spend time in the mortal world and deal with the complications of rebuilding your life in place of or separate from your fetch (who could meddle with you personally without regard for specific narrative/stylistic beats), then increasing involvement in Courtly politics eventually attracted enough accolades and infamy to warrant sending a Huntsman after you (at which point a Court offered more defense but not total defense), and after that you had the defense of your life and your holdings and your Clarity as imperiled by direct intercession from the True Fae (who were at their most constrained within the territory of a freehold acting directly against its entitled nobility) while managing emergent aspects of your Lost condition that the Hedge and Arcadia can best sustain.<br /> <br /> There's also the fact of how the Clarity system worked, which made the biggest difficulty high-Wyrd character had in maintaining Clarity a function of having so many things that could prompt a roll and having the consequences of failure on those rolls cascade so readily \u2014 at Wyrd 7, losing Clarity meant a full week of being more susceptible to losing Clarity and having a harder time interacting with anything that wasn't born from the Hedge, while successfully retaining your Clarity meant you got a little bit better at putting things together (regardless of where on the scale you were) but could completely lose that benefit for a scene and get saddled with a substantial penalty on all your actions from exposure to something as simple as a stroke of lightning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T09:00:30-08:00","id":1160524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160510#post1160510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So for us that just recently got into Changeling the Lost and aren't very well versed in the setting etc etc. I look forward to the 2ed coming out and david hills version really sold me into changeling.<br /> But it seems to be more or less a flamewar going on about the 1st ed, &amp;quot;Underhill ed&amp;quot; and the new Rose and Meghan &amp;quot;2nd ed&amp;quot;.<br /> Im pretty aware that we can't really say that much about the kickstarted 2ed yet, but more to come. But could someone explain the differences between 1ed and Mr. Underhills version, eg. vision, of the game as it was. <br /> <br /> <br /> Also on the second thing, why are so many people 'upset' about the Kiths only being 12 in the core book when there will be rules to make your own. It seems like a minor thing that's easily customizable and a long writeup of dozens of them just seems like a waste of space that could be used for setting stuff or other more important things that's not as easy to just make yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the kiths thing: <br /> Part of it is that we had a whole bunch of them in 1E, and the reduction in number means that a lot of players with only the 1E books will crack open the 2E core as soon as they get it and find that their favorites aren't in there. Assuming that they're doing this prior to getting ahold of Book of Kiths, they'd need to homebrew them personally using the kith creation rules. While this might not be difficult for some players, others might have trouble with it or have a Storyteller that only allows published kiths in their games. This could prove especially shocking to people who hadn't been following the previews closely and were still expecting the 100 kiths promised in the Underhill previews. The fact that the new kith descriptions are so long means that some people are wishing that there had been more kiths in the same space. I don't think anyone has proposed that any of the other important information shouldn't have been included, but rather that they would have preferred 24 kiths at half the length each over 12 full length ones. I actually like the new details given, even if I would have thoroughly enjoyed having a few more. As someone who enjoys writing kiths, I've been having fun trying to convert my own (as well as some of my favorite canon kiths) into the new format, so I'm not as bothered by it as some. Granted, some are trickier than others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T09:12:45-08:00","id":1160527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160510#post1160510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So for us that just recently got into Changeling the Lost and aren't very well versed in the setting etc etc. I look forward to the 2ed coming out and david hills version really sold me into changeling.<br /> But it seems to be more or less a flamewar going on about the 1st ed, &quot;Underhill ed&quot; and the new Rose and Meghan &quot;2nd ed&quot;.<br /> Im pretty aware that we can't really say that much about the kickstarted 2ed yet, but more to come. But could someone explain the differences between 1ed and Mr. Underhills version, eg. vision, of the game as it was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note, his surname is just Hill. The \u201cUnderhill\u201d moniker refers to the fact that it was developed \u201cUnder Hill\u201d, and it sounds very fairy tale.<br /> <br /> So, one difference between 1st Edition and Underhill is the role of Kiths and Seemings. In 1e, Seemings were fairytale archetypes, and Kiths were specific expressions of those archetypes. In Underhill, Kith was how your Keeper changed you, and Seeming was how you changed yourself. Specifically, each Seeming, though it still resembled a fairytale archetype, was largely defined by its means of reclaiming agency, and were heavily inspired by common psychological responses to trauma.<br /> <br /> Another big change was Courts. In 1e, the four Seasonal Courts were pretty much the assumed default, and their role in Changeling society was pretty analogous to Covenants in Requiem. In Underhill, the custom Court creation rules were the assumed default, and a few examples were given of Courts created using those rules, including the Seasonal Courts. Courts roles changed to primarily be about maintaining a Bullwark - a ritual that keeps the Gentry and their minions away by forcing them to abide by a narrative the Courts controlled in order to invade the Freehold.<br /> <br /> Another big change was the addition of the Huntsmen, which didn\u2019t exist at all in 1e but took over one of the many roles previously played by the Gentry. Instead of there being an ever-present threat that your Keeper might come for you to bring you back, the fear is that your Keeper might send a Huntsman after you to do the same on their behalf. In so doing, they allowed the Gentry to remain the distant threat, while making the immediate threat even more immediate. They also serve as something of a dark mirror to Changelings.<br /> <br /> The big thing that sold me on Underhill, and was closely tied into the Seeming rules, was Clarity, which shifted from being about sanity in 1e to being about perception in Underhill, and brought the post-traumatic stress metaphor much more to the forefront.<br /> <br /> There were some other, more mechanical changes as well, like how Contracts worked, how Pledges worked, etc. but I think I covered most of the bigger narrative differences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-19-2017, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T10:38:15-08:00","id":1160557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160510#post1160510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also on the second thing, why are so many people 'upset' about the Kiths only being 12 in the core book when there will be rules to make your own. It seems like a minor thing that's easily customizable and a long writeup of dozens of them just <b>seems like a waste of space that could be <i>used for setting stuff or other more important things</i></b> that's not as easy to just make yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I consider &quot;setting stuff&quot; as wasted space. I've never used a 2e premade setting,PC or ST. Personally, I'd rather drop the entire bit on premade settings for space dedicated to Kiths, which are, generally, far more universally applicable to a game than the setting kernels would be in my opinion. I don't need help in designing settings; even if they're fun to read they're not productive page-count usage <i>for me personally</i>.<br /> <br /> YMMV, of course.","signature":""