g system one I've been dying to read.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, NOW it's up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T10:48:06-08:00","id":1161207,"title":"","content":"Omg, someone give a rundown! I'm on the fence to let a friend buy me in, or do it myself to get the preview sooner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T10:55:59-08:00","id":1161211,"title":"","content":"Looking good! Character Creation, Powers, Merits, Contracts, The Hedge and more!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T10:57:41-08:00","id":1161212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161207#post1161207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Omg, someone give a rundown! I'm on the fence to let a friend buy me in, or do it myself to get the preview sooner.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, scanning through the ToC:<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 3</b><br /> Character Creation (self explanatory)<br /> Anchors (the Changeling version of Virtue/Vice, &quot;Needle&quot; and &quot;Thread&quot;, also Touchstones)<br /> Changeling-exclusive traits (Wyrd, Glamour, Clarity, Mask, Mien, Portaling, Cold Iron, and Bedlam)<br /> Merits<br /> Contracts<br /> Crowns (primarily showcases Seasonal Crowns)<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 4</b><br /> CofD ruleset (rolling dice, action types, Willpower, you know the drill)<br /> Hedge rules<br /> Pledges<br /> Oneiromancy<br /> Tokens","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 11-21-2017, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T10:58:15-08:00","id":1161213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161203#post1161203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, NOW it's up.</div> </div> </div> </div>omgomgomg thank you!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13733-betterworldz","name":"BetterWorldz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T11:52:18-08:00","id":1161229,"title":"","content":"Just wanna say, I love the Gristlegrinder's blessing. If there was a way to make it so their stomach didn't eat the target, and made them akin to a mobile prison, I'd sqwee with mischievous intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T11:57:26-08:00","id":1161234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Second Preview</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...<br /> A character's seeming forms from what happened to her in Arcadia, how she escaped it, or how she approaches the world now. This cannot change once play starts, <b>but a kith may modify the<br /> character's seeming or make it more specific</b>. Look over the six seemings: the Beast, the Darkling, the Elemental, the Fairest, the Ogre, and the Wizened, starting on p. XX.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> <b>A kith is a refinement of seeming.</b> If your character served a specific purpose in Arcadia, she was molded to that task. <i>Kith is the resulting transformation, which spans all seemings.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>So the <b>bolded </b>portions really seem to indicate that Kiths are just expressions of the Seeming. I know that any kith can be matched to any seeming (as per the <i>italicized</i> part), but I thought that Seeming and Kith were supposed to be, more or less, divorced?<br /> <br /> I thought that it was said on the forums that Seeming was, contrary to 1st edition, not always what your keeper (or Faerie itself) made you into yet Kith very much is. A Kith can't be a specific expression of a Seeming unless Seemings were also broad spectrums of Kiths. The previews have not been very explicit about this despite them being pretty explicit on the previews and forums.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Q: did Seemings change?<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Step Five: Add Lost Template<br /> Choose seeming, <b>kith (if any)</b>, court (if any), Needle, Thread, Touchstone(s), Wyrd, frailties (if any), a second favored Regalia, and Contracts. Describe fae mien. </div> </div> </div>The possibility of not having a Kith, wouldn't this mean that Seeming is necessarily what you were changed into?<br /> <br /> Edit 2:<br /> and now this breakdown makes me think I was right all along as they don't specifically mention Beasts as animals or Elementals as made out of elements:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beast: Savage survivalists, passionate and deadly. <br /> Darkling: Lurkers hiding in the shadows, silent but ever watchful. <br /> Elemental: Unbridled and unchained, the true forces of nature. <br /> Fairest: Stately and elegant, forever loved and craving true connection. <br /> Ogre: Warriors and brutes, blunt and to the point. <br /> Wizened: Crafters and builders, weary but not jaded. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":654,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","user":"xiongrey","date":". 11-21-2017, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T12:01:22-08:00","id":1161236,"title":"","content":"After a quick first peek at a bit of the manuscript #2, I can say I am a little puzzled about this Clarity system, but at the same time I'm excited about it, for its uniqueness and looking forward to try and see how it works in-game!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11079-bardobobs","name":"bardobobs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T12:03:14-08:00","id":1161237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161234#post1161234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So the <b>bolded </b>portions really seem to indicate that Kiths are just expressions of the Seeming. I know that any kith can be matched to any seeming (as per the <i>italicized</i> part), but I thought that Seeming and Kith were supposed to be, more or less, divorced? <br /> <br /> I thought that it was said on the forums that Seeming was, contrary to 1st edition, not always what your keeper (or Faerie itself) made you into yet Kith very much is. A Kith can't be a specific expression of a Seeming unless Seemings were also broad spectrums of Kiths. The previews have not been very explicit about this despite them being pretty explicit on the previews and forums.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Q: did Seemings change?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's really sounding like Kith is less a sub-x and more of the primary z splat. Most changelings, kinda like I found out the hard way in 1e, really seem to manifest their specific faeness via contracts (and, hopefully, merits like the Begotten and other 2e races.) It seems to me that the new default might be Seeming and Court, with Kith being more like 2e Bloodlines than 1e kiths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T12:09:45-08:00","id":1161238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161237#post1161237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's really sounding like Kith is less a sub-x and more of the primary z splat. Most changelings, kinda like I found out the hard way in 1e, really seem to manifest their specific faeness via contracts (and, hopefully, merits like the Begotten and other 2e races.) It seems to me that the new default might be Seeming and Court, with Kith being more like 2e Bloodlines than 1e kiths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking of them more like bloodlines makes sense. I hope it's that way or at least that's how I'll run them.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> but wait, what does that make Entitlements? Z.5 splat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T12:19:06-08:00","id":1161242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161238#post1161238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking of them more like bloodlines makes sense. I hope it's that way or at least that's how I'll run them.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> but wait, what does that make Entitlements? Z.5 splat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Add onto it the almost literal tropeness of Changeling and the Wyrd. It makes sense that brings who left a world of pure fantasy and confusion (I've been reading never-ending story until I get the previee) might not know exactly what they are capable of when they get back to the real world. Some powers seemed like fantasy, others seem like they are impossible. Even traits and powers you have on your sheet from the start might only &quot;suddenly manifest at a dramatic moment&quot;, meaning you can start with a Kith right away, start with a Kith and have it manifest to the other players later, or start without a Kith while you wait for either a one you like to show up in Kith and Kin, or for you and your storyteller to brew one up. So long as seeming and contracts and merits work like the other 2e games.... a beautiful flaming swordsman might just start as a Summer Fairest with combat merits and fire elemental contracts...and later, as if suddenly revealing your power, you manifest the dual Kith merit you bought by manifesting two appropriate Kith powers that you've had all along but supressed/forgot/kept hidden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T12:22:16-08:00","id":1161244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161238#post1161238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking of them more like bloodlines makes sense. I hope it's that way or at least that's how I'll run them.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> but wait, what does that make Entitlements? Z.5 splat?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm going to suggest that we call it the Z' splat (aka Z-prime if you aren't a fan of calculus). Its not like we need to be bound to exactly three splats anyhow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T12:29:32-08:00","id":1161246,"title":"","content":"Just finished the manuscript. And i like it.<br /> I like especially what was done with the pledge system and i really like sealing. I was thinking of how to introduce in play the trope of fairies not being allowed to say something untrue and i think sealings will help. Changeling would be used to the idea that everything they say could become binding and so would carefully word their statements so that they always have some wiggle room.<br /> <br /> I kinda wished they added special environmental tilts in the hedge section. But its not really a problem, i'll just continue using the Lair traits featured in Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T12:31:04-08:00","id":1161247,"title":"","content":"Reaping as a way of obtaining Glamour was sorely needed and I love it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T12:42:02-08:00","id":1161253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161244#post1161244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm going to suggest that we call it the Z' splat (aka Z-prime if you aren't a fan of calculus). Its not like we need to be bound to exactly three splats anyhow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Some games have more than one X (Beast, and Deviant, iirc), so it wouldn't be odd to have two Z splats instead of one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T12:54:52-08:00","id":1161254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far, we've added 2 sections to the Changeling: The Lost Second Edition Companion supplement, and 2 sections to our book of kiths (officially titled KITH AND KIN)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that answers my question ^.^ I shall call it Kith and Kin then ^.^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T13:11:51-08:00","id":1161257,"title":"","content":"Who else loved the <b><i>Summon The Loyal Servant Contract?</i></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T13:39:03-08:00","id":1161263,"title":"","content":"&quot;Needle is like the changeling's Myers-Briggs personality type,&quot; .... seriously -.-","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T13:41:31-08:00","id":1161264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161263#post1161263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Needle is like the changeling's Myers-Briggs personality type,&quot; .... seriously -.-</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that stood out for me too. I work with at team of educational psychologists. M-B tests mean jack. <br /> <br /> Mantle has changed significantly. Very much looking forward to the new guidelines for designing them. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T13:52:55-08:00","id":1161267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161263#post1161263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Needle is like the changeling's Myers-Briggs personality type,&quot; .... seriously -.-</div> </div> </div> </div>Hum yeah i noticed that too. I got to say i'm not impressed with the Needle. There is nothing there i can see that is original for changeling. The Thread thing is alright tho.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T13:59:31-08:00","id":1161268,"title":"","content":"I think my biggest issue with this current iteration is the Court Contracts. Which isn't to say that the contracts themselves are in some way non-functional or problematic, just that their presence has an adverse impact on the larger picture. I still have some emotional investment in Changeling 2nd Edition opening up Courts to allow particular freeholds and regions to be as weird as they need to be. The fact of the matter is even if the Court building system is 100% perfect, backed up by a 100% perfect system for designing new contracts, the fact there are 40 (39? Looks like autumn is missing one) distinct mechanical powers for the Seasonal Courts gives them so much &quot;weight&quot; as to render any other Courts &quot;that weird thing you can do if you really want to.&quot;<br /> <br /> The amount of effort to just physically write-up one Court capable of matching any of the Seasonal's breadth and depth of unique magics is simply too much of a buy-in for any Changeling game to have any greater expectation of a proper new faction than any other gameline. (Arguably still easier to implement new Tribes and Orders since they basically boil down to an affinity list for things that already exist and a unique merit.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T14:25:52-08:00","id":1161279,"title":"","content":"... can someone tell me what the difference is between &quot;The changeling unleashes his court's chosen emotion.&quot; and &quot;The emotion is from the court most closely associated with the character's own (Spring/Summer, Autumn/Winter).&quot; in the bedlam rules (which also are annoyingly tied to only work if you use Seasonal Courts)?<br /> <br /> <b>edit</b>: Okay. So if you make you're own court system you'll end up needing to make up a write up, mantle, a giant number of contracts, a bedlam emotion condition, merits. Anything else?<br /> <br /> <b>edit2</b>: Damn it, looks like Fae Mount's example masks still make no sense. I was hoping they'd fix that from the Hill version.<br /> <br /> <b>edit3:</b> I feel like I'm missing something obvious, why is the cost of Hostile Takeover &quot;Cost: 2 Glamour, or 2 Glamour + 1 Willpower (see below)&quot; rather than &quot;2 Glamour&quot; when there doesn't seem to be anything below which actually asks for willpower?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 11-21-2017, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T14:48:19-08:00","id":1161288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161279#post1161279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>edit3:</b> I feel like I'm missing something obvious, why is the cost of Hostile Takeover &quot;Cost: 2 Glamour, or 2 Glamour + 1 Willpower (see below)&quot; rather than &quot;2 Glamour&quot; when there doesn't seem to be anything below which actually asks for willpower?</div> </div> </div> </div>...make a note of that when it becomes time for errata phase?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T14:48:48-08:00","id":1161289,"title":"","content":"This is still about the first preview, but something occured to me at work today - Artists use Crafts in both their Kith Blessing and in &quot;Tools Of The Trade&quot;. Yet, it references both painters and composers - isn't making music, writing or painting an Expression roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T14:49:36-08:00","id":1161290,"title":"","content":"Between kiths and these courts, coming up with custom material will be quite a workload.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T15:16:31-08:00","id":1161304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>E11even-E11even</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161290#post1161290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Between kiths and these courts, coming up with custom material will be quite a workload.</div> </div> </div> </div>When isn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T15:27:30-08:00","id":1161306,"title":"","content":"Kith is the W-splat.<br /> <br /> You know, the splat that makes you go, &quot;Wait, what?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T15:31:47-08:00","id":1161307,"title":"","content":"Summary of my impressions:<ul><li>Needle and Thread are really fun in concept but, like Virtue and Vice, not <i>terribly</i> useful in play, nor terribly critical to how a character is portrayed or played. Touchstones, as they always do, suffer from the &quot;Good thought process behind it, but bad implementation&quot; issue as well. Maybe the better solution would've been to just scrap Touchstones and turn the Needle and Thread into Clarity armour, or ways to restore it, or both?</li> <li>The Wyrd's longevity change just feels weird. In practice, it's not meaningful (Changelings aren't likely to die of old age), but the idea that the more powerful Changelings can be truly ancient just by being what they are is fun.</li> <li>For pity's sake, <i>get rid</i> of anything that only kicks in at Wyrd 6+. There is bugger-all point in having a feature that only exists for a vanishingly rare percentage of games; most are not going to make it to Wyrd 6+, so anything that only affects that is largely going to be wasted word count. Either integrate them as features lower down (like Changelings starving unless their Glamour is above their Wyrd at every level) or don't use them at all.</li> <li>(While I'm at it, why have Changelings starve from Glamour hunger when they are far more likely to die of other things in any scenario when they have 0 Glamour and can't readily recharge, long before they'd die or even suffer the effects of starvation?)</li> <li>Clarity as something that can get damaged and healed is fun; it plays with a lot of what Changelings are. However, tying that healing to Touchstones is a <i>terrible idea</i>, for the same reason Touchstones themselves are. Having scenes happen &quot;on camera&quot; for 3-5 players means 3-5 scenes after an adventure in which 2-4 players are likely just sitting around. Party-splitting being a dicey proposition at the best of times, this basically encourages it. This is even worse in chat-based games, where longer posts can render scenes glacial in pace. And if it's happening &quot;off-camera&quot;, well... What's the bloody point of Touchstones at all? There are better ways to encourage PCs to connect to those around them and, importantly, involve them in the story.</li> <li>On the subject of Clarity... Putting something so difficult to heal the damage of as the primary way to be harmed in dreams is a fast way for players to be <i>scared</i> of dreams, when they should ideally want to revel in it.</li> <li>The Court Mantle merits are awesome.</li> <li>Cloak of Night is a Contract that every Stealth mechanic ever should take notice of. Might tweak it by allowing a +1 Glamour surcharge to affect additional characters?</li> <li><b>Hedgespinning.</b> I am very happy with this. It might get mechanically heavy in play, but the hefty Beat reward for Changelings getting inconvenienced and the rewards for finding things make it heavily worthwhile. The Hedge's active, slightly hungry nature is also nicely presented in this aspect, and in its participation in Chases.</li> <li>I'm kinda meh on the Pledge systems. They seem a bit lackluster, except for Sealing.</li> </ul><br /> Overall, despite the majority of my comments being negative, the Hedge being so much more interesting is all I ever really wanted out of 2e. Much as I criticize, the problems I have are things I can fix on my own for my own games. The ideas in the Hedge section were what I was after, so I'm gonna say I'm happy with my pledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T15:33:28-08:00","id":1161308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161268#post1161268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think my biggest issue with this current iteration is the Court Contracts. Which isn't to say that the contracts themselves are in some way non-functional or problematic, just that their presence has an adverse impact on the larger picture. I still have some emotional investment in Changeling 2nd Edition opening up Courts to allow particular freeholds and regions to be as weird as they need to be. The fact of the matter is even if the Court building system is 100% perfect, backed up by a 100% perfect system for designing new contracts, the fact there are 40 (39? Looks like autumn is missing one) distinct mechanical powers for the Seasonal Courts gives them so much &quot;weight&quot; as to render any other Courts &quot;that weird thing you can do if you really want to.&quot;<br /> <br /> The amount of effort to just physically write-up one Court capable of matching any of the Seasonal's breadth and depth of unique magics is simply too much of a buy-in for any Changeling game to have any greater expectation of a proper new faction than any other gameline. (Arguably still easier to implement new Tribes and Orders since they basically boil down to an affinity list for things that already exist and a unique merit.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Then don't try. <br /> <br /> I'm serious. Trying to create 40 new Contracts each and every time for a homebrew Court system is <i>fucking insane</i>. You want a functioning system, you only need, like, ten, total. How many are your players going to buy to begin with? <br /> <br /> That, and the complaint &quot;There's too much awesome in the core Courts!&quot; strikes me as...a bit pedantic. If it's really that hard, reskin other Contracts and dress them up in good thematics.<br /> <br /> Also, for me: Dude, what happened to Goblin Vows? I liked those. On the other hand, Clarity is actually way better than I had braced for (it's something to keep in mind, but severe mental damage is an annoyance, not a character-breaker, and hitting zero is either a plot hook or a brief knockout). I'll have to see the Comatose Condition before I make a final judgement, but otherwise it's looking good (I say Comatose because nobody likes having to sit out part of the game because their character is out of it-thankfully the Persistent, at least, involves a Dreaming scene where the character and repairing her mind is the focus).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T15:40:00-08:00","id":1161309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161308#post1161308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude, what happened to Goblin Vows? I liked those.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded. I was very surprised to not see them in there. Not that it'd take much to houserule them back in, but still.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T15:43:52-08:00","id":1161310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161308#post1161308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> Then don't try. <br /> <br /> I'm serious. Trying to create 40 new Contracts each and every time for a homebrew Court system is <i>fucking insane</i>. You want a functioning system, you only need, like, ten, total. How many are your players going to buy to begin with? <br /> <br /> That, and the complaint &quot;There's too much awesome in the core Courts!&quot; strikes me as...a bit pedantic. If it's really that hard, reskin other Contracts and dress them up in good thematics.<br /> <br /> Also, for me: Dude, what happened to Goblin Vows? I liked those. On the other hand, Clarity is actually way better than I had braced for (it's something to keep in mind, but severe mental damage is an annoyance, not a character-breaker, and hitting zero is either a plot hook or a brief knockout). I'll have to see the Comatose Condition before I make a final judgement, but otherwise it's looking good (I say Comatose because nobody likes having to sit out part of the game because their character is out of it-thankfully the Persistent, at least, involves a Dreaming scene where the character and repairing her mind is the focus).</div> </div> </div> </div>This doesn't address the actual concern at all. The issue is that the main courts have so much weight of content that custom courts won't be as desirable just because they can't match up with the mechanical options they give the player. Dressing up current abilities thematically as something else is still extra work, which is the core issue with making custom courts to begin with, and isn't a real solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12885,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","user":"E11even-E11even","date":". 11-21-2017, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T16:01:42-08:00","id":1161312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>E11even-E11even</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161310#post1161310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dressing up current abilities thematically as something else is still extra work, which is the core issue with making custom courts to begin with, and isn't a real solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean...custom setting stuff is difficult and intensive to begin with.<br /> <br /> The Courts themselves involve: the basic emotion they represent, what their role is in the local freehold and the region, how said roles interact with the other Courts, the history behind the Court on how and why it formed, and write-ups on the major NPCs for each Court. Even in other TRPGs, not just CofD stuff, custom setting stuff is a lot of work. And you'd be doing roughly the same things as Court creation.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what you were expecting on it NOT being a huge workload.<br /> <br /> (by the by: aren't rules to create your own Contracts also apart of the CtL2e core rulebook?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T16:03:15-08:00","id":1161313,"title":"","content":"The whole &quot;High Wyrd only&quot; bits of the game have never sat well with me, no matter the edition.<br /> <br /> Lords of Summer mentioning the Summer throwing Frailties at people to make tests harder? How many new recruits are going to have that high a Wyrd? In ten years or so of playing Lost, I've never seen Bedlam used <i>once</i>.<br /> <br /> The high Wyrd stuff, yeah, it's a relic that needs left behind in 1e. Especially since so many Stormwinder types seem so terrified of letting Wyrd get up high enough to truly experience all the game's splendors.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11533-bluegrass-beast","name":"Bluegrass Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T16:04:36-08:00","id":1161314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161308#post1161308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then don't try.<br /> <br /> I'm serious. Trying to create 40 new Contracts each and every time for a homebrew Court system is <i>fucking insane</i>. You want a functioning system, you only need, like, ten, total. How many are your players going to buy to begin with?<br /> <br /> That, and the complaint &quot;There's too much awesome in the core Courts!&quot; strikes me as...a bit pedantic. If it's really that hard, reskin other Contracts and dress them up in good thematics.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well yes. The point I'm getting at is that I'd prefer a version of Changeling wherein I can build my own Freehold without little to no worries about how it stands up to the &quot;default&quot; group. The fact that I'm not going to write-up 40 contracts (or probably even 10) is the problem. Unless myself or another storyteller is really committed to a certain concept, a Seasonal Freehold is going to be overwhelmingly easier to integrate into the story and to impact the players in a robust and meaningful way. And if someone is willing write-up a bunch of powers, that doesn't need to be section in the corebook, thats just Rule Zero. &quot;There are unique courts all over the world&quot; ceases to be a feature of the game, if the effort required to implement it is equal to or greater than its counterparts that don't discuss an open y-axis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T16:21:43-08:00","id":1161322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161314#post1161314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well yes. The point I'm getting at is that I'd prefer a version of Changeling wherein I can build my own Freehold without little to no worries about how it stands up to the &quot;default&quot; group. The fact that I'm not going to write-up 40 contracts (or probably even 10) is the problem. Unless myself or another storyteller is really committed to a certain concept, a Seasonal Freehold is going to be overwhelmingly easier to integrate into the story and to impact the players in a robust and meaningful way. And if someone is willing write-up a bunch of powers, that doesn't need to be section in the corebook, thats just Rule Zero. &quot;There are unique courts all over the world&quot; ceases to be a feature of the game, if the effort required to implement it is equal to or greater than its counterparts that don't discuss an open y-axis.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And?<br /> <br /> You are failing to convince me. The game is not marketed towards instant-mix local Freeholds. &quot;If the Storyteller is committed&quot; is a pretty damn big <i>if</i> to invoke if you're explaining the difficulty of homebrew. I would think that the Storyteller being committed is the whole point; a system just gives the effort a goal, it can't be summoned from nothing.<br /> <br /> And I say it very much is appreciated in the corebook, thank you. Having actual baselines is, y'know, better than by the seat-of-your-chair guestimation. See the Omega Point system from Unknown Armies-that is literally a spell-design system, because creative magic with limitations is the whole point of Unknown Armies. Does that make it bad that there are already schools present in the core? Fuck no, it means you don't have to devote the first session to creating what magic you're using to begin with if nobody wants to fuck around with Omega Points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T16:44:39-08:00","id":1161331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161322#post1161322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are failing to convince me</div> </div> </div> </div> So.... why does <b>schizoPOP</b> need to convince you of anything? That poster is well within their rights to be disappointed over the difficulty of making even a bare bones court system, let alone one that compares to the seasonals, without needing to convince anyone of anything.<br /> <br /> I do agree with the points made by schizoPOP. The sheer amount of even bare bones mechanics is going to make the barrier for any custom court very high to the point of being unlikely to show up in play. The ability to make a new court system is like saying that I could become president. Technically, theoretically possible. Realistically? Likely not going to happen.<br /> <br /> And I've had a number of people end up wanting to drop out of a changeling game because they don't want to use the Seasonals. So, its a very real concern to a lot of us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 11-21-2017, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T16:45:20-08:00","id":1161332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161314#post1161314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well yes. The point I'm getting at is that I'd prefer a version of Changeling wherein I can build my own Freehold without little to no worries about how it stands up to the &quot;default&quot; group. The fact that I'm not going to write-up 40 contracts (or probably even 10) is the problem. Unless myself or another storyteller is really committed to a certain concept, a Seasonal Freehold is going to be overwhelmingly easier to integrate into the story and to impact the players in a robust and meaningful way. And if someone is willing write-up a bunch of powers, that doesn't need to be section in the corebook, thats just Rule Zero. &quot;There are unique courts all over the world&quot; ceases to be a feature of the game, if the effort required to implement it is equal to or greater than its counterparts that don't discuss an open y-axis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please bare in mind, you're talking about a setting that not only has existed for 10+ years, but one that has, in both its incarnations, taken months of work to get right. Naturally they're going to have it polished up pretty well - that's why they use it as an example. Doing away with that will only leave everyone in the dark as to what a polished freehold could look like. As everyone else has noted, making your own stuff for a tabletop RPG to any satisfaction requires time, work and passion that has to at least match a fraction of what the original writers of the game had. Complaining at how it's work to do <i>work</i> isn't criticism, particularly when we don't even have the systems to do your primary critique, making contracts.<br /> <br /> If you're really that bent out of shape about this aspect, then take a page out of Demon's book and find people in your player group who are interested in fleshing out the courts with you. Draw from their creativity, get their input in how they would see things working, see if they see anything unbalanced in the custom stuff and make something interesting happen. If something comes up and it isn't covered by the system as written, then make a consensus among everyone on how it should or even could work, or make that into a plot point. Heck, I'd be surprised if there weren't people chomping on the bit to make their own freeholds without even playing a game of Changeling; ask them if you can use their freehold.<br /> <br /> A final note, if the system is made super easy, then it's just going to be a mad-libs style system that won't be engaging because it's just a jumble. Even in games like Demon, where making your own custom powers is given a thorough walk-through, it is work to complete. If you don't find that kind of work satisfying, then what are you doing trying to make your own?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T16:50:27-08:00","id":1161336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161312#post1161312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean...custom setting stuff is difficult and intensive to begin with.<br /> <br /> The Courts themselves involve: the basic emotion they represent, what their role is in the local freehold and the region, how said roles interact with the other Courts, the history behind the Court on how and why it formed, and write-ups on the major NPCs for each Court. Even in other TRPGs, not just CofD stuff, custom setting stuff is a lot of work. And you'd be doing roughly the same things as Court creation.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what you were expecting on it NOT being a huge workload.<br /> <br /> (by the by: aren't rules to create your own Contracts also apart of the CtL2e core rulebook?)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I know that creating a custom setting is intensive; I've done it before. But this isn't an entire setting. It's a court.<br /> <br /> Developing NPCs and histories is different from cooking up mechanical abilities. You shouldn't have to build your own branches of play mechanically to come up with a court, that's ridiculous. And at least 10 per court 'rotation' to match the season? Come on, people have lives. The biggest barrier between people playing tabletop RPGs regularly is already time, and this just exacerbates it.<br /> <br /> Also, throwing in rules to make your own content in the core book doesn't fix the problem. Core books need rules and content, not recipes to cook up more content ourselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T17:17:27-08:00","id":1161344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>E11even-E11even</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161336#post1161336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I know that creating a custom setting is intensive; I've done it before. But this isn't an entire setting. It's a court.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might as well be.<br /> <br /> Courts in CtL, at least from my readings, are a HUGE part of the setting. Besides the usual of providing a faction for players to join and to promote faction-politicking gameplay, they also provide the means for changelings to fight back against the True Fae. Either defensively of providing a support group to fall back on, or offensively as having the strength of numbers to deal with any Huntsman or True Fae coming their way.<br /> <br /> The only way they wouldn't is if everyone went Courtless...but even then, it'd be strange if the PCs never interacted with changelings that are in a Court at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Developing NPCs and histories is different from cooking up mechanical abilities. You shouldn't have to build your own branches of play mechanically to come up with a court, that's ridiculous. And at least 10 per court 'rotation' to match the season? Come on, people have lives. The biggest barrier between people playing tabletop RPGs regularly is already time, and this just exacerbates it.<br /> <br /> Also, throwing in rules to make your own content in the core book doesn't fix the problem. Core books need rules and content, not recipes to cook up more content ourselves. </div> </div> </div>...and you've lost me. Are you saying that there shouldn't be &quot;Build-a-[insert mechanic here]&quot; to begin with?<br /> <br /> (and therefore no custom courts for anyone)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T17:22:59-08:00","id":1161345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161344#post1161344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...and you've lost me. Are you saying that there shouldn't be &quot;Build-a-[insert mechanic here]&quot; to begin with?<br /> <br /> (and therefore no custom courts for anyone)</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but in a core book content is more important. More kiths would serve the core book better than rules to make your own, which would be fine in the Book of Kiths. Same with courts and other mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T17:51:57-08:00","id":1161355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161322#post1161322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And?<br /> <br /> You are failing to convince me. The game is not marketed towards instant-mix local Freeholds. &quot;If the Storyteller is committed&quot; is a pretty damn big <i>if</i> to invoke if you're explaining the difficulty of homebrew. I would think that the Storyteller being committed is the whole point; a system just gives the effort a goal, it can't be summoned from nothing.<br /> <br /> And I say it very much is appreciated in the corebook, thank you. Having actual baselines is, y'know, better than by the seat-of-your-chair guestimation. See the Omega Point system from Unknown Armies-that is literally a spell-design system, because creative magic with limitations is the whole point of Unknown Armies. Does that make it bad that there are already schools present in the core? Fuck no, it means you don't have to devote the first session to creating what magic you're using to begin with if nobody wants to fuck around with Omega Points.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't actually need an intricate build-your-own system in order for custom courts to work, or at least be significantly more approachable.<br /> <br /> Alright some examples here:<br /> <br /> Say I want to make a new mage order, I literally need to pick three skills that are appropriate. That is the only thing that mage orders give you that doesn't key off of some other part of the system. If I want a new order to stand as tall as its canon counterparts I need to add one merit. Eyeballing the merits that do exist, the most complicated order merit clocks in 220 words, plus another 40 for the dot that swaps between ministries. So basically 300 words should cover absolutely everything you need to implement a new order mechanically. If you don't want to write-up a merit, it has the rules for Nameless Orders, which is the paint-by-number mystery cult initiation with added option of rote specialties. It won't necessarily be as potent or unique a proper Order merit, but it should still give you something functional and distinct from its counterparts.<br /> <br /> This incidentally, is what I'm hoping the Mantle creation guidelines will be like. Enough fill-in-the-blank mechanics that someone who doesn't want to worry about the math can still can create a Mantle that adds to a character in a way the canon courts don't.<br /> <br /> If I go to werewolf, all I need is a favored renown, three favored gifts, and an extra blurb in the Siskur-Dah condition. The canon tribes are structured to have a unique proprietary gift, but there isn't actually a &quot;common-uncommon&quot; dynamic so having a tribe with &quot;Death,Rage, Technology&quot; as an affinity list doesn't break anything. And since they draw from a commonly available pool every new Shadow Gift that gets published makes designing a new tribe to be &quot;distinct&quot; easier. So about 100 words should cover a fully functional custom tribe, though obviously if you do want it to have unique gift that makes things complicated.<br /> <br /> If court contracts were structured more like &quot;unlock this third regalia&quot; this structure could apply, though it wouldn't necessarily be the best for the game at large.<br /> <br /> Now I can't say for certain that the underhill version was actually better in this regard because we never actually got to see what those court contracts looked like, but the structure presented was one generic contract, one contract with a &quot;fill-in-the-blank&quot; component, and one &quot;other&quot; contract. In essence, you only needed to write-up one custom power, which should put you word-count-wise in the same range as the above examples. If you do want to reskin, you only need to be able to find one example contract that fits rather than figure out which combination of seasonal contracts best fit your vision.<br /> <br /> Now word count is certainly not the end-all-be-all of how easy it is to implement something. Strictly speaking the easiest creation method is probably the nameless order, which'd likely be longer than a new tribe. However, all the mechanics of a whole new mage pentacle could fit in just the contract list of one seasonal court.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T18:01:14-08:00","id":1161358,"title":"","content":"$887 to go until the next stretch goal. It would be pretty awesome if we managed to hit it tonight, although that would be a stretch. Probably another novella goal for the next one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T18:02:57-08:00","id":1161359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161312#post1161312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean...custom setting stuff is difficult and intensive to begin with.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what you were expecting on it NOT being a huge workload.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats why i preffer the supplement threadmills games. Why make effort in designing a power when i can just buy a published one. But yeah this concerns because i bought into the Kickstarter because i got fired up with the idea of running a Directional courts game. But if its gonna be a mechanical nightmare like designing gifts for the Pure i might retreat my pledge (still catching up with the previews, so there still hope)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 11-21-2017, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T18:14:21-08:00","id":1161363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161332#post1161332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please bare in mind, you're talking about a setting that not only has existed for 10+ years, but one that has, in both its incarnations, taken months of work to get right. Naturally they're going to have it polished up pretty well - that's why they use it as an example. Doing away with that will only leave everyone in the dark as to what a polished freehold could look like. As everyone else has noted, making your own stuff for a tabletop RPG to any satisfaction requires time, work and passion that has to at least match a fraction of what the original writers of the game had. Complaining at how it's work to do <i>work</i> isn't criticism, particularly when we don't even have the systems to do your primary critique, making contracts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will note that to everyone ganging up on <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"526\" data-vbnamecard=\"526\">schizoPOP</a> that your (not Schizo\u00b4s) point might have a better leg to stand in if it werent because Hill version did promise a &quot;make court of the umbrella if you feel like&quot; with a system that allowed for that.<br /> <br /> Personally i wasnt fond of it but if i did and bought into the earlier days of the previews, put money on the kickstarter to check it out and found that &quot;court of the umbrella&quot; wasnt possible anymore then I would be fair criticism to point that out and decide whether to continue to supporting or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161332#post1161332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Draw from their creativity, get their input in how they would see things working, see if they see anything unbalanced in the custom stuff and make something interesting happen. If something comes up and it isn't covered by the system as written, then make a consensus among everyone on how it should or even could work, or make that into a plot point. Heck, I'd be surprised if there weren't people chomping on the bit to make their own freeholds without even playing a game of Changeling; ask them if you can use their freehold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man i really hope one day to meet this fabled tables OPP sells me, my half my tables are the most unimaginative people possible but will exploit any broken mechanic in their favor and the other half dont read a book even if put a gun on their heads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 11-21-2017, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T18:19:39-08:00","id":1161368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161331#post1161331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So.... why does <b>schizoPOP</b> need to convince you of anything? That poster is well within their rights to be disappointed over the difficulty of making even a bare bones court system, let alone one that compares to the seasonals, without needing to convince anyone of anything.<br /> <br /> I do agree with the points made by schizoPOP. The sheer amount of even bare bones mechanics is going to make the barrier for any custom court very high to the point of being unlikely to show up in play. The ability to make a new court system is like saying that I could become president. Technically, theoretically possible. Realistically? Likely not going to happen.<br /> <br /> And I've had a number of people end up wanting to drop out of a changeling game because they don't want to use the Seasonals. So, its a very real concern to a lot of us.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm saying I have not had that problem. Besides people liking the Seasonals, I find it weird that schizoPOP is effectively complaining that using the skeleton of the Court design is too much work when there's an assumed default...when the Seasonals were the assumed default in the Underhill version too, just not at the front of the book. <br /> <br /> In fact, I fail to see how the Underhill version was much better, given how design of a new Court system was apparently levied on the ST every game, instead of every game where defaults (including the sample settings) every chronicle. That seems like an incredible burden to put on people by default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T18:19:50-08:00","id":1161369,"title":"","content":"As someone who wanted to run an Australian game, I guess I'll have to do a lot of work when the old system only took five minutes to make..... yay....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T18:23:10-08:00","id":1161370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161355#post1161355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In essence, you only needed to write-up one custom power, which should put you word-count-wise in the same range as the above examples. If you do want to reskin, you only need to be able to find one example contract that fits rather than figure out which combination of seasonal contracts best fit your vision.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was easier than that, Hills court had 3 contracts. Emotional contract (insert emotion), Favored contract from the list and Fatespinning. So the only thing you had to do was, pick an emotion, pick a contract from the list and you were good to go.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T18:47:33-08:00","id":1161376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161363#post1161363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will note that to everyone ganging up on <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"526\" data-vbnamecard=\"526\">schizoPOP</a> that your (not Schizo\u00b4s) point might have a better leg to stand in if it werent because Hill version did promise a &quot;make court of the umbrella if you feel like&quot; with a system that allowed for that.<br /> <br /> Personally i wasnt fond of it but if i did and bought into the earlier days of the previews, put money on the kickstarter to check it out and found that &quot;court of the umbrella&quot; wasnt possible anymore then I would be fair criticism to point that out and decide whether to continue to supporting or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason everyone is responding to their post as so is because they're commenting on the difficulty of making an entire freehold when, as far as I can tell, the systems for doing so have yet to be unveiled. It is a preemptive complaint about how court making is difficult just because custom works will be compared to a twice-polished freehold that people can use by default, which comes off poorly to people who actively make original content for the games <i>without</i> systems and rules to do so. As someone who indulges in making custom stuff myself, it feels nonsensical to make such a judgement without the rules out in the first place.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how your example of David Hill's comment on 'making a court of the Umbrella' is entirely relevant to the situation. As noted, the rules/systems for creating a Freehold, Courts and Contracts have not been released yet, and from what I have seen there is nothing in the rules about how you can't make a 'Court of the Umbrella'. Heck, in writing this post I've even made up a Freehold of Umbrellas based on various uses of the umbrella (Sun/Parasols, Shine/Reflectors, Hail/Bartitsu, Rain/Normal Umbrellas). Granted, this post has gone through a couple iterations (I don't like fire-and-forget posts), but I spent less than half an hour and used Wikipedia and I'm fairly satisfied with the concepts. The minutia has yet to be ironed out, but as noted, I've spent less than half an hour on it so far.<br /> <br /> ...I get the feeling this topic is starting to get petty. It may be an idea to change topics for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T18:54:06-08:00","id":1161378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161376#post1161376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I get the feeling this topic is starting to get petty. It may be an idea to change topics for now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wholeheartedly agree. <br /> <br /> Anyhow, we've got $773 to go to the next goal. Hitting it today would be cool, but will more likely occur overnight. Still, Changeling is trucking at a pretty good pace. Not having any sub-$2000 days a week in is pretty impressive. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T19:00:09-08:00","id":1161380,"title":"","content":"Does anyone know if Brownie's Boon stacks with Good Time Management? If so, that can make things get pretty ridiculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T19:11:16-08:00","id":1161384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161358#post1161358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">$887 to go until the next stretch goal. It would be pretty awesome if we managed to hit it tonight, although that would be a stretch. Probably another novella goal for the next one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks like it:<br /> <br /> Next stretch goal has been added. At $107k, there will be a novella themed around Winter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161376#post1161376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I get the feeling this topic is starting to get petty. It may be an idea to change topics for now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Was about to comment myself and how odd it seems for everyone making very self-assured judgement calls on game systems we haven't actually seen yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T19:17:19-08:00","id":1161385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161384#post1161384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Looks like it:<br /> <br /> Next stretch goal has been added. At $107k, there will be a novella themed around Winter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it will take that long to hit it. We have $582 to go to the art budget increase now. This kickstarter is just pounding along. I haven't done the math yet, but I know we are easily past the amount Demon had raise by its midway point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T19:53:45-08:00","id":1161397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1160426#post1160426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My interpretation is that hobgoblins cannot retreat from the Summer Court's blessing - just as Spring becoming Summer is an intrinsic fact, so too do the blessings of the various Courts establish rules that the Fae must obey. That is the power of the Courts, where the laws of the blessings are...well, law.<br /> <br /> As for if a hobgoblin or another Fae know that a blessing is in effect, I'm not sure, but I'm certain that hobs that have lived around a freehold long enough will catch on to the seasons and what they mean for any hobs abound, enough to be wary about particular things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, you've got it. The Wyrd enforces the Court Bargains such that the Gentry and their servants simply can't break them. They don't instinctively know <i>why</i> they can't skewer this impertinent changeling on a whim in Spring, and they can get all the way to the point where they have the sword in-hand and are about to make the fatal thrust, but they still can't do it. But a lot of the Fae, especially Titles that do the Keeper thing a lot and have a lot of goblin servants or spend a lot of time poking around in human dreams, have come up against the Bargains before or heard the stories secondhand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T21:42:36-08:00","id":1161419,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2229_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2229\" data-vbnamecard=\"2229\">Meghan Fitzgerald</a> Thanks for confirming that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, another question here for everyone to ponder; I've noticed a number of Contracts (Mastermind's Gambit, Elemental Weapon, Primal Glory) note an Elemental's affinity with an element for their Seeming bonus. What does that mean for a non-Elemental, however? Is it just the closest approximation the Changeling has to an &quot;elemental affinity&quot;, such as a Beast Artist having an affinity for Ink/Water, or a Fairest Diver with Darkness? What if their kith/Seeming doesn't really lend itself to an obvious element?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T22:02:00-08:00","id":1161421,"title":"","content":"Court Goodwill is very interesting both mechanically and for world building. Now I really want to see a Dark Eras update so I can try it out with the Directional Courts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.c