ing-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161437#post1161437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the Hell? Why am I only just now finding out the Kickstarter released? It used to be way more advertised everytime we have a kickstarter. Its been out for what 8 days already?</div> </div> </div> </div>...uh...you been away from computers and/or similar devices the past few days?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T00:12:41-08:00","id":1161440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161439#post1161439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...uh...you been away from computers and/or similar devices the past few days?</div> </div> </div> </div>A lil, been busy with work and only catch up a lil bit when I come home, but I didn't think I was this disconnected. I remember a few weeks ago (a month?) someone was talking about the Changeling Kickstarter would be after Chevaliers but I thought people were saying it would be next month.<br /> <br /> My bad I usually look for stickies for Kickstarters but I don't see a Kickstarter for Changeling Sticky. Glad I didn't miss this though. But seriously the link to the kickstarter should have been in the first post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T00:37:31-08:00","id":1161444,"title":"","content":"So...anyone notice the armor up contract missing from the shield contracts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T02:39:44-08:00","id":1161455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161358#post1161358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">$887 to go until the next stretch goal. It would be pretty awesome if we managed to hit it tonight, although that would be a stretch. Probably another novella goal for the next one?</div> </div> </div> </div> I believe so, probably Winter Novella.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T02:52:50-08:00","id":1161456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161307#post1161307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For pity's sake, <i>get rid</i> of anything that only kicks in at Wyrd 6+. There is bugger-all point in having a feature that only exists for a vanishingly rare percentage of games; most are not going to make it to Wyrd 6+, so anything that only affects that is largely going to be wasted word count. Either integrate them as features lower down (like Changelings starving unless their Glamour is above their Wyrd at every level) or don't use them at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to have to disagree with this.<br /> <br /> Besides the use for NPCs, 2e makes jumping to these levels much more appealing than 1e did (at least in terms of the math). In all the 2e games I've been involved in, people raised their type's power stat much faster than in 1e. While nobody's bought it yet, there's two games that have gotten well past the 30 XP mark (so someone could have) and all the PCs are in the 3-4 range already in under a year. I'd wholly expect that if either game continues for two years (which is pretty average for us), we'll have PCs with 6+. In my longest 1e CofD game, which went for over three years, nobody bothered going over 3 in their power stat (mixed game).<br /> <br /> So, however anecdotal, I can't imagine 2e is making such play anything but more common than it was in the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T03:06:49-08:00","id":1161458,"title":"","content":"My thoughts.<br /> <br /> Changelings got hit with both some nerfs and buffs.<br /> <br /> Nerf, no Goblin vows or 1e pledge system means no granting yourself or others merits in exchange for keeping a pledge (Oaths might still be able to grant a single dot in a merit, like an Oath joining a Court grants a free dot in Mantle). I think a dot in a merit with the Motley tag would fit perfectly as a bonus for Motley Oaths.<br /> <br /> Sort of nerf is there is no longer an Embracing the Wyrd feature.<br /> <br /> Buffs are way more contracts. Instead of 5 dots of contracts, its 4 Common or Goblin contracts (each equviliant to \u2022\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022 contracts) and 2 Royal Contracts (which are equivlamt to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 contracts) so its like getting 22 dots of contracts. I guess this makes up for the no Goblin vows or Embracing the Wyrd nerf).<br /> <br /> I'll give you an example you could make a starting Character with Glimpse of a Distant Mirror (basically use a mirror to scry via another mirror), Portents and Visions (find out stuff about someone's pasted or future), Summon Loyal Servant (creates a quasi hedge ghost out of an element), Boon of the Shuttling Spider (walk on roofs, walls, and slippery surfaces), Discreet Summons (Royal, summon an object of up to size 5 or Hobgoblin with a Wyrd of up to 3), Red Revenge (+3 to Iniatitive, Intimidation, all physical stats (boosting devived stats) and 3/3, so instant tank). Tell me that isn't a nice boost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T03:25:49-08:00","id":1161462,"title":"","content":"Do Parkour and other Chase modifier merits apply to Hedge? I don't see anything for or against it, so my knee jerk reaction isn't to forbid it, but it feels... odd to allow it?<br /> <br /> Am I just missing anything like the old Vainglory Contracts, or are they not there? I see Mask of Superiority, but anything like Song of Distant Arcadia or the rest? Controlling elements? Elemental weapon is not the same as controlling the environment - did I overlook it?<br /> <br /> EDIT - Ah, found the Control Elements one. Elemental Fury.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 11-22-2017, 06:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T03:46:22-08:00","id":1161464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161462#post1161462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Parkour and other Chase modifier merits apply to Hedge? I don't see anything for or against it, so my knee jerk reaction isn't to forbid it, but it feels... odd to allow it?<br /> <br /> Am I just missing anything like the old Vainglory Contracts, or are they not there? I see Mask of Superiority, but anything like Song of Distant Arcadia or the rest? Controlling elements? Elemental weapon is not the same as controlling the environment - did I overlook it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect some of the Vainglory aspects may have been turned off since Changelings acquired Scouring the Mask. <br /> Not sure about Control Elements, I kinda hope Goblin Vows will be added back (or are just further back in the chapters) since I could see those filling in the niche of that Contract.<br /> <br /> ...So opinion on new Weaving rules? <br /> I am under positive impression but they feel bit too complex to get my head around them at the moment without some kind of gameplay example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T04:06:47-08:00","id":1161469,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">In my opinion, the worst thing in this edition is clarity, changeling should be a game about fantastic stories and be the protagonist of your own history, but binding the touchstone to the way to heal clarity track is really annoying. A changeling without a touchstone can't heal all the clarity damage he suffered. It looks like a support character is more important than the main character, and it is not fun.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Maybe using your thread or the needle to heal clarity track too would be a good way</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7761-glauber","name":"Glauber","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7761_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T05:41:31-08:00","id":1161481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161464#post1161464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suspect some of the Vainglory aspects may have been turned off since Changelings acquired Scouring the Mask.<br /> Not sure about Control Elements, I kinda hope Goblin Vows will be added back (or are just further back in the chapters) since I could see those filling in the niche of that Contract.<br /> <br /> ...So opinion on new Weaving rules?<br /> I am under positive impression but they feel bit too complex to get my head around them at the moment without some kind of gameplay example.</div> </div> </div> </div> Found the Control Elements one, now called Elemental Fury. I did just overlook that one. And sadness about the loss of Vainglory.<br /> <br /> By Weaving, do you mean dream weaving and hedgespinning? Its... different. I'm going to have to play with it a lot more to see how it feels. On the one hand, everyone can do it about equally, depending if their personal specialties come up. On the other, it means that you really can't be a specialist either. Heck. Wyrd level doesn't even figure into the rolls. <br /> <br /> Or did you mean Hedgespun Items? Pretty nice rules, pretty straight forwards. <br /> <br /> PS The Goblin Bounty merit talks about having access to &quot;common fruits&quot; - what's a common fruit in this version? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T05:46:24-08:00","id":1161482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Glauber</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161469#post1161469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">In my opinion, the worst thing in this edition is clarity, changeling should be a game about fantastic stories and be the protagonist of your own history, but binding the touchstone to the way to heal clarity track is really annoying. A changeling without a touchstone can't heal all the clarity damage he suffered. It looks like a support character is more important than the main character, and it is not fun.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Maybe using your thread or the needle to heal clarity track too would be a good way</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> I'll point out that your touchstone doesn't have to be a person, it can be an idea, a place, maybe even an object. <br /> <br /> So one touchstone could be your fetch, another could be your Teddybear from when you were a child (or young at heart adult), another could be the home you were raise, another the temple/church you go to, another could be environmentalism, and another could be a belief in protecting free speech, and another your dog or cat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T05:52:04-08:00","id":1161484,"title":"","content":"I think that the changeling should have a better way to heal normal damage as well, the changeling is not a human anymore and shouldn't be considered as one for healing purpose. In the beast book they put the changeling in the same category of vampires, werewolf and creatures that was never human, or was human but has since been totally transformed into or merged with a supernatural being. <br /> <br /> So because of that a think they should have a better way to heal than just eat goblin fruit, maybe spend glamour to do so, like mages can spend mana to heal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7761-glauber","name":"Glauber","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7761_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T06:18:36-08:00","id":1161490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Glauber</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161484#post1161484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the changeling should have a better way to heal normal damage as well, the changeling is not a human anymore and shouldn't be considered as one for healing purpose. In the beast book they put the changeling in the same category of vampires, werewolf and creatures that was never human, or was human but has since been totally transformed into or merged with a supernatural being.<br /> <br /> So because of that a think they should have a better way to heal than just eat goblin fruit, maybe spend glamour to do so, like mages can spend mana to heal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or use a healing contract...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T06:19:24-08:00","id":1161491,"title":"","content":"A Changeling with Wyrd 10, Composure 10, and Wits 10 will have a Clarity track of 20, before any icons get taken into account, which means twenty touch stones. <br /> <br /> It's also means 30 dream health.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T06:26:48-08:00","id":1161494,"title":"","content":"Huh. Someone claimed that the game needed to get rid of anything from Wyrd 6+. I presume they were thinking about Bedlam. I don't see anything that suggests that bedlam is restricted to Wyrd 6+? There's nothing in the bedlam section and nothing in the Wyrd section that says it. The only thing in the Wyrd section that's restricted to 6+ is that's the level changelings take major frailties. And even then, you're still taking minor ones earlier. <br /> <br /> So, am I missing anything that's really restricted to 6+ Wyrd?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T06:43:57-08:00","id":1161498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161482#post1161482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll point out that your touchstone doesn't have to be a person, it can be an idea, a place, maybe even an object.<br /> <br /> So one touchstone could be your fetch, another could be your Teddybear from when you were a child (or young at heart adult), another could be the home you were raise, another the temple/church you go to, another could be environmentalism, and another could be a belief in protecting free speech, and another your dog or cat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It can help but doesn't solve the problem, the problem is that the touchstone should be a element to help narrative and add drama for the PC, but this clarity healing system gives too mutch importance to this element and in some cases it will be more important than the PC itself. And for a PC to have more than one touchstone the character need to have a touchstone merit so he needs to spend xp to do so.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7761-glauber","name":"Glauber","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7761_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T06:55:02-08:00","id":1161503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Glauber</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161498#post1161498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It can help but doesn't solve the problem, the problem is that the touchstone should be a element to help narrative and add drama for the PC, but this clarity healing system gives too mutch importance to this element and in some cases it will be more important than the PC itself. And for a PC to have more than one touchstone the character need to have a touchstone merit so he needs to spend xp to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is the montage more important that every scene before and after it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T07:00:11-08:00","id":1161505,"title":"","content":"Oh crap your right I misread that, the Changeling only starts with one touch stone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T07:06:17-08:00","id":1161507,"title":"","content":"Just hit the 103k point!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T07:21:26-08:00","id":1161510,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2229_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2229\" data-vbnamecard=\"2229\">Meghan Fitzgerald</a> Thank you for the answer!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T07:36:20-08:00","id":1161514,"title":"","content":"So, Quick question (related to someone else's a few pages back):<br /> The Elemental Blessing uses a specific elemental medium to do stuffs at range. What if the Elemental isn't an Elemental because the changeling was made into that elemente during the Durance?<br /> <br /> My assumption would be that each elemental is associated even with the (quasi-personality) traits of a specific element then it's that element that the Elemental has affinity in.<br /> (for example, a Changeling is remade into a Satyr to continually groom her keepers wild lawn. However the changeling could not give up on leaving and very slowly but very surely wittled down the defenses, inch by inch, of her keepers demesne till she escaped back (as in: she gained her Seeming of Elemental w/ a Water association through her means of escape (elemental due to the sheer force of will and water because it's expressed in a way similar to water eroding anything and everything in its path)).<br /> <br /> My other assumption is that, regardless of how a Changeling obtains their Seeming, the Seeming changes the Mein in related ways. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> tl;dr:<br /> 2 Assumptions:<br /> - The element associated with an Elemental who wasn't made an Elemental is the element most closely associated to the expression of what the Changeling is an Elemental in the first place.<br /> - The Seeming changes the Mein regardless of how the changeling obtained that Seeming. <br /> <br /> Are these assumptions correct?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T07:46:48-08:00","id":1161516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Glauber</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161484#post1161484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the changeling should have a better way to heal normal damage as well, the changeling is not a human anymore and shouldn't be considered as one for healing purpose. In the beast book they put the changeling in the same category of vampires, werewolf and creatures that was never human, or was human but has since been totally transformed into or merged with a supernatural being.<br /> <br /> So because of that a think they should have a better way to heal than just eat goblin fruit, maybe spend glamour to do so, like mages can spend mana to heal.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're def entitled to that opinion so I'm not saying its a wrong opinion.<br /> <br /> But all the same, I prolly wouldn't want to run it that way even if it were to change to be that. I like how each Gameline heals reinforces certain themes and ways of playing. I like that werewolf wounds just start closing up soon after opening. I like that vampires run their blood to heal up a body that shouldn't be alive anymore. I like that the Bound can let their Geist's plasm cover up and 'heal' wounds. and I like that Mages can either use a spell to heal themselves or hurt themselves to use a spell. It all plays nicely to the themes and play styles.<br /> <br /> Because of that, I like how changelings would look and feel like these creatures that, if hurt, they bleed and flee into a cabin in the woods to have some weird fruits (or if you're all modern: A Goblin-Grass Smoothie <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).<br /> <br /> But anyway, not saying you're wrong (its easy enough to home-brew in), but just wanted to say why I like it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> sorry for the Quadruplet posts ^.^; I was going back through the posts that I didn't see since I left the office yesterday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":654,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","user":"xiongrey","date":". 11-22-2017, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T08:14:12-08:00","id":1161522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161514#post1161514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Quick question (related to someone else's a few pages back):<br /> The Elemental Blessing uses a specific elemental medium to do stuffs at range. What if the Elemental isn't an Elemental because the changeling was made into that elemente during the Durance?<br /> <br /> My assumption would be that each elemental is associated even with the (quasi-personality) traits of a specific element then it's that element that the Elemental has affinity in.<br /> (for example, a Changeling is remade into a Satyr to continually groom her keepers wild lawn. However the changeling could not give up on leaving and very slowly but very surely wittled down the defenses, inch by inch, of her keepers demesne till she escaped back (as in: she gained her Seeming of Elemental w/ a Water association through her means of escape (elemental due to the sheer force of will and water because it's expressed in a way similar to water eroding anything and everything in its path)).<br /> <br /> My other assumption is that, regardless of how a Changeling obtains their Seeming, the Seeming changes the Mein in related ways.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> tl;dr:<br /> 2 Assumptions:<br /> - The element associated with an Elemental who wasn't made an Elemental is the element most closely associated to the expression of what the Changeling is an Elemental in the first place.<br /> - The Seeming changes the Mein regardless of how the changeling obtained that Seeming.<br /> <br /> Are these assumptions correct?</div> </div> </div> </div> Your Satyr example is kind of not going to work, simply because a Seeming is once again chosen by the Gentry, not by the changeling. Its based on the role that the Others gave you in their games. In Hill's version, sure, that'd work. Not so much in the official version.<br /> <br /> Fundamentally, a Seeming is going to be what you were turned into, what affinities the Others instilled in you. So, while its theoretically possible to be an Elemental made up of non-primal elements, its going to be how your Keeper chooses to shape you. The mein isn't going to be changed by the seeming, simply because the seeming has pretty much been part of your mein since the beginning of your Durance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 11-22-2017, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T08:35:35-08:00","id":1161526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161522#post1161522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Your Satyr example is kind of not going to work, simply because a Seeming is once again chosen by the Gentry, not by the changeling. Its based on the role that the Others gave you in their games. In Hill's version, sure, that'd work. Not so much in the official version.<br /> <br /> Fundamentally, a Seeming is going to be what you were turned into, what affinities the Others instilled in you. So, while its theoretically possible to be an Elemental made up of non-primal elements, its going to be how your Keeper chooses to shape you. The mein isn't going to be changed by the seeming, simply because the seeming has pretty much been part of your mein since the beginning of your Durance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not so from the book or Rose's and Meghan's previews. Here's the bit in the book:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CtL2e 2nd Preview</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Step Five: Add Lost Template<br /> We have the basic aspects. Now to add the Glamour.<br /> Seeming<br /> A character's seeming <b>forms from what happened to her in Arcadia, how she escaped it, <u>or</u> how<br /> she approaches the world now.</b> This cannot change once play starts, but a kith may modify the <br /> character's seeming or make it more specific.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Bolded</b> the important bit. <br /> <br /> The important part of a Seeming that binds all in a Seeming together regardless of how a Lost obtains the Seeming is the underlining Archetype nicely listed here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beast: Savage survivalists, passionate and deadly. <br /> Darkling: Lurkers hiding in the shadows, silent but ever watchful. <br /> Elemental: Unbridled and unchained, the true forces of nature. <br /> Fairest: Stately and elegant, forever loved and craving true connection. <br /> Ogre: Warriors and brutes, blunt and to the point. <br /> Wizened: Crafters and builders, weary but not jaded. </div> </div> </div>My confusion is that, while the Elemental doesn't need to be literal, it's blessing does mention an associated element.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T08:36:54-08:00","id":1161527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161522#post1161522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Your Satyr example is kind of not going to work, simply because a Seeming is once again chosen by the Gentry, not by the changeling. Its based on the role that the Others gave you in their games. In Hill's version, sure, that'd work. Not so much in the official version.<br /> <br /> Fundamentally, a Seeming is going to be what you were turned into, what affinities the Others instilled in you. So, while its theoretically possible to be an Elemental made up of non-primal elements, its going to be how your Keeper chooses to shape you. The mein isn't going to be changed by the seeming, simply because the seeming has pretty much been part of your mein since the beginning of your Durance.</div> </div> </div> </div>This doesn't seem accurate. By the text, Seeming is about the *entire* story of your Durance, not just what was done to you by your Keeper (which is what kith is).<br /> <br /> For example, a Durance can easily go like this:<br /> <br /> 1) Taken, turned into satyr gardener by Keeper<br /> 2) Try to find a way out, foiled at every turn by complex rules and barriers<br /> 3) Finally, talk to your watering can, who admires your determination and turns you into water to escape through the soil<br /> <br /> With all three steps of this story in play, your Seeming could be Elemental-- perhaps a translucent satyr made of water.<br /> <br /> Take out step 3, and you could end up a Wizened, a skilled satyr who had to be shrewd to whittle and trim their way out. That's a different story.<br /> <br /> Take out step 2 on top of that, and you might be a Beast, learning to embrace your goat-like nature to bite and tear your way free. That's an entirely different story still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13580-hsienfan","name":"Hsienfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T09:01:54-08:00","id":1161530,"title":"","content":"Reaping is safer now, instead of a automatic clarity loss, its just a breaking point and you can heal the clarity damage with Touchstones and Resolving the conditions.<br /> <br /> In fact if a Changeling with Wyrd 1 Reaps a stranger its only a Breaking Point dice pool of 3 instead of five, or a pool of 2 if the Changeling has no feelings on the event and the clarity damage is likely to be 1 mild at most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 11-22-2017, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T09:35:38-08:00","id":1161534,"title":"","content":"Another quick question, but this time on Court Crowns.<br /> <br /> So each Crown is displayed differently and as different objects but only one explicitely says that it is located on the head. See below:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [Spring]<br /> The Crown wreathes around the queen's head, cascading down her shoulders to a resplendent robe of young blooms.<br /> <br /> [Summer]<br /> Mahogany branches and emerald leaves braid together in the Crown, wrapping down into a magnificent breastplate.<br /> <br /> [Autumn]<br /> Red and yellow leaves crown the queen, fanning out behind her like great wings.<br /> <br /> [Winter]<br /> Frozen ashes make the Crown, flowing down into a shimmering mantle of gray and silver. </div> </div> </div><br /> - Spring's Crown specifically mentions that it rests on the head before bustling into a robe.<br /> - Summer's Crown says that it rests where a normal breastplate would, but it words it as &quot;wrapping down into...&quot; which makes it ambiguous if the crown is also on the head or not.<br /> - Autumn's Crown says that it is on the back, but the wording before it is &quot;leaves crown the queen&quot;. The wording of 'crown' as a lowercase verb would indicate it resting on the head as well but again: ambiguous.<br /> - Winter's Crown says that it is a mantle (a cloak/cape mantle) and so would indicate it rests on the shoulders but again the wording of &quot;flowing down into a...&quot; is ambiguous.<br /> <br /> Spring's is not ambiguous at all, Winter's is less ambiguous than the others (as the cape can be the one 'flowing down') but it is still not clear.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T10:22:44-08:00","id":1161549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161462#post1161462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I just missing anything like the old Vainglory Contracts, or are they not there?</div> </div> </div> </div>Words of Memories Never Lived is functionally replaced by the Goblin Contracts Blessing of Forgetfulness and Lost Visage. Songs of Distant Arcadia was subsumed into the Fairest boon for Blessing of Perfection in Underhill and is still there now as a benefit you apply to someone else. Splendor of the Envoy's Protection is kind of present in The Royal Court.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T10:47:17-08:00","id":1161554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161526#post1161526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not so from the book or Rose's and Meghan's previews. Here's the bit in the book:</div> </div> </div> </div> And yet, this is from chapter 1 preview.<br /> <br /> &quot;The abductees are changed into faerie creatures to play particular roles in the True Fae\u2019s fantasies; these roles are Seemings&quot;<br /> &quot;seeming: A changeling\u2019s physical aspect, which reflects the role he played in Faerie and the talents he used to escape.&quot;<br /> &quot;We played our roles and spoke our lines, and our costumes became our seemings and kiths, our second skins&quot;<br /> &quot;Sometimes, a True Fae needs their servant to be more than just a Fairest or Darkling. Sometimes, a changeling looks into a golden box she shouldn't have, or eats a fruit from a strange tree after three days of fleeing her master's hounds. Sometimes, the soul, for whatever strange and occult reason, just fits into a particular shape. This specialization of roles is called a kith.&quot;<br /> <br /> This seems to imply that your Seeming, while it does have a hand in the escape, is still primarily determined by the role assigned to you by the Keeper. Perhaps Seeming solidified as you fled bound between two or three different Seemings, but there's still going to be a tie to your original role in there somehow. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hsienfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161527#post1161527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This doesn't seem accurate. By the text, Seeming is about the *entire* story of your Durance, not just what was done to you by your Keeper (which is what kith is).</div> </div> </div> </div> Umm... you are thinking Underhill version when it comes to Kith. Kiths are considered refinements of Seemings - the two are interrelated.<br /> <br /> &quot;kith: A subcategory of seeming, representing more specific abilities and needs.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161549#post1161549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Words of Memories Never Lived is functionally replaced by the Goblin Contracts Blessing of Forgetfulness and Lost Visage. Songs of Distant Arcadia was subsumed into the Fairest boon for Blessing of Perfection in Underhill and is still there now as a benefit you apply to someone else. Splendor of the Envoy's Protection is kind of present in The Royal Court.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 11-22-2017, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T11:41:32-08:00","id":1161572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161554#post1161554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Umm... you are thinking Underhill version when it comes to Kith. Kiths are considered refinements of Seemings - the two are interrelated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having never read &quot;Underhill&quot; at any length, I'm afraid I can't speak for it.<br /> <br /> It seems clear enough to me that Kiths are refinements of Seemings, AND they reflect the role your Keeper wanted for you. Those aren't mutually exclusive, because your Seeming in 2e encompasses many different events at once, and Kith is just one of them.<br /> <br /> I won't harp on about it after this, but in short: When your Seeming is intended to be a reflection of the entire fairy tale that you survived (including but not limited to how your Keeper initially shaped you), I see a lot of room in a character's backstory to be any Seeming they want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13580-hsienfan","name":"Hsienfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T11:51:47-08:00","id":1161574,"title":"","content":"In order for a Changeling to reap glamour, does the target have to be experiencing emotion similar to when a Changeling can harvest it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12885,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","user":"E11even-E11even","date":". 11-22-2017, 02:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T12:06:50-08:00","id":1161578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161534#post1161534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another quick question, but this time on Court Crowns.<br /> <br /> So each Crown is displayed differently and as different objects but only one explicitely says that it is located on the head. See below:<br /> <br /> - Spring's Crown specifically mentions that it rests on the head before bustling into a robe.<br /> - Summer's Crown says that it rests where a normal breastplate would, but it words it as &quot;wrapping down into...&quot; which makes it ambiguous if the crown is also on the head or not.<br /> - Autumn's Crown says that it is on the back, but the wording before it is &quot;leaves crown the queen&quot;. The wording of 'crown' as a lowercase verb would indicate it resting on the head as well but again: ambiguous.<br /> - Winter's Crown says that it is a mantle (a cloak/cape mantle) and so would indicate it rests on the shoulders but again the wording of &quot;flowing down into a...&quot; is ambiguous.<br /> <br /> Spring's is not ambiguous at all, Winter's is less ambiguous than the others (as the cape can be the one 'flowing down') but it is still not clear.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case, it's less &quot;crown&quot; and more &quot;royal regalia&quot; - that is, an adornment that the King/Queen wears to show their status and power. Rather than just being something that sits on their head, this is something akin to a full on mantle effect (which is appropriate). It covers their body, it is completely associated with their Court, and it leaves no room for interpretation as to who that person is. Since &quot;regalia&quot; has been taken by contracts, it makes sense that they used &quot;crown&quot; instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161549#post1161549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Words of Memories Never Lived is functionally replaced by the Goblin Contracts Blessing of Forgetfulness and Lost Visage. Songs of Distant Arcadia was subsumed into the Fairest boon for Blessing of Perfection in Underhill and is still there now as a benefit you apply to someone else. Splendor of the Envoy's Protection is kind of present in The Royal Court.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks Satchel. Honestly, the thing that disappoints me most about losing Vainglory is that I don't have a way for my Kamen Rider Changelings to Henshin now - that's what I loved in particular about Vainglory. You could use it to show off your Changeling form without outright giving others ensorcellment, which was helped by normal people seeing it as an elaborate costume. Still, I do have a few custom courts coming along, including one that's based around partying...I could swing a custom contract out of that effect.<br /> <br /> That said, I've not looked too deeply into casting off one's mask as of yet, just that Dull Beacon is still around so it is still a thing.<br /> <br /> Also, has anyone noticed that &quot;Autumn's Fury&quot; allows for the storm you summon to use lightning as an attack, with a die pool based on the activation successes...and yet the contract has no roll for it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 11-22-2017, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T12:39:49-08:00","id":1161587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161554#post1161554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And yet, this is from chapter 1 preview. <br /> <br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>There seems to be some discrepancies and contradictions in the book previews now :/ I'm confused as to which one is the case since in Chapter 1 (or preview 1, I don't remember the specific chapter), the seemings are explicitely stated to be how the Keeper changed a Changeling. And many places seem to indicate that Kith and Seeming are intricately tied. <br /> <br /> However, the second Preview in the CC section explicitly says that a Seeming can be What the Keeper/Arcadia made you, How you escaped, <b>or </b>How you cope now that you're in the real world. Emphasis on the <b>Or</b> particle. And a few places, especially on the forums, the devs have said that the Kiths are mostly divorced from Seemings in that any seeming can have any kith. <br /> <br /> <br /> So these contradictions have me tottally confused now. Could one of the Devs, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2229_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2229\" data-vbnamecard=\"2229\">Meghan Fitzgerald</a> or <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2\" data-vbnamecard=\"2\">Rose Bailey</a> clarify?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T13:03:32-08:00","id":1161591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>E11even-E11even</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161574#post1161574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In order for a Changeling to reap glamour, does the target have to be experiencing emotion similar to when a Changeling can harvest it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think, since Reaping replenishes your full Glamour pool and leaves the victim in a deppressive/non-emotional state, that Reaping likely doesn't require the victim to actively be feeling or portraring any emotion as you're essentially ripping emotions from the source.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161578#post1161578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In this case, it's less &quot;crown&quot; and more &quot;royal regalia&quot; - that is, an adornment that the King/Queen wears to show their status and power. Rather than just being something that sits on their head, this is something akin to a full on mantle effect (which is appropriate). It covers their body, it is completely associated with their Court, and it leaves no room for interpretation as to who that person is. Since &quot;regalia&quot; has been taken by contracts, it makes sense that they used &quot;crown&quot; instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, that makes sense, Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":654,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","user":"xiongrey","date":". 11-22-2017, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T14:05:19-08:00","id":1161607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161578#post1161578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kamen Rider Changelings</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish to know the story behind this as a casual fan of power rangers and sentai.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12235-emmens","name":"emmens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12235_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T14:36:21-08:00","id":1161613,"title":"","content":"Backed it, have been reading the previewed chapters in bits and pieces, and I'm really liking it. The introduction is lovely.<br /> <br /> That said, I will throw my voice into some of the concerns above that the text seems to have a degree of confusion about the relationship between Seeming and Kith, and that hurts its ability to hook me on the concepts no matter how individually evocative the descriptions for each one are. If according to part of the text Seeming can mean one of these three things and be determined by anything between them (which seems to be the intent), but everywhere else suggests it's only one thing by relation to something much more specific, there seems to be some mixed messaging going on.<br /> <br /> I myself don't think it makes a lot of sense for Kiths, which have a pretty objective meaning and role, to be derived from something that is deliberately much broader in definition and more symbolic than literal. So the presentation feels a bit inconsistent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T14:53:03-08:00","id":1161617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161578#post1161578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks Satchel. Honestly, the thing that disappoints me most about losing Vainglory is that I don't have a way for my Kamen Rider Changelings to Henshin now - that's what I loved in particular about Vainglory. You could use it to show off your Changeling form without outright giving others ensorcellment, which was helped by normal people seeing it as an elaborate costume. Still, I do have a few custom courts coming along, including one that's based around partying...I could swing a custom contract out of that effect.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>emmens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161607#post1161607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish to know the story behind this as a casual fan of power rangers and sentai.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, me personally I'm ok waiting it out for Deviant before going whole hog with &quot;Kamen Riders in CofD&quot;. Especially since thematically Deviant makes a bit more sense for Kamen Riders then Changelings do. Especially with the older Showa Riders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T14:58:18-08:00","id":1161618,"title":"","content":"Anyone know if there's already a template to homebrew Court Contracts in 2e?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T15:41:11-08:00","id":1161633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>emmens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161607#post1161607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wish to know the story behind this as a casual fan of power rangers and sentai.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've only really made two of them, based on Kamen Rider Chalice and Kamen Rider TheBee - their transformation gear is relatively unobtrusive on their bodies, particularly Chalice's, and with Vainglory they both had a &quot;henshin&quot; option. Chalice in particular was interesting because, as a Changeling with Riddlekith, he could transform himself to get new abilities and appearances, which is something the show had for their Chalice, and since the Changeling had amnesia I planned for him to use Riddlekith to basically do angst about how he didn't know who he was - no Kith, no self. His keystone would be his Fetch, as it is basically all that remains of his past self.<br /> <br /> Plus, there was some kickass artwork for Chalice: <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://static.zerochan.net/Kamen.Rider.Blade.full.1138599.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> TheBee, on the other hand, was more born from pondering on an idea I'd made in a discussion a number of months ago regarding the idea of Batman as a Gentry, and Harley Quinn and Joker as Changelings. It evolved into Gotham City itself being the keeper (The City That Knows Crime), and thus a Bee villain came about in my head, which turned into a Changeling using TheBee as a reference for art. He was far looser from his inspiration though, being an ex-criminal from a family who promoted such behaviors, and as a Changeling he's able to turn into animals (particularly bees and striped cats), sneak around and basically be a menace while trying to go straight. Unlike my other Changeling, he wants nothing to do with his Fetch, though he's just as unlikely to actually kill it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T16:22:16-08:00","id":1161645,"title":"","content":"The Crown of Thorns Token is pretty awesome, but if word of its existance became know to Werewolves, Vampires, Demons, Mages, Mummies, Promeathans etc... It would be very dangerous to the Changeling who has the Crown of Thorns because those splats have a much harder time getting a fuel stat filled then a Changeling, drain power of the Crown of Thorns is worth hundreds of Times its weight in gold to other templates. <br /> <br /> Example a Vampire Elder with BP 10 with 0 vitae left, the Vampire makes a deal with a Changeling with Wyrd 10 with 75 Glamour to use the Crown of Thorns on the Changeling.<br /> <br /> Over 75 turns the Vampire uses the Crown of Thorns to drain 75 glamour from the Changeling, which becomes vitae for the Vampire. So the Elder ends up with 75 vitae which normally would invovle draining blood from multiple other vampires with a variety of risks, such as blood addiction and viniculum. Then the Changeling as part of the deal with the Vampire Reaps the Vampire for all 75 Glamour back. Both are at full. <br /> <br /> This even works better with a Mage because the Mage can remove the Condition caused by getting Reaped, and turn all that new Mana into Tass.<br /> <br /> Between the Crown of Thorns and Steal the Solid Reflection with the Wizened benifit that can allow the Changelings to pull out solidified versions of other splats fuel stats like Tass, Vitriol (well it sort acts as fuel), Fruits from a Mandorgea Garden, etc..., Changelings can be good at dealing in other fuels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T18:45:37-08:00","id":1161686,"title":"","content":"So, is Ensorcellment in the mortal appendix, or is it not a thing anymore?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T19:28:25-08:00","id":1161711,"title":"","content":"really loving that the Summer Court still has their signature &quot;orbital solar laser&quot; power and that the text goes out of the way to say that it is real, actual straight up sunlight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T20:52:30-08:00","id":1161742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161686#post1161686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, is Ensorcellment in the mortal appendix, or is it not a thing anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div> My guess is it's in the conditions appendix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T21:21:53-08:00","id":1161749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161578#post1161578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could use it to show off your Changeling form without outright giving others ensorcellment</div> </div> </div> </div>Dropping the Mask now applies Spooked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T01:20:52-08:00","id":1161785,"title":"","content":"Wonder how many Court Contracts sample non-season Courts will have...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T01:28:43-08:00","id":1161789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161785#post1161785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wonder how many Court Contracts sample non-season Courts will have...</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess, 3 freeholds worth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T02:29:46-08:00","id":1161798,"title":"","content":"Ensorcellment is probably going to be an appendix. After all, ghouls, wolfbloods and sleepers/walkers were all in the back of the book. Why ruin a good thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T02:57:29-08:00","id":1161802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161798#post1161798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ensorcellment is probably going to be an appendix. After all, ghouls, wolfbloods and sleepers/walkers were all in the back of the book. Why ruin a good thing?</div> </div> </div> </div> The minor splat is Fae Touched, I think Ensorcellment will be a condition, not a splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T03:17:36-08:00","id":1161806,"title":"","content":"Interesting thing about Clarity damage - Severe Clarity damage overwrites Mild Clarity damage, rather than pushing it right, as happens with physical damage. The example given on page 34 is of someone with 2 levels of Mild damage taking a single level of Severe, giving them one level of Severe and one level of Mild. <br /> <br /> If that had been physical damage, they would have ended up with one level of Severe and 2 levels of Mild.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T05:20:52-08:00","id":1161834,"title":"","content":"I know that in hedge a changeling doesn't have a mask, but could he use the benefits of drop the mask?<br /> <br /> Would it still alert the nearby fae beings and open the gates of the hedge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7761-glauber","name":"Glauber","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7761_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T07:23:12-08:00","id":1161853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161802#post1161802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The minor splat is Fae Touched, I think Ensorcellment will be a condition, not a splat.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sleepers were covered alongside sleepwalkers. Mundane human merits that can't be applied to ghouls were in the ghoul appendix. Etc. Anything related to human PCs tends to have its own separate appendix mixed together.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T11:55:12-08:00","id":1161932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161853#post1161853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sleepers were covered alongside sleepwalkers. Mundane human merits that can't be applied to ghouls were in the ghoul appendix. Etc. Anything related to human PCs tends to have its own separate appendix mixed together.</div> </div> </div> </div> I guess that is a possiblity, but they haven't mentioned that yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T12:54:14-08:00","id":1161942,"title":"","content":"So these are my opinions after rereading the manuscripts a few days (and a few rests) later.<br /> <br /> Concerning the number of kith presented i wish to amend my previous position. After giving the matter much thought i've come to the conclusion that (for me at least) the number of kith presented is ... enough for the the purpose of the core book. The kith presented also offer a varied enough presentation of concepts. I still cant stop feeling like there is one (or two max) concept missing (like one the waterbased one perhaps???The swimmerkin, waterborn or .. the ogre one). No matter. <br /> The reason i've changed my mind is that i think that the merits offer a lot of the variety for character options that were in the kith in 1st ed.<br /> <br /> Concerning the anchor traits.<br /> The more i read about it the more i like the Thread anchor as something that does an admirable job at informing an important character trait for a changeling. I know this isnt exactly what the trait is but i see it as what got you through everything and what you focused on to get out.<br /> But that said, the more i like the Thread trait the more i come to dislike the Needle trait. This trait could be put in any of the gameline with little to no change.<br /> All of that said, I've already figured a replacement for the needle trait so it is a minor nitpick in the end.<br /> <br /> All in all i am excited to read the next manuscript. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T13:36:34-08:00","id":1161953,"title":"","content":"I sadly haven't had time to read the entire second preview, but here's my impressions from the parts I have read:<br /> <br /> Love new Mantles, they're powerful and evocative, and the way higher levels improve the early abilities as well as unlocking new ones really reinforces the notion that monarchs are not to be trifled with.<br /> <br /> Contracts are far more hit than miss, most of my favorite powers made it in, although frequently with name and mechanical changes. There were a few notable exceptions though. Did Become the Primal Foundation get folded into Summon Loyal Servant? The elemental clause there feels underwhelming compared to how the old contract worked.<br /> <br /> Blessing of Perfection starts out really weak. At Wyrd 1-2 it's unlikely to give a better bonus than the object or character has naturally, and it may well be a downgrade. Maybe it should increase the bonus by 1/2 Wyrd instead of <i>replacing</i> it with [Wyrd]?<br /> <br /> Might of the Terrible Brute only working in grapples is interesting conceptually, but it feels awfully restrictive that it doesn't help characters who want to punch things without going into a grapple, or weapon users. Stealing attributes while grappling seems like it would fit better as a seeming variant than the base effect. <br /> <br /> <br /> Clarity is very different. I've read through it a couple of times, trying to really understand it and judge it on its own merits, not in comparison to other versions. My biggest concern with it is how it uses Wits+Composure to determine your maximum. Your average, base character in this system only starts with 4. Now, granted, Changelings get an extra attribute, and player characters are above average, so it's reasonable to assume that most players will start with at least 5. Unless the player min maxes those attributes there's no margin of error between 'full health' and 'wound penalties'. Wits and Composure are already heavily favored in the CoD system, to the point that my group is only half joking when we say that playing a character with less than 3 composure is hard mode. <br /> <br /> Of course, that brings me to my other observation, which is that it feels strange that a character's odds of clarity damage depends more on their wyrd than the severity of the trauma. Even a fairly devastating personal loss that rolls six or seven dice probably won't damage a Wyrd 1-2 Changeling's clarity at all, whereas a Wyrd 9 Changeling might have more clarity to lose, but is going to take a big hit pretty much every the breaking point roll 'hits'.<br /> <br /> All that said, I love Icons, and how they mesh with this system. Easily the coolest and most thematic part of the system, and I'm glad I read that part before griping too loudly about how hard it was to raise the clarity max, which was my initial knee jerk reaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T14:21:17-08:00","id":1161968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161953#post1161953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sadly haven't had time to read the entire second preview, but here's my impressions from the parts I have read:<br /> <br /> Love new Mantles, they're powerful and evocative, and the way higher levels improve the early abilities as well as unlocking new ones really reinforces the notion that monarchs are not to be trifled with.<br /> <br /> Contracts are far more hit than miss, most of my favorite powers made it in, although frequently with name and mechanical changes. There were a few notable exceptions though. Did Become the Primal Foundation get folded into Summon Loyal Servant? The elemental clause there feels underwhelming compared to how the old contract worked.<br /> <br /> Blessing of Perfection starts out really weak. At Wyrd 1-2 it's unlikely to give a better bonus than the object or character has naturally, and it may well be a downgrade. Maybe it should increase the bonus by 1/2 Wyrd instead of <i>replacing</i> it with [Wyrd]?<br /> <br /> Might of the Terrible Brute only working in grapples is interesting conceptually, but it feels awfully restrictive that it doesn't help characters who want to punch things without going into a grapple, or weapon users. Stealing attributes while grappling seems like it would fit better as a seeming variant than the base effect. <br /> <br /> <br /> Clarity is very different. I've read through it a couple of times, trying to really understand it and judge it on its own merits, not in comparison to other versions. My biggest concern with it is how it uses Wits+Composure to determine your maximum. Your average, base character in this system only starts with 4. Now, granted, Changelings get an extra attribute, and player characters are above average, so it's reasonable to assume that most players will start with at least 5. Unless the player min maxes those attributes there's no margin of error between 'full health' and 'wound penalties'. Wits and Composure are already heavily favored in the CoD system, to the point that my group is only half joking when we say that playing a character with less than 3 composure is hard mode. <br /> <br /> Of course, that brings me to my other observation, which is that it feels strange that a character's odds of clarity damage depends more on their wyrd than the severity of the trauma. Even a fairly devastating personal loss that rolls six or seven dice probably won't damage a Wyrd 1-2 Changeling's clarity at all, whereas a Wyrd 9 Changeling might have more clarity to lose, but is going to take a big hit pretty much every the breaking point roll 'hits'.<br /> <br /> All that said, I love Icons, and how they mesh with this system. Easily the coolest and most thematic part of the system, and I'm glad I read that part before griping too loudly about how hard it was to raise the clarity max, which was my initial knee jerk reaction.</div> </div> </div> </div> Before a Changeling hits Wyrd 10, most will likely have clarity protecting/healing magics in place and at least a couple of extra touchstones if they are smart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T14:44:23-08:00","id":1161973,"title":"","content":"A Motley with of say 4 each with Pure Clarity contract and both seeming effects on it can block 4 breaking points and provide 4 +2 armour against 4 more per scene. That is enough to protect against most of the clarity breaks. <br /> <br /> Then add Fortifying Presence to heal each others Clarity and with the Fairest effect also adds the Fairests Presence to the healed Changelings defence against the next breaking point that Changeling experiences.<br /> <br /> A Changeling with Pure Clarity can Reap people with minimal concern relatively often, where they know other they are unlikely to get hit by another breaking point, which means plentiful Glamour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 11-23-2017, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T15:00:45-08:00","id":1161977,"title":"","content":"Is anyone interested in the none Clarity mechanics, like variety of contracts and merits revealed? <br /> <br /> Or the rules of Onieromancy. Or Hedge spinning? <br /> <br /> What happens if you banish or remove an Eidolon from a dream before it's finished, does it become a Hedge Ghost, I mean it meantions in the Glossary that Hedge Ghosts can be the dead, or parts of emotions or DREAMS, so an exiled Eidolon could become a Hedge Ghost, I mean they are mechanically similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 11-23-2017, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T15:07:39-08:00","id":1161979,"title":"","content":"I'll also add that for some contracts and other elements, like Discreet Summons we need the anatoginist chapter to know what a basic Hobgoblin looks like mechanically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T15:32:04-08:00","id":1161982,"title":"","content":"I have seen a lot of discussion about the lack of Kiths on 2nd edition but how are better covered. Is this something in the previews or just something Rose said is how its gonna be done? I ask because I pledge and got the 2 PDFs previews but I cant find Kiths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T15:36:02-08:00","id":1161983,"title":"","content":"I think for the next big reveal it will the Shared Nightmares: Anatongists (which should have Fetches, True Fae, Hobgoblins, Hedge Ghosts, Huntsmen, and maybe Mirror People in it). <br /> <br /> And the other Chapter will have the Settings and Court Creation rules, like the the Council of Elves, Hong Kong, Ipswitch, and the one with the Tidal Courts. <br /> <br /> So that should be interesting and give us a more complete view of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T15:54:16-08:00","id":1161987,"title":"","content":"Does any else realize how much they must have changed the Far Touched Template given the change to rules like Contracts, Onieromancy, Seemings and few other things? <br /> <br /> I mean if say the Fae Touched get two Common Contracts instead of two one dot contracts related to their Seeming to start off with, that makes them more powerful to start off with. <br /> <br /> Will they be able to gain Royal Contracts at all? <br /> <br /> Do they still have Seemings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T16:25:26-08:00","id":1162002,"title":"","content":"I'd like to talk Hedgespinning and Dreamweaving. I don't think I have fully grasped them unfortunately.<br /> <br /> Also is it me or are Thorns missing rules? I don't really see how they could cause breaking points or cause Changeling's Integrity turn into Clarity...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T16:51:11-08:00","id":1162010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161973#post1161973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Motley with of say 4 each with Pure Clarity contract and both seeming effects on it can block 4 breaking points and provide 4 +2 armour against 4 more per scene. That is enough to protect against most of the clarity breaks.<br /> <br /> Then add Fortifying Presence to heal each others Clarity and with the Fairest effect also adds the Fairests Presence to the healed Changelings defence against the next breaking point that Changeling experiences.<br /> <br /> A Changeling with Pure Clarity can Reap people with minimal concern relatively often, where they know other they are unlikely to get hit by another breaking point, which means plentiful Glamour.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is just asking the ST to amp things up to keep things interesting, lest the party fall victim to Invincible Player Syndrome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T17:38:47-08:00","id":1162021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.kicktraq.com/projects/200664283/changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition/#chart-exp-projection\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/019/112/506/aca47791b81e61e04b8c380fff717c34_original.jpe?crop=faces&amp;w=160&amp;h=90&amp;fit=crop&amp;v=1510192032&amp;auto=format&amp;q=92&amp;s=ea747aa2c768afbabd3f85b9f78fda5f\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.kicktraq.com/projects/200664283/changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition/#chart-exp-projection\" target=\"_blank\"> Changeling: The Lost 2nd Edition </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.kicktraq.com/projects/200664283/changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition/#chart-exp-projection\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.kicktraq.com/projects/200664283/changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition/#chart-exp-projection </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Contribute to help create, publish, and distribute the 2nd Edition of the CHANGELING: THE LOST tabletop roleplaying game. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The projected final tally is a low of 142,995 to a high of 193,989.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T18:19:26-08:00","id":1162026,"title":"","content":"So what sort of additional stretch goals do you think we will be getting? Obviously Spring Novella and Summer Novella, and Steed/Shield/Mirror/Sword sections of K&amp;K, and Dancers at Dusk, Swords at Dawn, Goblin Markets, Victorian lost will be added to the Arcadian Memories Bundle. <br /> <br /> That still leaves a lot of potential stretch goals. <br /> <br /> Some possibilities: A full Setting Book or two, an Interactive Audio Story, Jumpstart, Ready Made Characters, Character Sheets, Condition Cards, Expanding the Entitlements section for more Entitlements, including Noble Entitlements like Lost Pantheon, Vizers, or Black Apples, a Novel, a Companion Section on Talespinning, an Antagonist Book, a Book of Contracts, The Hedge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T18:22:24-08:00","id":1162027,"title":"","content":"BTW the next Stretch goal after Winter Novella is adding Fear Maker's Promise Compilation to the Arcadian Memories Bundle, it's only a $1,000 stretch goal at $108,000 where to get to Winter Novella, we have to get to $107,000.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 11-23-2017, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T18:41:55-08:00","id":1162034,"title":"","content":"Perhaps another stretch goal will be an equivalent of &quot;Heirs to Hell&quot;, detailing what children of Changelings (and or Fetch) are like as well as an expansion on Fae Touched?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T18:53:55-08:00","id":1162039,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">\u200bOmega, use the edit feature instead of spamming replies. Thanks.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T20:04:02-08:00","id":1162065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1162034#post1162034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps another stretch goal will be an equivalent of &amp;quot;Heirs to Hell&amp;quot;, detailing what children of Changelings (and or Fetch) are like as well as an expansion on Fae Touched?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can like this idea only once, sadly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T20:25:06-08:00","id":1162074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161942#post1161942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Concerning the number of kith presented i wish to amend my previous position. After giving the matter much thought i've come to the conclusion that (for me at least) the number of kith presented is ... enough for the the purpose of the core book. The kith presented also offer a varied enough presentation of concepts. I still cant stop feeling like there is one (or two max) concept missing (like one the waterbased one perhaps???The swimmerkin, waterborn or .. the ogre one). No matter.<br /> The reason i've changed my mind is that i think that the merits offer a lot of the variety for character options that were in the kith in 1st ed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Were the kith shown in any of the previews PDFs? I cant find them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T20:30:36-08:00","id":1162076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1162074#post1162074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Were the kith shown in any of the previews PDFs? I cant find them.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, in the first one, just use the Adobe search feature to find Kiths.<br /> <br /> As for Childern of Fae creatures like Changelings, Eidolons, Hedge Ghosts, True Fae, Hobgoblins. Fetches, Mirror People, Huntsmen, I can see something along those lines in Kith and KIN book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 11-23-2017, 11:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T20:36:31-08:00","id":1162078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1162074#post1162074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Were the kith shown in any of the previews PDFs? I cant find them.</div> </div> </div> </div>What Omega just said.<br /> Its at page 56 of the first manuscript, if this help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T20:46:12-08:00","id":1162080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1162076#post1162076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, in the first one, just use the Adobe search feature to find Kiths.<br /> <br /> As for Childern of Fae creatures like Changelings, Eidolons, Hedge Ghosts, True Fae, Hobgoblins. Fetches, Mirror People, Huntsmen, I can see something along those lines in Kith and KIN book.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1162078#post1162078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What Omega just said.<br /> Its at page 56 of the first manuscript, if this help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks guys, as it is a subsection under winter i miss it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T21:30:27-08:00","id":1162084,"title":"","content":"...gosh dangit Changeling, I'd gotten over my idea for a token TARDIS! Stop tempting me to make a cabinet that allows a Changeling to travel to any place they've already been, with the drawback that the cabinet changes some aspect of the coordinates it lands at (instead of beside a house you arrive in the attic, or the neighbor's house, or five minutes after you wanted to arrive, or <i>before</i> you wanted to arrive, ect.). The catch? It's loud when it arrives and goes, attracting attention from whomever the user doesn't want to get attention from (such as the original owner). It's one of those ideas that just sticks with me. :/<br /> <br /> That said, I do like the varieties of tokens showcased. The idea that an Oath-Forged Token can be used directly against its creator the way that it is is rather terrifying though, which is something I like for balancing out its benefits. It really adds weight to the fact that Changelings guard them with zeal. Same for the stolen and the &quot;marinated&quot; tokens. They're just...awesome, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T22:00:18-08:00","id":1162094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1161953#post1161953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did Become the Primal Foundation get folded into Summon Loyal Servant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Props and Scenery, Whispers of Morning, Elemental Fury, and Red Revenge fill most of the conceptual niches. Summon Loyal Servant is an old Communion clause.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Blessing of Perfection starts out really weak. </div> </div> </div>It starts out more useful for aiding an unskilled character in using fairly technical Mental Skills, which seems appropriate for a Common Contract running at low optimization. The bigger concern, I'd think, would be that Wyrd isn't used for determining bonuses like that in many other Contracts \u2014 an Attribute would seem more appropriate (probably Intelligence or Wits).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unless the player min maxes those attributes there's no margin of error between 'full health' and 'wound penalties'. </div> </div> </div>This would appear to be by design, given the necessity of Touchstones for restoring damage and the fact that the bonus for no damage still results in a net positive for anyone who didn't set both Attributes to 1 on purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T23:00:55-08:00","id":1162100,"title":"","content":"So. There are still Hedgespun Items around (which I love, since that was part of what I really loved in 1e), but you can't make them with Hedgespinning?<br /> In fact, I can't find any rules about how to make them. Am I just blind or are they missing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T00:35:17-08:00","id":1162114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1162100#post1162100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So. There are still Hedgespun Items around (which I love, since that was part of what I really loved in 1e), but you can't make them with Hedgespinning?<br /> In fact, I can't find any rules about how to make them. Am I just blind or are they missing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess you'd make them using the token creation rules? Leave an object in a part of the hedge so long it starts to get it's components replaced by spiderweb or flames.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 11-24-2017, 03:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T01:02:56-08:00","id":1162117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted 