he materials needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well they do have effects. They're supernaturally good at what they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T01:13:36-08:00","id":1162120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1162118#post1162118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well they do have effects. They're supernaturally good at what they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. Extremely bland tokens instead.<br /> <br /> In 1e they required adventures in the Hedge, in the Underhill version they were built by part dream, part solid object, part intangible object, but now... they are just tokens as anything else? That's... really boring, to be honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T01:40:12-08:00","id":1162124,"title":"","content":"Oh, we crossed 107k. So Winter will indeed be coming in a novella.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T01:53:24-08:00","id":1162125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1162120#post1162120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok. Extremely bland tokens instead.<br /> <br /> In 1e they required adventures in the Hedge, in the Underhill version they were built by part dream, part solid object, part intangible object, but now... they are just tokens as anything else? That's... really boring, to be honest.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're items made of whatever you want. How is that boring @_@","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 11-24-2017, 05:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T04:13:41-08:00","id":1162139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1162117#post1162117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Damn it. That removes the fun part. Now they are just tokens without effects instead. :/<br /> <br /> The thing I loved about them was the adventures one could have in digging up the materials needed.</div> </div> </div> </div> On this matter.<br /> <br /> You can just hedgespin (as in the hedge shaping rules) any outfit you want, using the base subtle shifting rules. And I don't see any rules about that being temporary. Am I wrong that you can just create hedgespun outfits at whim without the bonuses?<br /> <br /> You'll still have to be taking the appropriate actions, find the appropriate materials / area to shape in, so there's an entire story in itself right there.<br /> <br /> And, considering that you're shaping directly from items in the hedge, which had absorbed the wild magic of Faerie, it could be considered magical by the first method of creating tokens, so you could have all the bonuses like that, if your ST is willing.<br /> <br /> So, we're looking at slightly different methods and rules of doing things than the 1e or Underhill editions, but I think its roughly the same story. <br /> <br /> TL;DR - The method of creation of hedgespun outfits and items now seems to come down to a question - how much do you enjoy the new Hedgespinning and Dream Shaping rules? Because that's how you make said outfits and items.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T14:40:02-08:00","id":1162262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1162117#post1162117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn it. That removes the fun part. Now they are just tokens without effects instead. :/</div> </div> </div> </div>That was literally always what a Hedgespun Item was. The process of Hedgespinning a token was a way to assemble a magical item; &quot;Hedgespun&quot; was never very mechanically involved as a basic concept.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The thing I loved about them was the adventures one could have in digging up the materials needed. </div> </div> </div>As MCN points out, steering the Hedge towards a desired outcome to mix together a desired set of components is how you accomplish the basic process of mashing reagents together into the right shape; all that remains to be done afterward is leave it alone in the most dangerous parts of the Hedge or use it to swear oaths by, and that's the kind of thing you put that sort of investment toward anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T14:45:04-08:00","id":1162265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1162139#post1162139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> On this matter.<br /> <br /> You can just hedgespin (as in the hedge shaping rules) any outfit you want, using the base subtle shifting rules. And I don't see any rules about that being temporary. Am I wrong that you can just create hedgespun outfits at whim without the bonuses?<br /> <br /> You'll still have to be taking the appropriate actions, find the appropriate materials / area to shape in, so there's an entire story in itself right there.<br /> <br /> And, considering that you're shaping directly from items in the hedge, which had absorbed the wild magic of Faerie, it could be considered magical by the first method of creating tokens, so you could have all the bonuses like that, if your ST is willing.<br /> <br /> So, we're looking at slightly different methods and rules of doing things than the 1e or Underhill editions, but I think its roughly the same story.<br /> <br /> TL;DR - The method of creation of hedgespun outfits and items now seems to come down to a question - how much do you enjoy the new Hedgespinning and Dream Shaping rules? Because that's how you make said outfits and items.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSo if I want to make a sweet, sweet, battleaxe for my Viking inspired changeling he can either...<br /> \u200bLeave it in the hedge a long time and let it naturally soak up faeirie magic.<br /> \u200bMake a crap ton of oaths upon it.<br /> \u200bOr Hedge Spin one, from Spite, wrath, hedge wood, and stone, or glacial ice, or dragon bone, or something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T16:45:03-08:00","id":1162283,"title":"","content":"Sorry if this has been asked before. I backed the kickstarter and I am wondering if there is a PDF of the outline of the book or something. or is it just the updates that get emailed out thus far?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T16:52:14-08:00","id":1162284,"title":"","content":"There is. In the &quot;updates&quot; there's links, for backers only, that contain the previews for the first four(?) chapters of the book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T18:08:18-08:00","id":1162299,"title":"","content":"Likely next Tuesday we will get Chapters 5 Shared Nightmares (antagonists and allies) &amp; 6 Kingdoms of the Earth (city settings).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T18:21:32-08:00","id":1162308,"title":"","content":"The next 3 stretch goals are Fear Maker's Promise for the Arcadian Memories Compilation, which we are only $231 (stretch goal is $108,000)from, then it's another section being added to the Kith and Kin: Mirror at $112,000, and then at $114,000 they will make a Kith and Kin add on for $15 for all pledges below $50 (it's already included in Pledges above $50).<br /> <br /> Prediction, the Kith and Kin add on will cause a spike in donations from those who find shipping too expensive in their country, such as Australians, but still want Kith and Kin. <br /> <br /> Also note that further Kith and Kin stretch goals won't make the add on more expensive, it's staying at $15.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 11-24-2017, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T18:34:47-08:00","id":1162310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_contain