 folding a different paper crane. <br /> <br /> I'm a bit confused over how critical folding the crane in this case is to the operation of the Contract. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Character Concept Challenge Night! How would y'all build a dragon in this edition now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T15:42:05-08:00","id":1162815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1162694#post1162694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, one thing I notice about these new Contracts. There's talk about doing things like playing a silver flute, or folding an origami crane out of a leaf, or jumping up and down to regale the Wyrd with stories of your athletic prowess. Then, the Action is declared to be Instant. As per page 20 of the WoD core book, Instant Actions are defined as taking between 1 to 3 seconds.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a game that has the Build Equipment action included in its copy of the core mechanics. Nothing about a prerequisite activity contradicts &quot;the Contract itself takes an instant action \u2014 one turn or one to three seconds in action scenes and a few seconds outside of those circumstances, by the book's own reference \u2014 to invoke.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T16:47:55-08:00","id":1162824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1162815#post1162815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing about a prerequisite activity contradicts &quot;the Contract itself takes an instant action \u2014 one turn or one to three seconds in action scenes and a few seconds outside of those circumstances, by the book's own reference \u2014 to invoke.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> The contract doesn't SAY its a prerequisite action, though. You're guessing there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T20:10:34-08:00","id":1162884,"title":"","content":"I'd say good odds we hit the next stretch goal tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T22:42:20-08:00","id":1162909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1162807#post1162807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am having a bout of bad luck. Issues with my email and I only have updated 8-12 but the first 7 got deleted... ( and no longer in my trash because ... fml )<br /> <br /> I tried to log into Kickstarter to see if it had the links and it says that it can\u2019t find my email. I just don\u2019t even get it. I pledged 100 and I am getting the emails. ...<br /> <br /> Anyway, someone (here) said there were links to the manuscript at the bottom of the emails. I\u2019m not sure if it\u2019s my phone or not, but there are no links in the ones I have. I don\u2019t even know who I should contact in Kickstarter about retrieving the lost updates. -Flails- I am so bad at this!</div> </div> </div> </div>If that was me, it's the first and sixth emails... which, yeah.<br /> <br /> However, the next preview should be coming out tomorrow, and _hopefully_ it'll have links to the earlier ones.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T23:35:46-08:00","id":1162916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1162909#post1162909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that was me, it's the first and sixth emails... which, yeah.<br /> <br /> However, the next preview should be coming out tomorrow, and _hopefully_ it'll have links to the earlier ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of the updates (including links to previews) appear on the kickstarter page (<a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition/posts/2051283\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects.../posts/2051283</a>)<br /> <br /> If you're having trouble logging into kickstarter, I'd first double-check your email (for instance, I used an email that auto-forwards to my main email). After that, contact kickstarter to see if they can figure out what's going on","signature":"","edited":{"userid":18839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18839-zilaenor","user":"zilaenor","date":". 11-27-2017, 02:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18839-zilaenor","name":"zilaenor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T23:57:37-08:00","id":1162920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1162909#post1162909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, the next preview should be coming out tomorrow, and _hopefully_ it'll have links to the earlier ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it follows the pattern of the other previews, it'll be out on the 29th so it's unlikely to be up tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T00:39:24-08:00","id":1162923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1162920#post1162920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it follows the pattern of the other previews, it'll be out on the 29th so it's unlikely to be up tomorrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first preview was posted a couple of minutes after the KS began; the second was posted 21st November, just before 3 pm EST, so... reasonable guess is the third will follow suit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T01:02:08-08:00","id":1162930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1162923#post1162923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The first preview was posted a couple of minutes after the KS began; the second was posted 21st November, just before 3 pm EST, so... reasonable guess is the third will follow suit.</div> </div> </div> </div>The dates kickstarter says when I look up the updates are November 15th for the first preview and November 22nd. So the pattern would make the third happen on the 29th.<br /> <br /> Edit: Seems I assumed the dates kickstarter was listing weren't customisable depending on location. For me it will be happening on the 29th (which isn't tomorrow), for americans it would be 28th (which is only just became tomorrow a short while ago).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 11-27-2017, 04:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T05:21:39-08:00","id":1162963,"title":"","content":"I'm a recent backer and I have to say, I am really excited about everything I've read so far. My only complaints are that yeah, there should have been more kiths in the corebook, and I don't like that iron does aggravated damage to changelings just from touch now. I liked that before, while changelings were still vulnerable to iron, they could still handle it, while it was totally poisonous to the true fae. It's a really minor thing that's easy to houserule away, but it's still something I'm not a fan of. Otherwise though, I cannot wait to play this!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","name":"Lady Gray","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T06:29:14-08:00","id":1162977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lady Gray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1162963#post1162963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a recent backer and I have to say, I am really excited about everything I've read so far. My only complaints are that yeah, there should have been more kiths in the corebook, and I don't like that iron does aggravated damage to changelings just from touch now. I liked that before, while changelings were still vulnerable to iron, they could still handle it, while it was totally poisonous to the true fae. It's a really minor thing that's easy to houserule away, but it's still something I'm not a fan of. Otherwise though, I cannot wait to play this!</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that there is a difference between Cold Iron, Iron, and Steel.<br /> <br /> Cold Iron - Custom hand made by an artisan with care. Most effective vs. Changelings. Exceedingly rare unless dealing with mortal hunters.<br /> Iron - Mass produced, spit out at a high rate. Wrought iron for example. Less effective vs. Changelings but still cancels out protective contracts. Example wrought iron fence.<br /> Steel - Iron mixed with carbon. Not any more or less effective vs. a changeling than a human. Well much less effective against a changeling than any form of iron. Changeling can use defensive kith blessings and contracts against steel.<br /> <br /> Unless they are a hunter expecting changelings they aren't brining iron. Or a little old lady with a fence...but that example just toss a jacket over it when you hop the fence and you'll be fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T06:36:08-08:00","id":1162979,"title":"","content":"So now we have almost all the non mechanic information on Rose And Meghans version of the Huntsmen.<br /> They're not spiritual beings anymore,they have a desire to be free from The Hunt but dont want to not exist anymore. They're actually older than the Fae,being the first inhabitants of Arcadia. And you can actually help them recover their free will,thus ending their hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T06:46:05-08:00","id":1162984,"title":"","content":"So I've finally been catching up on the kickstarter previews and had a question about Seemings and Favored Attributes. The text reads: &quot;As well, every seeming has three favored Attributes from either Power, Finesse, or Resistance traits. Take an additional dot in one of these.&quot;<br /> <br /> It seems a little unclear to me but we are meant to take only one dot in one of the three appropriate (Power, Finesse, or Resistance) traits, is that correct? It isn't meant to be read take a dot in each of the traits for Power, Finesse, or Resistance, right?<br /> <br /> Apologies if this has already been asked and answered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T06:54:47-08:00","id":1162987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1162977#post1162977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that there is a difference between Cold Iron, Iron, and Steel.<br /> <br /> Cold Iron - Custom hand made by an artisan with care. Most effective vs. Changelings. Exceedingly rare unless dealing with mortal hunters.<br /> Iron - Mass produced, spit out at a high rate. Wrought iron for example. Less effective vs. Changelings but still cancels out protective contracts. Example wrought iron fence.<br /> Steel - Iron mixed with carbon. Not any more or less effective vs. a changeling than a human. Well much less effective against a changeling than any form of iron. Changeling can use defensive kith blessings and contracts against steel.<br /> <br /> Unless they are a hunter expecting changelings they aren't brining iron. Or a little old lady with a fence...but that example just toss a jacket over it when you hop the fence and you'll be fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>This always kills me because the purpose of mixing carbon into iron is to purify it. Wrought (and most other types of non-steel iron) run a gamut of having from 50%~80% iron and 50%~20% impurities (rubble, salt crystals, etc.). The term steel always indicates iron that has been put through a purification process. Of the various processes for making steel, use of carbon is one of the best because the final product is 97%~99% pure iron. So...yeah...<br /> <br /> Frankly the term &quot;cold steel&quot; (&quot;cold iron&quot; being a more apocryphal term) has always been an alliteration referring to iron's ability to conduct heat. At room temperature it usually feels cold because as soon as you pick it up it starts absorbing your body heat... <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T07:34:45-08:00","id":1162997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1162984#post1162984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've finally been catching up on the kickstarter previews and had a question about Seemings and Favored Attributes. The text reads: &amp;quot;As well, every seeming has three favored Attributes from either Power, Finesse, or Resistance traits. Take an additional dot in one of these.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> It seems a little unclear to me but we are meant to take only one dot in one of the three appropriate (Power, Finesse, or Resistance) traits, is that correct? It isn't meant to be read take a dot in each of the traits for Power, Finesse, or Resistance, right?<br /> <br /> Apologies if this has already been asked and answered.</div> </div> </div> </div> 1 dot in either Dexterity, Wits, or Manipulation for Darklings and Wizened, 1 dot in either Stamina, Compsure, or Resolve for Beasts and Elementals, and 1 dot in either Strength, Intelligence, or Presence for Fairest and Orgers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T08:12:06-08:00","id":1163003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Frankly the term &quot;cold steel&quot; (&quot;cold iron&quot; being a more apocryphal term) has always been an alliteration referring to iron's ability to conduct heat. At room temperature it usually feels cold because as soon as you pick it up it starts absorbing your body heat... </span><br /> </span><br /> </div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> I always thought it was just a poetic reference to iron weapons. In modern day terms, we still use the phrase cold steel, or hot lead. Its the same kind of idea. When I say hot lead, most people get that I'm talking about bullets, not a random lump of lead that's being heated <br /> <br /> And I have always been driven crazy that somehow steel doesn't count as iron just because it uses different names in the English language. Like, what do you do if we have a language that calls iron and steel the same word? <br /> </span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T08:19:52-08:00","id":1163006,"title":"","content":"Just gonna say, I love the route they're taking with the Huntsmen. Very interesting. The idea of them being older than the True Fae of Arcadia, and even sympathetic, makes for all sorts of intriguing plot hooks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T08:23:20-08:00","id":1163008,"title":"","content":"Regarding the Huntsmen - what happens if, while a Huntsman is tracking a changeling but hasn't captured him, the changeling goes into the Bastion where the Huntsman's heart lies? Can the Huntsman follow the changeling in and find his heart, or does he lose the trail altogether?<br /> <br /> And if you return a Huntsman's heart, does that destroy the Title that keeps him hunting, or just send it back to the True Fae? Because if it's the latter a changeling isn't any better off for releasing a Huntsman from his bondage. But in the former case freeing a Huntsman permanently diminishes the Fae who bound him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T08:41:18-08:00","id":1163011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lady Gray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1162963#post1162963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a recent backer and I have to say, I am really excited about everything I've read so far. My only complaints are that yeah, there should have been more kiths in the corebook, and I don't like that iron does aggravated damage to changelings just from touch now. I liked that before, while changelings were still vulnerable to iron, they could still handle it, while it was totally poisonous to the true fae. It's a really minor thing that's easy to houserule away, but it's still something I'm not a fan of. Otherwise though, I cannot wait to play this!</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth noting that only <i>cold Iron</i> does aggravated damage at touch. The Lost can still handle reg Iron against anything fae or Fae.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1162987#post1162987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This always kills me because the purpose of mixing carbon into iron is to purify it. Wrought (and most other types of non-steel iron) run a gamut of having from 50%~80% iron and 50%~20% impurities (rubble, salt crystals, etc.). The term steel always indicates iron that has been put through a purification process. Of the various processes for making steel, use of carbon is one of the best because the final product is 97%~99% pure iron. So...yeah...<br /> <br /> Frankly the term &quot;cold steel&quot; (&quot;cold iron&quot; being a more apocryphal term) has always been an alliteration referring to iron's ability to conduct heat. At room temperature it usually feels cold because as soon as you pick it up it starts absorbing your body heat...</div> </div> </div> </div>They state it in the book that it has less to do with the actual chemical make-up of the Iron/Steel and more to do with the <i>Idea</i> of iron. Which is why mass produced Iron things work against fae magic as long as it is refered to as 'iron' by common people. I'd imagine an &quot;iron&quot; cup which has only trace amounts of iron in its makeup would still work since it technically has iron in it and most consider it an iron cup.<br /> <br /> On the flip side, Cold Iron is mostly the pure <i>Idea</i> of iron rather than pure Iron itself. The act of hand making it mostly straight from the earth is more what counts rather than its chemical make-up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163008#post1163008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the Huntsmen - what happens if, while a Huntsman is tracking a changeling but hasn't captured him, the changeling goes into the Bastion where the Huntsman's heart lies? Can the Huntsman follow the changeling in and find his heart, or does he lose the trail altogether?<br /> <br /> And if you return a Huntsman's heart, does that destroy the Title that keeps him hunting, or just send it back to the True Fae? Because if it's the latter a changeling isn't any better off for releasing a Huntsman from his bondage. But in the former case freeing a Huntsman permanently diminishes the Fae who bound him.</div> </div> </div> </div>That will depend on the nature of the bargain the Title made to hollow out the Huntsman. Maybe the Title actually gains more 'power' by losing the Huntsman as their end of the bargain was fulfilled but not the other way around. It could also be the exact opposite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":654,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","user":"xiongrey","date":". 11-27-2017, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T10:12:41-08:00","id":1163044,"title":"","content":"I haven't seen anyone mention this:<br /> <br /> A number of the Kickstarter updates are open to the public. The manuscript previews are backer-only, but there are topical overviews that everyone can see.<br /> <br /> Clarity - <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition/posts/2053107\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects.../posts/2053107</a><br /> Oneiromancy - <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition/posts/2054688\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects.../posts/2054688</a><br /> Huntsmen - <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition/posts/2055911\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects.../posts/2055911</a><br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure this is intentional, but if that's not the case, feel free to nuke my post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T14:24:44-08:00","id":1163100,"title":"","content":"In British and Irish folklore, it's not &quot;cold iron&quot; that drives away the fairy folk -- it's just <i>iron. </i>Along with the sound of church bells, wearing your coat inside-out, and a variety of other inexplicable weaknesses. It's not a universal feature of fairy legends, either. The thing is, a vulnerability to such a common substance kind of limits the usefulness of fairies as either protagonists or antagonists. &quot;Cold iron&quot; as a separate substance from regular old iron first shows up, as far as I know, in early D&amp;D, where it causes extra damage to <i>demons.</i> Like a lot of things in early D&amp;D, this probably comes from a fantasy novel or story that Gygax had read and decided to use (and possibly misinterpreted.) A lot of games follow D&amp;D in making cold iron a special or even magical substance, although they define &quot;cold&quot; in a variety of different ways, some of which don't really make much sense (like the wrought iron interpretation mentioned above.)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.poetryloverspage.com/poets/kipling/cold_iron.html\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Cold Iron&quot;</a> is also the title of a poem by Rudyard Kipling, which is quite good but has nothing to do with fairies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/40-dspaul","name":"DSPaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T14:47:59-08:00","id":1163102,"title":"","content":"I dunno, the story and myths surrounding \u201ccold iron\u201d being stronger and more well known versus the the actual facts and classifications of iron, actually seems more on-theme to CtL then it not being so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T15:55:29-08:00","id":1163115,"title":"","content":"I rather like this presentation for Huntsmen. Though some things are different, the essential ideas all seem to still be there, and they're written in a very fetching way. The humanist approach to the Huntsmen as characters plays strongly to their role of twisted mirrors as antagonists to the Lost. The tone is definitely more personal, and I think that's to their advantage. The part with their stolen heart and the possibility of swaying the Huntsman through it opens up some very interesting, though difficult and exceptional, possibilities in responding to their threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T16:04:28-08:00","id":1163117,"title":"","content":"From a game design standpoint, I get why you want to make all this iron and cold iron stuff. Banes are generally stuff that, while easy to get a hold of, is generally not something that is common, especially in weapons. Fire and wood stakes aren't usually used as weapons, it has to be a deliberate choicce to take them. Same with silver bullets. <br /> <br /> Being able to have a supernatural's bane, just because most knives are made from steel, is actually pretty bad. From a supernatural standpoint, you're in a world made of flames. From a hunter standpoint, there's no need to research and look into things. You want to make a bane easily retrieved, but require some planning.<br /> <br /> Its just that the difference behind &quot;cold iron&quot; regular iron and steel is a bit tricky to talk about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T19:11:00-08:00","id":1163141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163115#post1163115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...they're written in a very <b>fetch</b>ing way...</div> </div> </div> </div>Eheheheheh...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T20:04:06-08:00","id":1163148,"title":"","content":"Mirrors stretch goal achieved!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T20:27:08-08:00","id":1163154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163003#post1163003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I always thought it was just a poetic reference to iron weapons. In modern day terms, we still use the phrase cold steel, or hot lead. Its the same kind of idea. When I say hot lead, most people get that I'm talking about bullets, not a random lump of lead that's being heated<br /> <br /> And I have always been driven crazy that somehow steel doesn't count as iron just because it uses different names in the English language. Like, what do you do if we have a language that calls iron and steel the same word?<br /> [/FONT]<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You won't find one. All cultures recognize that steel is lighter and stronger than Iron, the nature of steel from all view points and uses is much different from Iron. In 600 BC iron was not considered valuable, but steel was most precious. Much like how bronze is not copper even though it is made from copper. To put it simply, too much changes in the nature of the metal for it to be considered the same thing anymore.<br /> <br /> Edit: Further more, if you heat up steel again and melt it, it does not separate out into iron and carbon. It stays one new thing, steel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":".  Horse wasn't dead yet 11-27-2017, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T00:21:57-08:00","id":1163186,"title":"","content":"It's a shame that the semantic argument of iron vs. cold iron wasn't nixed forever in 2E. The conceptual iron one is probably the easiest to use for an actual game though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":". 11-28-2017, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T03:10:37-08:00","id":1163193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163154#post1163154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You won't find one. All cultures recognize that steel is lighter and stronger than Iron, the nature of steel from all view points and uses is much different from Iron. In 600 BC iron was not considered valuable, but steel was most precious. Much like how bronze is not copper even though it is made from copper. To put it simply, too much changes in the nature of the metal for it to be considered the same thing anymore.<br /> <br /> Edit: Further more, if you heat up steel again and melt it, it does not separate out into iron and carbon. It stays one new thing, steel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Iron and steel are generally very different, but the truth is it's a spectrum. You won't find any pure iron. It all has different amounts of impurities, and different types of iron has different names because of it. Wrought iron, cast iron, pig iron, etc. Steel just happen to have a higher rate of carbon, and there's no natural cut off point. In fact, cast iron contains more carbon than most steel types.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T06:47:37-08:00","id":1163215,"title":"","content":"It works pretty well I\u2019m game terms right? I mean it feels very fae right? Semantics aside, isn\u2019t the mechanics very in line with the feeling of the content?<br /> <br /> Idk, I\u2019ve never minded and indeed liked the iron mechanics in CtL. I wanted clarification on what counts in 1st ed and they clarified it in 2nd so I\u2019m happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":654,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","user":"xiongrey","date":". 11-28-2017, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T07:42:36-08:00","id":1163226,"title":"","content":"*Reads latest preview*<br /> <br /> Urge to sqwee rising...!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T07:49:19-08:00","id":1163227,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2241\" data-vbnamecard=\"2241\">Omegaphallic</a> . You wanted to see HedgeGhosts Right? they are in the next preview","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T08:23:00-08:00","id":1163236,"title":"","content":"No spirits, angels, or ghosts (other than Hedge ghosts) in the antagonist chapter! No more arbitrarily eaten up word count because they are &quot;core!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T08:40:43-08:00","id":1163242,"title":"","content":"I love Hong Kong's Societies. Makes me wonder how they and other supernaturals get along in the city--Something like the polite emnity of the shen in the old World of Darkness? They certainly can't hide from each other in such a small space.<br /> <br /> Reykjavik's Seasonal Courts are interesting, too. I notice they don't exactly have a dedicated &quot;militant&quot; court like standard Summer (Winter comes closest, but comes with a lot of other associations)-- I can see how that might possibly be an American quirk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13580-hsienfan","name":"Hsienfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T09:00:00-08:00","id":1163258,"title":"","content":"couldn't help but read some of the latest preview over my cup of pre-work coffee. skipped right ahead to the section detailing the alternative courts.<br /> <br /> wow! these are way better than i was expecting. tbh the alternate courts in 1e left me a little cold. happy to say that i am really digging this fresh take. especially hard-e-lee! sorta sad that they are not complete write-ups, as each court is missing the &quot;give and take&quot; mechanic, crown descriptions and court contracts. i also like the council of elves ... showing that there can be alternate takes on even the Seasonal Courts depending on their region.<br /> <br /> seriously tho, very cool.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T09:28:18-08:00","id":1163264,"title":"","content":"As a small tangent from the iron/cold iron/steel thing, did we ever get a clear answer on whether siderite/Perfect Iron from Mage's Signs of Sorcery does anything with the Fae? It's possible that it was stated somewhere, but I'm not sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T09:40:20-08:00","id":1163271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163264#post1163264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a small tangent from the iron/cold iron/steel thing, did we ever get a clear answer on whether siderite/Perfect Iron from Mage's Signs of Sorcery does anything with the Fae? It's possible that it was stated somewhere, but I'm not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's stated in the Signs of Sorcery preview that all perfected materials still acts as banes if the original material was a bane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T09:51:58-08:00","id":1163272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163271#post1163271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's stated in the Signs of Sorcery preview that all perfected materials still acts as banes if the original material was a bane.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright. I kind of expected more, but I suppose it's reasonable that they don't to avoid further cries of &quot;Mage Superiority.&quot;<br /> <br /> Although, I guess any splat that can move stuff in and out of twilight could Perfect materials if they wanted, but I'm just getting off on a tangent here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T10:21:43-08:00","id":1163275,"title":"","content":"Perfected materials also remove any qualifiers when determining whether it's a bane or not. If the bane is a blessed silver knife that needs to have been submerged in blood in the last 24 hours, you could still use any piece of lunargent since the base of the bane is silver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T10:39:43-08:00","id":1163277,"title":"","content":"On Ipswich: <br /> <br /> I wonder if Lovecraft jokes are a thing there. It literally has deep one hybrids as its primary Fae-Touched ethnicity, many of whom are fishermen who spend much of their time underwater. The Asrai were natives that assimilated into the European settlers by crossbreeding and a site of strange, disquieting transformations inflicted on visitors, even. Mirror Universe Innsmouth.<br /> <br /> I can see a good one-shot being all about diving into the mysteries of the place despite unhappy locals trying to drive the players off.<br /> <br /> On Huntsmen-I wish we had stats, but I'm fine with the hobgoblins instead. Otherwise, awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T10:41:21-08:00","id":1163278,"title":"","content":"Are the extra courts going to have contracts and give-and-take in the full release?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T10:48:51-08:00","id":1163280,"title":"","content":"i <i>Love</i> the other courts! It gives a lot of ideas for customization for pretty much anywhere!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T12:44:26-08:00","id":1163312,"title":"","content":"I think true fae should get the advantage archmages do wherein they auto win clash of wills against lower tier beings. At least in the hedge or arcadia. Granted thats a rule ive used for all beings of that sorta tier (rank 6+ ephemera, archmages, etc) in my games so that may be personal preference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T13:17:03-08:00","id":1163320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163312#post1163312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think true fae should get the advantage archmages do wherein they auto win clash of wills against lower tier beings. At least in the hedge or arcadia. Granted thats a rule ive used for all beings of that sorta tier (rank 6+ ephemera, archmages, etc) in my games so that may be personal preference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are lower tier beings any creature that isn't one of the Gentry? Or is it versus beings of lesser Power Stat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","user":"Firefly Night","date":".  fixed html code for quote 11-28-2017, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T14:32:09-08:00","id":1163336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firefly Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163320#post1163320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are lower tier beings any creature that isn't one of the Gentry? Or is it versus beings of lesser Power Stat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically typical PC tier characters: Changelings, Vampires, Werewolves, etc. Likely also includes hobgoblins and ephemera of rank 5 or less. I've always had gentry on that cosmological tier, at least when in the hedge or arcadia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T14:50:40-08:00","id":1163341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163264#post1163264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a small tangent from the iron/cold iron/steel thing, did we ever get a clear answer on whether siderite/Perfect Iron from Mage's Signs of Sorcery does anything with the Fae? It's possible that it was stated somewhere, but I'm not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've not heard of siderite/perfect iron in this context, and I don't have the book that this is from. However, the previews have stated that &quot;cold iron&quot; is one that is worked by hand and passion without any magic involved. If the product was already cold iron and a Mage enhanced it with magic, I think that would actively downgrade it - treating it with magic would be adding another step in the process of crafting it, and thus it would go against what cold iron is. You'd effectively get what you would if you treated mass produced iron with it. It would have some effect, just not the same as cold iron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T15:14:39-08:00","id":1163349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163341#post1163341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've not heard of siderite/perfect iron in this context, and I don't have the book that this is from. However, the previews have stated that &quot;cold iron&quot; is one that is worked by hand and passion without any magic involved. If the product was already cold iron and a Mage enhanced it with magic, I think that would actively downgrade it - treating it with magic would be adding another step in the process of crafting it, and thus it would go against what cold iron is. You'd effectively get what you would if you treated mass produced iron with it. It would have some effect, just not the same as cold iron.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. I'm sure a smart mage could find a loophole. If you could find a non-magical way to pass things in and out of Twilight, I wonder if it would still count...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T16:19:04-08:00","id":1163372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163349#post1163349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm. I'm sure a smart mage could find a loophole. If you could find a non-magical way to pass things in and out of Twilight, I wonder if it would still count...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what kind of loophole there could be. By using magic on it to enhance it, you're reworking it and changing its nature, which as I've noted is basically adding another step to how it has been forged. You get some benefits, sure, but you're still losing the &quot;cold iron&quot; trait it had from the start.<br /> <br /> As for a non-magical way to get something into twilight, I can't honestly think of a way to do it outside of a Demon gadget, or some overly complicated device humanity manages to make that isn't innately magical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T16:59:01-08:00","id":1163392,"title":"","content":"Perfected metals remove any and all other qualifers - Siderite is *Iron; it affects fae like cold iron, a monster that can only be hurt by meteroic iron like meteroic iron, an Oni that can only be hurt by thousand-folded steel like thousand-folded steel and so on. That's the <i>point</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T17:25:07-08:00","id":1163406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>E11even-E11even</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163278#post1163278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the extra courts going to have contracts and give-and-take in the full release?</div> </div> </div> </div> This is a very good question, if they don't get courts contracts I don't see anyone using them.<br /> <br /> Although the Iceland one is just a variant of the Seasonal Courts, so it does have Court Contracts.<br /> <br /> Truth be I could see giving the Society of Night access to the Contracts of Summer, the Society of Day access to the contracts of Spring, and the Society of Morning access to Contracts of Autumn or Winter.<br /> <br /> As for the Antagonists, they seem to fall roughly into five categories. <br /> <br /> Fae Horrors: Hobgoblins and Huntsmen use variants of the Hobgblin rules. (Fluff wise different creatures, but mechanically built simularily). Both can use the Dread Powers from the CoD corebook, although this means you actually need that book to use those (and all the example Hobgoblins do). Each also gets some of their own Dread Powers, although I think Huntsmen can take Hobgoblin Dread Powers. Want an irony, a Wyrd 10 Hobgoblin or Huntsmen actually have more merits then True Fae Titles with 10 Wyrd (although that True Fae would have 5 Titles with their own merits so the True Fae would have a higher total between titles).<br /> <br /> Hedge Emphereals: Hedge Ghosts (dead people a little more like regular ghosts), Hedge Ghosts (never human a little more like spirits) which are slightly mechanically different and then there are their variants, Important Eidolons, Extra Eidolons, Loyal Servants, with their own mechanics. A starting Changeling with Resolve 5 and trading it's merits for Wyrd 3 actually has Important Eidolons with Wyrd 8, which is shockingly powerful, even the True Fae will think twice before invading that Changelings dreams. <br /> <br /> Fetches: Fetches. No surprises here. <br /> <br /> True Fae: True Fae<br /> <br /> Loyalists: True Loyalists, Privateers, Bridge Burners (who are really interesting). Similar variety as regular Changelings, which will get a great boost with the Kith and Kin Book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 11-28-2017, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T17:50:02-08:00","id":1163413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163406#post1163406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a very good question, if they don't get courts contracts I don't see anyone using them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of hyperbolic to say, because frankly I don't give a shit if they get court contracts or not. If I get a chance to run a changeling game, I am fully intent on using one of these settings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T17:53:10-08:00","id":1163414,"title":"","content":"Minor point of confusion: Fetches can gain Court Goodwill (and presumably other supernaturals or even mortals could too, under the right circumstances) The text says they're ineligible for Mantle, does that include the secondhand mantle effects associated with high Goodwill, or can they just not purchase Mantle proper? Courts are by Changelings for Changelings, but it would be neat if superlative allies were able to earn a watered down blessing as a sign of their deep ties to the court in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T20:09:42-08:00","id":1163445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163406#post1163406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a very good question, if they don't get courts contracts I don't see anyone using them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't either. If they don't get contracts or give-and-take then they're basically halves of courts that will still take a ton of work to use. That would be a lot of space dedicated to unusable content. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T20:13:19-08:00","id":1163448,"title":"","content":"Actually, something that surprised me:<br /> <br /> No mention of Milestones in regards to resolving Fetches. The new text implies benefits for doing so, but there's no discussion of the 1e versions of those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T20:25:53-08:00","id":1163450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>E11even-E11even</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163278#post1163278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the extra courts going to have contracts and give-and-take in the full release?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering this text is 99% complete, probably not.<br /> <br /> And we aren't exactly in the middle of a blowback on the level of Beast's KS that's prompting mass writing revisions.<br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> ...which once again prompts me to ask:<br /> <br /> Is this book supposed to have &quot;Create-a-Contract&quot; rules along with &quot;Create-a-Court&quot; and &quot;Create-a-Kith&quot; rules, or is it just the latter two?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 11-28-2017, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T20:35:19-08:00","id":1163455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163450#post1163450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering this text is 99% complete, probably not.<br /> <br /> And we aren't exactly in the middle of a blowback on the level of Beast's KS that's prompting mass writing revisions.<br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> ...which once again prompts me to ask:<br /> <br /> Is this book supposed to have &quot;Create-a-Contract&quot; rules along with &quot;Create-a-Court&quot; and &quot;Create-a-Kith&quot; rules, or is it just the latter two?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you sort of need &quot;Create-a-Contract&quot; for &quot;Create-a-Court&quot; to work, but I don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T20:40:05-08:00","id":1163457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>E11even-E11even</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163445#post1163445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't either. If they don't get contracts or give-and-take then they're basically halves of courts that will still take a ton of work to use. That would be a lot of space dedicated to unusable content.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the game doesn't work because court contracts are so overwhelmingly powerful that not having the option to take them makes non-seasonal courts unusable, then the game is already broken. If you don't like the fact that not every single court is getting custom contracts made, that is totally fine. The suggestion that any other court is totally unsable because they don't have those contracts in the core rulebook and that it is wasted space, however, is disingenuous, panicky, and inflammatory. The key draw of Underhill for me was being able to create custom courts with ease. If I recall correctly, court contracts were never a part of that draft. Give-and-takes are easy to make, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> already has made some good suggestions for the Reykjav\u00edk freehold. I don't see what renders this chapter so unusable in your or Omega's minds. Frankly, of everything previewed so far, the settings and antagonists have been my favourite part. So again, if you don't like it, that's totally your prerogative. But at the same time, other people are allowed to love it and enjoy it. I for one do, And I've seen plenty of comments in the kick starter and on other forums that would seem to indicate I'm not alone. That means the space isn't wasted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T20:41:23-08:00","id":1163458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163457#post1163457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the game doesn't work because court contracts are so overwhelmingly powerful that not having the option to take them makes non-seasonal courts unusable, then the game is already broken. If you don't like the fact that not every single court is getting custom contracts made, that is totally fine. The suggestion that any other court is totally unsable because they don't have those contracts in the core rulebook and that it is wasted space, however, is disingenuous, panicky, and inflammatory. The key draw of Underhill for me was being able to create custom courts with ease. If I recall correctly, court contracts were never a part of that draft. Give-and-takes are easy to make, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> already has made some good suggestions for the Reykjav\u00edk freehold. I don't see what renders this chapter so unusable in your or Omega's minds. Frankly, of everything previewed so far, the settings and antagonists have been my favourite part. So again, if you don't like it, that's totally your prerogative. But at the same time, other people are allowed to love it and enjoy it. I for one do, And I've seen plenty of comments in the kick starter and on other forums that would seem to indicate I'm not alone. That means the space isn't wasted.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you for the lecture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T20:45:37-08:00","id":1163459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>E11even-E11even</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163458#post1163458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thank you for the lecture.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feel free to explain your point of view of why you think they're unusable. I'm genuinely all ears. Why exactly do we have to have custom contracts for every court just because the seasonal ones do? I'm not opposed to having them, I just fail to see how the content breaks down if you don't. <br /> <br /> And yes, if you say no one's going to use the part of the book that I am most excited to use, I think it's fair game to point out that others might have a different opinion than you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T21:15:50-08:00","id":1163466,"title":"","content":"Umm... Okay, three problems with the preview:<br /> 1) If you're going to require the Chronicles of Darkness Rulebook for basically all of your antagonist rules... then just say that in the introduction chapter and not waste massive amounts of page count on the &quot;repeating the Chronicles of Darkness Rulebook&quot; chapter.<br /> 2) What are the emotions for these courts and how do they work with Bedlam?<br /> 3) How do the courts which don't &quot;Change Seasons&quot; work with the rules for when hedge-portals close?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T22:02:09-08:00","id":1163477,"title":"","content":"Anyways, next stretch goal has been revealed: and sure enough, to match the KS new &quot;turn of the season&quot;, at $117k, the Spring novella will get made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T22:18:22-08:00","id":1163480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163457#post1163457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the game doesn't work because court contracts are so overwhelmingly powerful that not having the option to take them makes non-seasonal courts unusable, then the game is already broken. If you don't like the fact that not every single court is getting custom contracts made, that is totally fine. The suggestion that any other court is totally unsable because they don't have those contracts in the core rulebook and that it is wasted space, however, is disingenuous, panicky, and inflammatory. The key draw of Underhill for me was being able to create custom courts with ease. If I recall correctly, court contracts were never a part of that draft. Give-and-takes are easy to make, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> already has made some good suggestions for the Reykjav\u00edk freehold. I don't see what renders this chapter so unusable in your or Omega's minds. Frankly, of everything previewed so far, the settings and antagonists have been my favourite part. So again, if you don't like it, that's totally your prerogative. But at the same time, other people are allowed to love it and enjoy it. I for one do, And I've seen plenty of comments in the kick starter and on other forums that would seem to indicate I'm not alone. That means the space isn't wasted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Building on this:<br /> <br /> Writers have word counts to work with, and often getting across the conceptual space players will be gaming/imagining in takes the precedence. It's more important, for instance, that you comprehend that, in my project's case, the interplay between societal expectations and interpersonal relationships and the cynicism and low-key hopes and how that shapes you between these things for Paris than it was to give out a contract that embodies Black Rose's bond to Severance. With a well stocked game much as Changeling Second is, it's often enough to offer appropos Contracts at a discount. This was a couple of people's attitude.<br /> <br /> I'll admit, I'm wrapping up Chapter 4 still, so I can't comment on the setting subject, but the simple fact of the matter is that if you are looking for something present in Underhill that's absent here....you'll be disappointed, because Underhill operated much the same way, even down to Seasonal Courts still having more contracts.<br /> <br /> In the mean time, while there are points I have quibbles about, the simple and honest fact of the matter for me as this goes is that this version is just simply better-better written and more fully realized. Each entry makes me wish more and more that Rose would notice that I e-mailed her about wanting to write for Changeling Second, because I'm falling in love with Changeling all over again.*<br /> <br /> *And also I resolved my investigations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T22:24:39-08:00","id":1163481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163480#post1163480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Each entry makes me wish more and more that Rose would notice that I e-mailed her about wanting to write for Changeling Second, because I'm falling in love with Changeling all over again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I fully support this endeavour, especially if it means Paris can get snuck back into the Companion along with Toronto (Inshallah). But Paris Courts or not, having you back on Changeling would be awesome Arc!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T22:34:46-08:00","id":1163483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163481#post1163481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fully support this endeavour, especially if it means Paris can get snuck back into the Companion along with Toronto (Inshallah). But Paris Courts or not, having you back on Changeling would be awesome Arc!</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. I wouldn't be surprised(nor blame anyone) if my little stunt cost me work with OP for a while.<br /> <br /> Either way, it <i>does</i> mean you are going to see more of the Changeling Guy when he's not occupied by work or alcohol/cooking focused weekends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T00:36:16-08:00","id":1163495,"title":"","content":"We've got enough Courts that need expansion (Contracs, Give &amp; Take, Harvest &amp; Bedlam Emotion, etc) or rules update to support a whole supplement...<br /> <br /> - Society of Morning<br /> - Society of Day<br /> - Society of Night<br /> <br /> - Court of the Azure Serpent<br /> - Court of the Black Tortoise<br /> - Court of the White Tiger<br /> - Court of the Vermillion Bird<br /> - Court of the Yellow Dragon<br /> <br /> - Court of Coins<br /> - Court of Barter<br /> - Court of Favors<br /> - Court of Shady Deals<br /> <br /> - High Tide<br /> - Ebb Tide<br /> - Low Tide<br /> - Flood Tide<br /> <br /> - Sun Court<br /> - Moon Court<br /> <br /> - Court of Blood<br /> - Court of Snow<br /> - Court of Ash<br /> <br /> - Court of Science<br /> - Court of Art<br /> <br /> - Dawn Court<br /> - Dusk Court<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd throw in for good measure a Court system founded by Scheherazade herself after her Durance of 1001 nights (in Arcadia)...<br /> <br /> Court al-sabt<br /> Court al-ahad<br /> Court al-ithnayam<br /> Court al-thalatha<br /> Court al-arba'a<br /> Court al-khamis<br /> Court al-jumu'ah","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T01:28:22-08:00","id":1163496,"title":"","content":"I hope to see proper Courts write-ups from Hong Kong, Reykjav\u00edk, New England and New Orlean in the CtL 2E Companion. Other way - they are slightly unusable as they are now, without specific Contracts and Give &amp; Take sections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T01:49:45-08:00","id":1163498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163466#post1163466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Umm... Okay, three problems with the preview:<br /> 1) If you're going to require the Chronicles of Darkness Rulebook for basically all of your antagonist rules... then just say that in the introduction chapter and not waste massive amounts of page count on the &quot;repeating the Chronicles of Darkness Rulebook&quot; chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the fact they keep reproducing those chapters in their rulebooks baffles me-they never did it in NWoD, why are they doing it now?<br /> <br /> As for the new courts, while I think inluding emotions for them would be very useful, I think creating contracts is a fair thing to leave to the GM, especially when there are so many alternate courts to cater to-though again, if they stopped reproducing those antagonist rules there would be plenty of space. As for the give and take, I wouldn't be surprised if leaving those out was a conscious choice, since that's the sort of thing that really defines a court and freehold more than almost anything else, and I for one like the idea of crafting my own unique ones to really make my mark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","name":"Lady Gray","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T01:57:44-08:00","id":1163500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lady Gray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163498#post1163498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the fact they keep reproducing those chapters in their rulebooks baffles me-they never did it in NWoD, why are they doing it now?</div> </div> </div> </div>The intent originally was so that the game is fully playable with just the gameline's book. Unfortunately this book requires Core for some of it's content.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T02:39:09-08:00","id":1163506,"title":"","content":"Errata-<br /> <br /> Whispers of Morning (the contract) calls out hedge ghosts as being in Twilight. The hedge ghost section talks about the hedge not having a &quot;state of twilight&quot; but that ghosts are just incorporeal. I get that the intent is that hedge ghosts are something like the strix, who are intangible shadows, but still. The contract probably needs to be updated or something, since its pretty contradictory here. Or that it can't be used in the hedge, or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 11-29-2017, 06:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T06:29:18-08:00","id":1163526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163466#post1163466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Umm... Okay, three problems with the preview:<br /> 1) If you're going to require the Chronicles of Darkness Rulebook for basically all of your antagonist rules... then just say that in the introduction chapter and not waste massive amounts of page count on the &quot;repeating the Chronicles of Darkness Rulebook&quot; chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't. The Horror mechanics are reproduced in abbreviated form in the Hobgoblins section and all of the mechanics for Hedge ghosts are self-contained.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163506#post1163506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Errata-<br /> <br /> Whispers of Morning (the contract) calls out hedge ghosts as being in Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;She exists on a different frequency than creatures in Twilight&quot; doesn't seem to actually entail Hedge ghosts being in Twilight and the Dematerialize Numen has the same effect on Hedge ghosts in the Hedge as what happens to them when they leave it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-29-2017, 09:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T06:30:21-08:00","id":1163527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163457#post1163457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the game doesn't work because court contracts are so overwhelmingly powerful that not having the option to take them makes non-seasonal courts unusable, then the game is already broken. If you don't like the fact that not every single court is getting custom contracts made, that is totally fine. The suggestion that any other court is totally unsable because they don't have those contracts in the core rulebook and that it is wasted space, however, is disingenuous, panicky, and inflammatory. The key draw of Underhill for me was being able to create custom courts with ease. If I recall correctly, court contracts were never a part of that draft. Give-and-takes are easy to make, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> already has made some good suggestions for the Reykjav\u00edk freehold. I don't see what renders this chapter so unusable in your or Omega's minds. Frankly, of everything previewed so far, the settings and antagonists have been my favourite part. So again, if you don't like it, that's totally your prerogative. But at the same time, other people are allowed to love it and enjoy it. I for one do, And I've seen plenty of comments in the kick starter and on other forums that would seem to indicate I'm not alone. That means the space isn't wasted.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Court Contracts existed, we just didn't have them, except for the Honsu specific ones.<br /> <br /> I would really have prefered Court Contracts with more versitily between court systems, like Contracts of Emotion (court emotion) and the Contract of Talespinning was goung to be, so many Seasonal Court Contracts, they really pushed the Seaonal Courts hard, too hard IMO.<br /> <br /> Still unusable is too strong a word, its just they feel incomplete without even a couple of court contracts.<br /> <br /> I wasn't expecting the level of treatment the Seasonal Courts got, but even one or two Contracts with Court (or Society) variants would have been fine.<br /> <br /> Perhaps that will happen in the Companion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163526#post1163526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't. The Horror mechanics are reproduced in abbreviated form in the Hobgoblins section and all of the mechanics for Hedge ghosts are self-contained.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;She exists on a different frequency than creatures in Twilight&amp;quot; doesn't seem to actually entail Hedge ghosts being in Twilight and the Dematerialize Numen has the same effect on Hedge ghosts in the Hedge as what happens to them when they leave it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Read it again, several of the actual Hobgoblins depicted, such as Trod Troll and Briar Wolves have Dread Powers that AREN'T in the Changeling Corebook, but are in the CoD book, so to use them you need the CoD book.<br /> <br /> And it specifically meantions you can use that Dread Powers and Numina from the CoD corebook when building your own Hobgoblins, Huntsmen, and Numina, so you'll want the CoD corebook for things like blast.<br /> <br /> Still not a big deal, but it would be a good idea to offer the CoD corebook as an add on for $10 as someone else suggested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 11-29-2017, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T07:58:39-08:00","id":1163554,"title":"","content":"Kith and Kin's now available as an add-on, for those who aren't getting it automatically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T10:47:14-08:00","id":1163611,"title":"","content":"Adding my 2 cents, I think it's fine that the non-seasonal courts don't have full write-ups (at least in the CORE) considering how the word count goes. <br /> <br /> The reason is because we have all the tools necessary for anything we want now. We have full write-ups for the traditional and familiar seasonal courts (histories, give&amp;take, emotions, court contracts, fluff, mantle, ETC). And then we have the overview (history and Fluff) of nine other Court structures that are wildly different from eachother. <br /> <br /> In essence, the CORE gives us the tools to know how Courts can be different in different regions (with several examples) and what kind of stuff goes into one (with 4 examples per thing per seasonal court). It gives the ST/Troupe everything that they would need to make their own (in a shared creation creation way a la WW Pack rules). And if a Troupe wants to forego that and just make the seasonal freehold, they have that. <br /> <br /> The only thing we're missing is Tips &amp; Tricks/Guidelines for filling in the blanks which I suspect will be in the Summer preview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T11:15:14-08:00","id":1163622,"title":"","content":"Spring Novella is next. And the CoD corebook will likely end up an add on, but not this week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T11:19:51-08:00","id":1163623,"title":"","content":"Wait do &quot;traditional&quot; seasonal Courts have &quot;Harvests&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T13:20:40-08:00","id":1163675,"title":"","content":"I was doing a close reading of the pdfs so far and this passage keeps gnawing at me. <br /> <br /> &quot;The abductees are changed into faerie creatures to play particular roles in the True Fae\u2019s fantasies; these roles are Seemings, which correspond to fairy-tale character archetypes like the big, bad wolf (Beast), the ice queen (Fairest), the miracle worker (Wizened), and so on. Changelings turn the forms and powers forced on them against their fae Keepers, and escape from Arcadia.&quot;<br /> <br /> Does this suggest that every PC/NPC should be based on a specific fairy tale? I realize from a fair amount of personal research that the world of folklore is very broad, but it also means a bit of searching, if you are interested in a particular type of character. <br /> <br /> (However, to simply argue against myself, there is a vast difference between Andersen's <i>The Snow Queen</i> and Disney's <i>Frozen</i>, so there is probably a lot of theme and variation work available here.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5435-mhicwombat","name":"MhicWombat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T13:24:07-08:00","id":1163677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MhicWombat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163675#post1163675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was doing a close reading of the pdfs so far and this passage keeps gnawing at me. <br /> <br /> &quot;The abductees are changed into faerie creatures to play particular roles in the True Fae\u2019s fantasies; these roles are Seemings, which correspond to fairy-tale character archetypes like the big, bad wolf (Beast), the ice queen (Fairest), the miracle worker (Wizened), and so on. Changelings turn the forms and powers forced on them against their fae Keepers, and escape from Arcadia.&quot;<br /> <br /> Does this suggest that every PC/NPC should be based on a specific fairy tale? I realize from a fair amount of personal research that the world of folklore is very broad, but it also means a bit of searching, if you are interested in a particular type of character. <br /> <br /> (However, to simply argue against myself, there is a vast difference between Andersen's <i>The Snow Queen</i> and Disney's <i>Frozen</i>, so there is probably a lot of theme and variation work available here.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it implies broad archetypes with the potential to be specific fairy tales if desired. But the water Satyr example from a few pages back is a totally valid concept, and it is clearly not tied to one specific tale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T17:04:20-08:00","id":1163763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163527#post1163527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Read it again</div> </div> </div> </div>No amount of reading is going to make a double handful of Dread Powers and Numina with relatively self-explanatory names equate to &quot;basically all of [the game's] antagonist rules.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Relatedly: It's interesting to look at how the common mechanics for Hedge ghosts diverge from the regular ephemeral being mechanics; Manifestations boil down to equivalents of Materialize and Reach and have hard-locked narrative durations, the Glamour economy is broader and more use-dependent than the Essence economy, frailties are more numerous than bans and banes, and even the most powerful Hedge ghost doesn't have access to a Create Influence while outside the Hedge.<br /> <br /> Anyone else notice that the Huntsmen's perspective seems to be generally closer to how Wyrded interaction with the wider world operates compared to the more fickle and tricksy fae that is the stock-in-trade of fae beings as typically encountered?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T17:48:01-08:00","id":1163782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163763#post1163763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone else notice that the Huntsmen's perspective seems to be generally closer to how Wyrded interaction with the wider world operates compared to the more fickle and tricksy fae that is the stock-in-trade of fae beings as typically encountered?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would chalk it up to the Huntsmen being the denizens of an earlier, rawer Arcadia, with the temperament to match those simpler and more essential assumed paradigms. They are seemingly concerned with less convoluted things than the Gentry, as they predate them and don't partake fully of their rulebooks of promises and oath-bound magic. They're beings hearkening to a more primordial facet of the fantastic worlds between the real world and Arcadia, as I see it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T18:44:33-08:00","id":1163793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163763#post1163763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No amount of reading is going to make a double handful of Dread Powers and Numina with relatively self-explanatory names equate to &amp;quot;basically all of [the game's] antagonist rules.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Relatedly: It's interesting to look at how the common mechanics for Hedge ghosts diverge from the regular ephemeral being mechanics; Manifestations boil down to equivalents of Materialize and Reach and have hard-locked narrative durations, the Glamour economy is broader and more use-dependent than the Essence economy, frailties are more numerous than bans and banes, and even the most powerful Hedge ghost doesn't have access to a Create Influence while outside the Hedge.<br /> <br /> Anyone else notice that the Huntsmen's perspective seems to be generally closer to how Wyrded interaction with the wider world operates compared to the more fickle and tricksy fae that is the stock-in-trade of fae beings as typically encountered?</div> </div> </div> </div> Hedge Ghosts are interesting. And yeah, Glamour is piss easy for them to get compared to other Ephemerals, it's really their greatest strength compared to other Ephemerals. <br /> <br /> Still with reach and a friendly Changeling willing to open choice Hedge Gateways, they don't need to make an in person appearance, it really doesn't benifit them like Ghosts and Spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T20:53:56-08:00","id":1163810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lady Gray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163498#post1163498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think creating contracts is a fair thing to leave to the GM,.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, is one of the things I loath in a game when it ask me to play game developer for them. If i have to run a game I dislike to also having to think powers from the ground up, I have to run a game and i cant get people just to playtest if a power is broken or too weak. And i lack the knowledge on how to make one.<br /> <br /> If the game ask me to make fluff justifications for how and why the courts function? Sure that is reasonable. It doesnt require the knowledge in making mechanics or playtesting. <br /> <br /> Same thing with the seeming variants and only including 2 of for contract with the game telling me<br /> <br /> &quot;The Contracts below present two seeming benefits each, but Storytellers are encouraged to add their own.&quot;<br /> <br /> When some of the seeming benefits change radically the use of a contract. That road leads to things like &quot;Diplomat\u2019s Protection&quot; ( a very OP rote in mage). <br /> <br /> This isnt like games like FATE/AW in which tell you to make any effect because in the end they are just window dressing and just define when you get to roll the same diceroll or a +/- that only range from 1 to 5. <br /> <br /> This mechanics are more complex to balance. And to me the OPP not putting mechanics and dropping the responsability on me is something I feel is unreasonable, like buying an novel with its last chapter as blank pages with a pencil and message of &quot;let your imagination fly&quot;.<br /> <br /> I was full on board with Changeling 2nd from that i read and even the elements i dislike (Pledges, dreams and clarity) were easy enough to ignore/use 1st edition version. But that attitude that also came from Werewolf, is big drawback to me to the point I am considering dropping my pledge. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T21:05:06-08:00","id":1163813,"title":"","content":"I can't say I understand the depth of some posters' aversion to making their own rules. Tabletop for me has a strong, pervasive component of &quot;I want to do [X], what happens?&quot; &quot;...There aren't really rules for that, let me think.&quot; Like an almost every session component. The rules that are in the book are guidelines for common actions, and to give you a framework on how to handle the infinite universe of wild, crazy, boneheaded stunts players will want to attempt, because there's no possible way to cover every possible option. At all, let alone in exhaustive depth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T21:36:57-08:00","id":1163818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163813#post1163813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't say I understand the depth of some posters' aversion to making their own rules. Tabletop for me has a strong, pervasive component of &quot;I want to do [X], what happens?&quot; &quot;...There aren't really rules for that, let me think.&quot; Like an almost every session component. The rules that are in the book are guidelines for common actions, and to give you a framework on how to handle the infinite universe of wild, crazy, boneheaded stunts players will want to attempt, because there's no possible way to cover every possible option. At all, let alone in exhaustive depth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rules give a common ground in the playerbase, and it makes it easier on GMs who might not have experience enough with the system to feel comfortable to homebrew a lot. Having to homebrew things from nothing is actually one of the reasons I didn't play nWoD before 2e and why I can't really see myself ever running an Exalted game.<br /> <br /> Hopefully the rules to aid in the creation of courts, contracts, and kiths with be detailed enough to be suitable.... but it is rather weird that the setting-chapter's courts can't really be used out of the box because they lacking things like what emotions the courtiers get bonuses to feed on, how they work with bedlam, and how their Give and Take works because those are all important mechanics which are necessary for them to be used. Not having court-contracts is understandable, and you can easily run a game where no one takes any court contracts... But Emotion/Bedlam/Give &amp; Take are rather necessary mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T00:11:58-08:00","id":1163834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163818#post1163818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Emotion/Bedlam/Give &amp; Take are rather necessary mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, first, I'm also disappointed that there's been no indication of any guides on how to create-your-own, and that these mechanics aren't part of the write-up. Still hoping the guides'll be in the fourth preview, I suppose.<br /> <br /> But I think Emotion and Bedlam are pretty easy to hack. Unless I'm missing something, the Emotion bit merely gives the Changeling an extra Glamour upon harvest if it's favored. That's easy to houserule: every player just picks an emotion for themselves, preferably resonant with the Court they're joining, but I don't think it's a big deal to disassociate that with the Court. The settings courts generally seem to move this extra Glamour point into a non-emotion-based harvesting anyways (gain a point when X happens); I think that's a better general approach than requiring an emotion be pegged to a court, anyways: it's more flexible.<br /> <br /> The Bedlam bit has two parts: the Condition inflicted, and the fact that it's easier/harder to inflict a particular one based on Seasonal stuff. Harder to houserule, but I'd find it reasonable to just pick one of the four as a favored emotion, or to have the table agree on some set of Conditions that you're allowed to inflict. (This is the kind of thing you can tap the community for creating new emotion/condition pairs, though, too.) For easier/harder, the simplest solution is to say that you can get a +2 or +3 for a favored Condition, in return for -2/-3 for all the rest, or don't favor any. Sledgehammer approach to houseruling, but I think it'll do in a pinch.<br /> <br /> The Give&amp;Take you'd have to come up with whole cloth, though. Not impossible, but definitely some real work. I'd love to see the forum take a crack at coming up with those, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T00:18:20-08:00","id":1163835,"title":"","content":"I think part of the difficulty in understanding the complaint, is that you never have to make up Courts, or Contracts, or whatever. You can just use the fully flushed out stuff in the books. There's nothing wrong with playing a Seasonal Court game until someone else does the other sample Courts a full write-up.<br /> <br /> Nothing in CtL 2e so far (or the CofD 1e or 2e in general, or even Exalted for that matter) have ever said, &quot;you have to homebrew to use this game.&quot; Homebrew is certainly encouraged, and the games make it clear that the fully flushed out options presented are not meant to be the totality of the setting. But you never have to homebrew to use the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T00:31:11-08:00","id":1163837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163834#post1163834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, first, I'm also disappointed that there's been no indication of any guides on how to create-your-own, and that these mechanics aren't part of the write-up. Still hoping the guides'll be in the fourth preview, I suppose.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only chapter left to be previewed is the chapter which is described to be: &quot;Storytelling advice, including Chronicle-building, rules for creating new Courts and Contracts, and player safety advice.&quot; So that sort of information makes sense to have not appeared in the previews yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I think Emotion and Bedlam are pretty easy to hack. Unless I'm missing something, the Emotion bit merely gives the Changeling an extra Glamour upon harvest if it's favored. That's easy to houserule: every player just picks an emotion for themselves, preferably resonant with the Court they're joining, but I don't think it's a big deal to disassociate that with the Court. The settings courts generally seem to move this extra Glamour point into a non-emotion-based harvesting anyways (gain a point when X happens); I think that's a better general approach than requiring an emotion be pegged to a court, anyways: it's more flexible. </div> </div> </div>Except the courts which have been previewed don't seem to have any ties to any emotions, and it seems very odd that the &quot;default&quot; court system would be the only court system which follows the glamour rules that each court gives a bonus to feeding from a specific emotion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Bedlam bit has two parts: the Condition inflicted, and the fact that it's easier/harder to inflict a particular one based on Seasonal stuff. Harder to houserule, but I'd find it reasonable to just pick one of the four as a favored emotion, or to have the table agree on some set of Conditions that you're allowed to inflict. (This is the kind of thing you can tap the community for creating new emotion/condition pairs, though, too.) For easier/harder, the simplest solution is to say that you can get a +2 or +3 for a favored Condition, in return for -2/-3 for all the rest, or don't favor any. Sledgehammer approach to houseruling, but I think it'll do in a pinch. </div> </div> </div>Needing to make up sets conditions to use any of the premade settings is the exact sort of thing for why I think the amount of material they provided isn't enough, and it'd be pretty dumb to just use one of the four considering it would often be a giant stretch to justify them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Give&amp;Take you'd have to come up with whole cloth, though. Not impossible, but definitely some real work. I'd love to see the forum take a crack at coming up with those, though. </div> </div> </div>No one is suggesting it's impossible, I'm suggesting it's dumb to ignore something which matters so much to how a freehold functions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163835#post1163835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think part of the difficulty in understanding the complaint, is that you never have to make up Courts, or Contracts, or whatever. You can just use the fully flushed out stuff in the books. There's nothing wrong with playing a Seasonal Court game until someone else does the other sample Courts a full write-up.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if I want to run a game which isn't in America or Europe....?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 11-30-2017, 03:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T00:32:09-08:00","id":1163838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163810#post1163810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree, is one of the things I loath in a game when it ask me to play game developer for them. If i have to run a game I dislike to also having to think powers from the ground up, I have to run a game and i cant get people just to playtest if a power is broken or too weak. And i lack the knowledge on how to make one.<br /> <br /> If the game ask me to make fluff justifications for how and why the courts function? Sure that is reasonable. It doesnt require the knowledge in making mechanics or playtesting. <br /> <br /> Same thing with the seeming variants and only including 2 of for contract with the game telling me<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;The Contracts below present two seeming benefits each, but Storytellers are encouraged to add their own.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> When some of the seeming benefits change radically the use of a contract. That road leads to things like &amp;quot;Diplomat\u2019s Protection&amp;quot; ( a very OP rote in mage). <br /> <br /> This isnt like games like FATE/AW in which tell you to make any effect because in the end they are just window dressing and just define when you get to roll the same diceroll or a +/- that only range from 1 to 5. <br /> <br /> This mechanics are more complex to balance. And to me the OPP not putting mechanics and dropping the responsability on me is something I feel is unreasonable, like buying an novel with its last chapter as blank pages with a pencil and message of &amp;quot;let your imagination fly&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> I was full on board with Changeling 2nd from that i read and even the elements i dislike (Pledges, dreams and clarity) were easy enough to ignore/use 1st edition version. But that attitude that also came from Werewolf, is big drawback to me to the point I am considering dropping my pledge. </div> </div> </div> </div> Let's not be hasty, this may get addressed in the companion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T00:59:35-08:00","id":1163841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163837#post1163837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if I want to run a game which isn't in America or Europe....?</div> </div> </div> </div>Set it somewhere the Seasonal Courts make sense, or reskin them but keep their mechanics so you don't have to homebrew them, etc.<br /> <br /> Last time I checked, a rather large part of Asia is in the northern temperate zone to have the same default four seasons as (most of) Europe, Canada, and the US. Chile, Argentina, and a few other parts of South America are in the southern band, as is the southern tip of South Africa, Australia, and most of New Zealand. Or screw local weather and decide a place has been Westernized enough that people honor the four seasons strongly enough there that the Seasonal Courts work as mystical entities even though the local scientific climates don't operate that way. You can even use that for some story hooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T01:33:43-08:00","id":1163844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MhicWombat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163675#post1163675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does this suggest that every PC/NPC should be based on a specific fairy tale? I realize from a fair amount of personal research that the world of folklore is very broad, but it also means a bit of searching, if you are interested in a particular type of character.</div> </div> </div> </div> Nah. The role your Keeper puts you in can be a fairy tale, or it could be as a gladiator, to a garden statue. People tend towards fairy tale roles just because, well, that's kinda what the game is about. But it really could be anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T02:51:17-08:00","id":1163852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163837#post1163837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except the courts which have been previewed don't seem to have any ties to any emotions, and it seems very odd that the &quot;default&quot; court system would be the only court system which follows the glamour rules that each court gives a bonus to feeding from a specific emotion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that Glamour is harvested from emotion, it does make sense that each court would give a bonus to feeding from emotion. The conditions a courtier gains a free glamour from does work as a hint for what emotion they work on.<br /> <br /> For the sake of example: the Society of Morning gains a glamour by gaining knowledge through reckless pursuit. That sounds like Giddiness/Excitement to me, and the mantle benefits work well with that; being giddy to know something new, or to gossip with others. The Society of Day gains one by resolving a conflict, and its mantle benefits grant bonuses to basically improve and repair items or relationships, which to me speaks of Pride, the ego that <i>you</i> are the one to solve these problems that others could/do not (though Irritation works too). The Society of Night gains a glamour from following a hunt to its logical conclusion and its mantle benefits solving, deliberating or dealing with problems; Stubbornness springs to mind, though that doesn't sound entirely like an emotion.<br /> <br /> There are other interpretations, but emotions can be found in both the actions that grant glamour and what the mantle benefits are too.<br /> <br /> ...hmm, this actually gave me some insight into how to improve my own freehold currently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T03:23:00-08:00","id":1163854,"title":"","content":"On the matter of Courts:<br /> <br /> Its plain to see that Seasonal is not only the default, its very heavily built into the game's default assumptions to the point of influencing how Seemings work. Given the sheer amount of effort to create a new Court - above and beyond pretty much any other gameline as far as I can tell - its inevitable that a number of people are going to be unhappy with the presentation. Especially when each setting has a unique court system that can't be used without &quot;fixing&quot; them.<br /> <br /> I personally don't think its asking for too much to have these example settings we have to be playable. With Vampire, the &quot;new&quot; covenants in the equivalent chapter were all playable, if mechanically lite; and that's not counting the settings that tweaked the existing Covenants in new ways, no mechanical changes needed. I could start up a game using any of those settings with no problem. With Werewolf and Mage, you kept the default 5 tribes/orders. Demon, Promethean and Beast settings don't rely on their y-axis at all, or any other mechanics. Changeling, however, is presenting each setting with an unique court system that you need to sit down and patch to make functional at the base.<br /> <br /> Right now, we have this... dissonance going on. The setting chapter is presenting all these options and different courts... that will very likely never be used by the overwhelming majority of games. The default is Seasonal. Making new takes a lot of effort, prohibitively so for what I imagine is the vast majority of changeling gamers. Realistically expecting <br /> <br /> And I'm going to be clear on this point. Court Contracts are necessary for many games. We can talk a big game about how you don't <i>need</i> Court Contracts, but I can tell you from personal experience that many players find that to be quite dissatisfying. Gamers tend to like fun powers. Its a thing. If the powers aren't there, the players will, on average, have less fun. Based on my personal experience and what I've heard from other STs, and even other GMs in other games, this seems to hold true. Yes, ideally, you don't need the powers or mechanics to have fun, but from what I've seen and heard, it absolutely adds to the game for a large number of people. <br /> <br /> Earlier, someone called the different setting chapter useless. I'm not going to go that far; I'm sure that some people will find them inspirational for something (I'm not one of them), but I can't help but feel that we would be far better served by showing the Seasonal Courts in these settings, rather than some unplayable Court systems. Barring a future book that makes these, or other, Courts playable, the majority of games are going to be using Seasonal, and I think it would have been far more helpful to showcase how these four Courts change depending on where you go. Like... a Vegas game has the four Courts identify with suits of cards, and they weave rituals of poker and blackjack games into their Season. I did that back in 1e, and it was fun.<br /> <br /> I can completely understand how a number of people feel upset over this. It can feel almost deceptive. See, you can have any Court system you want. Its easy. You just need to write this up, and then... oh, wait, forgot all the other bits. And your players would like Contracts. And... and it just keeps building until it feels impossible to get done. Or literally becomes impossible, because we're busy people who want to have fun, not do hours worth of homework in order to have fun, and we need to socialize with our friends and family. <br /> <br /> Personally, I think we just all have to step back from this issue. Its unfortunate, but people are going to have to accept that Changeling is the game of Seasonal Courts. That may change in the future, or with massive amounts of homebrew material (which might put off groups as well, so that's another factor to consider), but right now, I feel that is our only realistic option at this given point in time. It is what it is. Deny it, get mad, try to bargain, get depressed, whatever it takes, but in the end, its something we either have to accept, or just leave the game behind.<br /> <br /> Instead, we can all grumble about my pet peeve with the material - the lack of mirror monsters and dream critters! Yay! ((Please pause for coughing and crickets)) Jokes aside, I feel like I'm going to need to start working up some rules for mirror'd parts of the hedge, as well as consider what kind of critters inhabit these areas. Hobs don't quite fit, in my opinion, for various reasons, and I'm not quite sure of my grasp of hedge ghosts yet. Like, I can grok strix, spirits, regular ghosts and angels. All of them have quirks and abilities and motivations that tie into how they operate and how they get essence. I'm not quite sure on what hedge ghosts do yet - they feel just kinda... there.<br /> <br /> Also, I wonder if Mirror Space should use regular hedge rules, or if it needs its own quirks like the Dreaming Roads do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T04:21:15-08:00","id":1163859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163763#post1163763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No amount of reading is going to make a double handful of Dread Powers and Numina with relatively self-explanatory names equate to &quot;basically all of [the game's] antagonist rules.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, if it's not been done already - It sounds like the sort of thing that should be brought to the designers attention. Either include the powers or remove them from the NPCs. It's not that difficult. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T07:15:02-08:00","id":1163900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163835#post1163835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think part of the difficulty in understanding the complaint, is that you never have to make up Courts, or Contracts, or whatever. You can just use the fully flushed out stuff in the books. There's nothing wrong with playing a Seasonal Court game until someone else does the other sample Courts a full write-up.<br /> <br /> Nothing in CtL 2e so far (or the CofD 1e or 2e in general, or even Exalted for that matter) have ever said, &quot;you have to homebrew to use this game.&quot; Homebrew is certainly encouraged, and the games make it clear that the fully flushed out options presented are not meant to be the totality of the setting. But you never have to homebrew to use the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demon requires homebrew to design interlocks for each character. It's recommended that the Storyteller design three unique powers for every player character very early on so they can start guessing which embeds are part of the cipher sequence. I agree that changeling doesn't seem to require homebrew rules to fill in any gaps though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T07:15:11-08:00","id":1163901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163854#post1163854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </d