e players will, on average, have less fun. Based on my personal experience and what I've heard from other STs, and even other GMs in other games, this seems to hold true. Yes, ideally, you don't need the powers or mechanics to have fun, but from what I've seen and heard, it absolutely adds to the game for a large number of people. <br /> <br /> Earlier, someone called the different setting chapter useless. I'm not going to go that far; I'm sure that some people will find them inspirational for something (I'm not one of them), but I can't help but feel that we would be far better served by showing the Seasonal Courts in these settings, rather than some unplayable Court systems. Barring a future book that makes these, or other, Courts playable, the majority of games are going to be using Seasonal, and I think it would have been far more helpful to showcase how these four Courts change depending on where you go. Like... a Vegas game has the four Courts identify with suits of cards, and they weave rituals of poker and blackjack games into their Season. I did that back in 1e, and it was fun.<br /> <br /> I can completely understand how a number of people feel upset over this. It can feel almost deceptive. See, you can have any Court system you want. Its easy. You just need to write this up, and then... oh, wait, forgot all the other bits. And your players would like Contracts. And... and it just keeps building until it feels impossible to get done. Or literally becomes impossible, because we're busy people who want to have fun, not do hours worth of homework in order to have fun, and we need to socialize with our friends and family. <br /> <br /> Personally, I think we just all have to step back from this issue. Its unfortunate, but people are going to have to accept that Changeling is the game of Seasonal Courts. That may change in the future, or with massive amounts of homebrew material (which might put off groups as well, so that's another factor to consider), but right now, I feel that is our only realistic option at this given point in time. It is what it is. Deny it, get mad, try to bargain, get depressed, whatever it takes, but in the end, its something we either have to accept, or just leave the game behind.<br /> <br /> Instead, we can all grumble about my pet peeve with the material - the lack of mirror monsters and dream critters! Yay! ((Please pause for coughing and crickets)) Jokes aside, I feel like I'm going to need to start working up some rules for mirror'd parts of the hedge, as well as consider what kind of critters inhabit these areas. Hobs don't quite fit, in my opinion, for various reasons, and I'm not quite sure of my grasp of hedge ghosts yet. Like, I can grok strix, spirits, regular ghosts and angels. All of them have quirks and abilities and motivations that tie into how they operate and how they get essence. I'm not quite sure on what hedge ghosts do yet - they feel just kinda... there.<br /> <br /> Also, I wonder if Mirror Space should use regular hedge rules, or if it needs its own quirks like the Dreaming Roads do?</div> </div> </div> </div> There are dream critters, Important Eidolons, Extra Eidolons, living Props, Hedge Ghosts (some Hedge Ghosts could have their origins in Dream Bastions or prefer to live in them).<br /> <br /> Then there are Hobgoblins with Dream Steps contract, Huntsmen, and True Fae visiting the dreams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T08:13:18-08:00","id":1163928,"title":"","content":"I would have been fine with Seasonal Courts being treated as default by the rules if discussion before hand didn't suggest otherwise. I was really looking forward for making my own Courts but amount of work it takes now if just disheartening.<br /> Denying players access to Seasonal Contracts is tough, especially so if I have to try to create my own collection to replace them!<br /> Bedlam Rules are aggressively non-compatible with non-Seasonal Courts, it feels like they were copied full cloth from 1st edition without consideration for more fluid Court system.<br /> <br /> It's incredibly frustrating. I can totally work with Season Courts, I even like them, but I pledged my money and hyped for 2e while being promised flexible and easy to implement custom Court rules. 1st, 2nd, and 3rd Manuscript Previews simply don't deliver on this, and I am filling rather pessimistic about Custom Court Rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":". 11-30-2017, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T08:32:37-08:00","id":1163932,"title":"","content":"aaaand I'm a backer. I had to get a debt card especially for this event, but it does looks like it would worth the hassle :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T08:38:47-08:00","id":1163933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163928#post1163928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that Seasonal Courts don't have Harvests</div> </div> </div> </div>They're in the Mantle Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T08:46:22-08:00","id":1163938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163933#post1163933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're in the Mantle Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I stand corrected. The difference in formatting was bit misleading. Thank you. I shall edit my reply immediately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T08:51:49-08:00","id":1163940,"title":"","content":"I have to confess that I really can't see the difficulty in creating new court contracts as needed, or to borrow as appropriate from any of the existing Arcadian/Seasonal/Goblin contracts.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm not seeing some obvious problem with a scenario like &quot;I'm playing a Night Society assassin, so can I take this Mirror power and this Winter one as court contracts? And can I make a new contract that lets me create a dagger out of shadows?&quot; The answer would be &quot;Sure,&quot; or maybe &quot;I'm concerned the new contract is too easy to use. Let's make the Loophole one bashing damage of your own spilled blood left on the scene.&quot;<br /> <br /> The principle, I do understand. Big chunks of the world don't have four seasons. But it seems like people are worried about a workload that isn't going to be much of anything, once actual play starts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13580-hsienfan","name":"Hsienfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T09:05:55-08:00","id":1163948,"title":"","content":"Also, thinking about the Give &amp; Take of the Dragon Court:<br /> <br /> As long as the three societies are &quot;in harmony&quot; (i.e. not in open conflict of any kind), then the Gentry are forced to be polite in the human world of Hong Kong. No kidnapping, no wanton brutality... This doesn't apply in the Hedge, and it's arguable how much Societal infiltration from the mainland might eventually count as &quot;disharmony.&quot;<br /> <br /> Just one idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13580-hsienfan","name":"Hsienfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T09:30:14-08:00","id":1163955,"title":"","content":"Yeah. the existing Seasonal Contracts are incredibly easy to reskin to reflect the themes of your custom courts. Beside the flowery prose describing the effect, the only other factor that really flavors the mechanics is the Loophole. So yeah, Contracts are not really a big thing for me. I'd just like to see Crowns detailed. Give and Take would be cool too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T09:36:40-08:00","id":1163957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hsienfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163940#post1163940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm not seeing some obvious problem with a scenario like &quot;I'm playing a Night Society assassin, so can I take this Mirror power and this Winter one as court contracts? And can I make a new contract that lets me create a dagger out of shadows?&quot; The answer would be &quot;Sure,&quot; or maybe &quot;I'm concerned the new contract is too easy to use. Let's make the Loophole one bashing damage of your own spilled blood left on the scene.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Why bashing damage? Why not lethal? Only a dagger or other weapons allowed? Can i make a shadowgun? Etc etc etc. That kind of question that are a drag to create your own mechanics. Especially when you don't have a group at your beck and call to waste time playtesting. Or wasting time retconning because you accidentally made &quot;Diplomatic immunity: The contract&quot;. I get some people don't care about mechanics and just rule 0 everything. But others do care about having mechanics for stuff, that was playtested and made by people whose job was to make it. Otherwise, if the game asks me to make so many mechanics why I am paying for a 200+ book? I might as well play freeform theater with my friends and save me shipping cost. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163835#post1163835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing in CtL 2e so far (or the CofD 1e or 2e in general, or even Exalted for that matter) have ever said, &quot;you have to homebrew to use this game.&quot; Homebrew is certainly encouraged, and the games make it clear that the fully flushed out options presented are not meant to be the totality of the setting. But you never have to homebrew to use the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't certainly &quot;have to do anything&quot; but if the game feels incomplete because of lack of contract, seeming benefits for regalias, etc. Then complaining that the game &quot;suggest me to homebrew&quot; is a valid complaint. And then there are rules actually missing like tokens. Sure we got rules for how an object becomes a token but not rules on how do design powers for them. So we end up with using only the barebones examples. <br /> <br /> Which begs the question if I am under no &quot;obligation&quot; to make homebrew. Then whats the point of giving me rules for how an object transforms into a Token when I just have to pick one of the list. Might as well just ask the player to spend XP and no question asked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T09:40:13-08:00","id":1163958,"title":"","content":"So i guess i'm in the middle of the opinions about contracts and new courts.<br /> Right now i feel it is too daunting (for me) to create my own court contract + court mantle merit.<br /> But honestly i feel that with a few examples i will more comfortable. And it appears that this will be in the next chapter to be shown from what i understand.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T10:48:40-08:00","id":1163979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163957#post1163957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why bashing damage? Why not lethal? Only a dagger or other weapons allowed? Can i make a shadowgun? Etc etc etc. That kind of question that are a drag to create your own mechanics. Especially when you don't have a group at your beck and call to waste time playtesting. Or wasting time retconning because you accidentally made &quot;Diplomatic immunity: The contract&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually find that kind of tinkering fun, especially when your player gets something new and shiny that they're happy with. This sounds like a difference in perspective, which I won't argue (what you're saying is 100% legitimate), but there is one thing...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I get some people don't care about mechanics and just rule 0 everything. But others do care about having mechanics for stuff, that was playtested and made by people whose job was to make it. Otherwise, if the game asks me to make so many mechanics why I am paying for a 200+ book? I might as well play freeform theater with my friends and save me shipping cost. </div> </div> </div>I think we should wait for the storytelling chapter in next week's preview, and the promised guidelines to build your own contracts and courts. I suspect they'll be better than Rule Zero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13580-hsienfan","name":"Hsienfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T10:55:58-08:00","id":1163984,"title":"","content":"While I agree that different courts might be a problem, I think the Storytelling section will likely have a juice section. I could tell certain themes among all of the mantle effects, so those won't be hard to homebrew. It shouldn't be hard to pick an Emotion for a given Court, and then a Condition. Mages hafta make their own Aura, so the ST has it slightly easier. Really, the biggest toughie will be Give and Take, Contracts, and to a lesser degree Crown effects. However, I think that they do indeed cover that, I just hope it has the wordcount it needed.<br /> <br /> My biggest concern so far, besides the beaten dead horse that is the Kiths, which is solved by the Kith and Kin stuff... is the Hobgoblin issue. I like how theyre designed, but I bought the God Machine Chronicle book. I didn't get the Chronicles of Darkness. And if MOST of chronicles of darkness is the same as God Machine Chronicle, AND reprinted in the Changeling book.. Im wincing at the idea I'd have to buy the whole CofD core JUST to be able to interpret and design Hobgoblins. I mean, as it is right now, I might RARELY bust out a hobgoblin, and MORE often just throw Hedge Ghosts at my players. If I already have to buy the CofD core book just for the Dread Powers, why reprint it in the Changeling book? You can easily say &quot;Buy the corebook&quot; like 1e, and then get a LOT of extra wordcount for Changeling.. or edit out something. Like.. the 12 kiths.<br /> <br /> Its kind of the same situation with them, really. An easy solution would be to take Kiths out of the core book, like what was done with Bloodlines. Mention that they exist, make them a second Z splat that can develop through play and exploring, shift all the kiths into the Supplement, and use that wordcount for the Dread Powers. Cuz those, as it stands, are more handy than the few Kiths we have, when most of us will be waiting for the Kith and Kin stuff to even finish our characters. At least as a Z splat, optional, but powerful, we won't feel so incomplete. We'll just have to get used to the Vampire//Promethean model and define our changeling with a vague X and Y and their powers, and then &quot;double down&quot; on our specific faeness with the Kith.<br /> <br /> Similarly, if the Example Courts arent gonna have an Emotion, or Contracts, or a Crown etc.. why spend wordcount on the Mantle? That could also be switched into the supplement, if the dread powers need too much word count. Put various Courts in the supplement, with Mantle, Emotion, Contracts, Crown, Give and Take, etc. I don't think anyone would mind, especially since the backers will have access to that info easily enough from the previews, and actual buyers AFTER the kickstarter are gonna be seriously lacking in a lot of setting elements.<br /> <br /> I really think info on Dread Powers right now is more valuable than the incomplete information we have on the optional Courts and the Kiths, and those things, as it stands, are better explored in supplements than the core. I mean, what are people gonna think if they just have the Core with its 12 kiths, and then LATER discover hundreds or at least dozens of premade, prebalanced, preexplained Kiths?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T11:10:39-08:00","id":1163988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hsienfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1163979#post1163979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we should wait for the storytelling chapter in next week's preview, and the promised guidelines to build your own contracts and courts. I suspect they'll be better than Rule Zero.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really hope so but the lacking rules for token doesnt fill me with hope. I really hope I am proven wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T12:14:36-08:00","id":1164008,"title":"","content":"Just wanted to say to the development/creative team that this is seriously a great game/book. I'm truly excited to run this for a group and personally, I enjoy every part of it. I know a lot has been said about the number of kiths, the length of fluff for the current kiths, etc. etc. however, I find it perfect. For myself, the &quot;fluff&quot; allows me to really picture and understand what it is I am looking at. It allows me to start getting a game ready, a character ready, an antagonist ready, and what have you. So. All that said, thank you all for giving us yet <b>another</b> insanely awesome game!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Kinda I want to&quot; - Trent Reznor<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent.ftpa1-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/27973518_2040009129348529_5319855605701568493_n.jpg?oh=9c85c5c9d4a0769a1249ea2f3e62ca43&amp;oe=5B002AA5\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12143-eldritchminister","name":"EldritchMinister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T12:18:14-08:00","id":1164011,"title":"","content":"Over the years, and with multiple systems, I have had fun introducing many people to rpg. One of my nieces recently joined her first game ... much to her mother's consternation. <br /> <br /> What I have seen is that the clearer the core rule presentation, the easier it is for players to pick up. I think this is why I am currently happy with the Seasonal Courts. I know when next I run CtL I will have at least one neophyte player. This makes for a decent, clear jumping off point that a new player can grasp quickly.<br /> <br /> For my own game with veteran players, however, U will probably come up with my own Courts. Heck, I've got a year plus to plan this (due to current gaming). That should give me enough lead time to triangulate between the old rules, the Underhill suggestions, and the new rules to come up with something appropriate to Las Vegas (where they want the game set) and that does not simply devolve to the Four Suits (which I could handle simply as a reskinning of the Seasons). I mean, there is so much more to Vegas than the Strip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5435-mhicwombat","name":"MhicWombat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T12:19:24-08:00","id":1164012,"title":"","content":"Yeah, in spite of the fact I shouldn't, I really WANT to run a game of this for friends! (Well, shouldn't till the game I'm planning for the new year starts and has gone on for at least a WHILE.) Superb stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T13:12:21-08:00","id":1164034,"title":"","content":"...no really, can we put a lid on &quot;To homebrew or not to homebrew&quot; until the rules are actually out? As is it feels like needless panicking.<br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Next stretch goal is up. At $119k, CtL dice will be added to the Onyx Dice app.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T13:31:34-08:00","id":1164040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1164034#post1164034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...no really, can we put a lid on &quot;To homebrew or not to homebrew&quot; until the rules are actually out? As is it feels like needless panicking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will the next preview contain rules for Token then? Or rules for the missing seeming blessings for the regalias?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T15:14:27-08:00","id":1164081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1164040#post1164040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Will the next preview contain rules for Token then? Or rules for the missing seeming blessings for the regalias?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this shall suffic