oin Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T19:47:19-08:00","id":1164155,"title":"","content":"And we go to the Sping Novella at $117k - as we are past it, we look now for the Changeling: The Lost D10 For OnyxDice App. Backers with at least <b>CtL</b> 2E PDF tier ( i.e. $25+ ) will get the new, shiny e-dice for free. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T20:28:00-08:00","id":1164166,"title":"","content":"And the next tier is already up: <br /> <br /> At $123k, there will be a CtL2 Jumpstart made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T09:09:37-08:00","id":1164295,"title":"","content":"Well, I really hope the last three Kith and Kin stretch goals are soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T09:40:26-08:00","id":1164302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>E11even-E11even</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1164295#post1164295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I really hope the last three Kith and Kin stretch goals are soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, I do hope those will come sooner rather than later.<br /> <br /> But I also want to agree with the Eldritch Minister in saying that, outside of my last post's points, I really adore this version. It is amazing. Clarity really feels like the underhill's traumatic feel, but clarified (heh) it somewhat. Each of the courts now feels both evocative AND useful. Mantle isn't just balanced, it's awesome. Five dots in mantle almost feels more epic than the crown itself, which rightly feels more like a sixth dot of mantle. <br /> <br /> And the Hedge. Omg, the Hedge. I can't even put into words how amazing that is. The Skein becoming the Dreaming Roads.. The Mirror World... Hedge Ghosts.. the streamlining of hedge navigation into an epic chase against the Hedge's attention. Just.. everything. The way it feels Narnia, Wonderland, Fantasia etc isn't your arcadian memories but rather the Hedge.. just wow. That alone makes it feel so much more fairytale. <br /> <br /> And yet, they introduced many elements of owod changeling. There is more childlikeness and childishness. There is more make believe and fantasy, alongside of gameplaying and system gaming. Making bridgeburners more obviously Dauntain/autumn people was a BRILLIANT move. <br /> killing dreams and creativity... seriously, kudos to whoever made that change, it made bridgeburners vastly more interesting to me. I never used them before, and I can't wait to use them.<br /> <br /> I'm on the same page as Sean. The nostalgia reminds me of the days (when we called him Arc XD) when the game first came out and we were all wild eyed and inspired. When it inspired so many creative juices. It's a great sign that almost all of everyone's issues with it so far boil down to word count. People's doubts and fears about the changes are mostly gone, and almost every issue will be solved by the companion book, because we all want MORE. We love it, and each of us has different ideas about what was left out that shouldn't have been, but.. that's an amazing sign. While some have some gripes about certain things, it looked like most of them knew the solution already. Most of us grok everything, and like a glamour addict, need a bigger fix XD<br /> <br /> Seriously, huge kudos and mad respect to the team. It's bloody BRILLIANT and beautifully mad. I can't wait to solve my billing and bump up my pledge. I can't wait to get the colorful and prestige changeling book we all wanted (comparing green and white 1e versus dreaming 20 almost hurts sometimes)...I can't wait for the Durance to be over.<br /> <br /> Ps. Please tell me some of the extra art budget was/will be spent on Stephanie Pui-Mun Law or Melissa Uran. Id give up an Icon to get more of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":935,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","user":"Cleverest of Things","date":".  My never ending battle with autocorrect 12-01-2017, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T10:49:25-08:00","id":1164322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1164302#post1164302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed, I do hope those will come sooner rather than later.<br /> <br /> But I also want to agree with the Eldritch Minister in saying that, outside of my last post's points, I really adore this version. It is amazing. Clarity really feels like the underhill's traumatic feel, but clarified (heh) it somewhat. Each of the courts now feels both evocative AND useful. Mantle isn't just balanced, it's awesome. Five dots in mantle almost feels more epic than the crown itself, which rightly feels more like a sixth dot of mantle. <br /> <br /> And the Hedge. Omg, the Hedge. I can't even put into words how amazing that is. The Skein becoming the Dreaming Roads.. The Mirror World... Hedge Ghosts.. the streamlining of hedge navigation into an epic chase against the Hedge's attention. Just.. everything. The way it feels Narnia, Wonderland, Fantasia etc isn't your arcadian memories but rather the Hedge.. just wow. That alone makes it feel so much more fairytale. <br /> <br /> And yet, they introduced many elements of owod changeling. There is more childlikeness and childishness. There is more make believe and fantasy, alongside of gameplaying and system gaming. Making bridgeburners more obviously Dauntain/autumn people was a BRILLIANT move. <br /> killing dreams and creativity... seriously, kudos to whoever made that change, it made bridgeburners vastly more interesting to me. I never used them before, and I can't wait to use them.<br /> <br /> I'm on the same page as Sean. The nostalgia reminds me of the days (when we called him Arc XD) when the game first came out and we were all wild eyed and inspired. When it inspired so many creative juices. It's a great sign that almost all of everyone's issues with it so far boil down to word count. People's doubts and fears about the changes are mostly gone, and almost every issue will be solved by the companion book, because we all want MORE. We love it, and each of us has different ideas about what was left out that shouldn't have been, but.. that's an amazing sign. While some have some gripes about certain things, it looked like most of them knew the solution already. Most of us grok everything, and like a glamour addict, need a bigger fix XD<br /> <br /> Seriously, huge kudos and mad respect to the team. It's bloody BRILLIANT and beautifully mad. I can't wait to solve my billing and bump up my pledge. I can't wait to get the colorful and prestige changeling book we all wanted (comparing green and white 1e versus dreaming 20 almost hurts sometimes)...I can't wait for the Durance to be over.<br /> <br /> Ps. Please tell me some of the extra art budget was/will be spent on Stephanie Pui-Mun Law or Melissa Uran. Id give up an Icon to get more of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>My issue with this edition isn't the quality of the content, but the quantity. I also like a lot of what I've read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T11:32:14-08:00","id":1164342,"title":"","content":"Holy Crap, I got super busy at work and missed that there's a Jumpstart coming soon in the Stretch Goals! That will make it stupid easy to run something at the local game store or with my co-workers to gaege interest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T12:12:34-08:00","id":1164354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>E11even-E11even</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1164322#post1164322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My issue with this edition isn't the quality of the content, but the quantity. I also like a lot of what I've read.</div> </div> </div> </div>Last I checked, isn't &quot;quality over quantity&quot; a thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T13:35:10-08:00","id":1164372,"title":"","content":"I may have already missed this part of the discussion, but do some of the changes to the kiths previewed seem strikingly different from anything in other games and in some cases needing a bit more information (looking at you Gristlegrinder). I hope that they will provide more information to clarify or maybe some tweeks to this before people just run around gulping down everything in sight.<br /> <br /> Also, some of the concepts seem muddled to me.<br /> <br /> Example: Ogres are creatures of violence. They escaped the hedge by forcing themselves on other things or other beings. They have been shaped by the violence inflicted on them sure, but they are typified by the fact that they used violence (and probably still use it) and it marked them. So why then is their Affinity Contract the Shield? I mean sure Ogres are probably tough but it is by inflicting their will on the resistant or the unwilling that they are defined, so wouldn't Sword make more sense?<br /> <br /> Now I am still super excited about this project and I am backing it, but there are parts of this I wish I understood more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10263-azrenogre","name":"AzrenOgre","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T13:39:38-08:00","id":1164375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1164354#post1164354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Last I checked, isn't &amp;quot;quality over quantity&amp;quot; a thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>If by thing, you mean clever saying, then yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T13:57:22-08:00","id":1164379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1164302#post1164302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm on the same page as Sean. The nostalgia reminds me of the days (when we called him Arc XD)</div> </div> </div> </div>I still by and large expect most people to call me Arc, as a random aside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T14:34:16-08:00","id":1164392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1164302#post1164302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ps. Please tell me some of the extra art budget was/will be spent on Stephanie Pui-Mun Law or Melissa Uran. Id give up an Icon to get more of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stephanie Law is a great artist and a great person, in general. I am totally cool with her getting her feet back into Changeling. However, I sincerely hope that we keep Melissa Uran far enough away from Changeling. I do not want anime/manga in my Changeling. She already dominates my Changeling: The Dreaming and Exalted collection. However, if we can get Tony DiTerlizzi back ... i'll be so happy!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T16:55:39-08:00","id":1164427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firefly Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1164392#post1164392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stephanie Law is a great artist and a great person, in general. I am totally cool with her getting her feet back into Changeling. However, I sincerely hope that we keep Melissa Uran far enough away from Changeling. I do not want anime/manga in my Changeling. She already dominates my Changeling: The Dreaming and Exalted collection. However, if we can get Tony DiTerlizzi back ... i'll be so happy!</div> </div> </div> </div>DiTerlizzi's work is fantastic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T17:12:24-08:00","id":1164431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1164166#post1164166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the next tier is already up: <br /> <br /> At $123k, there will be a CtL2 Jumpstart made.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really hope they reach this goal, a quick start version of the rules is a fundamental thing. It allows new players/dms to test the game without feeling they gotta make a huge investment in buying/reading the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T17:21:41-08:00","id":1164432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1164431#post1164431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really hope they reach this goal, a quick start version of the rules is a fundamental thing. It allows new players/dms to test the game without feeling they gotta make a huge investment in buying/reading the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's pretty no chance this goal won't be hit in the next 36 hours, let alone the rest of the campaign. I think we're pretty safe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T18:19:01-08:00","id":1164442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1164431#post1164431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really hope they reach this goal, a quick start version of the rules is a fundamental thing. It allows new players/dms to test the game without feeling they gotta make a huge investment in buying/reading the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>It almost a certainty they will they are almost to $121,000, so it will be another day or two and it will be reached. I bet another Kith and Kin Section will be next. <br /> <br /> So far we have 3/4 (75%) of the Novellas<br /> 3/6 of the Kith and Kin additional chapters. <br /> Digital Dice<br /> 2 chapters to the Changeling Companion (Entitlements and Freeholds). <br /> A +$15 Kith and Kin add on. <br /> Fear Makers Promise and Equinox Road added to Arcadian Memories Bundle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T18:20:02-08:00","id":1164443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1164302#post1164302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet, they introduced many elements of owod changeling. There is more childlikeness and childishness. There is more make believe and fantasy, alongside of gameplaying and system gaming. Making bridgeburners more obviously Dauntain/autumn people was a BRILLIANT move.<br /> killing dreams and creativity... seriously, kudos to whoever made that change, it made bridgeburners vastly more interesting to me. I never used them before, and I can't wait to use them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I've wondered about that.<br /> <br /> Looking through C20, I get the impression that there was a bigger push to have more elements from CtL to make it similar. Oaths overall being a more fleshed out sub-system when it previously wasn't (including rules for creating your own Oaths). The Contract Art being made a thing at all. Then there's the Seasonal Arts themselves. While yes, stuff like references to the Seasonal Courts is a Dark Ages: Fae thing, not so much the Seasonal Arts.<br /> <br /> Like, I was overall getting the idea that C20 was made slightly more palatable to players who's only experience with faerie stuff is with Lost.<br /> <br /> Kind of amusing since the two games, even in their most recent incarnations, are still polar opposites:<ul><li><i>Changeling the Lost</i> is a game about having something terrible and horrible happening to you and you are trying to recover from and move on from those horrible events that scarred you.</li> <li><i>Changeling the Dreaming</i> is a game about having something wonderful and amazing happen to you...and you have to watch as that wonderful thing gets taken from you, not just Banality, but from time itself.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Which...well, YMMV on that. Recent events showing that people aren't too fond of WoD and CofD mixing. Since we got enough people who are really not happy with aspects of Requiem showing up in the VtM5. And the bit with the Contagion Chronicle had people wondering if they were not-so-subtlety bringing back oWoD-style metaplot into the metaplot-agnostic CofD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T16:22:32-08:00","id":1164682,"title":"","content":"In Stealing the Solid Reflection I noticed that if you have both of the Seeming benefits, by raw you should be able to pull out living beings with mystical powers for 1 additional glamour. <br /> <br /> Discreet Summons is also really powerful having seen the Hobgoblin rules, being about to summon a Hobgoblin with Wyrd 3 which is pretty powerful, especially for a first level character, 26 trait dots, 20 skill dots, 7 merit dots, 3 Dread Powers, 2 common or Goblin contracts, 8/3 glamour Max/Spendable per turn. <br /> <br /> Example Hobgoblin 5 strength, 2 Dex, 5 stamina, 4 presence, 2 manipulation, 2 composure, 2 Intelligence, 2 wits, 2 resolve. Skills 5 Brawl, 5 Athletics, 5 Persuasion, 5 Expression. 2 Striking looks, 5 Allies (Trod Trolls). Dread Powers Invulerible, Surprise Entrance, Miracle. Contracts Loyal Servant, Glimpse of a Distant Mirror. Size 5. Minor Frality: Duck Feathers. Tell me that isn't powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T18:05:07-08:00","id":1164712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1164682#post1164682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Stealing the Solid Reflection I noticed that if you have both of the Seeming benefits, by raw you should be able to pull out living beings with mystical powers for 1 additional glamour.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also going to be pretty poorly off unless you're sporting some near-eldritch-tier Wyrd yourself, and the least circuitous route to getting this in place is being a Unicorn who's sworn an oath with a Domovoi for their knowledge of a Royal Contract that risks pissing off an entire class of Hedge-being. There's an inherent tangle of complication built into the scenario even if its effects didn't require the presence of the person in question and have a hard limit of one scene.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Discreet Summons is also really powerful having seen the Hobgoblin rules, being about to summon a Hobgoblin with Wyrd 3 which is pretty powerful, especially for a first level character, 26 trait dots, 20 skill dots, 7 merit dots, 3 Dread Powers, 2 common or Goblin contracts, 8/3 glamour Max/Spendable per turn. </div> </div> </div>The tradeoff being, of course, that it's contested by a commensurately powerful goblin (where shooting for something mystically potent but easily led is kind of its own problem) unless you make a compelling offer of payment (where &quot;compelling&quot; is determined by fiat and an explicit statement of intent that the creature in question is capable of Sealing as one of the fae), it can't do jobs that require it to leave your presence or attention without there being a Fairest somewhere in the chain of events that led to you gaining this power (in which case it's a direct or indirect risk to your Clarity, especially if you invoke the Loophole), and it only performs one task unless you roll well or are serving as a beacon for the Fae. As before, this is a Royal Contract whose effects are risky to exploit as it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T19:24:07-08:00","id":1164723,"title":"","content":"Next Stretch Goal is up: at $125k, &quot;Night Horrors: Grim Fears&quot; will be added to the Arcadian Memories bundle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 12-02-2017, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T11:22:57-08:00","id":1164837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1164302#post1164302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed, I do hope those will come sooner rather than later.<br /> <br /> But I also want to agree with the Eldritch Minister in saying that, outside of my last post's points, I really adore this version. It is amazing. Clarity really feels like the underhill's traumatic feel, but clarified (heh) it somewhat. Each of the courts now feels both evocative AND useful. Mantle isn't just balanced, it's awesome. Five dots in mantle almost feels more epic than the crown itself, which rightly feels more like a sixth dot of mantle. <br /> <br /> And the Hedge. Omg, the Hedge. I can't even put into words how amazing that is. The Skein becoming the Dreaming Roads.. The Mirror World... Hedge Ghosts.. the streamlining of hedge navigation into an epic chase against the Hedge's attention. Just.. everything. The way it feels Narnia, Wonderland, Fantasia etc isn't your arcadian memories but rather the Hedge.. just wow. That alone makes it feel so much more fairytale. <br /> <br /> And yet, they introduced many elements of owod changeling. There is more childlikeness and childishness. There is more make believe and fantasy, alongside of gameplaying and system gaming. Making bridgeburners more obviously Dauntain/autumn people was a BRILLIANT move. <br /> killing dreams and creativity... seriously, kudos to whoever made that change, it made bridgeburners vastly more interesting to me. I never used them before, and I can't wait to use them.<br /> <br /> I'm on the same page as Sean. The nostalgia reminds me of the days (when we called him Arc XD) when the game first came out and we were all wild eyed and inspired. When it inspired so many creative juices. It's a great sign that almost all of everyone's issues with it so far boil down to word count. People's doubts and fears about the changes are mostly gone, and almost every issue will be solved by the companion book, because we all want MORE. We love it, and each of us has different ideas about what was left out that shouldn't have been, but.. that's an amazing sign. While some have some gripes about certain things, it looked like most of them knew the solution already. Most of us grok everything, and like a glamour addict, need a bigger fix XD<br /> <br /> Seriously, huge kudos and mad respect to the team. It's bloody BRILLIANT and beautifully mad. I can't wait to solve my billing and bump up my pledge. I can't wait to get the colorful and prestige changeling book we all wanted (comparing green and white 1e versus dreaming 20 almost hurts sometimes)...I can't wait for the Durance to be over.<br /> <br /> Ps. Please tell me some of the extra art budget was/will be spent on Stephanie Pui-Mun Law or Melissa Uran. Id give up an Icon to get more of them.</div> </div> </div> </div> Personally for art I think they should concider Clyde Caldwell and Larry Elmore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","d