:24-08:00","id":1164951,"title":"","content":"My hype is gettng HYPED UP","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12235-emmens","name":"emmens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12235_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T03:19:37-08:00","id":1165004,"title":"","content":"Wait so what are regalia, like the Mirror's regalia for the kithbook. I feel I am missing something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T03:25:24-08:00","id":1165005,"title":"","content":"Regalia are the six basic groups of Contracts. So AFAIK that Regalia sections added for the Kith stretch goals are Kiths focus on the same themes as the Regalia in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T09:25:28-08:00","id":1165072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzrenOgre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1164372#post1164372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may have already missed this part of the discussion, but do some of the changes to the kiths previewed seem strikingly different from anything in other games and in some cases needing a bit more information (looking at you Gristlegrinder). I hope that they will provide more information to clarify or maybe some tweeks to this before people just run around gulping down everything in sight.<br /> <br /> Also, some of the concepts seem muddled to me.<br /> <br /> Example: Ogres are creatures of violence. They escaped the hedge by forcing themselves on other things or other beings. They have been shaped by the violence inflicted on them sure, but they are typified by the fact that they used violence (and probably still use it) and it marked them. So why then is their Affinity Contract the Shield? I mean sure Ogres are probably tough but it is by inflicting their will on the resistant or the unwilling that they are defined, so wouldn't Sword make more sense?<br /> <br /> Now I am still super excited about this project and I am backing it, but there are parts of this I wish I understood more.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I had the same problem with Ogres and Shield being a pair. I am also sad that kiths' aren't gaining bonuses based on Wyrd now. It feels similar to werewolf in that category- you had no reason to really raise it besides the Clash of Wills type of deals. And in this case, it also acts as a damage modifier against your Clarity, so I really don't see a good reason the average player will be raising it through the course of a normal game.","signat