er","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T11:37:29-08:00","id":1165102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165100#post1165100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> We know that the book was going to exist even without the add-on chapters.<br /> <br /> I have no idea what's going on with the book, but just saying it might be possible. I could also be totally wrong too</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh definitely. I still hope we can get some clarification on what's in the book, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T12:36:27-08:00","id":1165117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165094#post1165094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b Which came first, the Ogre or the Shield? Was the Ogre section rewritten to reflect them as Shields, or were they given shields because of the write up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. I think there were signs this was where the Seeming concept was going, but I don't know how relevant they are now.<br /> <br /> I started watching <i>Leverage</i> entirely because of this forum and it's hard to un-see the Seeming concepts in light of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T07:51:08-08:00","id":1165304,"title":"","content":"Maybe I just skated over it in my reading, but I don't fully understand the role of Goblin queens in the setting. The concept is very cool but what exactly IS a goblin queen? Are they just another hobgoblin, just one that used to be mortal? Is there more to them than that? If the latter, then could you point me to the section where they're elaborated on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","name":"Lady Gray","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T08:10:14-08:00","id":1165311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lady Gray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165304#post1165304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I just skated over it in my reading, but I don't fully understand the role of Goblin queens in the setting. The concept is very cool but what exactly IS a goblin queen? Are they just another hobgoblin, just one that used to be mortal? Is there more to them than that? If the latter, then could you point me to the section where they're elaborated on?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/goblin-contracts-changeling-the-lost/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/goblin-contracts-changeling-the-lost/\" target=\"_blank\"> Goblin Contracts [Changeling: The Lost] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/goblin-contracts-changeling-the-lost/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/goblin-contracts-changeling-the-lost/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Get too much goblin debt, become a Hedge Denizen. Hedge Denizen is a condition. <br /> <br /> To become a Goblin Queen either advance Hedge Denizen to the next stage, or become the heir of a Goblin Queen (to resolve and end the Goblin Queen Condition you can choose a child to inherit the condition, making them a Goblin Queen).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T08:10:26-08:00","id":1165312,"title":"","content":"Goblin Queens are one of two things... either they're a Changeling who got too in Goblin Debt and a few other things happened, OR they're a mortal (I think child only?) that Changeling kidnapped to take their place as the Queen. It's supposed to be kinda like the movie Labyrinth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T08:36:36-08:00","id":1165320,"title":"","content":"Thanks a lot guys, I guess I just didn't look through the changeling conditions. Wow, that looks really cool and I like the concept even more now. I am definitely going to make a recurring Goblin queen character for my campaign when I eventually run this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","name":"Lady Gray","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T08:43:43-08:00","id":1165322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lady Gray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165320#post1165320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks a lot guys, I guess I just didn't look through the changeling conditions. Wow, that looks really cool and I like the concept even more now. I am definitely going to make a recurring Goblin queen character for my campaign when I eventually run this.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the record, we've not gotten Conditions yet, so it makes sense how you &quot;missed&quot; this, since it really only mentions Hedge Denizen in the Goblin Debt part of Goblin Contracts being a thing. We should be getting the rest of it today though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T10:39:02-08:00","id":1165353,"title":"","content":"Fae Touched are amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T10:39:37-08:00","id":1165354,"title":"","content":"And now with part four, we have rules for making Courts, Contracts, and Kiths. Have fun!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T10:52:19-08:00","id":1165363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165322#post1165322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the record, we've not gotten Conditions yet, so it makes sense how you &quot;missed&quot; this, since it really only mentions Hedge Denizen in the Goblin Debt part of Goblin Contracts being a thing. We should be getting the rest of it today though.</div> </div> </div> </div>SPEAKING OF WHICH:<br /> <br /> So the fourth and final part of the CtL2e corebook manuscript is out. It has:<br /> <br /> Chapter 7: Storytelling<br /> <br /> -Setting up a Chronicle<br /> -Player Safety rules<br /> -<i><b>CUSTOMIZATION RULES</b></i>: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Kiths</li> <li>Courts &amp; Mantles</li> <li>Contracts</li> <li>Goblin Contracts</li> </ol><br /> Appendix 1: Fae-Touched<br /> <br /> -Becoming Fae-touched<br /> -Fae-touched in changeling society<br /> -Example fae-touched<br /> -Rules for creating and playing a fae-touched<br /> <br /> Appendix 2: Equipment<br /> <br /> Appendix 3: Tilts<br /> <br /> Appendix 4: Conditions<br /> <br /> Ok, NOW we can talk about CtL2's &quot;create-a-___________&quot; rules and how viable they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T10:55:59-08:00","id":1165365,"title":"","content":"Worth noting that the mechanics for how a Kith could let a Changeling fly are given a bit of an explanation. And good gods I want to see the Freehold of Prague now! Contagion Chronicle maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T11:22:45-08:00","id":1165371,"title":"","content":"Customization rules are pretty much exactly what I feared them to be. They break down the necessary considerations well enough but ultimately a Storyteller is going to have be eyeballing a bunch of mechanics and hoping they didn't inadvertently create something too weak/powerful. Nothing here is crunchy or well defined enough to bypass the usual obstacles to implementing custom material.<br /> <br /> Please don't take this to mean that I actively dislike the product as a whole, but all prior complaints stand. Maybe we'll get something better if we hit the corresponding stretch goal for the companion book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T11:27:49-08:00","id":1165374,"title":"","content":"Fae Touched don't die early anymore, don't have Seemings anymore, instead getting a bonus die to rolls to keep her promise.<br /> <br /> They start off with 2 common regalia contracts and can buy more, including Royal Contracts which can make them powerful eventually. <br /> <br /> Automatic oath with their Changeling upon being reunited. <br /> <br /> One beef I have with the new rules is there is side bar for having Fae Touched Retainers. <br /> <br /> Also the Oath that makes one Fae Touched can be inherited, usually by family, creating the possibility of Fae Touched Families like Ghoul Families.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T12:46:35-08:00","id":1165389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>4th Preview</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A Beast is an animal to her core, but a Hunterheart exhibits only those animal traits that make her a better hunter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've said it before... but there are inconsistencies with how Seeming and Kith is presented in this book. <br /> <br /> It's annoying. Well, regardless when I run this, I'm going to rule it that a beast is not just a literal animal (but can be).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T12:49:26-08:00","id":1165390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165389#post1165389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've said it before... but there are inconsistencies with how Seeming and Kith is presented in this book.<br /> <br /> It's annoying. Well, regardless when I run this, I'm going to rule it that a beast is not just a literal animal (but can be).</div> </div> </div> </div>I might be wrong, but I think that is basically saying that if you're a Beast Hunterheart, you only exhibit those traits, and similarly, it's going to emphasize the hunter traits of any other Seeming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T13:12:38-08:00","id":1165400,"title":"","content":"Eh, either way: at least now I can finally get started on building my Toontown freehold and courts...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T13:19:35-08:00","id":1165403,"title":"","content":"One thing that I doubt will get mentioned much, but I'm glad is in there are the discussion of different comfort/safety mechanisms you can use in a game. Definitely nice to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T13:40:07-08:00","id":1165409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165390#post1165390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I might be wrong, but I think that is basically saying that if you're a Beast Hunterheart, you only exhibit those traits, and similarly, it's going to emphasize the hunter traits of any other Seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I need to read a bit earlier I guess because in the &quot;Build a Court&quot; section has this mention:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ... a vulpine Darkling Hunterheart or a ... </div> </div> </div>\u200bWhich indicates that just because the Keeper made one into an animal doesn't make them a beast (or any other way). That's good cause I really didn't want it to go the way of 1st ed (all beasts were animals w/ kith as the specific animal. All fairest were elves w/ kith as the specific trope. All elementals were made of an element w/ kith as the specific element. all darklings were made from darkness and shadows w/ kith as the specific expression. ETC).<br /> <br /> I did not want that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T13:42:12-08:00","id":1165410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165403#post1165403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that I doubt will get mentioned much, but I'm glad is in there are the discussion of different comfort/safety mechanisms you can use in a game. Definitely nice to see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Its an important section to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T18:01:08-08:00","id":1165476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165371#post1165371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Customization rules are pretty much exactly what I feared them to be. They break down the necessary considerations well enough but ultimately a Storyteller is going to have be eyeballing a bunch of mechanics and hoping they didn't inadvertently create something too weak/powerful. Nothing here is crunchy or well defined enough to bypass the usual obstacles to implementing custom material.<br /> <br /> Please don't take this to mean that I actively dislike the product as a whole, but all prior complaints stand. Maybe we'll get something better if we hit the corresponding stretch goal for the companion book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you unpack this a bit more? I found the Kith and Court guides to be very concrete. Contracts, admittedly I would like some explicit benchmarks, but I think they are still workable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T19:03:58-08:00","id":1165494,"title":"","content":"How would you say Fae Touched compare to other minor templates? <br /> <br /> I'm give you a basic sense of it. A brand new Fae Touched whose Changeling escaped Arcadia.<br /> <br /> She has two Common Contracts, Loyal Servant amd Glimpse of a Distant Mirror. She can Seal the promises of mortals. When fortifying her promise add 1 bonus die to the pool. Her and her Changeling can harvest glamour from each other, and can spend a glamour to find out the others location, emotions, and so on. She can make Oaths to Changelings. She can get court goodwill. Use Fae Touched Merits. <br /> <br /> Loyal Servant, Glimpse of a Distant Mirror, and Sealings don't require a roll and there for can't fall unless someine else uses magic that causes a clash of wills. <br /> <br /> Loyal Servants means this new character Fae Touched can summon Loyal Servants from fire, electricity, air, gravity, sound, water, earth, shadow, poop, light, plastic, diamonds, and countless other substances. <br /> <br /> That's pretty powerful, but a ghoul can use three disciplines, use vitae to heal, and some other stuff. But has a much harder time refueling, dependent on vampires for fuel. Actually the Fae Touched can harvest glamour from Vampires so can she.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T19:25:17-08:00","id":1165498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165494#post1165494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you say Fae Touched compare to other minor templates?<br /> <br /> I'm give you a basic sense of it. A brand new Fae Touched whose Changeling escaped Arcadia.<br /> <br /> She has two Common Contracts, Loyal Servant amd Glimpse of a Distant Mirror. She can Seal the promises of mortals. When fortifying her promise add 1 bonus die to the pool. Her and her Changeling can harvest glamour from each other, and can spend a glamour to find out the others location, emotions, and so on. She can make Oaths to Changelings. She can get court goodwill. Use Fae Touched Merits.<br /> <br /> Loyal Servant, Glimpse of a Distant Mirror, and Sealings don't require a roll and there for can't fall unless someine else uses magic that causes a clash of wills.<br /> <br /> Loyal Servants means this new character Fae Touched can summon Loyal Servants from fire, electricity, air, gravity, sound, water, earth, shadow, poop, light, plastic, diamonds, and countless other substances.<br /> <br /> That's pretty powerful, but a ghoul can use three disciplines, use vitae to heal, and some other stuff. But has a much harder time refueling, dependent on vampires for fuel. Actually the Fae Touched can harvest glamour from Vampires so can she.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One thing the text implies, namely the Fae Touched sees the Fetch of their linked changeling as what they REALLY ARE. I think the other thing to not discount is Fae Touched are lacking a lot of information about their state that say... a ghoul probably will know more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T19:41:11-08:00","id":1165503,"title":"","content":"It probably helps that Changeling societies tend to be a lot less cutthroat than Vampire societies are (if you pardon the pun). Ghouls tend to be on a pretty short leash and can't really do much against their masters - while Fae Touched aren't typically <i>equals</i> with Changelings, they're at least not yanked around nearly so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T04:33:22-08:00","id":1165547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165476#post1165476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you unpack this a bit more? I found the Kith and Court guides to be very concrete. Contracts, admittedly I would like some explicit benchmarks, but I think they are still workable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I can help here because while I found the court and contract making sections much more useable, the kith making section was...lacking in key elements.<ul><li>Power Ceiling - How much bonus can a Kith trickery give, what's the upper limit of that power? This needs to be spelled out.</li> <li>Power Floor - What is the minimum mark. At the least a kith should be able to do X, if it does less than X it should be considered for a merit/contract/ect.</li> </ul>Those two pieces of information would make the Kith creation section worth while. Otherwise you end up with Kiths like my Efreet (used alternate spelling to not step on official Ifrit kith)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T05:15:49-08:00","id":1165552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165503#post1165503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It probably helps that Changeling societies tend to be a lot less cutthroat than Vampire societies are (if you pardon the pun). Ghouls tend to be on a pretty short leash and can't really do much against their masters - while Fae Touched aren't typically <i>equals</i> with Changelings, they're at least not yanked around nearly so much.</div> </div> </div> </div> Even bigger Fae Touched are usually not going to be subjected to the abuse that Ghoul gets as a matter of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T06:46:44-08:00","id":1165564,"title":"","content":"huh. so we aren't gonna have entitlements in the corebook, huh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T06:50:23-08:00","id":1165565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firefly Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165564#post1165564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">huh. so we aren't gonna have entitlements in the corebook, huh?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not super surprising. Mage is the only 2e core to talk about their z-splat in any detail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T07:15:12-08:00","id":1165567,"title":"","content":"Finally got around to check the new preview, still no rules to how to design tokens <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> And the guide to making Contracts is barebones and doesn't take into account Seeming variations. At least the mantle construction is better done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T08:03:26-08:00","id":1165572,"title":"","content":"I REALLY hope that Companion section on Courts will use those of corebook Freeholds as examples to show it's rules. Without those examples of using guidlines we do not have anything CONCRETE about those Courts in Rejkiavik, New Orleans, New England and Hong Kong. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T08:13:39-08:00","id":1165575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165476#post1165476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you unpack this a bit more? I found the Kith and Court guides to be very concrete. Contracts, admittedly I would like some explicit benchmarks, but I think they are still workable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the Trickery guideline is essentially &quot;glamour and dice pool to do a thing, except when it isn't.&quot; There's no real scaling considerations here. The Hunterheart's hitting with the insensate tilt may be fine, but the immobolized tilt might be a bit much. What buffs are acceptable? Is Wyrd an ok damage bonus? even for a ranged attack?<br /> <br /> Mantle is a little better in that it has a few more actual specifics that can be applied in a variety of contexts, but you'd still have a hard time matching the canon mantles with just those guidelines.<br /> <br /> A brief list of splats that don't really fit any guidelines listed:<br /> <br /> Artist kith (its a self buff)<br /> Bright One (debuff with no roll)<br /> Leechfinger (offensive effect with no roll)<br /> Notary (no roll or cost)<br /> Playmate (no roll, weird cost)<br /> <br /> Summer Mantle (Grants points of armor, Automatic Success effect on the 4th dot not the 5th)<br /> Autumn Mantle (Effects Glamour costs and Goblin Debt)<br /> Winter Mantle (Non-roll Debuff at 4 dot)<br /> Morning Mantle (Automatic Success at 4 dots)<br /> Day Mantle (Effects glamour costs at 4)<br /> Icelandic Sprint Mantle (Grants merit at 1 dot)<br /> Icelandic Winter Mantle (Grants damage bonus)<br /> High Tide Mantle (Automatic Success at 4 dots)<br /> Low Tide Mantle(Interacts with investigation system)<br /> Coin Mantle (interacts with goblin debt)<br /> Barter Mantle (interacts with goblin debt)<br /> Favor Mantle (grants merit at 2 dots, more goblin debt)<br /> Shady Deals Mantle (More goblin debt, can ignore a condition)<br /> <br /> And for this list I ignored edge cases. (Like &quot;have a +1 to your effective resistance attribute&quot; shows up in a few places but it seems within the possibility of &quot;bonus dice to a slightly broader roll&quot;.) I also just completely ignored the 5 dot mantles effects since &quot;unique magical effect&quot; covers a lot of ground, even if its not terribly helpful for balancing. And while thinking of an effect comparable to &quot;inflict someone with tilt or condition&quot; which shows up on a few kiths isn't too hard, I'd hesitate to say what is comparable to the Helldiver, who has a lot individual considerations that the rest don't. <br /> <br /> (For the record, I love the helldiver kith.)<br /> <br /> You can argue that some of these are clearly designed to be exceptions to the rule, but if at least 1 in 3 of them don't match the guidelines or the examples, they aren't really &quot;fringe cases.&quot; I cannot build custom material with just the listed guidelines with any confidence that it will &quot;fit&quot; into the gameline without issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T09:29:43-08:00","id":1165596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165575#post1165575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well the Trickery guideline is essentially &amp;quot;glamour and dice pool to do a thing, except when it isn't.&amp;quot; There's no real scaling considerations here. The Hunterheart's hitting with the insensate tilt may be fine, but the immobolized tilt might be a bit much. What buffs are acceptable? Is Wyrd an ok damage bonus? even for a ranged attack?<br /> <br /> Mantle is a little better in that it has a few more actual specifics that can be applied in a variety of contexts, but you'd still have a hard time matching the canon mantles with just those guidelines.<br /> <br /> A brief list of splats that don't really fit any guidelines listed:<br /> <br /> Artist kith (its a self buff)<br /> Bright One (debuff with no roll)<br /> Leechfinger (offensive effect with no roll)<br /> Notary (no roll or cost)<br /> Playmate (no roll, weird cost)<br /> <br /> Summer Mantle (Grants points of armor, Automatic Success effect on the 4th dot not the 5th)<br /> Autumn Mantle (Effects Glamour costs and Goblin Debt)<br /> Winter Mantle (Non-roll Debuff at 4 dot)<br /> Morning Mantle (Automatic Success at 4 dots)<br /> Day Mantle (Effects glamour costs at 4)<br /> Icelandic Sprint Mantle (Grants merit at 1 dot)<br /> Icelandic Winter Mantle (Grants damage bonus)<br /> High Tide Mantle (Automatic Success at 4 dots)<br /> Low Tide Mantle(Interacts with investigation system)<br /> Coin Mantle (interacts with goblin debt)<br /> Barter Mantle (interacts with goblin debt)<br /> Favor Mantle (grants merit at 2 dots, more goblin debt)<br /> Shady Deals Mantle (More goblin debt, can ignore a condition)<br /> <br /> And for this list I ignored edge cases. (Like &amp;quot;have a +1 to your effective resistance attribute&amp;quot; shows up in a few places but it seems within the possibility of &amp;quot;bonus dice to a slightly broader roll&amp;quot;.) I also just completely ignored the 5 dot mantles effects since &amp;quot;unique magical effect&amp;quot; covers a lot of ground, even if its not terribly helpful for balancing. And while thinking of an effect comparable to &amp;quot;inflict someone with tilt or condition&amp;quot; which shows up on a few kiths isn't too hard, I'd hesitate to say what is comparable to the Helldiver, who has a lot individual considerations that the rest don't. <br /> <br /> (For the record, I love the helldiver kith.)<br /> <br /> You can argue that some of these are clearly designed to be exceptions to the rule, but if at least 1 in 3 of them don't match the guidelines or the examples, they aren't really &amp;quot;fringe cases.&amp;quot; I cannot build custom material with just the listed guidelines with any confidence that it will &amp;quot;fit&amp;quot; into the gameline without issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the Trickery guidelines are more intended to act as an easy reference rather than a limit on what you can do with them. For example, the Chirurgeon update that I've been working on doesn't fit it perfectly, but I think that it would still fit the game anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T09:51:34-08:00","id":1165603,"title":"","content":"Say it with Geoffery Rush now:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jl0hMfqNQ-g\" data-code=\"jl0hMfqNQ-g\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/jl0hMfqNQ-g/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T10:43:59-08:00","id":1165621,"title":"","content":"&lt;insert rant reiterating points I've already made&gt;<br /> <br /> ...therefore the game in its current state will have an adverse impact on people who wish to play kiths beyond the twelve presented (which are by no means all-encompassing, nor should they be) or a non-seasonal court.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T11:08:42-08:00","id":1165628,"title":"","content":"I'm with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> on this one. I am pretty sure that there is no power floor or ceiling <u>on purpose</u>. All of the 2nd Edition books have mostly done away with that concept as, in practice, power balance tends to be moot or at the very least very different to the white room scenario that the power balance was designed for.<br /> <br /> I think the bottom line with the creation of these powers and abilities is that there are many different things they could do and the examples give a large breadth of samples. In the end, don't worry about balance beyond what makes sense. For the bird like Kith focused on flight, giving it's ability to straight up fly might be too much and just adding a few inches to the jump height might not be enough. But you would be the best arbitrator on what makes most sense for your setting.<br /> <br /> Same goes for the Mantles, the Crowns, the Contracts, the Court Bargains, and other creation tools they've given in the appendix. <br /> <br /> If you want to not create anything (or just reskin a few things) use the fully fully fleshed out Seasonal Courts that most your troupe will immediately understand anyway. If you don't mind doing a few homebrewing but not everything, use one of the examples from the alternative courts listed in the 3rd preview and fill in the blanks using the creation tools in the 4th preview. And if you don't mind creating everything, just use the tools in the 4th preview. <br /> <br /> Don't worry too much on balance, you'd know best what makes sense power wise and more importantly: what is best at evoking what you want to evoke with that kith or court or contract or otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":654,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","user":"xiongrey","date":". 12-06-2017, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T11:27:10-08:00","id":1165633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165628#post1165628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> on this one. I am pretty sure that there is no power floor or ceiling <u>on purpose</u>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because it was made on purpose I doesn't mean that is good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165628#post1165628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the bottom line with the creation of these powers and abilities is that there are many different things they could do and the examples give a large breadth of samples. In the end, don't worry about balance beyond what makes sense. For the bird like Kith focused on flight, giving it's ability to straight up fly might be too much and just adding a few inches to the jump height might not be enough. But you would be the best arbitrator on what makes most sense for your setting.<br /> <br /> Same goes for the Mantles, the Crowns, the Contracts, the Court Bargains, and other creation tools they've given in the appendix.<br /> <br /> If you want to not create anything (or just reskin a few things) use the fully fleshed out Seasonal Courts that most your troupe will immediately understand anyway. If you don't mind doing a few homebrewing but not everything, use one of the examples from the alternative courts listed in the 3rd preview and fill in the blanks using the creation tools in the 4th preview. And if you don't mind creating everything, just use the tools in the 4th preview.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be on board with that if Chrod wasnt such a crunchy system. Its basically a Crunchy system with a designs philosophy of &quot;balance doesn't matter&quot; so they dont have to put effort on it. That kind of thing flies with systems like FATE/PbtA because their mechanics is 1 and everything else is just a paint job for the exact same bonuses. Any power or anything you do is &quot;just +/- 1 to 5&quot; and situation you can apply to it, nothing else and everything else is just fluff with no mechanical weight. While Chrod has many MANY moving parts and things that radically change how a mechanic works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165628#post1165628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't worry too much on balance, you'd know best what makes sense power wise and more importantly: what is best at evoking what you want to evoke with that kith or court or contract or otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually no, many people don't know &quot;whats best what makes sense power wise&quot; that's why they pay for a game instead of just made one up themselves. You said flying for free is too much, I say is such as a useless ability that's is gonna see so little use because of the &quot;masquerade&quot; that's might as well be free (same with breathing underwater) whats best is not obvious.<br /> <br /> That kind of foresight to powers leads to OP things like &quot;diplomatic immunity rote&quot;, &quot;enchanting voice&quot; merit in OWOD, Pure breed, etc. This a huge problem in Chrod lately it's avoiding of putting any kind of effort on their mechanic hiding behind the excuse of &quot;balance doesn't exist&quot;.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't have an issue with the Kiths as I will copy paste 1st editions seemings and kiths. But contracts are incredibly vague and thats a huge blow against the game. More if I care about making my own courts (which fortunately I don't because we got a write up for the directionals).<br /> <br /> But I already gonna have to ban tokens as there is no goddam mechanic on how to design powers for them. So I will probably stick around to how long the Kickstarter reaches before pulling my pledge the last day, as I cannot support that lazy design philosophy of OPP anymore. Unless something changes of course.<br /> <br /> Bear in mind, I am not calling the people who make this game lazy, they obviously put a lot of effort into making this game but OPP has a certain design philosophy of putting lots of effort in the fictions and little else in the mechanics and a worrying approach of leaving me, the consumer, to do their work for them in balancing mechanics hiding by a flawed ideology of &quot;game balance doesn't exist&quot; which has too many holes as a theory. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 12-06-2017, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T11:36:00-08:00","id":1165634,"title":"","content":"For the record, I don't think Pop is wrong, per se-just the degree to which they are correct. I mean, compare this to the history of actual play reports involving such things <i>without</i> rules, and, well.<br /> <br /> Not wrong, particularly for certain play groups who are more common than we might think. I'm just not sure that that equals being right.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Sorry for vagueness, I am both learning how to make home security systems run as they should and editting a hard sci-fi novel while also sort of vaguely wanting to be helpful here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T11:45:15-08:00","id":1165635,"title":"","content":"I'm going to hard disagree on this particular point, especially with the corollary that &quot;this is how its supposed to work.&quot; If make a murderhobo kith who gets to add five to all forms of damage all the time always, it doesn't matter if it &quot;makes sense&quot; for the story. The same theme can in fact be implemented in ways that don't give a player a more pronounced advantage over the other. Game balance in CofD may be a bit more nuanced than just &quot;who has the highest numbers,&quot; but that doesn't mean the concept has somehow vanished. Cult of Personality costs 10 vitae to activate for a reason.<br /> <br /> And whether or not I particular mind isn't the issue. Its whether or not I can get 3-6 other people to be on the exact same page. I've run into both &quot;let's stick with published mechanics&quot; and &quot;can I do this weird thing that doesn't really match anything printed?&quot; Loose guidelines doesn't really cater to either, since its not going to satisfy the former, and the latter still needs to &quot;sell&quot; their pitch.<br /> <br /> And I'm not arguing that this game is in any way unplayable, or even bad on its own merits. Just that in practice, with just information we have presented right now, when it comes to playing a non-seasonal or a kith outside of the twelve, the barrier for entry is no easier than playing an eighth clan or a 6th tribe, or whatever other splat whose respective gameline didn't feel the need to bring up custom material in the corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T13:11:49-08:00","id":1165650,"title":"","content":"I did notice the guidelines for making your own Kith and etc. were a little limited in that regard. They help (like the pertinent pointer that an exceptional success is worth more in some things like combat so relevant blessings need to be much more limited in scope), but in some things there are almost more examples in the book that balk the suggested guidelines than not.<br /> <br /> Of course, the guidelines are just suggested standards, which are useful to fall back on if you're not use of how to handle something. The examples in and of themselves are useful, and there are a number of notes I appreciate that the creation rules have, but they suffer from not being more detailed and I wish there was a bit more lateral depth to them.<br /> <br /> On a completely different note, the section on table safety and the attention throughout on the subject are still very good, and I'm quite happy the book has that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 12-06-2017, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T13:46:25-08:00","id":1165661,"title":"","content":"I must admit, the guidelines are less thorough than I'd have liked. However, much like Demon and its gadget creating rules, I'm confident that the companion books will address these problems. As it stands, it's something that works very well for me.<br /> <br /> Does that mean that dissatisfaction with the product currently is unfair? Not at all. As I said before, judging something before we had the rules was silly - now that we have them, looking through them and judging them on their own merits is alright. I do feel that the current set-up is workable, but if you feel not, that's on you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165567#post1165567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally got around to check the new preview, still no rules to how to design tokens <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And the guide to making Contracts is barebones and doesn't take into account Seeming variations. At least the mantle construction is better done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't that discussed last week? The players and ST work together for the effects, and the hardware as it were works towards that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T15:37:14-08:00","id":1165684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165661#post1165661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't that discussed last week? The players and ST work together for the effects, and the hardware as it were works towards that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont remember if that was a discussion in any of the updates. Yes any creation of any magic item requires the player and DM to determine the effect but then what effect correspond to what levels of point is up in the air.<br /> <br /> Same with how to create drawbacks and catchs for the token. No guide whatsover that i could find in the manuscripts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T16:05:44-08:00","id":1165690,"title":"","content":"I guess I can understand your points Loki and Pop.<br /> <br /> Coming from Demon that had Interlocks and a Final Truth that had a lot of variation that, on standard, the ST had to create (or get the players to create in some variants), putting work into the creation of new powers for non-standard courts and contracts seemed reasonable for me. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T19:08:59-08:00","id":1165735,"title":"","content":"Well, we WILL get the book Kith &amp; Kine with at least few dozens of Kith, finally. So there WILL BE much more examples. But to the premier of it - what can take even to 2 years after finalization of CtL 2E - we are all left with corebook guidlines. \ud83d\ude15","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T19:27:26-08:00","id":1165738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165735#post1165735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, we WILL get the book Kith &amp; Kine with at least few dozens of Kith, finally. So there WILL BE much more examples. But to the premier of it - what can take even to 2 years after finalization of CtL 2E - we are all left with corebook guidlines. \ud83d\ude15</div> </div> </div> </div>I think those two years will be for the physical edition; the digital edition should be along a good amount quicker due to the fact that PDFs can be altered easier if there are typos and such (which is what the Advanced copies are for). Physical editions are for after when the errata is compiled and corrected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T19:31:15-08:00","id":1165740,"title":"","content":"We are year and a half after Mage 2E premiere and STILL we do not have even PDF for Signs of Sorcery. I just point you all those supplements - CtL 2E Companion and Kith &amp; Kine - they can TAKE AWHILE...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T19:43:58-08:00","id":1165745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165740#post1165740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are year and a half after Mage 2E premiere and STILL we do not have even PDF for Signs of Sorcery. I just point you all those supplements - CtL 2E Companion and Kith &amp; Kine - they can TAKE AWHILE...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! Sorry, I thought you were referencing the Changeling core book itself. I agree with you, supplements can take a good while before they're released. Hopefully they won't be too long, but given the given example...yeah, I can see your worry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T20:06:14-08:00","id":1165751,"title":"","content":"Oh nice, it looks like a PDF + POD at cost item has been added a day or two ago.<br /> <br /> Suddenly backing this should be feasible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T20:17:26-08:00","id":1165753,"title":"","content":"Was going to make a whole long post, but Imma just leave it at this from CtL's sister game:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i><b>Dreams Do Not Follow Rules</b></i><br /> \u201c<i>A foolish consistency</i>,\u201d wrote Emerson, \u201c<i>is the<br /> hobgoblin of little minds</i>.\u201d The process that we set out<br /> here to create new kiths can, in most cases, be used to<br /> \u201creverse engineer\u201d the existing kiths\u2026 but exceptions<br /> exist. <b><i>The very last step in the kith creation process is<br /> not \u201cmake sure everything is perfectly balanced with<br /> regards to game mechanics and that no kith is more<br /> powerful than any other,\u201d but rather \u201cmake sure the<br /> kith represents your vision for it, and will be interesting<br /> and fun to play.\u201d</i></b><br /> Throughout this process, please remember to<br /> mentally append \u201cunless breaking this rule makes for<br /> a more interesting character\u201d to anything that seems<br /> to apply as a blanket statement. </div> </div> </div>When it comes to the custom stuff, as long as the players and ST are fine with it and have fun with whatever custom stuff they come up, that should be all that matters. Not worrying over how &quot;balanced&quot; it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T20:34:13-08:00","id":1165758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165753#post1165753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> When it comes to the custom stuff, as long as the players and ST are fine with it and have fun with whatever custom stuff they come up, that should be all that matters. Not worrying over how &quot;balanced&quot; it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Suddenly I'm less apprehensive about presenting any potential Changeling ST with my idea for a custom merit to produce ink from his claws and fingers...and have a desire to purchase Changeling: The Dreaming 20th anniversary edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T20:44:49-08:00","id":1165760,"title":"","content":"These creation and customization rules are unbelievably insufficient. There's no way these can do what they need to, especially with such emphasis on this being a 'toolbox.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T21:05:23-08:00","id":1165763,"title":"","content":"&quot;<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165753#post1165753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not worrying over how &quot;balanced&quot; it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a relief, now I can finally play that kith I have been dreaming about that as special ability reduces the target number of all social rolls to 5.<br /> <br /> And has a custom regalia that functions like the Shield and sword regalias all rolled up in one....but as a bonus their power level for common is the equivalent of both regalias royals and then the Royals are even better.<br /> <br /> I can't wait to get into an endless argument with the ST in question about how he/she should totally allow for my ideas because &quot;muh vision!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Hell, why do I even need a 60+ dollar book to tell me to just to use my imagination and that rules don't need to constrain me? I can just use an empty box and pretend I shoot 1 hit kill lasers! *Wiiiiiii*<br /> <br /> No, but seriously quoting anything from OWoD as an argument for &quot;balance doesn't matter&quot; is the equivalent of pointing out Chernobyl as an argument for &quot;nuclear safety measure aren't needed&quot;. When it gave us some jewels like &quot;enchanting voice&quot; and &quot;purebreed&quot;.<br /> <br /> Botton line is: Sure we can all rule 0 everything but that doesn't mean that we don't need actual rules for things, especially in crunchy systems like this one. You need rules to establish an objective baseline so the vision and egos in a table have an impartial mediator of sorts. A good table with everyone in synch doesn't need that but not all tables are that most are 3 people in synch 1 who is good but isn't in synch with the rest and 1 shithead. Rules serve to limit the latter 2.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And I am gonna add another problem with that theory of &quot; When it comes to the custom stuff, as long as the players and ST are fine with it&quot; as a DM, how do I know if I am a fine with something? If I don't have a good guide on how it should function? Your equation requires the agreement of both the DM and player as an excuse for &quot;balance doesn't matter&quot; but as a DM, and one who cares about balance, then how do you get &quot;my agreement&quot;?<br /> <br /> If balance isn't needed because DM and player approval are more important but DM needs balance to approve something then you are bitting you are running in circles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 12-07-2017, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T21:33:58-08:00","id":1165767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>E11even-E11even</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165760#post1165760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These creation and customization rules are unbelievably insufficient. There's no way these can do what they need to, especially with such emphasis on this being a 'toolbox.'</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165763#post1165763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a relief, now I can finally play that kith I have been dreaming about that as special ability reduces the target number of all social rolls to 5.<br /> <br /> And has a custom regalia that functions like the Shield and sword regalias all rolled up in one....but as a bonus their power level for common is the equivalent of both regalias royals and then the Royals are even better.<br /> <br /> I can't wait to get into an endless argument with the ST in question about how he/she should totally allow for my ideas because &quot;muh vision!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Hell, why do I even need a 60+ dollar book to tell me to just to use my imagination and that rules don't need to constrain me? I can just use an empty box and pretend I shoot 1 hit kill lasers! *Wiiiiiii*<br /> <br /> No, but seriously quoting anything from OWoD as an argument for &quot;balance doesn't matter&quot; is the equivalent of pointing out Chernobyl as an argument for &quot;nuclear safety measure aren't needed&quot;. When it gave us some jewels like &quot;enchanting voice&quot; and &quot;purebreed&quot;.<br /> <br /> Botton line is: Sure we can all rule 0 everything but that doesn't mean that we don't need actual rules for things, especially in crunchy systems like this one. You need rules to establish an objective baseline so the vision and egos in a table have an impartial mediator of sorts. A good table with everyone in synch doesn't need that but not all tables are that most are 3 people in synch 1 who is good but isn't in synch with the rest and 1 shithead. Rules serve to limit the latter 2.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And I am gonna add another problem with that theory of &quot; When it comes to the custom stuff, as long as the players and ST are fine with it&quot; as a DM, how do I know if I am a fine with something? If I don't have a good guide on how it should function? Your equation requires the agreement of both the DM and player as an excuse for &quot;balance doesn't matter&quot; but as a DM, and one who cares about balance, then how do you get &quot;my agreement&quot;?<br /> <br /> If balance isn't needed because DM and player approval are more important but DM needs balance to approve something then you are bitting you are running in circles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get you guys are frustrated with the current guidelines. As I've noted, I'd have preferred something more robust. However, there's no reason to be using that kind of attitude to people who are fine with them.<br /> <br /> As I have noted much earlier, people have been making custom content for the games <i>without</i> any kind of guidelines for it. People were making custom content for the game back when David Hill was producing Changeling: The Lost, and any guidelines included there were far less decisive than what the current version has granted us. There is a thread in this very forum that is 39 pages long of people posting and discussing various kiths they have created for others to see for David Hill's version, and already there's a thread being made of Kiths for the current version of the game. There is even a thread for custom contracts. The guidelines we have gotten may not be idiot-proof, but they are far and away better than having nothing and are still useful.<br /> <br /> If you don't feel you can create something with the current guides, I'm sorry they don't inspire you. Talk with someone about them, work with them, or even look to the forums for something someone else has worked on. Remember that we have supplements coming out in the future that will likely address any fallacies that you find, much in the same way that &quot;Flowers of Hell&quot; added a plethora of options for Embeds, Exploits and Gadget creation for Demon: The Descent. However, please do not call them &quot;unbelievable insufficient&quot; when people have been working with much less for far longer than this campaign has been out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T21:50:50-08:00","id":1165769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165767#post1165767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I get you guys are frustrated with the current guidelines. As I've noted, I'd have preferred something more robust. However, there's no reason to be using that kind of attitude to people who are fine with them.<br /> <br /> As I have noted much earlier, people have been making custom content for the games <i>without</i> any kind of guidelines for it. People were making custom content for the game back when David Hill was producing Changeling: The Lost, and any guidelines included there were far less decisive than what the current version has granted us. There is a thread in this very forum that is 39 pages long of people posting and discussing various kiths they have created for others to see for David Hill's version, and already there's a thread being made of Kiths for the current version of the game. There is even a thread for custom contracts. The guidelines we have gotten may not be idiot-proof, but they are far and away better than having nothing and are still useful.<br /> <br /> If you don't feel you can create something with the current guides, I'm sorry they don't inspire you. Talk with someone about them, work with them, or even look to the forums for something someone else has worked on. Remember that we have supplements coming out in the future that will likely address any fallacies that you find, much in the same way that &quot;Flowers of Hell&quot; added a plethora of options for Embeds, Exploits and Gadget creation for Demon: The Descent. However, please do not call them &quot;unbelievable insufficient&quot; when people have been working with much less for far longer than this campaign has been out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not using this attitude towards anyone. This is how I feel about the product. The entire point of this is to discuss how we feel about the game, and that's what we're doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T22:17:43-08:00","id":1165773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165763#post1165763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;<br /> <br /> That's a relief, now I can finally play that kith I have been dreaming about that as special ability reduces the target number of all social rolls to 5.<br /> <br /> And has a custom regalia that functions like the Shield and sword regalias all rolled up in one....but as a bonus their power level for common is the equivalent of both regalias royals and then the Royals are even better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yeah.<br /> <br /> If that's the kind of game that you want to play/run, then do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can't wait to get into an endless argument with the ST in question about how he/she should totally allow for my ideas because &quot;muh vision!&quot;. </div> </div> </div>And that is completely different issue then the viability of custom rules.<br /> <br /> Frankly, if you're picking fights with your STs or if the relationship between players and STs is that antagonistic, your table has problems. The ST and the players are supposed to be working together on this, not against each other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hell, why do I even need a 60+ dollar book to tell me to just to use my imagination and that rules don't need to constrain me? I can just use an empty box and pretend I shoot 1 hit kill lasers! *Wiiiiiii* </div> </div> </div>Also, your ridiculously over-the-top snark-asm is prompting me to not even bother to take your opinion seriously.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, but seriously quoting anything from OWoD as an argument for &quot;balance doesn't matter&quot; is the equivalent of pointing out Chernobyl as an argument for &quot;nuclear safety measure aren't needed&quot;. When it gave us some jewels like &quot;enchanting voice&quot; and &quot;purebreed&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Then you missed the point of my quote entirely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EDIT: And I am gonna add another problem with that theory of &quot; When it comes to the custom stuff, as long as the players and ST are fine with it&quot; as a DM, how do I know if I am a fine with something? If I don't have a good guide on how it should function? </div> </div> </div>You figure it out during play. If the way how the dice are coming down seems off, you adjust. Don't see what's the problem. <br /> <br /> And if you run with players or STs that get really stingy or pissed off from adjusting modifiers up and down...I really don't know what to tell you. Aside from being confused on running players that seem to have a vehement hatred for Golden Rule.<br /> <br /> Like, unhealthily so.<br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------------<br /> Really, this doesn't seem hard to me.<br /> <br /> Changeling the Lost, and the other Chronicles of Darkness games for that matter, aren't competitive games or part of organized play. It doesn't have anything like Pathfinder Society or Shadowrun Missions. There's no official space where you are required to run the rules as RAW. So no. I don't see why one needs to obsess so much over balance. Adjust if your players aren't happy with a certain aspect of your custom, and keep going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T01:58:20-08:00","id":1165791,"title":"","content":"Also, something I've found frustrating in all this, is that there's this weird &quot;never good enough&quot; attitude around homebrew guidelines.<br /> <br /> If you're going to homebrew, you have to eventually get used to taking off the training wheels. Homebrewing custom content is a skill that grows and develops with practice. No matter how much page space CtL 2e puts into it, and supplements put into it, and so on, if you're going to make your own stuff, you've got to eventually do it enough that you start to get a feel for what's right for you and your group.<br /> <br /> No set of homebrew guidelines, and series of examples, and so on, is ever going to do that for you. At some point you just have to start homebrewing, accept that you'll make some mistakes, and learn and etc.<br /> <br /> The point of, &quot;don't worry about balance,&quot; is not, &quot;make whatever gonzo craziness you can to exploit the system,&quot; but to not get stressed over things like, &quot;is this subset of a Skill to get exceptional success on 3 instead of 5 successes just the right amount of broadness.&quot; Or to allow yourself to break a &quot;rule&quot; for something when it just makes sense. Like if I'm making a Weaponmaster Kith, it's not going to break the game if the 3 success for exceptional bonus gets linked to a preferred weapon selected at creation instead of a single Skill. Most of the time it's effectively one Skill anyway, but it means a Weaponmaster of archery can be a good archer with Athletics, Firearms, or Survival as bows straddle a few Skills like that. Yes it's &quot;breaking the rule,&quot; but it's why they're guidelines not hard rules. So you can make that kind of judgement call for something that's fun to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T03:13:06-08:00","id":1165802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165767#post1165767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get you guys are frustrated with the current guidelines. As I've noted, I'd have preferred something more robust. However, there's no reason to be using that kind of attitude to people who are fine with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what? You are right, that came out very harshly and I apologize. It just incredibly frustrating to get my issues dismissed as &quot;well don't worry about balance&quot;. When you do worry about it, is like saying &quot;don't worry about your broken leg&quot; or &quot;don't worry about sexism and/or any other kind of ism&quot; when you do worry about that stuff.<br /> <br /> But here is the main thing, my complaint is not about homebrewing something very &quot;out of the game&quot; like making up my own auspice or making up my own clan. Things that, yeah it goes beyond the core premise of the game.<br /> <br /> But instead is about having to homebrewing stuff that are part of the core premise of the game (tokens and Seeming benefits).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165791#post1165791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No set of homebrew guidelines, and series of examples, and so on, is ever going to do that for you..</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what would have been enough? Each contract having 6 seeming benefits and a guide to make tokens (put them in the companion) ala Lore of the forsaken with fetish that has a dot by dot of what effect it can have. It's not like I want to homebrew stuff, I actively hate to having to homebrew powers and I am sick of OPP forcing me to do so by not updating stuff and just shoving more and more &quot;location/time&quot; write up.<br /> <br /> If OPP had released all the gifts missing updates in Forsaken. And put the courts (directional, dawn/dusk, day and night) and update from 1st. Then that's all I need. I would use that and tell anyone with a homebrew coming to my table &quot;No, pick from the game and that's it&quot;.<br /> <br /> I am not complaining that the game doesn't let me do something so out of place that &quot;Sure no homebrewing guidelines would be enough&quot; but stuff that are A) Very basic and B) We don't get ANY guidelines whatsoever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165773#post1165773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So no. I don't see why one needs to obsess so much overbalance. Adjust if your players aren't happy with a certain aspect of your custom, and keep going.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because as the problem comes from the player being happy and the Dm not. Or vice-versa.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165773#post1165773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you missed the point of my quote entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't miss your point, just pointing out that quotes come from a game whose system is notoriously easy to break and which even people who like the game admit the system is godawful. Again is like hearing from the soviet union on the unimportance of safety measure on the nuclear plant during Chernobyl.<br /> <br /> So there is little to do in the end more than A) Voting with my wallet and not supporting system design laziness. B) Telling people I know to not buy OPP products for the same reason. C) Keep bringing up this issue until OPP maybe, hopefully, change their design philosophy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 12-07-2017, 06:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T03:25:54-08:00","id":1165805,"title":"","content":"It is annoying that if you take a contract that isn't from your seeming's regalia you have a 80% chance of needing to homebrew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T03:28:47-08:00","id":1165806,"title":"","content":"I'm not a big homebrewer, but I've thrown my hat in now and then with 1st edition; I created a decent contract and a new kith. The contract was tough but not a huge headache. I get that people want clear, robust and detailed rules for making their own stuff, and I'll grant you that the rules given could definitely be better, but as written, I think they're good enough to at least provide a starting point. Though I agree that they should definitely have done a better job of showing how the rules apply to already existing contracts-court related stuff in particular.<br /> <br /> That being said, I can see where people are coming from with their dissatisfaction. I was excited by the Underhill version to make my own courts, and the rules we have now are definitely not as clear and efficient as those ones. That's only to be expected considering court creation is no longer a vital part of the game, but the point still stands; people had their hopes up-not unreasonably-that they'd be able to do something to a degree that it turns out they won't be able to do. But this is all just my two cents on the matter.<br /> <br /> What I guess I'm really trying to say is that if your're not happy about the rules given, that's fine and reasonable and I'm sorry that you feel the way you do. If you're happy about what we have, then great, I am too.<br /> <br /> (And they really should have put some actual rules for designing Tokens. I feel as though they intended Tokens to be far-reaching and very flexible, but leaving GMs totally afloat isn't the best rout to take.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165805#post1165805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is annoying that if you take a contract that isn't from your seeming's regalia you have a 80% chance of needing to homebrew.</div> </div> </div> </div> I assumed the seeming bonus to contracts was just meant for those specific seemings. Maybe I missed something, but I didn't think you were strictly meant to design bonuses for them-they were just incentives for those seemings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","user":"Lady Gray","date":". 12-07-2017, 06:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","name":"Lady Gray","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T04:05:09-08:00","id":1165812,"title":"","content":"Now that I've had a chance to read it, I can actually comment on some content-things -<br /> I think the biggest thing the homebrew chapter is missing is worked examples, using one of the published contract/court/kith sets as a way to mechanically build using these guidelines. While they're not core-books, both Equinox Road in 1E (Courts and Contracts) and Demon's Storyteller's Guide (Interlocks) had some very nice worked examples which actually explained the reasoning behind the design choices made for those examples. Particular shout out to the Reflections contract series, it's a player favourite.<br /> <br /> Ultimately the big problem is that it's there's the broad guidelines and the end results (e.g. the published contract/court/kith sets) and there's no guidance on how to get from the start point (general guidelines) to the endpoint (functional game mechanic) and why you'd make certain decisions. And I say this as someone who's happy homebrewing anything, ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T04:22:22-08:00","id":1165814,"title":"","content":"nevermind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 12-07-2017, 08:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T04:46:11-08:00","id":1165823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lady Gray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165806#post1165806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assumed the seeming bonus to contracts was just meant for those specific seemings. Maybe I missed something, but I didn't think you were strictly meant to design bonuses for them-they were just incentives for those seemings.</div> </div> </div> </div>It says that the two shown are examples iirc and that GMs should feel free to add additional ones for the other seemings (presumably because writing six of them for each arcadian contract would take up much more time and space than just thinking up a seeming benefit for the seeming associated with it's regalia + a single other thematic seeming).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T07:06:29-08:00","id":1165859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165812#post1165812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that I've had a chance to read it, I can actually comment on some content-things -<br /> I think the biggest thing the homebrew chapter is missing is worked examples, using one of the published contract/court/kith sets as a way to mechanically build using these guidelines. While they're not core-books, both Equinox Road in 1E (Courts and Contracts) and Demon's Storyteller's Guide (Interlocks) had some very nice worked examples which actually explained the reasoning behind the design choices made for those examples. Particular shout out to the Reflections contract series, it's a player favourite.<br /> <br /> Ultimately the big problem is that it's there's the broad guidelines and the end results (e.g. the published contract/court/kith sets) and there's no guidance on how to get from the start point (general guidelines) to the endpoint (functional game mechanic) and why you'd make certain decisions. And I say this as someone who's happy homebrewing anything, ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see where you're coming from with this. Do you think that it would help anyone if I worked their Windwing example? It wouldn't be official, but it would connect to the section anyway. I could even work my Chirurgeon update while I'm at it, to show one that doesn't follow the rules precisely. I'm willing to do this, although it might take a few days to get it up, as I'm currently out of town for my brother's wedding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T08:14:47-08:00","id":1165876,"title":"","content":"Also for the record, the only problem that I don't think can be remedied is the court contract balance. (Because even with a team of professional developers on hand every step of the way, designing 2 disciplines worth of powers still requires a fair amount of effort.)<br /> <br /> The solution to the kith problem really is just &quot;publish more kiths.&quot; I don't actually need infinite kiths, I just want there to be an evocative choice for most characters, and we lack options for &quot;made of tough stuff&quot; or &quot;one with nature.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't need every possible mantle bonus broken down, but more than a few paragraphs would be appreciated to help ensure that each court is distinct and interesting to play, rather than just reskinned versions of each other. (also maybe some example effects for the 5th dot that are modular, because &quot;unique supernatural effect&quot; doesn't really offer much to work from.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T09:07:26-08:00","id":1165884,"title":"","content":"Soooo... It looks like <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/DarkerDaysRadio/posts/10154814913091076\" target=\"_blank\">Darker Days Radio is interviewing Meghan</a> on Saturday. If you've got Changeling questions, go post them on DDR's facebook!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T09:09:41-08:00","id":1165885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165758#post1165758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suddenly I'm less apprehensive about presenting any potential Changeling ST with my idea for a custom merit to produce ink from his claws and fingers...and have a desire to purchase Changeling: The Dreaming 20th anniversary edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>C20 is excellent and worth your time. It's a game about bittersweet truth also, but in a very different way from its Chronicles of Darkness cousin.<br /> <br /> And for what it's worth, I wouldn't disallow the ink. Seems like something that would be fun to hash out as a custom kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13580-hsienfan","name":"Hsienfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T11:29:44-08:00","id":1165902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165802#post1165802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because as the problem comes from the player being happy and the Dm not. Or vice-versa.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then the ST and the player compromise and works something out so both parties are happy.<br /> <br /> Simple enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't miss your point, just pointing out that quotes come from a game whose system is notoriously easy to break and which even people who like the game admit the system is godawful. Again is like hearing from the soviet union on the unimportance of safety measure on the nuclear plant during Chernobyl. </div> </div> </div>You're still missing the point.<br /> <br /> The point wasn't to compare the two different core systems of WoD and CofD. The point was to point out the side-bar of &quot;player and ST fun should come first over game balance&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, I fundamentally disagree with the notion that you seem to have that CofD is ripe for easy meta-gaming when it's not. D&amp;D and Pathfinder are over there, not here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T13:19:40-08:00","id":1165923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165859#post1165859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can see where you're coming from with this. Do you think that it would help anyone if I worked their Windwing example? It wouldn't be official, but it would connect to the section anyway. I could even work my Chirurgeon update while I'm at it, to show one that doesn't follow the rules precisely. I'm willing to do this, although it might take a few days to get it up, as I'm currently out of town for my brother's wedding.</div> </div> </div> </div>I for one, absolutely think that would help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T13:25:42-08:00","id":1165926,"title":"","content":"The expanded stuff on Fetches and Bridgeburners is pretty great! I have several ideas for Bridgeburners that might make compelling post-fetch level antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T13:49:11-08:00","id":1165937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165926#post1165926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The expanded stuff on Fetches and Bridgeburners is pretty great! I have several ideas for Bridgeburners that might make compelling post-fetch level antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div> Fetches grow in power with you, so I don't think there is a Fetch level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T14:00:49-08:00","id":1165942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165859#post1165859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can see where you're coming from with this. Do you think that it would help anyone if I worked their Windwing example? It wouldn't be official, but it would connect to the section anyway. I could even work my Chirurgeon update while I'm at it, to show one that doesn't follow the rules precisely. I'm willing to do this, although it might take a few days to get it up, as I'm currently out of town for my brother's wedding.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that'd be fantastic.<br /> <br /> All systems have a lot of baked in assumptions that aren't necessarily player facing, so even just working through the assumptions (like when the various CoD combat discussions come up, the idea that dicepools are deliberately engineered to be low so you burn willpower constantly) makes it easier to design things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T14:53:35-08:00","id":1165952,"title":"","content":"Okay, I'll start working on it and post it up when I'm able. Hopefully that will help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T15:55:23-08:00","id":1165964,"title":"","content":"We are in the last six days, hopefully it goes really well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T16:38:56-08:00","id":1165973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165937#post1165937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fetches grow in power with you, so I don't think there is a Fetch level.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, I thought about that after I posted. Its hard to really place a Fetch anywhere on the 'Scale' of power-level. But that brings me to one of the things I love about the new Fetches: their scalability! If the players don't really want to do the interpersonal fresh-outa-hedge Fetch stories but aren't adverse to the Fetch being involved at somepoint, they're just as viable for emotional drama later in the story as they are just out of the gate!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T16:56:53-08:00","id":1165975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165937#post1165937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fetches grow in power with you</div> </div> </div> </div>Which manuscript preview is this in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-07-2017, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T17:10:38-08:00","id":1165978,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> the third.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T17:14:29-08:00","id":1165979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165978#post1165978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> the third.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.<br /> <br /> As an aside to the powers that be. A finished 'just text' document would be super cool to have from these Kickstarters. Truly the Chronicles and World of Darkness would not be what it is without its art, but as someone who's carrying a lot of books on their ereader the big pdfs are a slog and they don't translate art well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T17:19:06-08:00","id":1165980,"title":"","content":"My biggest complaint is something else:<br /> <br /> No Entitlements! Seriously, where are the Entitlements?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T17:47:47-08:00","id":1165984,"title":"","content":"Fetches had Wyrd equal to their Changeling counterparts in first edition too, they always scaled with the player. To an extent, anyway. Echoes aren't as powerful as Contracts, generally speaking, no access to Mantle and limited access to other supernatural merits, etc. Come to think of it, it's slightly odd that a Changeling who focuses on expanding her repetoire widens the power gap with the Fetch much more quickly than one who just pumps Wyrd.<br /> <br /> Although speaking of Mantle I'm still curious whether Court Goodwill can get a fetch access to the secondhand Mantle blessings. Or Fae Touched, for that matter. I quite like them, and while the merit is never mentioned directly by name the paragraphs under the Courts heading imply that they are eligible, even likely to acquire dots of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T17:53:41-08:00","id":1165985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165980#post1165980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest complaint is something else:<br /> <br /> No Entitlements! Seriously, where are the Entitlements?</div> </div> </div> </div>The expanded breadth of oath benefits and the establishment of oath-forged tokens as a core thing go a fair ways, as does the new precedent of Merits with Mantle prerequisites.<br /> <br /> An entitlement was pretty much always an unlocalized motley with proprietary resources and an associated oath in practice; 2e's given plenty of concrete ways to get changelings into trouble without adding a heightened rate of narrative interest to a purpose-built social grouping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T19:32:46-08:00","id":1165999,"title":"","content":"Entitlements expanded in the Companion was also the first stretch goal. So we're going to get info on them soon enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T19:34:39-08:00","id":1166001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165980#post1165980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest complaint is something else:<br /> <br /> No Entitlements! Seriously, where are the Entitlements?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the companion, it was the first stretch goal.<br /> <br /> I find the whole &quot;changeling can escape any bonds by 1 glamour&quot; ability weird. Aside that it makes grapple and grapple relating merit completely useless. It seems weird that are various contracts and kith ability that boost on grapple. <br /> <br /> Personally I know that ability will go in the trashcan alongside the new pledge, clarity and dream systems. But still very weird thing to add. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T19:42:19-08:00","id":1166002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165985#post1165985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An entitlement was pretty much always an unlocalized motley with proprietary resources and an associated oath in practice; 2e's given plenty of concrete ways to get changelings into trouble without adding a heightened rate of narrative interest to a purpose-built social grouping.</div> </div> </div> </div>But... But I like heightened rates of narrative influence over tiny things! I'm not sure what it means, but it sounds like exactly what I've been missing from the new books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10825-crosswords","name":"Crosswords","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T19:48:37-08:00","id":1166005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1166001#post1166001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the companion, it was the first stretch goal.<br /> <br /> I find the whole &quot;changeling can escape any bonds by 1 glamour&quot; ability weird. Aside that it makes grapple and grapple relating merit completely useless. It seems weird that are various contracts and kith ability that boost on grapple.<br /> <br /> Personally I know that ability will go in the trashcan alongside the new pledge, clarity and dream systems. But still very weird thing to add.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps that means we shouldn't consist grapples bonds for that purpose. Certainly adds more credence to the image of a Huntsman dragging a changeling back through the Hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T20:34:35-08:00","id":1166013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crosswords</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1166002#post1166002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But... But I like heightened rates of narrative influence over tiny things! I'm not sure what it means, but it sounds like exactly what I've been missing from the new books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dropped a key phrase from that sentence, as sometimes happens when I'm fussing over word order:<br /> <br /> The purely narratively-backed priority of attention the Fae gave to a character who belonged to a noble order is the nearest thing to a unique quality of entitlements in an edition where unique oath-based tokens and powers are commonplace and the benefits of the broader-scale changeling social apparatus can just <i>fall off</i> in the event of excessive debts.<br /> <br /> I would rather we have the stronger emphasis on how goblins interact with changeling society be in the corebook than entitlements if I had to pick between the two, because one of these things informs the wider world of the setting and one is a more exclusive layer of the symbolic dressings that Courts and pledgecraft already get into.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1166001#post1166001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the whole &quot;changeling can escape any bonds by 1 glamour&quot; ability weird. Aside that it makes grapple and grapple relating merit completely useless. It seems weird that are various contracts and kith ability that boost on grapple.</div> </div> </div> </div>It specifically requires a Clash of Wills to beat magically-backed bindings and costs Glamour for every use, and changelings do not exclusively use their abilities on other changelings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1166005#post1166005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certainly adds more credence to the image of a Huntsman dragging a changeling back through the Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Huntsmen have the capacity for a Dread Power that specifically counts as the hardest counter to portaling's grapple-escape that exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-07-2017, 11:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T00:34:35-08:00","id":1166034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165980#post1165980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest complaint is something else:<br /> <br /> No Entitlements! Seriously, where are the Entitlements?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sounds like you're feeling a bit... entitled... to entitlements.<br /> <br /> (I'll see myself out. And take the Scarecrow Ministry with me)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T03:28:25-08:00","id":1166045,"title":"","content":"We are less than $700 till expanded Courts in Companion!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T05:05:40-08:00","id":1166059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1166001#post1166001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I find the whole &quot;changeling can escape any bonds by 1 glamour&quot; ability weird. Aside that it makes grapple and grapple relating merit completely useless. It seems weird that are various contracts and kith ability that boost on grapple.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, its not as bad as all that. Changelings rarely end up in combat (and thus grappling) with other Lost - usually, we're talking some variation of hobs, dream critters, mirror folk, huntsmen, mortals and the like. And Portaling (which is apparently the term for opening gateways as well as slipping bonds) is unique to changelings. Arguably not apply to Loyalists, as they might not have escaped, and thus haven't &quot;forged a Contract with Faerie itself, so that not even dreams can hold them prisoner.&quot; In either case, my point remains - the overwhelming majority of opponents the PCs will face won't have innate, anti-grapple abilities. <br /> <br /> So, not really useless. And, in the case of the three contracts (might of the terrible brute, growth of ivy, beast clause of boon of the scuttling spider) and the one kith (gristlegrinder), there's still Clash of Wills in the case of using it against other changelings. And, as the ST, you can throw enough dice on the NPC's clash pool to make it stick if you really want/need to. Or just have them use an iron chain as an assist - that will put an end to portaling real quick. You're probably going to need iron in the first place - all darklings turn intangible as part of their seeming, and there are numerous abilities that have a similar effect. Huntsmen already have powers that specifically act like iron for purposes of capturing changelings, so that's not an issue there.<br /> <br /> You're mostly going to see this come into play when changelings deal with mortals that don't know better. Get in trouble with the police or kidnapped? Slip away. That's going to come with story complications of its own, but hardly a powerful ability - escaping mortal captivity is not exactly rocket science for supernaturals. Its a neat, thematic ability that really doesn't have that big of an effect on major threats, but potentially interesting story hooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T05:53:15-08:00","id":1166068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1166059#post1166059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, its not as bad as all that. Changelings rarely end up in combat (and thus grappling) with other Lost - usually, we're talking some variation of hobs, dream critters, mirror folk, huntsmen, mortals and the like.<br /> <br /> <br /> And Portaling (which is apparently the term for opening gateways as well as slipping bonds) is unique to changelings. Arguably not apply to Loyalists, as they might not have escaped, and thus haven't &quot;forged a Contract with Faerie itself, so that not even dreams can hold them prisoner.&quot; In either case, my point remains - the overwhelming majority of opponents the PCs will face won't have innate, anti-grapple abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, not in my games. Lost vs Lost is the standard for my games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1166059#post1166059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're mostly going to see this come into play when changelings deal with mortals that don't know better. Get in trouble with the police or kidnapped? Slip away. That's going to come with story complications of its own, but hardly a powerful ability - escaping mortal captivity is not exactly rocket science for supernaturals. Its a neat, thematic ability that really doesn't have that big of an effect on major threats, but potentially interesting story hooks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont really use humans in my games as much. Its a matter of personal taste honestly, the ammount of work i have to put to work around the ability far surpass any thematic benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T06:08:47-08:00","id":1166074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165980#post1165980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest complaint is something else:<br /> <br /> No Entitlements! Seriously, where are the Entitlements?</div> </div> </div> </div> The Changeling Companion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1166045#post1166045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are less than $700 till expanded Courts in Companion!</div> </div> </div> </div> The stretch goals after that are Summer Novella at $134,000, then $136,000 is Dancers at Dusk joining the Arcadian Memories Bundle, then at $142,000 Shield Kith chapter for Kith and Kin. <br /> <br /> In the comments section James has said he plans on Steed at $150,000 and Sword at $157,000. So pray we hit at least $157,000, which is not that much higher then demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 12-08-2017, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T10:08:02-08:00","id":1166117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1165371#post1165371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Customization rules are pretty much exactly what I feared them to be. They break down the necessary considerations well enough but ultimately a Storyteller is going to have be eyeballing a bunch of mechanics and hoping they didn't inadvertently create something too weak/powerful. Nothing here is crunchy or well defined enough to bypass the usual obstacles to implementing custom material.<br /> <br /> Please don't take this to mean that I actively dislike the product as a whole, but all prior complaints stand. Maybe we'll get something better if we hit the corresponding stretch goal for the companion book.</div> </div> </div> </div> There maybe something more meaty in the companion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T12:17:39-08:00","id":1166143,"title":"","content":"we hit the stretchgoal! 130,000 get!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12235-emmens","name":"emmens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12235_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T12:44:37-08:00","id":1166145,"title":"","content":"Up next the last of the Novellas, Summer at $134,000! <br /> <br /> After that Dancers at Dusk for the Arcadian Memories Bundle at $136,000.<br /> <br /> And Kiths and Kin Shield section at $142,000.<br /> <br /> I hope we get at least $160,000 for the whole kick starter by the end, the trending on the Kicktraq suggests it will, although the projection is more pessimistic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T12:55:35-08:00","id":1166148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1166145#post1166145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Up next the last of the Novellas, Summer at $134,000! <br /> <br /> After that Dancers at Dusk for the Arcadian Memories Bundle at $136,000.<br /> <br /> And Kiths and Kin Shield section at $142,000.<br /> <br /> I hope we get at least $160,000 for the whole kick starter by the end, the trending on the Kicktraq suggests it will, although the projection is more pessimistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>The projections really aren't good at predicting the last couple days though and the surge in pledges that usually accompanies them. The algorithm they use is based off of how many dollars were received the previous day. So a projection on a slow day will be lower than a projection on a high day. $160,000 should be doable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T15:04:05-08:00","id":1166167,"title":"","content":"After reading the preview, it seems we lost quite a bit of the original changes that appeared in the old Open Development posts, which is unfortuante. Still the current content isn't bad, though I was horrified at the disappearance of so many kiths, and disappointed that we don't get the Dual Kiths merit while Enchanting Performance doesn't really deserve its name anymore.<br /> <br /> Also some things could be phrased more clearly, especially when it come to Seeming Blessings and Contracts.<br /> For example, can Darkling who become smoke or light move in this form? Can they be damaged? is it an Instant or a Reflexive action? or can the Talon and Wing Contract actually allow a Changeling to swim or fly or does it just make them faster?<br /> <br /> On the good side: the Elemental Warrior merit made it! Yay! the Seemings are way better mechanically than they were and are still very interesting fluff wise; Goblin debt is a really cool concept, as are Goblin Queens; the Fae-touched are a good addition; the new Bedlam mechanics are an improvement; Clarity has become rather more interesting.<br /> <br /> All in all, the game looks rather good, and my only big complaint is the dearth of Kiths.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T16:39:26-08:00","id":1166192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1166167#post1166167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All in all, the game looks rather good, and my only big complaint is the dearth of Kiths.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if it helps, the forums are trying to convert some of the old ones to the new format.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T17:13:58-08:00","id":1166199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1166148#post1166148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The projections really aren't good at predicting the last couple days though and the surge in pledges that usually accompanies them. The algorithm they use is based off of how many dollars were received the previous day. So a projection on a slow day will be lower than a projection on a high day. $160,000 should be doable.</div> </div> </div> </div> Glad to hear it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T17:19:17-08:00","id":1166200,"title":"","content":"Based on previous OPP kickstarters it seems reasonably likely that Changeling will at least make it to 150 if the last three days experience the usual closing surge. I don't know about 157, we might end up with one regalia missing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T19:05:39-08:00","id":1166223,"title":"","content":"For the customisation of kith i am somewhat okay. Honestly i suck at mechanics but knowing i have access to the forum does lessen the worry.<br /> I understand much better by actually doing it so i'll try to make a kith.<br /> <br /> Lets see, in the last changeling (1e) that i ran i had a npc that i quite that didnt really fit the kith given in the core so i'll go with that.<br /> <br /> The character is Grand P\u00e8re l'horloge (translate to grandfather clock). In 1e i had him as a manikin elemental with 'time' as his element for the contracts. <br /> For 2e i'll call the kith the timekeepers (why not, i'm not great at names but i like it). Taken by the True Fae for the purpose of observing and managing time. Now it seems simple but in Arcadia one can imagine that time is ... wonky to say the least. The character was put in charge of managing a big clock, for example when something broke he would have to replace it with a part of him. Eventually he escaped and found out he was as much clockwork clock as he was a man. Which doesn't exactly make sense since he was losing part for the clock, maybe the clock gained his memories and think it is him?<br /> I can imagine a few seeming that would work so that is nice. Heck even Beast would work if you go that you had to hunt down 'time' when it escape from the clock.<br /> <br /> Now for the mechanics.<br /> Kith blessing: On any craft rolls to repair or build a time piece (clock, watches, etc), achieving three success counts as a exceptionnal success.<br /> The manuscript does say that with craft since its not incredibly strong one could allow the bonus any craft specialty but for now i don't mind having it limited to time pieces.<br /> <br /> Time awareness (there has to be a better name): The timekeeper always know what the time is and how much time has passed. In the hedge or other situation where time doesnt flow linearly he can spend a glamour and roll ... wits+occult+wyrd (why not) to know how much time has passed both in the hedge and ironside.<br /> This feels... weak? so maybe remove the glamour cost? But the manuscript says that the trickery power require a glamour cost. <br /> <br /> All in all i have to say that i am not exactly feeling confident that i can make a satisfying kith only with the guidelines in the corebook. Like i said above, it doesn't matter much since i have access to many amazing people that are way better than i am at the mechanical side of things in this forum. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T20:14:18-08:00","id":1166231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1166223#post1166223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the customisation of kith i am somewhat okay. Honestly i suck at mechanics but knowing i have access to the forum does lessen the worry.<br /> I understand much better by actually doing it so i'll try to make a kith.<br /> <br /> Lets see, in the last changeling (1e) that i ran i had a npc that i quite that didnt really fit the kith given in the core so i'll go with that.<br /> <br /> The character is Grand P\u00e8re l'horloge (translate to grandfather clock). In 1e i had him as a manikin elemental with 'time' as his element for the contracts.<br /> For 2e i'll call the kith the timekeepers (why not, i'm not great at names but i like it). Taken by the True Fae for the purpose of observing and managing time. Now it seems simple but in Arcadia one can imagine that time is ... wonky to say the least. The character was put in charge of managing a big clock, for example when something broke he would have to replace it with a part of him. Eventually he escaped and found out he was as much clockwork clock as he was a man. Which doesn't exactly make sense since he was losing part for the clock, maybe the clock gained his memories and think it is him?<br /> I can imagine a few seeming that would work so that is nice. Heck even Beast would work if you go that you had to hunt down 'time' when it escape from the clock.<br /> <br /> Now for the mechanics.<br /> Kith blessing: On any craft rolls to repair or build a time piece (clock, watches, etc), achieving three success counts as a exceptionnal success.<br /> The manuscript does say that with craft since its not incredibly strong one could allow the bonus any craft specialty but for now i don't mind having it limited to time pieces.<br /> <br /> Time awareness (there has to be a better name): The timekeeper always know what the time is and how much time has passed. In the hedge or other situation where time doesnt flow linearly he can spend a glamour and roll ... wits+occult+wyrd (why not) to know how much time has passed both in the hedge and ironside.<br /> This feels... weak? so maybe remove the glamour cost? But the manuscript says that the trickery power require a glamour cost.<br /> <br /> All in all i have to say that i am not exactly feeling confident that i can make a satisfying kith only with the guidelines in the corebook. Like i said above, it doesn't matter much since i have access to many amazing people that are way better than i am at the mechanical side of things in this forum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, if you don't mind, maybe any craft roll to repair or build &quot;Clockwork&quot;? Which will still MOSTLY be time pieces, but could be other things (I actually read a piece where clockwork was used to make 3-D printed non-electronic devices capable of interacting with wireless internet, through use of springs, cogs, and the like).<br /> <br /> I think Time Awareness is particularly weak, I think it should offer that result as a costless bonus. If you don't mind me making a suggestion... how about the roll (and expenditure of glamour) letting you DECIDE on how long had passed (within reason, which can be negotiated with the GM) while in such a location?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T20:26:51-08:00","id":1166234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1166231#post1166231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, if you don't mind, maybe any craft roll to repair or build &quot;Clockwork&quot;? Which will still MOSTLY be time pieces, but could be other things (I actually read a piece where clockwork was used to make 3-D printed non-electronic devices capable of interacting with wireless internet, through use of springs, cogs, and the like).<br /> <br /> I think Time Awareness is particularly weak, I think it should offer that result as a costless bonus. If you don't mind me making a suggestion... how about the roll (and expenditure of glamour) letting you DECIDE on how long had passed (within reason, which can be negotiated with the GM) while in such a location?</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like those suggestions. Thank you. <br /> I'll probably work a bit more on the kith and post it in the kith making thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T11:14:02-08:00","id":1166501,"title":"","content":"We just hit $134k. And so the seasons are complete as we now have the Summer novella.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T15:55:02-08:00","id":1166553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbco