n they hold glamour and their fuel is at the same time to the same limit?<br /> Or does their pool have to be used for both now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T06:19:18-08:00","id":1180147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1180097#post1180097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK so I've been wondering something about Hedge Denizen condition.<br /> What about the non-changelings? <br /> How much glamour can they hold?<br /> Do they become Wyrd 1 Hobgoblins?<br /> Because the wording implies they have a way to use glamour and I'm wonder what exactly that is.<br /> And what of other supernaturals that becomes Hobgoblins, what happens to their power trait? <br /> Can they hold glamour and their fuel is at the same time to the same limit?<br /> Or does their pool have to be used for both now?</div> </div> </div> </div> These are important questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T08:44:16-08:00","id":1180175,"title":"","content":"Making a note for the future errata thread: Unless changeling Touchstones are supposed to work dramatically differently from other monsters', Clarity attack rolls should probably receive a +2 dice bonus when the changeling has no Touchstones <i>at all</i> rather than no <i>attached</i> Touchstones, as per <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zXoidmr88S_my76fkV-ITr27wHSdtVdeFMfcpXMkhY4/edit#heading=h.w7029yo7yepq\" target=\"_blank\">the Vampire FAQ</a>; the consequences of having no attached Touchstone has generally been &quot;you lose the bonus due to insufficient maintenance&quot; rather than &quot;the bonus turns into a penalty,&quot; with the latter instead being a consequence of outright losing your ties to the wider world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T11:38:27-08:00","id":1180209,"title":"","content":"For Environmental Tilts created by Contracts, how powerful is the effect? # of Successes?<br /> <br /> Overall, Contracts are pretty well written and balanced, but there are some outliers that may warrent another look.<br /> <br /> Some of the Wizened Seeming bonuses completely remove size restrictions. Does this mean Tattermedalion's Workshop with both blessings can blow up a balloon until it is a functioning Deathstar or other planet sized things. They can also change the appearance of the entire planet. Even barring the insane, this allows for buildings, monuments, etc. Shouldn't it have *some* size limitation?<br /> <br /> You run into a similar issue with Loopholes on Contracts that have a scaling effect based on the Glamour spent. Elemental Fury allows you to, with the loophole, blanket the entire planet in every environmental tilt simultaniously. Even barring apocalyptic uses, dropping *every* environmental tilt for free on a &quot;large enough&quot; area feels disproportionately strong.<br /> <br /> Changeling Hours is definately better than the playtest, but it runs into some serious balance issues. I don't see anything stopping you from freezing someone's shirt in time, effectively trapping them. I also dont see anything stopping an Air Elemental from trapping people inside solid blocks of impennitrable air. Changelings themselves can clash against this effect, true, but almost anything else is screwed.<br /> <br /> Hidden Reality is a plotbuster, as written. You can just conveniently find a signed confession of the killer or some other really easy clue to solve the plot. You could argue that a changeling can't create something based on information they don't know, but then how could they create carkeys with ridges in a pattern they don't know, or a functioning gun when they arent a master gunsmith?<br /> <br /> Stealing the Solid Reflection with both seeming blessings seems to let you copy fully powered supernatural creatures. Is that the intent?<br /> <br /> Whispers of Morning still allows a Changeling easy access to reflexively going incorporeal. Is that less of a problem in actual play than it seems on paper?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 01-28-2018, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T12:18:09-08:00","id":1180220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1180209#post1180209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of the Wizened Seeming bonuses completely remove size restrictions. Does this mean Tattermedalion's Workshop with both blessings can blow up a balloon until it is a functioning Deathstar or other planet sized things.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. The Build Equipment action, of which Jury Rigging is a subset and which Tatterdemalion's Workshop operates as, is still subject to the need for materials (not necessarily <i>proper</i> materials, but the Contract very specifically works in a way that requires you to be working <i>with materials</i>) and the limits of adding features, to say nothing of how a balloon is not a complex object and there is no &quot;normal version&quot; of a planet-sized object for the product to work as well as.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They can also change the appearance of the entire planet. Even barring the insane, this allows for buildings, monuments, etc. Shouldn't it have *some* size limitation? </div> </div> </div>Let's talk for a moment about how you're applying a Contract that affects a mundane item by mimicking some of a discrete actor's process to a thing that no non-hyper-exceptional changeling could possibly work in a <i>scene</i>, much less an instant action.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You run into a similar issue with Loopholes on Contracts that have a scaling effect based on the Glamour spent. Elemental Fury allows you to, with the loophole, blanket the entire planet in every environmental tilt simultaniously. Even barring apocalyptic uses, dropping *every* environmental tilt for free on a &quot;large enough&quot; area feels disproportionately strong. </div> </div> </div>&quot;She may also spend additional points of Glamour&quot; suggests to me that this comes <i>after</i> the Loophole applies, even before getting into how a Loophole removes the Glamour cost for &quot;the Contract's basic effect.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Changeling Hours is definately better than the playtest, but it runs into some serious balance issues. I don't see anything stopping you from freezing someone's shirt in time, effectively trapping them. I also dont see anything stopping an Air Elemental from trapping people inside solid blocks of impennitrable air. Changelings themselves can clash against this effect, true, but almost anything else is screwed. </div> </div> </div>These are both solved by not allowing fiction-breaking things like &quot;you can affect someone's clothes to get around the person themselves being resistant to the effect&quot; and &quot;air is an element that is nigh-omnipresent, so any power that affects an element can be used anywhere.&quot;<br /> <br /> Specifically concerning the latter, we have two things to stand against it: First, that &quot;air elementals&quot; are more properly <i>wind</i> elementals or other things <i>associated with</i> air, like clouds or storms or gusts; and second, that the Elemental seeming bonus references &quot;an ever-burning flame&quot; rather than &quot;an unstoppable fire&quot; \u2014 an Elemental with Changeling Hours is going to be making breezes that keep blowing or mist that doesn't disperse, not <i>invisible walls</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hidden Reality is a plotbuster, as written. You can just conveniently find a signed confession of the killer or some other really easy clue to solve the plot. You could argue that a changeling can't create something based on information they don't know, but then how could they create carkeys with ridges in a pattern they don't know, or a functioning gun when they arent a master gunsmith? </div> </div> </div>Anything you make goes away at the end of the scene or when someone stops paying attention to it, neither of which is generally going to <i>solve</i> any give plot that doesn't rely on resolution that can be handled immediately<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Stealing the Solid Reflection with both seeming blessings seems to let you copy fully powered supernatural creatures. Is that the intent? </div> </div> </div>Costs Glamour and Willpower regardless of the Loophole, has all its stats capped by your Wyrd, and will explicitly require at least one oath to another changeling to allow you to pull it off in the first place on top of only working for a scene.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whispers of Morning still allows a Changeling easy access to reflexively going incorporeal. Is that less of a problem in actual play than it seems on paper? </div> </div> </div>I should say so. It's only reflexive if you pay Glamour and it's a Royal Contract.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T12:22:45-08:00","id":1180221,"title":"","content":"I've got questions, too, regarding some Contracts.<br /> <br /> <b>Skinmask</b> - Does the Contract allow you to pick and choose which features of the target you want? Like if you wanted to make a 'patchjob' where you took, say, that person's hair color, ethnicity, gender, etc, but kept your eye color, lip size and so on?<br /> <br /> <b>Wyrd-faced Stranger</b> - Does it work like that one Obfuscate Discipline from Vampire, where everyone sees a different person? How complete is the transformation? Does it include clothing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T12:30:12-08:00","id":1180223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1180221#post1180221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Skinmask</b> - Does the Contract allow you to pick and choose which features of the target you want? Like if you wanted to make a 'patchjob' where you took, say, that person's hair color, ethnicity, gender, etc, but kept your eye color, lip size and so on?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Copy the Mask of anyone you've physically met&quot; suggests the answer is no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Wyrd-faced Stranger</b> - Does it work like that one Obfuscate Discipline from Vampire, where everyone sees a different person? How complete is the transformation? Does it include clothing? </div> </div> </div>It specifically says that in the case of a group all observers see you as the same person and as a purely perceptual change I can't imagine the character's state of dress being specifically locked out of the lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T15:14:48-08:00","id":1180261,"title":"","content":"While we're on a roll of talking about how Contracts work, would you guys allow someone to take the attributes of a vehicle with Props And Scenery? To allow a Changeling to become a Volkswagen Beetle and drive themselves off the lot, as it were? Or would you rule the Changeling has only their own speed attribute to work off of, thus making the form utterly useless due to its size? Because I know people who would gleefully stick to the latter and then present a situation where a Changeling needs a car to do something and completely lacks one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T15:48:42-08:00","id":1180268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1180261#post1180261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While we're on a roll of talking about how Contracts work, would you guys allow someone to take the attributes of a vehicle with Props And Scenery? To allow a Changeling to become a Volkswagen Beetle and drive themselves off the lot, as it were? Or would you rule the Changeling has only their own speed attribute to work off of, thus making the form utterly useless due to its size? Because I know people who would gleefully stick to the latter and then present a situation where a Changeling needs a car to do something and completely lacks one.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a Royal Contract, you all but need the Ogre blessing to be able to turn into something the size of a car with any reliability, and the way acceleration works doesn't really present much immediate concern.<br /> <br /> That being said, the spirit of the Contract is pretty definitely not &quot;the limited mobility benefit means you can operate yourself as an inanimate object&quot; \u2014 if you've got a buddy, they can run you as a normal vehicle, but Chrysalis-for-cars this ain't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T16:31:15-08:00","id":1180281,"title":"","content":"Not sure if this is errata or a deliberate change between editions...in the section on the Hedge, it mentions that the appearance of the Hedge reacts to, among other things, a character's Wyrd, with high-Wyrd characters subconsiously shaping the Hedge around them. However, there aren't actually any systems given for that. Is this meant to be something the ST wings, or is the system missing? I ask mainly because Beast: The Primordial refers to the same mechanic (in the 1e book) for what happens when a Beast enters the Hedge. If that system is no longer in us for Changeling 2e, then I assume I needn't keep using it for Beast 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T18:40:45-08:00","id":1180313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1180281#post1180281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if this is errata or a deliberate change between editions...in the section on the Hedge, it mentions that the appearance of the Hedge reacts to, among other things, a character's Wyrd, with high-Wyrd characters subconsiously shaping the Hedge around them. However, there aren't actually any systems given for that. Is this meant to be something the ST wings, or is the system missing? I ask mainly because Beast: The Primordial refers to the same mechanic (in the 1e book) for what happens when a Beast enters the Hedge. If that system is no longer in us for Changeling 2e, then I assume I needn't keep using it for Beast 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>*compares between editions*<br /> <br /> Yeah I guess not. Unless if it's all been folded into Hedgespinning, but that's actively trying to alter the Hedge and not passively from the changeling just being there. For now it's just ST fiat and fluff to describe the scene.<br /> <br /> Could be a chance the old 1e sub-system might pop up in the upcoming Hedge sourcebook, but we'll see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T18:43:58-08:00","id":1180314,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the Death Star isn't a valid choice given that it surely has weapon and armor values greater than 5 each, let alone combined, but the lack of a size restriction and the always done in one turn still leaves a lot of room for headaches. For example, weaving an impromptu shelter in the Hedge. People have woven sticks, vines and leaves into dwellings for millennia, but being able to do so in one turn allows you to construct a prison around an enemy group with very little opportunity for them to react. <br /> <br /> I agree that the contracts where you can spend additional glamour for additional effects/targets/area almost certainly aren't intended to let you treat those values as infinite if you meet the loophole, but it would be nice to have it specified how it is supposed to work. Eh, something to ask about in the errata pass, and if we don't get an answer I have ideas on how I would run it. <br /> <br /> Speaking of stuff to remember for the errata pass, there's some discrepancy between the section on Frailties and the section on True Fae. The latter says True Fae never take bashing damage from anything but their banes... but even minor banes deal lethal damage per the information in chapter 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T19:12:00-08:00","id":1180319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1180268#post1180268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a Royal Contract, you all but need the Ogre blessing to be able to turn into something the size of a car with any reliability, and the way acceleration works doesn't really present much immediate concern.<br /> <br /> That being said, the spirit of the Contract is pretty definitely not &quot;the limited mobility benefit means you can operate yourself as an inanimate object&quot; \u2014 if you've got a buddy, they can run you as a normal vehicle, but Chrysalis-for-cars this ain't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks Satchel, that all does make sense. I'd say a Changeling in car form could still move slowly, since cars can be moved so long as the brakes aren't on, but yeah, unless driven by another person they'd not be making any high speed chases.<br /> <br /> Still, this means I can have a Changeling buddy-cop duo, one of them the cruiser and the other the driver. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T20:30:31-08:00","id":1180330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1180314#post1180314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure the Death Star isn't a valid choice given that it surely has weapon and armor values greater than 5 each, let alone combined, but the lack of a size restriction and the always done in one turn still leaves a lot of room for headaches. For example, weaving an impromptu shelter in the Hedge. People have woven sticks, vines and leaves into dwellings for millennia, but being able to do so in one turn allows you to construct a prison around an enemy group with very little opportunity for them to react.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's accelerated Jury Rigging, with all the issues that implies \u2014 a Fragile prison is going to be very little help (much less a Volatile one) even without getting into minutia like &quot;not having a Size restriction on the items you can throw together does not translate to an increase in your Speed rating.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Speaking of stuff to remember for the errata pass, there's some discrepancy between the section on Frailties and the section on True Fae. The latter says True Fae never take bashing damage from anything but their banes... but even minor banes deal lethal damage per the information in chapter 2. </div> </div> </div>It could be that the True Fae treat their frailties' damage as a category less, given that the same section specifically says that cold iron is the only thing that deals aggravated damage to them but major banes do just that; inability to heal the damage from a blow as long as you're in the presence of its cause is harm enough even without that damage being immediately life-threatening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T08:24:20-08:00","id":1180419,"title":"","content":"Couple of similar questions:<br /> 1. Does the condition of being a Changeling affect the ability to father/mother children? Sure the Changeling's actual form is an anthropomorphic candelabra, but by being Ironside they have regained traits based on their human soul... so what affects are hinted at in the books for this? ST wing it?<br /> <br /> 2. Are fetches able to father/mother offspring? They're described as accumulated sticks and mud and leaves and such, covered by a Mask, so I'm thinking... no?<br /> <br /> 3. Changelings look in a reflective surface and see their true form, not the Mask. How could they perceive their Mask? Squinting? Detailed commentary from friends?<br /> <br /> 4. Do other Changelings see through each other's Masks?<br /> <br /> 5. Do fetches see their true form, or perceive the Mask they generate? Seems odd to have fetches that don't know they're not &quot;real&quot;, if they can see through their own Mask as Changeling do (reflections). I'm thinking back to DE Lily, Sabre and Thorn fiction here, for one data point.<br /> <br /> Thanks,<br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T08:39:29-08:00","id":1180423,"title":"","content":"1: Not addressed in the released materials as of yet, but I could swear that Rose has discussed the topic before and there being a desire to not exclude players from being parents post-durance.<br /> <br /> 2: Similarly, no news on this topic as of yet.<br /> <br /> 3: A Changeling can spend a glamour to see the Mask for a few seconds, if I remember right from the Glamour section. This includes the Mask of any other Changelings.<br /> <br /> 4: Yes, they do, but they can strengthen their Mask for the scene by paying a Glamour so nobody can see their Mien, though this leave their shadow reflecting their true self for any Changelings who see it.<br /> <br /> 5: No they don't, and as far as I can tell nothing bar death will reveal a Fetch's true form to anyone. The magic that comprises a Fetch is very comprehensive and deliberate in order to make sure nobody realizes a human has been replaced, much less from the Fetch themselves, to the point that by its ommission I'm presuming a Fetch isn't even weak to iron like a Changeling is. I could swear at one point reading that a Fetch won't lose their Mask even if they travel into the Hedge, but I'm pretty sure that's not in the materials proper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T09:08:17-08:00","id":1180436,"title":"","content":"On what a Fetch is made out of, from what I read into the text, it seems that while fetches are <i>made</i> out of things like sticks and stones and broken bones they look and feel like a real person. What magic covers the parts that make a Fetch does not seem to be a Mask.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T09:19:04-08:00","id":1180439,"title":"","content":"And it seems implied that a Fae-Touched can see through the very specific Fetch of the changeling they are bound to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T10:44:30-08:00","id":1180453,"title":"","content":"While not reflected and discussed as mechanics, I believe some of the fluff makes reference to fetches making kids with their spouses. And, well, I would think the point of a fetch would be moot if they couldn't.<br /> <br /> Wouldn't be surprised if changelings-as-parents would get explored in depth in a later Heirs to Hell-esque book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T13:55:21-08:00","id":1180497,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Changelings being infertile except in exceedingly rare cases was a thing in first edition but Rose did say it was pointedly not the case now somewhere in a response. I don't think fetches were addressed there and I can't remember anything being said about their (in?)ability to conceive. <br /> <br /> In the fiction that's woven through the core it does mention a fetch and his spouse adopting, but that's circumstantial evidence at best.<br /> <br /> Personally I think the answer is &quot;usually no, but if the exception makes a better story go for it&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T15:09:02-08:00","id":1180513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1180439#post1180439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it seems implied that a Fae-Touched can see through the very specific Fetch of the changeling they are bound to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression Fae Touched could see past the Mask in all cases?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T17:51:48-08:00","id":1180552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1180513#post1180513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was under the impression Fae Touched could see past the Mask in all cases?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fetches and inactive tokens in particular are fae things whose Masks are typically stronger than average.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T19:03:28-08:00","id":1180570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1180552#post1180552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fetches and inactive tokens in particular are fae things whose Masks are typically stronger than average.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true; I had meant that Fae Touched can see through a Changeling's Mask, basically seeing what they can see, but my wording was rather vague.<br /> <br /> The main reason I see a Fae Touched being able to see past the Mask is...well, if not, what's the big problem with keeping them out of Fae dealings? If they could only see past one Changeling's Mask, one who is typically in Arcadia, then all Changelings have to deal with is a somewhat insane person with contracts and minor Fae powers a Fae Touched couldn't hope to master without tutelage from a Changeling, whom they can't identify anymore than a normal person. Fae Touched seeing past the Mask like a Changeling can, however, means they can actively seek out Changelings, making it much harder for them to be kept in the dark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T20:50:15-08:00","id":1180595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1180570#post1180570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is true; I had meant that Fae Touched can see through a Changeling's Mask, basically seeing what they can see, but my wording was rather vague.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but the reason haren brought it up was that <i>anyone</i> seeing through a fetch's Mask is unusual,* regardless of their ability to see what other fae creatures look like.<br /> <br /> *Admittedly between the highlighted potential flaws in a fetch's construction and the lack of explicit framing of its identical appearance as a form of Mask this may not hold true in 2e as it did in 1e, but the carried-over specification of tokens revealing their fae nature when active does supply a precedent for fae creations made from the inanimate to share a stronger guise of mundanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T22:32:09-08:00","id":1180613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1180595#post1180595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, but the reason haren brought it up was that <i>anyone</i> seeing through a fetch's Mask is unusual,* regardless of their ability to see what other fae creatures look like.<br /> <br /> *Admittedly between the highlighted potential flaws in a fetch's construction and the lack of explicit framing of its identical appearance as a form of Mask this may not hold true in 2e as it did in 1e, but the carried-over specification of tokens revealing their fae nature when active does supply a precedent for fae creations made from the inanimate to share a stronger guise of mundanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! I misread their post as being that a Fae Touched could only see past the Mask of the Changeling they were linked to. My bad.<br /> <br /> But in regards to a Fae Touched seeing past a particular Fetch's Mask, I don't think that would be the case. The fluff we've gotten on how a Fae Touched realizes the person they're with isn't right looks more akin to them recognising flaws more than anything else. The scent of mud even when clean, behavior or memory discrepancies, stuff that doesn't add up. From what I understand, the process isn't really seeing past the Mask, more they were perceptive of something being wrong.<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, the Mask of a Fetch is another tier compared to what Fae have; the Mask always falls when someone crosses into the Hedge, be they True Fae, Changeling or Hob. Fetch are made with the Mask in mind, so logically that would also fall if they entered it. The fact that we lack any mention of what a Fetch looks like past their human visage, and the lack of mention of any bane to iron, something universal to Fae and generally their items, makes me think that the magic that comprises a Fetch and their Mask is different to what empowers the Mask of a Changeling and their Keepers. Not unrelated, given the True Fae create Fetch to begin with, but different.<br /> <br /> However, this is all conjecture and based more on the lack of evidence than anything in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T23:38:38-08:00","id":1180629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1180497#post1180497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Changelings being infertile except in exceedingly rare cases was a thing in first edition but Rose did say it was pointedly not the case now somewhere in a response. I don't think fetches were addressed there and I can't remember anything being said about their (in?)ability to conceive.<br /> <br /> In the fiction that's woven through the core it does mention a fetch and his spouse adopting, but that's circumstantial evidence at best.<br /> <br /> Personally I think the answer is &quot;usually no, but if the exception makes a better story go for it&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Did not in 1E whole Spring Court was made when first Spring Queen wanted to conceive child after here Durance? Is it invalid legend in 2E rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T00:05:49-08:00","id":1180634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1180423#post1180423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1: Not addressed in the released materials as of yet, but I could swear that Rose has discussed the topic before and there being a desire to not exclude players from being parents post-durance.<br /> <br /> 2: Similarly, no news on this topic as of yet.<br /> <br /> 3: A Changeling can spend a glamour to see the Mask for a few seconds, if I remember right from the Glamour section. This includes the Mask of any other Changelings.<br /> <br /> 4: Yes, they do, but they can strengthen their Mask for the scene by paying a Glamour so nobody can see their Mien, though this leave their shadow reflecting their true self for any Changelings who see it.<br /> <br /> 5: No they don't, and as far as I can tell nothing bar death will reveal a Fetch's true form to anyone. The magic that comprises a Fetch is very comprehensive and deliberate in order to make sure nobody realizes a human has been replaced, much less from the Fetch themselves, to the point that by its ommission I'm presuming a Fetch isn't even weak to iron like a Changeling is. I could swear at one point reading that a Fetch won't lose their Mask even if they travel into the Hedge, but I'm pretty sure that's not in the materials proper.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could be an idea for an entitlement: an order of changeling sorcerers capturing and experimenting with Fetchs in order to discover the secret of their concealing magic, so It may be replicated for changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T06:16:46-08:00","id":1180686,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5803_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5803\" data-vbnamecard=\"5803\">Taidragon</a>! I strongly suspect the way 2e books go that the answers to my questions 1 and 2 are &quot;ST wing it.&quot; With, perhaps, a certain predisposition for fetches to be infertile.<br /> <br /> The thing about fetches as I understand them is, they are made from the scraps of the Changeling's soul left dangling on the Hedge or scraped off when their Keeper crafted a new mien, mixed up with natural bits the Keeper had laying around and glued together with very purposeful magic running off said soul bits. The point being to provide an imitation of the human sufficient to deceive mortals all the time; the fact it deceives other Fae creatures part of the time is a bonus. Since to the best of my knowledge the True Fae do not reproduce in a biological sense aside from, perhaps, specific Names they might assume, I'd expect that to be the last consideration they'd work into a Fetch.<br /> <br /> That said, there could be some really horrific stories that might come from really <b><i>wanting</i></b> to have a child as/with a fetch, especially if both are unaware of its nature. Especially good prologue material, for instance.<br /> <br /> My understanding was that Fae Touched received the Unseen Sense Merit applied to Changelings, not that they immediately and invariably pierced their Mask.<br /> <br /> Thanks again for the clarification on perceiving Masks!<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T10:34:58-08:00","id":1180801,"title":"","content":"Thinking back, fetches were addressed in first edition supplements as sometimes being able to conceive, but the children were inevitably off somehow, and could be exceedingly dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T11:27:59-08:00","id":1180818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1180801#post1180801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking back, fetches were addressed in first edition supplements as sometimes being able to conceive, but the children were inevitably off somehow, and could be exceedingly dangerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fetchspawn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T11:32:20-08:00","id":1180820,"title":"","content":"I'm still not convinced that Fetches have &quot;Masks&quot; in the first place. <br /> <br /> True the book(s) say that they are made from certain things but it never says they have a Mask at all. They simply look like the person they are impersonating. (or in other words: they don't look like what they were made of with a Mask making them look like the person they replace. They are made of weird things but simply and wholly look like the one they replace).<br /> <br /> Which makes sense because it's the Shadow (soul) that enables this in the first place. Destroying the Fetch means the Soul leaves and all that's left is the things it was made of. <br /> <br /> I don't think they ever say that a Fetch has a Mask at all (so it isn't bound by the same rules that Masks usually have. ie, it doesn't just have a stronger mask... it doesn't have a mask to &quot;see through&quot; at all).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T11:35:29-08:00","id":1180821,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">To this day my players are terrified of fetchspawns </span></span></span><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=398\" data-tempid=\"temp_398_1517340862467_822\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T12:05:50-08:00","id":1180836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1180801#post1180801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking back, fetches were addressed in first edition supplements as sometimes being able to conceive, but the children were inevitably off somehow, and could be exceedingly dangerous.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well if vampires can conceive by <b><i>wanting </i></b>it (dhampir) badly enough to twist fate and biology such that it happens, then surely Fae-mockeries such as fetch could under similar circumstances.<br /> <br /> &quot;I wanna be a real dad!&quot;<br /> /Pinocchio voice<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T15:34:09-08:00","id":1180901,"title":"","content":"The opening fiction of chapter five has the viewpoint character seeing her husband's true face reflected in the glass. It was consistently true in the fictions of first edition that Changelings and certain perceptive mortals would occasionally catch glimpses of a fetch's true makeup and it seems to have continued in second.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T16:00:41-08:00","id":1180918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1180836#post1180836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well if vampires can conceive by <b><i>wanting </i></b>it (dhampir) badly enough to twist fate and biology such that it happens, then surely Fae-mockeries such as fetch could under similar circumstances.<br /> <br /> &quot;I wanna be a real dad!&quot;<br /> /Pinocchio voice<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Child to Fetch-Dad: &quot;You're not my real dad!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-30-2018, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T16:06:25-08:00","id":1180921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1180918#post1180918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Child to Fetch-Dad: &quot;You're not my real dad!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Well I'm the best you've got, Mister!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T08:39:38-08:00","id":1181671,"title":"","content":"Sorry if this has been asked. Does anyone know when the books are going to be shipped or when we will have access to the PDFs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T10:57:22-08:00","id":1181714,"title":"","content":"Not yet, keep an eye on Monday notes and campaign emails to keep abreast of its progress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T13:12:25-08:00","id":1181773,"title":"","content":"Onyx Path has been loathe to give direct dates for such things for a long time. The production process of RPGs is much more transparent these days (not just because of Kickstarter). Back in the RPG boom where traditional print runs were still the norm, we basically knew, &quot;this product is probably in the pipeline,&quot; and then, &quot;this product is coming out on X date because they already know that's when the distributors will be getting it to stores.&quot;<br /> <br /> Seeing much more of the process is nice, but the cost of that to fans is that we don't get the, &quot;this is coming out on this date&quot; promises any more. This has only gotten more true since the new WW was started. While it impacts CofD books less, there's still the need to consult with the IP owners before progressing the product which can hold things up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T13:32:09-08:00","id":1181779,"title":"","content":"I'll say this though: past CofD corebook from a KS generally have a quicker return then, say, the WoD20 books.<br /> <br /> Edited text is already done and finalized, and all that's really left is art, layout, proof checks, and approval by nuWW before we see the Backer PDF. Which is overall generally the kind of thing that takes a few months. For instance, with Beast, it took 3 months before the Backer PDF was sent out since the end of its KS, and that had to factor in the rewriting that came due to the backlash of the KS manuscript.<br /> <br /> So, barring unusual circumstances, expect to see the CtL2 corebook PDF before the end of 2018.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 02-02-2018, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T07:32:57-08:00","id":1182591,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'd be surprised if it even took that long. But that might be because they just seem exceptionally on the ball with this one. Which is good!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T08:21:16-08:00","id":1188176,"title":"","content":"Quick question:<br /> <br /> For CtL 2e, to what extent does it invalidate material from the 1e sourcebooks? Sure--there may be mechanics changes, but I'm specifically thinking about the fluff and tone materials in things like Equinox Road and the like.<br /> <br /> What should I be worried about investing in, for compatibility purposes?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T12:15:36-08:00","id":1188255,"title":"","content":"It feels kind of weird to me that a Touchstone stays at a particular box when a Changeling's clarity amount is fluid. This means that if a Changeling starts with their Composure at a low level, their first Touchstone is going to get unhooked real darn quick when they take clarity damage, and all the other Touchstones they get will likewise stay at a relatively low level and get overwhelmed. A Changeling could start with a Clarity as low as 3, grind it up to 10 via raising their attributes, Wyrd and collecting icons, but their starting Touchstone will forever be locked at 2, and any others they collect will likewise be locked at the ones immediately after that.<br /> <br /> Granted, I doubt someone would deliberately have their starting attributes for calculating their Clarity as low as 1 each, but it still feels strange that a Touchstone can be so easily overcome even when the attributes it is based on have long outgrown that starting point. It's almost like a Changeling can grow more as a person and more established in the world, but the actual impact their touchstone has on them becomes less impactful with that growth and thus less meaningful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 02-21-2018, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T12:30:43-08:00","id":1188262,"title":"","content":"I think you should update the location of your Touchstones if you update your Composure. And I think it makes sense that Touchstones are more fragile the less Composure you have. It's not Wits or Icons that increase your connection to normality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T20:27:29-08:00","id":1188391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1188255#post1188255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Granted, I doubt someone would deliberately have their starting attributes for calculating their Clarity as low as 1 each, but it still feels strange that a Touchstone can be so easily overcome even when the attributes it is based on have long outgrown that starting point.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Easily&quot; here meaning &quot;relatively early in the worst-case scenario&quot; \u2014 your Touchstones don't detach until their corresponding boxes are marked with <i>severe</i> damage, i.e. the type of damage that takes an exceptional success on the Clarity attack roll to suffer.<br /> <br /> At the very beginning, Composure sets a changeling's Touchstones' resilience and Wits sets their capacity for more connections \u2014 Icons tack onto Wits's chunk of the track until the cap and then do most of their work providing a buffer for Kenning and recovery time and putting that much more room between you and rock bottom (which in turn gives you an excuse to leave recovering severe damage for later).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T09:19:06-08:00","id":1188535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1188391#post1188391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Easily&amp;quot; here meaning &amp;quot;relatively early in the worst-case scenario&amp;quot; \u2014 your Touchstones don't detach until their corresponding boxes are marked with <i>severe</i> damage, i.e. the type of damage that takes an exceptional success on the Clarity attack roll to suffer.<br /> <br /> At the very beginning, Composure sets a changeling's Touchstones' resilience and Wits sets their capacity for more connections \u2014 Icons tack onto Wits's chunk of the track until the cap and then do most of their work providing a buffer for Kenning and recovery time and putting that much more room between you and rock bottom (which in turn gives you an excuse to leave recovering severe damage for later).</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true. Severe damage is hard to come by unless you're already taking either some bad hits on Clarity or have taken enough for it to start rolling around and upgrading from taking it after a full row of Mild damage. However, it still feels strange that the resilience of the Touchstones is set so early on and cannot be altered later. Unlike something like a Seeming or Kith, things that cannot be permanently changed over the course of gameplay (at least not via the core book), there is mechanical weight to not having a high Composure at the start which no amount of Experience will change.<br /> <br /> All it would take is a bad roll on a Clarity attack to get Severe damage, and after that a slightly less bad roll to remove (at least the first) Touchstone from inhibiting Clarity damage. Starting with a high Composure grants a Changeling more time in this regard, or at least a higher threshold before that Touchstone is threatened. Having a low Composure means that threshold is low and stays low. Ths is something that cannot be changed over the course of the game, meaning a Changeling starting weak in that area will remain weak compared to others who started high, which goes against how the game in general runs. Players earn beats, fulfill conditions and spend Experience to shore up weak points. While Clarity can be increased by Icons with no real cost, Touchstones are simply static and vulnerable to Clarity attacks with a high initiating die pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T12:46:15-08:00","id":1188622,"title":"","content":"I'm still sure the intent is to update the position of the Touchstones along with Composure. It's just not written out because the writer probably thought it was obvious. Which doesn't mean it actually is obvious.<br /> A common problem with all CofD books is that the writer thinks something is obvious because they already have all of the information, without realising it's really not as obvious for the readers. A consequence of not having many (or possibly any) test readers (who hasn't themselves worked on the product) compared to other companies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 02-23-2018, 06:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T06:06:51-08:00","id":1188847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1188622#post1188622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A common problem with all CofD books is that the writer thinks something is obvious because they already have all of the information, without realising it's really not as obvious for the readers. A consequence of not having many (or possibly any) test readers (who hasn't themselves worked on the product) compared to other companies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and the information that the reader would need to understand is scattered throughout sections, embedded in only mildly-related sentences, and otherwise obscured--simply because the assumption was &quot;obvious&quot; during development. Half-Damned is egregious for this, of late. I really, <i>really</i> hope Changeling 2e doesn't so suffer!<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T01:14:06-08:00","id":1189364,"title":"","content":"That particular thing is something that my table has had humongous troubles with for Mage 2E, and yeah, there's an implicit expectation of familiarity that the games expect the reader to have to a more or lesser extent depending on gamelines...especially with the selection of language used for game terms. I've been on tables (including my own) that really struggled to pick up Werewolf or Mage because of a huge amount of information was not streamlined or obvious to the reader, but comparatively say, Demon has been picked up really easily.<br /> <br /> Personally one of the most useful things I discovered was a document that someone put together for each of the game lines called &quot;all x splat can do this:&quot; with a succinct one or two sentences per item list of the unique mechanics and what they do for that particular splat. Every book desperately needs a &quot;Quick Spellcasting Reference&quot; like Mage's but with the entire splat's mechanics condensed for easy reference, so I don't need to find the one sentence summary of how mage sight works or the roll for cover breaks or the requirements for shifting werewolf forms work in the pages of prose, often dozens of pages apart from each other.<br /> <br /> It'd do absolute wonders for accessibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":". 02-25-2018, 04:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T08:15:00-08:00","id":1189597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1189364#post1189364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That particular thing is something that my table has had humongous troubles with for Mage 2E, and yeah, there's an implicit expectation of familiarity that the games expect the reader to have to a more or lesser extent depending on gamelines...especially with the selection of language used for game terms. I've been on tables (including my own) that really struggled to pick up Werewolf or Mage because of a huge amount of information was not streamlined or obvious to the reader, but comparatively say, Demon has been picked up really easily.<br /> <br /> Personally one of the most useful things I discovered was a document that someone put together for each of the game lines called &quot;all x splat can do this:&quot; with a succinct one or two sentences per item list of the unique mechanics and what they do for that particular splat. Every book desperately needs a &quot;Quick Spellcasting Reference&quot; like Mage's but with the entire splat's mechanics condensed for easy reference, so I don't need to find the one sentence summary of how mage sight works or the roll for cover breaks or the requirements for shifting werewolf forms work in the pages of prose, often dozens of pages apart from each other.<br /> <br /> It'd do absolute wonders for accessibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can only dream, honestly, that Onyx Path may release 2-page (print it front and back) PDF cheat-sheets for their splats. These would make wonderful handouts and references at the table, and perhaps help aspiring Storytellers make sense of the games in terms humans understand.<br /> <br /> Case in point: I have a player who likes Mage (WoD). We're working with CofD materials and I thought--&quot;hey lets check out Mage 2e!&quot; Oh God... it... it hurts! <br /> <br /> So I'm backing away slowly and saying &quot;nice doggie&quot; long enough to find a narrative stick to beat the character's story arc to death with, at this point. <br /> <br /> At least Werewolf went from one-dimensional eco-warriors with anger issues (WoD) to half-spirits with an ecological niche and room for uncertainty. Changeling of course has homed in on its tropes and will, I believe, create more than enough opportunity to investigate mystery, as Mage would.<br /> <br /> Back to the point, however: plain language is often at a premium in the more obscure splat books, and that only <b><i>keeps</i></b> them obscure, rather then giving them the tools to shine. People &quot;get&quot; Vampire easily because we've had huge firehoses of its tropes washing over us in recent decades, through other media. Werewolf has similar, fundamental brand recognition, even if the actual game is far deeper than &quot;shapeshifting animal who will have issues in HS.&quot; (For example.)<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T08:41:40-08:00","id":1189880,"title":"","content":"I got my Arcadian Memories bundle!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://g