ain-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1238626#post1238626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would not someone have a Kith? There is no gain in this. Choosing not to have a Seeming seems a bit better, as that would prevent you from having the added weakness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d imagine the option was included for those who can\u2019t find one that fits their character and don\u2019t want to create their own or use a fan created one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T11:40:01-07:00","id":1238639,"title":"","content":"Also the corebook tries to frame kiths as being the game's equivalent of a z-splat, aka &quot;this is totally optional and you don't have to get this&quot;.<br /> <br /> ...make of that what you will.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T12:04:28-07:00","id":1238647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1238639#post1238639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also the corebook tries to frame kiths as being the game's equivalent of a z-splat, aka &quot;this is totally optional and you don't have to get this&quot;.<br /> <br /> ...make of that what you will.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which is <i>really weird</i> now, as from Previews I remember that Kiths where changed in 2E that Gentry forced on you - i.e. whole reason you were kidnapped to Arcadia, more or less - and Seemings were only yours characters 'answer' to that kidnapping - agreeing in the role putted by Others or going rebel against it. Not having Kith, in that light, is totally against games narrative. You need to be slave first, to become free from slavery...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T12:14:58-07:00","id":1238652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1238647#post1238647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Which is <i>really weird</i> now, as from Previews I remember that Kiths where changed in 2E that Gentry forced on you - i.e. whole reason you were kidnapped to Arcadia, more or less - and Seemings were only yours characters 'answer' to that kidnapping - agreeing in the role putted by Others or going rebel against it. Not having Kith, in that light, is totally against games narrative. You need to be slave first, to become free from slavery...</div> </div> </div> </div>That has been changed between the Hill version and the current one. Seeming <i>can</i> be a character's response, or a general role forced upon them by the Gentry. Kith, <i>mechanically</i> is optional, in that you don't <i>need</i> to have a Kith. It's like a Specialty, but for an X-Splat instead of a Skill (and they aren't restricted to specific X-Splats), and they have more mechanical heft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T12:40:57-07:00","id":1238661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1238533#post1238533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If they included the Toronto Courts without changing them severely, it would seem like they\u2019d stolen David Hill\u2019s idea and didn\u2019t bother crediting or paying him for it. It\u2019s the same problem with Tokyo. That\u2019s why we\u2019ll need to rely on fan updates based on the Underhill previews.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hill was the Dev, but did not write the Toronto setting, I'll look up who did later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T19:37:28-07:00","id":1238757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1238647#post1238647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Which is <i>really weird</i> now, as from Previews I remember that Kiths where changed in 2E that Gentry forced on you - i.e. whole reason you were kidnapped to Arcadia, more or less - and Seemings were only yours characters 'answer' to that kidnapping - agreeing in the role putted by Others or going rebel against it. Not having Kith, in that light, is totally against games narrative. You need to be slave first, to become free from slavery...</div> </div> </div> </div>Seemings have changed since the Hill previews. They can either be what the Gentry made you into, how you escaped, or what your new attitude is to your new life. This opens up what your life was like during and after your durance without necessarily affecting what Seeming your character is for the vast majority of the game.<br /> <br /> Likewise, a Kith isn't always something your Keeper bestowed upon you. In fact, it can be something you crafted and escaped Arcadia with, or found/earned via the Hedge after escaping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T07:11:13-07:00","id":1238900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">5) Hobgoblins and Huntsmen now have Virtues and Vices as well instead of solely relying on their Aspirations and concepts for shorthand characterization.<br /> 6) The hobgoblin Conditions have picked up a bonus to Clarity damage rolls \u2014 +1 for Hedge Denizen, +2 for Goblin Queen.</div> </div> </div> </div>7) The Sorcerer\u2019s Rebuke contract now has a loophole, which was missing from the previews.<br /> 8) The Mantle of Frost contract's exceptional success outcome has been removed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was there anything particular in the KS drafts that people felt like needed to be addressed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like how clarity damage is applied. Changelings only roll their Wyrd rating as a damage pool, no matter what the cause of the breaking point was, which is ridiculous at low Wyrd levels. If I understand correctly, a changeling with Wyrd 1 can experience the greatest trauma imaginable and he would still only roll one die. And that's without taking touchstones into account, which can reduce the roll even further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24457-draziel","name":"DRaziel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T13:32:42-07:00","id":1240566,"title":"","content":"Is the Errata thread for the purposes of making a later PDF and Print version without the errors or is the PDF that they sent the final one and they will send alongside an errata log with all the listed errors?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24237-pluvinarch","name":"Pluvinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T14:00:44-07:00","id":1240574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pluvinarch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1240566#post1240566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the Errata thread for the purposes of making a later PDF and Print version without the errors or is the PDF that they sent the final one and they will send alongside an errata log with all the listed errors?</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea with the errata thread is that many eyes make light work. Even with lots of editorial sweeps, things always creep through, especially with books this big. Fresh eyes help spot them though, especially when those fresh eyes are fans who have never seen the book before. Once the eratta thread is closed, the changes will be compiled and adjusted for the final PDF version. After that has been uploaded onto DTRPG, then the book with be made available by Print-On-Demand so that the printed copies should be error free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T14:02:34-07:00","id":1240576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1240574#post1240574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even with lots of editorial sweeps, things always creep through, especially with books this big.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heck, the Mage book still has errors that I'm noticing well after everyone combed over it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T14:03:42-07:00","id":1240577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1240574#post1240574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The idea with the errata thread is that many eyes make light work. Even with lots of editorial sweeps, things always creep through, especially with books this big. Fresh eyes help spot them though, especially when those fresh eyes are fans who have never seen the book before. Once the eratta thread is closed, the changes will be compiled and adjusted for the final PDF version. After that has been uploaded onto DTRPG, then the book with be made available by Print-On-Demand so that the printed copies should be error free.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice to know. Yes, that makes much more sense. Thanks<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24237-pluvinarch","name":"Pluvinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T19:33:40-07:00","id":1240689,"title":"","content":"Cool, the Jumpstart is off to Second Drafts!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DRaziel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1238900#post1238900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like how clarity damage is applied. Changelings only roll their Wyrd rating as a damage pool, no matter what the cause of the breaking point was, which is ridiculous at low Wyrd levels. If I understand correctly, a changeling with Wyrd 1 can experience the greatest trauma imaginable and he would still only roll one die. And that's without taking touchstones into account, which can reduce the roll even further.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really? There is the table of modifiers to your DP on p.104-105. And if we go with your suggestion on &quot;greatest trauma imaginable&quot;, which I'd say would be the equivalent of &quot;Strongly associated with the changeling\u2019s durance or results in a surrender to a True Fae&quot;, which is a modifier of +3. Which even if you were a newly made changeling at Wyrd 1, that's a 4 DP you're rolling for Clarity damage.<br /> <br /> Seems like enough of a deal to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T20:16:50-07:00","id":1240704,"title":"","content":"Those are modifiers to your breaking point roll, not to the clarity damage. All they do is increase the odds that you will have to roll that one die, and that it will be severe damage instead of mild.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T20:38:15-07:00","id":1240707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1240704#post1240704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are modifiers to your breaking point roll, not to the clarity damage. All they do is increase the odds that you will have to roll that one die, and that it will be severe damage instead of mild.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of the whole niche behind staying at Wyrd 1 forever \u2014 you have less pressing internal problems to deal with at the price of being less personally equipped to handle threats like Huntsmen and such. You don't have to deal with any frailties beyond the iron standard, either, but you also qualify for practically none benefits in the form of Merits, which is fine and good if you're playing a game solely devoted to struggling with the mundane obstacles to reclaiming your old life or forging a new one and substantially less so in the event that, say, dreameating hobgoblins find your Bastion to be fallow ground for sowing nightmares.<br /> <br /> Clarity's mechanical place in the game's resource management cycle is similar to Health in Vampire \u2014 very easy to maintain in the early game when you don't have the rider clauses for five different flavors of occult power dragging at your time. The later game is where that's supposed to be increasingly untenable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T23:46:55-07:00","id":1240737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DRaziel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1238900#post1238900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like how clarity damage is applied. Changelings only roll their Wyrd rating as a damage pool, no matter what the cause of the breaking point was, which is ridiculous at low Wyrd levels. If I understand correctly, a changeling with Wyrd 1 can experience the greatest trauma imaginable and he would still only roll one die. And that's without taking touchstones into account, which can reduce the roll even further.</div> </div> </div> </div>9) Several Conditions now add dice to Clarity damage rolls, including Lost, Frightened, Cowed, Paranoid, Amnesia, and other mundane emotional effects, in addition to more supernatural fare like Glamour Addicted and Oathbreaker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T02:30:32-07:00","id":1240772,"title":"","content":"Changeling Jumpstart is in second drafts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T20:23:24-07:00","id":1241139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1240689#post1240689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool, the Jumpstart is off to Second Drafts!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not really? There is the table of modifiers to your DP on p.104-105. And if we go with your suggestion on &quot;greatest trauma imaginable&quot;, which I'd say would be the equivalent of &quot;Strongly associated with the changeling\u2019s durance or results in a surrender to a True Fae&quot;, which is a modifier of +3. Which even if you were a newly made changeling at Wyrd 1, that's a 4 DP you're rolling for Clarity damage.<br /> <br /> Seems like enough of a deal to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another thing worth mentioning is how the higher your wyrd is, the closer to being akin to a true fae yourself--the purpose and intent behind events grows stronger with you, and your emotions more extreme, or, that was how it was in 1E, but I didn't see anything precluding emotional sensitivity in 2E. I'd say, the higher your wyrd is, the more sensitive you are to shocks--as all fae feel emotions deeply, strongly, like a tidal wave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T02:15:01-07:00","id":1241212,"title":"","content":"The only two benefits to having low Wyrd is no frailities and low clarity damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T10:17:11-07:00","id":1241367,"title":"","content":"Low Wyrd also limits the range of Huntsmen alerts and Hedge Gate opening that come with dropping your Mask, which is a requirement for making Bargain Pledges with Mortals and other non-Changelings. So Low Wyrd definitely helps make it easier to hide.<br /> <br /> I think... Correct me if I'm wrong, please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2776-nedolfnahoj","name":"nedolfnahoj","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T15:42:33-07:00","id":1241529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nedolfnahoj</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1241367#post1241367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Low Wyrd also limits the range of Huntsmen alerts and Hedge Gate opening that come with dropping your Mask, which is a requirement for making Bargain Pledges with Mortals and other non-Changelings. So Low Wyrd definitely helps make it easier to hide.<br /> <br /> I think... Correct me if I'm wrong, please.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'll give you huntsmen, but I can see being able to blow open a bunch of Hedge gates at once as being more of a huge benefit with some risks, then a negative. <br /> <br /> I mean what an awesome use for hedge gates as trap doors and other creative uses. <br /> <br /> Imagine I build a series of floor doors and then put carpets over them, then when someone attacks me in the room, I drop the mask and dozens of different gateways to the hedge open underneath my foes, dropping them in different parts of the hedge. Or using a series of Hedgegates for an ambush. <br /> <br /> I think one can get very creative with dropping the mask and using it's down sides to your advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T00:31:14-07:00","id":1241718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DRaziel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1238900#post1238900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">7) The Sorcerer\u2019s Rebuke contract now has a loophole, which was missing from the previews.<br /> 8) The Mantle of Frost contract's exceptional success outcome has been removed.</div> </div> </div> </div>9) Hunterhearts now have a choice between Survival and Investigation for their Kith Blessing (used to be Investigation only).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13733-betterworldz","name":"BetterWorldz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T08:25:06-07:00","id":1241847,"title":"","content":"From a setting or design standpoint, what does it mean that some Contracts require Willpower to activate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T09:16:56-07:00","id":1241868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1241847#post1241847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a setting or design standpoint, what does it mean that some Contracts require Willpower to activate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some Contracts by default require a Willpower, yes. Evoking the Loophole of a Contract also doesn't waive the Wilpower cost, just the Glamour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T09:22:39-07:00","id":1241872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1241868#post1241868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some Contracts by default require a Willpower, yes. Evoking the Loophole of a Contract also doesn't waive the Wilpower cost, just the Glamour.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. What I mean is, what makes a Contract cost Willpower alongside Glamour? Is there an underlying logic? I'm especially wondering since in the setting Contracts are described as mystical bargains between a changeling as a supernatural force, so what does it mean that for some of these bargains, one has to give away a small bit of oneself in order to get results?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T09:25:02-07:00","id":1241874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BetterWorldz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1241718#post1241718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 9) Hunterhearts now have a choice between Survival and Investigation for their Kith Blessing (used to be Investigation only).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>10) Theif of Reason (Sword) now has an Elemental seeming effect instead of a Beast one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13733-betterworldz","name":"BetterWorldz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T10:28:21-07:00","id":1241906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1241872#post1241872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right. What I mean is, what makes a Contract cost Willpower alongside Glamour? Is there an underlying logic? I'm especially wondering since in the setting Contracts are described as mystical bargains between a changeling as a supernatural force, so what does it mean that for some of these bargains, one has to give away a small bit of oneself in order to get results?</div> </div> </div> </div>These are usually contracts that deal with imposing your will on the scenario. This includes contracts that let you turn back time by ten seconds, to push fate towards a particular (if vague) outcome, or to make sure that at a meeting between potentially hostile people nobody does anything violent towards one another. Mechanically, this prevents the player from abusing the power of these contracts by imposing a cost that is harder to get/negate than Glamour via the Loophole. In-universe, it could easily be that for the contract to work the Changeling needs to invest some pretty serious effort to get the job done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T13:47:33-07:00","id":1242039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1240772#post1240772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling Jumpstart is in second drafts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty excited for this, do you think it'll take more than a month to finish up? I wouldn't think that too much would need to go into a jumpstart after the book is released.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-05T16:17:21-07:00","id":1243056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1242039#post1242039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty excited for this, do you think it'll take more than a month to finish up? I wouldn't think that too much would need to go into a jumpstart after the book is released.</div> </div> </div> </div>Final drafts isn't the last phase; after that's done, there are a bunch more phases. Several development passes, editing, layout and art direction, proofing, etc. So yes, more than a month.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T12:18:54-07:00","id":1248167,"title":"","content":"Jumpstart's off at Development while the Companion is now in Second Drafts!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T06:00:16-07:00","id":1249102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1248167#post1248167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jumpstart's off at Development while the Companion is now in Second Drafts!</div> </div> </div> </div> It seems to be moving up in a good pace, I hope they introduce Kith and Kin soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T23:35:20-07:00","id":1251290,"title":"","content":"Looks like the speedy development keeps going, since the Jumpstart is now off to Editing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T05:51:42-07:00","id":1251359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1251290#post1251290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks like the speedy development keeps going, since the Jumpstart is now off to Editing!</div> </div> </div> </div> I have a feeling that the Companion will be in Development in a week or two. And Art direction will be extremely brief when it gets there, as I don't think they are commissioning new art for it except maybe the cover, and maybe chapter titles or something minor like that. <br /> <br /> Also the Jumpstart and Companion are moving so quickly because A) they are small, the Companion only has 4 Chapters, no chapter fiction, little if any new art, and are very focused, and the Jumpstart is smaller then the Companion B) All the tough ground work for things like the Changeling template, the Hedge, and so on are already done, ect..., these are just some supplemary rules and examples of those rules, and not supplenary in the way of Signs of Sorcery which is like the second half of the corebook, but a small handful of additions and a small intro adventure.<br /> <br /> Kith and Kin as well as The Hedge will likely take much longer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T14:42:01-07:00","id":1251496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1251359#post1251359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a feeling that the Companion will be in Development in a week or two. And Art direction will be extremely brief when it gets there, as I don't think they are commissioning new art for it except maybe the cover, and maybe chapter titles or something minor like that.<br /> <br /> Also the Jumpstart and Companion are moving so quickly because A) they are small, the Companion only has 4 Chapters, no chapter fiction, little if any new art, and are very focused, and the Jumpstart is smaller then the Companion B) All the tough ground work for things like the Changeling template, the Hedge, and so on are already done, ect..., these are just some supplemary rules and examples of those rules, and not supplenary in the way of Signs of Sorcery which is like the second half of the corebook, but a small handful of additions and a small intro adventure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean. That's a lot of assumptions you're making there on very little information.<br /> <br /> Unless if I missed something and there was a rough page count estimate dropped somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T15:40:54-07:00","id":1251778,"title":"","content":"yeah, there hasn't been much talk about the page counts or art for the Jumpstart and Companion. Omegaphallic, being an ardent fan of the game, is most likely speculating using information gleaned from previous supplements that OPP has kickstarted in the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T19:59:45-07:00","id":1251820,"title":"","content":"Now when it comes to the Jumpstart, yes it's probably reasonable to assume it will have a relatively small page count. Art work, not so much. <br /> <br /> I got my C20 jumpstart over here. And while there is reused art from the C20 corebook, there is actually quite a bit of original artwork in it. <br /> <br /> And CtD was always one of the less popular WoD gamelines. Versus the way more popular CtL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T07:08:30-07:00","id":1251906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1251820#post1251820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now when it comes to the Jumpstart, yes it's probably reasonable to assume it will have a relatively small page count. Art work, not so much. <br /> <br /> I got my C20 jumpstart over here. And while there is reused art from the C20 corebook, there is actually quite a bit of original artwork in it. <br /> <br /> And CtD was always one of the less popular WoD gamelines. Versus the way more popular CtL.</div> </div> </div> </div> Really, I didn't expect they'd use the limited funds towards much in the way of art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T07:17:31-07:00","id":1251907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firefly Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1251778#post1251778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yeah, there hasn't been much talk about the page counts or art for the Jumpstart and Companion. Omegaphallic, being an ardent fan of the game, is most likely speculating using information gleaned from previous supplements that OPP has kickstarted in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div> What I did, was note the Kickstarter goal of $50,000, compared it to what I believed was the basic funding level for the Jumpstart and Companion, looked at how many subjects for the Companion we hit as stretch goals, and then noted how fast they we're moving through the process compared to a lot of other books. <br /> <br /> I estimate depending on how much art they get that they will be available in 2 to 3 months, before 2019.<br /> <br /> I also estimate Kith and Kin will take longer then both the Companion and Jumpstart combined, as the funding for that is likely nearly as large as the asking funding (not including stretch goals, just initial funding) for Changeling corebook. And it will have at least 6 Chapters, possibly an intro as well, <br /> and a Kin Chapter as well. That one I suspect will get more art too. Also remember that the stretch goals for Kith and Kin are to expand the already planned book, so it's funding will be larger then just what was stretch goaled for it. <br /> <br /> The Hedge I have no idea as I have nothing to base an estimate on, as it wasn't discussed in the Kickstarter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-16T10:37:28-07:00","id":1260934,"title":"","content":"So the Jumpstart was actually in post-editing development last week, but this week it seems to have sped along and is now in Art Direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-20T01:50:49-07:00","id":1261744,"title":"","content":"Do the old rules to willingly decrease your Wyrd via Glamour diet still apply?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T22:34:09-07:00","id":1262292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1261744#post1261744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the old rules to willingly decrease your Wyrd via Glamour diet still apply?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless if my Ctrl+F-fu failed me, changelings being able to deliberately lower their Wyrd isn't a thing period in 2e, at least in the corebook.<br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------------------<br /> Jumpstart must have quite a few Steed contracts under its belt, since now the thing is off to Proofing already! At this rate, I'm starting to wonder if this thing will beat the corebook to first release, or if the two will come out around the same time.<br /> <br /> Additionally, &quot;Oak, Ash, and Thorn&quot; is now in Development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T11:32:48-08:00","id":1270156,"title":"","content":"Per today\u2019s update, last day to update your BackerKit survey, shipping address, pledges, add-one, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T10:40:37-08:00","id":1273596,"title":"","content":"I just got here, so sorry if this was adressed: For those of us who didn't know of the kickstarter, when and how can we purchase 2nd ed? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24888-tiasdk","name":"TiasDK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T10:47:46-08:00","id":1273598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TiasDK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1273596#post1273596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just got here, so sorry if this was adressed: For those of us who didn't know of the kickstarter, when and how can we purchase 2nd ed? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It will be available through DTRPG at some point in the coming weeks, going from the fact that <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/soooo-unplugged-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\">last week's Monday Meeting Notes</a> have it firmly in the &quot;At Press&quot; stage of production.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T12:22:24-08:00","id":1274601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1273598#post1273598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It will be available through DTRPG at some point in the coming weeks, going from the fact that <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/soooo-unplugged-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\">last week's Monday Meeting Notes</a> have it firmly in the &quot;At Press&quot; stage of production.</div> </div> </div> </div>Finally! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","name":"Xaielao","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T14:30:08-08:00","id":1274625,"title":"","content":"I Didn\u2019t back the Kickstarter but Question? Can Animals by Faetouched","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T17:24:54-08:00","id":1274643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1274625#post1274625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I Didn\u2019t back the Kickstarter but Question? Can Animals by Faetouched</div> </div> </div> </div>Not without some really weird shit happening, seeing as Fae-Touched are made when two people make a promise, one of them becomes a changeling, and the other one keeps their side of the promise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T17:44:46-08:00","id":1274644,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s a way you could Stretch \u2018Make a Promise\u2019 to include Non Verbal communication and therefore Doggos","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T17:55:14-08:00","id":1274646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1274644#post1274644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s a way you could Stretch \u2018Make a Promise\u2019 to include Non Verbal communication and therefore Doggos</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the last step is &quot;the character who kept the promise goes into the Hedge to look for the character they made the promise with, then made their way back out,&quot; and the promises in question are not small things? Nah. Your dog might recognize you when you get back and know that your fetch is a fake, but it's not going to gain the ability to seal statements of intent or participate in oaths just because it loves you a lot.<br /> <br /> Now, hobgoblins, on the other hand\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T19:00:08-08:00","id":1274647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1274646#post1274646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the last step is &amp;quot;the character who kept the promise goes into the Hedge to look for the character they made the promise with, then made their way back out,&amp;quot; and the promises in question are not small things? Nah. Your dog might recognize you when you get back and know that your fetch is a fake, but it's not going to gain the ability to seal statements of intent or participate in oaths just because it loves you a lot.<br /> <br /> Now, hobgoblins, on the other hand\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>If a dog goes to the hedge to get its person back, I\u2019m not going to deny it faetouched status! That sounds like an awesome heartbreaking story!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T20:41:13-08:00","id":1274655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1274647#post1274647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a dog goes to the hedge to get its person back, I\u2019m not going to deny it faetouched status! That sounds like an awesome heartbreaking story!</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Fae-Touched&quot; doesn't just mean &quot;can see through the Mask&quot; and all the relevant mechanics of being Avowed that don't require personlike intelligence amount to a pair of one-die bonuses. Your dog is not going to become smart enough to use Contracts or navigate the Hedge or actually meaningfully interact with pledgecraft just because it loves you a lot!<br /> <br /> This is a very definite case of words meaning things! If your dog gains fae power from going into the Hedge to get you after faithfully guarding your home until your family moves away, it's not going to become a Fae-Touched dog, because several of the mechanics of being Fae-Touched have no relevance to dogs! That is a <i>different unique story-based circumstance!</i><br /> <br /> You gain nothing from trying to figure out how the Madness and Hedge Addiction Conditions apply to a dog or how the necessary actions of using simple Common Contracts like Seven-League Leap or Overpowering Dread or Hostile Takeover can even be done by a mentally ordinary dog that you would not have gotten with less headache by saying &quot;your faithful hound can always find you and has learned a few Dread Powers and how to speak from its long journey through the Hedge&quot; and being done with it, and doing that second thing <i>is what you have to do to not just be ignoring what Fae-Touched are</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T07:46:53-08:00","id":1274715,"title":"","content":"First edition even had a thing where animals that spent too long in the hedge became hobgoblins. It's pretty easy to just turn a dog into a wyrd one hobgoblin if you really want a dog empowered by Hedge magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T23:17:57-08:00","id":1275032,"title":"","content":"So, while it seems like the finalized hard copy corebooks are still getting sent to the shipper, and a PoD proof being ordered to look at...<br /> <br /> ...it looks backers will soon be seeing the CtL2e Jumpstart!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-19T10:40:05-08:00","id":1275326,"title":"","content":"Pretty damn excited about the Jumpstart to be honest. I've been hyping a few of my coworkers who've never RP'd ever and wanted to start them off with something like this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-19T10:49:36-08:00","id":1275327,"title":"","content":"Jumpstart PDFs should begin distribution tomorrow (Thursday)! So excited!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.