ank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T13:06:39-08:00","id":1281553,"title":"","content":"I just got mine yesterday, so some are probably taking a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T17:20:13-08:00","id":1282039,"title":"","content":"If the Storyteller's Screen PDF is on your list of rewards, double check your Digital Rewards tab - the code should be there. If it's not, please click on Rich's name on the KS page and use the contact creator button and I'll get the message.<br /> <br /> If the screen PDF isn't on your list or rewards but should be, double check to ensure you had it as an ADD ON reward and that payment was processed. The Reference Screen PDF was not part of any reward tier, only an Add On, so had to be confirmed in BackerKit. If the payment didn't process correctly, there's a chance the Add On wasn't properly processed.<br /> <br /> If you wanted the screen PDF and meant to add it to your rewards but forgot, the good news is that it's available for purchase on DrivethruRPG and is a pretty quick transaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22659-kickstarter-james","name":"Kickstarter James","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar22659_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T17:31:09-08:00","id":1282042,"title":"","content":"God the book is nice. And the embossing worked out better then the original cover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T19:31:45-08:00","id":1282057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kickstarter James</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1282039#post1282039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Reference Screen PDF was not part of any reward tier, only an Add On, so had to be confirmed in BackerKit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, sorry I didn't realize that, thought the pdf screen came with the physical one by default. Please ignore my Kickstarter PM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13733-betterworldz","name":"BetterWorldz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T21:23:07-08:00","id":1282078,"title":"","content":"were the grimms taken out due to the complications? also how do seemings work now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T22:14:39-08:00","id":1282083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1282078#post1282078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">were the grimms taken out due to the complications? also how do seemings work now</div> </div> </div> </div>The one from A Grimm Dark Era? <br /> <br /> I don't know about being left out due to complications, but yeah they're not in the corebook. <br /> <br /> As far as we know, there are no official plans to update any of the 1e Dark Eras material to 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T22:33:38-08:00","id":1282085,"title":"","content":"Grimms were taken out because they don't work with the Final Second Edition version of them. Seemings are back to the broad archetypes that you follow in faerie tales.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T22:45:00-08:00","id":1282088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1282078#post1282078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">were the grimms taken out due to the complications?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Grimms were never in the corebook to begin with and are still in the Dark Era where they're introduced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> also how do seemings work now </div> </div> </div>Archetypes of fae transformation as they were in 1e, albeit with a more nebulous point of acquisition instead of being the initial sketches of your Keeper's adjustments; you can be a Darkling because your Keeper made you one or because you made yourself one to escape or because the way you escaped turned you into one or anything in between, but becoming a Beast is no longer contingent upon casting aside your care for the pecking order, for example.<br /> <br /> On a more granular level, a lot of the old Ogre toolkit has been shuffled over to the Elementals by virtue of falling into the Sword Regalia. The Wizened have had the focus of their condition shifted away from their diminishment and toward the expertise born of long experience, while the Darklings have carried over the playtest writeup's emphasis on obscurity. The logic behind the Fairest's curse is a little more readily visible, and the Beasts' signature Regalia manages to facilitate the same easily-the-lone-wolf angle for a completely different reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Typo. 01-22-2019, 01:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T04:58:47-08:00","id":1282113,"title":"","content":"so Grimm were left out and seeming are just like 1st edition but now hangs more on how a changeling escaped Arcadia, thanks guys, much appreciated!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T11:20:50-08:00","id":1282161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1282113#post1282113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so Grimm were left out and seeming are just like 1st edition but now hangs more on how a changeling escaped Arcadia, thanks guys, much appreciated!</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this needs some clarity to give context to the answers. <br /> <br /> Grimm wasn't exactly <i>left out</i>, but instead it's just another name for Beasts (rather than its own Seeming).<br /> <br /> And Seeming doesn't really hang on a &quot;thing&quot; precisely. Think of each of the 2nd Seemings as a &quot;Story Archetype&quot;. A character is a Beast because they fit the mold of that Story Archetype. It's a very broad term and because of that, the &quot;why&quot; a character is that Seeming is totally variable. A character is Fairest because that's her Story. Why is it her Story? Well it could be because her Keeper made her Fairest, or because she needed to be Fairest to survive/escape, or She's Fairest because that kind of story is how she copes now that she's left Arcadia. The origin of gaining the Seeming has less of a role than the fact that that's the story you fit into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T11:33:57-08:00","id":1282164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1282161#post1282161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Grimm wasn't exactly <i>left out</i>, but instead it's just another name for Beasts (rather than its own Seeming).</div> </div> </div> </div>I would disagree. The Grims and Grimms are two very different Seemings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T13:57:14-08:00","id":1282195,"title":"","content":"&quot;Grim&quot; is a casual nickname for the Beast seeming, as in church grim. The Grimm seeming (as in Brothers Grimm) wasn't &quot;left out,&quot; it exists in Dark Eras as an era-specific seeming relevant to that time and place, just like many of the other character options you find in Dark Eras. If you'd like to update the mechanics and use it at your table in a modern game, feel free; but note that the Wyrd doesn't work on narrative logic anymore in 2e, so you probably won't see canonical support for doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T15:55:28-08:00","id":1288110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1282195#post1282195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> [...]but note that the Wyrd doesn't work on narrative logic anymore in 2e, so you probably won't see canonical support for doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Newcomer to Changeling here - can you explain what you mean by this? How did it used to work / how does it work now... and what, if anything, does this mean for 1e Fluff conversions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T16:58:20-08:00","id":1288116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anachronistic Jam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1288110#post1288110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Newcomer to Changeling here - can you explain what you mean by this? How did it used to work / how does it work now... and what, if anything, does this mean for 1e Fluff conversions?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't honestly mean a whole lot \u2014 1e split the difference between &quot;faerie magic works on principles of equal-if-sometimes-unusual exchange&quot; and &quot;faerie magic enforces the patterns of fairy tales as an in-universe end unto itself in a way that tends to produce describable narrative.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Underhill version of the game chose to focus on the latter, whereas the published version angles more distinctly toward the former for the understandable reason that, among other things, there's not really much need for there to be a force making things work like myth/legend/folklore in-universe when the universe is already set up for that to be the way things tend to work.<br /> <br /> For the non-mechanical aspects of 1e conversions, it pretty much only means that stuff like Talecrafting isn't baked into the way the universe works \u2014 changelings don't have magic powers because there's a story archetype that they were made to fill that gives them magic powers, they have magic powers because they were the somewhat-favored servants of beings who negotiated magic powers for themselves and their households. <a href=\"http://worsethanmanyfairies.tumblr.com/post/160842155600/thatgirlnevershutsup-violent-darts\" target=\"_blank\">It's a legal-political-economic framework rather than an abstract narrative framework</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T17:38:52-08:00","id":1288121,"title":"","content":"That said, the Hedge (being shaped by people's beliefs and stories) does have a lot of narrative aspects to it. So if you do want to update the Grimms to 2e at your table, you could build off that without contradicting anything in the corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-29T19:00:07-07:00","id":1328202,"title":"","content":"Stretch goals are getting closer! Oak, Ash, &amp; Thorn is off to Manuscript Approvals!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T01:20:45-07:00","id":1328238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1328202#post1328202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stretch goals are getting closer! Oak, Ash, &amp; Thorn is off to Manuscript Approvals!</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah it was stuck in Development for a long time. I still don't get what they do in development stage, I get what every other stage is except Development and post editing development. <br /> <br /> Hopefully the rest won't take too long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T02:47:55-07:00","id":1328244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1328238#post1328238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah it was stuck in Development for a long time. I still don't get what they do in development stage, I get what every other stage is except Development and post editing development. <br /> <br /> Hopefully the rest won't take too long.</div> </div> </div> </div>They\u2019re creating content that isn\u2019t a rehash of 1e nor so divorced from its roots it\u2019s not Changeling anymore. They\u2019re creating the mechanics, the fluff, the lore and in general trying to make things open ended that people can use it without it being so singular that people can\u2019t do new stuff with it. Development isn\u2019t easy, and I\u2019d prefer that it goes slower so they can do a more thorough job than blitzing through and making a really bad module that kills peoples\u2019 interests in future works. I do agree with the sentiment of being happy that it is moving along though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T04:39:23-07:00","id":1328253,"title":"","content":"I think it helps to focus on development stages as the part of the process where everything comes together. It's the stages where all the different parts of the book are brought together into a cohesive whole. <br /> <br /> The first development stage is the most important, because it's taking all the parts that the different authors have been working on, and turning them into a single manuscript that's one book instead of a bunch of parts of a book. The writing gets firmed up into one authorial voice. Mechanics are checked to keep them in-line with the rest of the game. Etc.<br /> <br /> The post-editing development is working in all the feedback from manuscript approval, content and copy editing, and so on to turn the manuscript into the final text. Again, it's the process of taking a bunch of little parts, and building the full book out of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T09:40:50-07:00","id":1328316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1328253#post1328253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it helps to focus on development stages as the part of the process where everything comes together. It's the stages where all the different parts of the book are brought together into a cohesive whole. <br /> <br /> The first development stage is the most important, because it's taking all the parts that the different authors have been working on, and turning them into a single manuscript that's one book instead of a bunch of parts of a book. The writing gets firmed up into one authorial voice. Mechanics are checked to keep them in-line with the rest of the game. Etc.<br /> <br /> The post-editing development is working in all the feedback from manuscript approval, content and copy editing, and so on to turn the manuscript into the final text. Again, it's the process of taking a bunch of little parts, and building the full book out of them.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you, so development is where they take the written parts, make sure they fit together, and make a whole out of them. Now I feel like I understand thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T21:30:53-07:00","id":1332775,"title":"","content":"OA&amp;T is in post-Editing Development!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T07:45:02-07:00","id":1332813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1332775#post1332775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OA&amp;T is in post-Editing Development!</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. What does that mean again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T08:06:21-07:00","id":1332816,"title":"","content":"It's actually currently in post-approval development, which means it just came back from WW approved and now I'm checking it over to see if it needs any tweaks before I send it to Dixie for editing!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T10:59:52-08:00","id":1347510,"title":"","content":"(cross-posted from other threads)<br /> <br /> New stuff revealed regarding &quot;Oak, Ash, and Thorn&quot; and &quot;Kith and Kin&quot; in the latest <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/episode-77-the-chronicles-of-meghan-the-fitzgerald/\" target=\"_blank\">Pathcast</a> in an interview with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2229_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2229\" data-vbnamecard=\"2229\">Meghan Fitzgerald</a> <br /> <br /> &quot;Oak, Ash, and Thorn&quot; (9:30 - 16:15)<ul><li>Entitlements: Aside from Build-an-Entitlement rules, it will include 3 example Entitlements. One of which is confirmed to be an old 1e Entitlement converted to 2e, the other two are brand new to CtL.</li> <li>Freeholds: Conflicts between freeholds, potential story seeds, etc.</li> <li>Courts &amp; Mantles: They confirm that there...will NOT be any example Courts. The reason being that the wordcount assigned was not enough to do a full dive into Courts. It's going to explore plots of your characters establishing a Court IC. Also... 2e Courtless! Organizations, Mantles, Bargains, and their version of &quot;court&quot; Contracts are what's also explored in this chapter.</li> <li>One word spoiler... &quot;BriarNET&quot;.</li> <li>Tokens: Baubles and Trinkets getting their 2e update.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> &quot;Kith and Kin&quot; (16:15-20:45)<ul><li>Meghan reiterates that this book is NOT a &quot;Book of Kiths&quot;...in the sense that no, the book is not filled with nothing but more example kiths.That no, the book is more accurately a &quot;Changeling 2e Player's Guide&quot;</li> <li>There is the one chapter devoted to Kiths...and reassures that there's &quot;a lot&quot;. She does talk about how not every 1e Kith is going to be converted in the chapter...due to the design changes from 1e to 2e. Specifically, a lot of the 1e Kiths are now redundant due to the design aim of kiths being divorced from Seemings. Example given was that in 1e, all the Seemings had their own water kith. But in 2e, it makes no sense to bring all of them forward, so now there's only the one water kith that all of the Seemings have access to.</li> <li>Oaths chapter: expanded and additional Oaths.</li> <li>Regalia: New Contracts and more importantly...&quot;Build-a-Regalia&quot; rules.</li> <li>First chapter is a &quot;Changeling psychology&quot; chapter. In exploring what it's like to roleplay a changeling. One example give was unusual cases of if a changeling emerged from the Hedge...in space. Or 100 years after they got taken. Or 100 years before you were born. The latter: oh hai Mummy tie-in potential!!!</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"